capacitor is increased, does its capacitance increase? Explain. Find the capacitance that can be obtained by combining three 10 µF capacitors in all possible ways.","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":4,"text":"What must be done to increase the capacitance of a capacitor? The plates of a parallel-plate capacitor are 50 cm² in area and 1 mm apart, (i) what is its capacitance? (ii) when the capacitance is connected to a 24 V battery, what is the charge on each plate? (iii) what is the energy of the capacitor? (κ = 1, ε₀ = 8.85 × 10⁻¹² C² N⁻¹ m⁻²) $","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":5,"text":"When the distance between the two parallel plates of a capacitor is doubled, by what percent does its capacitance change? Three capacitors of capacitance 3 µF, 10 µF and 15 µF are connected in series with 100 V battery. What is the charge and the potential difference on each capacitor?","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":6,"text":"When an insulating material is inserted between the conductors of a capacitor in a vacuum, does its capacitance increase or decrease? Explain. What is the equivalent unit of farad? A 35 µF capacitor is needed, but only 10 µF capacitors are available. How should a minimum number of 10 µF capacitors be connected so that the combination has a capacitance of 35 µF?","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":7,"text":"What must be done to increase the capacitance of a capacitor? The equivalent capacitance is 10 µF when n identical capacitors are connected in parallel and 0.4 µF when they are connected in series. Determine Nand the capacitance of each capacitor.","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":8,"text":"When an insulating material is inserted between the conductors of a capacitor in a vacuum, does its capacitance increase or decrease? Explain. What potential difference must be applied across a 10 µF capacitor if it is to have an energy content of 1.5 J?","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":9,"text":"If an insulating material is inserted between the conductors of a capacitor in a vacuum, does its capacitance increase or decrease? Explain. A charged capacitor of capacitance C = 35 µF is discharged through a resistor of resistance R = 100 Ω. What is the elapsed time when the voltage falls to 10% of its original value?","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":10,"text":"What is the concept of capacitance, and what factors influence the capacitance of a capacitor? Three capacitors have capacitances of 5 µF, 10 µF and 15 µF. (i) Find the equivalent capacitance when they are connected in parallel. (ii) Find the equivalent capacitance when they are connected in series. When the distance between two parallel plates having the charges of equal","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":11,"text":"Magnitude and opposite signs is reduced, what will happen to the capacitance and potential difference of the plates? Three capacitors of capacitances 3 µF, 10 µF and 15 µF are connected in series with 100 V battery. What is the charge and the potential difference on each capacitor? On what factors does the capacitance of the capacitor depend? In capacitor","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":12,"text":"Charging and discharging, why is a resistor required to connect with the capacitor? The plates of a parallel-plate capacitor are 50 cm² in area and 1 mm apart, (i) What is its capacitance? (ii) When the capacitor is connected to a 24 V battery, what is the charge on each plate? (iii) What is the energy of the capacitor? (ε₀ = 8.85 × 10⁻¹² C² N⁻¹ m⁻²) $","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":13,"text":"(i) When the charge on a capacitor is increased, does its capacitance increase? Explain. (ii) A capacitor stores charge Q at a potential difference V. What happens if the voltage applied to the capacitor is doubled? The equivalent capacitance is 10 µF when n identical capacitors are connected in parallel and 0.4 µF when they are connected in series. Determine Nand the capacitance of each capacitor.","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":14,"text":"Write down the 