 charges of equal","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":4,"text":"Magnitude and opposite signs is reduced, what will happen to the capacitance and potential difference of the plates? When an insulating material is inserted between the conductors of a capacitor in a vacuum, does its capacitance increase or decrease? Explain.","source":"2025 (Set 12)"}],"B9b":[{"number":1,"text":"Three capacitors of capacitance 3 µF, 10 µF and 15 µF are connected in series with 100 V battery. What is the charge and the potential difference on each capacitor?","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":2,"text":"The equivalent capacitance is 10 μF when n identical capacitors are connected in parallel and 0.4 μF when they are connected in series. Determine Nand the capacitance of each capacitor.","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":3,"text":"The plates of a parallel-plate capacitor are 50 cm² in area and 1 mm apart. (i) What is its capacitance? (ii) When the capacitor is connected to a 24 V battery, what is the charge on each plate? (ε₀ = 8.85 × 10⁻¹² C² N⁻¹ m⁻²) $ A 35 µF capacitor is needed, but only 10 µF capacitors are available. How","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":4,"text":"Should a minimum number of 10 µF capacitors be connected so that the combination has a capacitance of 35 µF? A 40 µF capacitor is needed, but only 8 µF capacitors are available. How","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":5,"text":"Should a minimum number of 8 µF capacitors be connected so that the combination has a capacitance of 40 μF? If two capacitors having the capacitances of 5 µF and 20 µF are connected","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":6,"text":"In series, find the equivalent capacitance of the combination of the two capacitors. If the potential difference of the combination is 200 V, find the potential difference of 20 µF capacitor.","source":"2025 (Set 12)"}]}}'::jsonb,0,true),
