rrent carrying conductor depend? (A. current, B. temperature, C. pressure)","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":15,"text":"In charging battery, the potential difference between the terminals is -------. (A. E + Ir, B. E – Ir, C. E)","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":16,"text":"If two batteries having equal emfs and equal internal resistances are connected in parallel, what is resultant internal resistance of combination? ! 2 (A. 2 r, B. , C. r ) \"","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":17,"text":"The amount of heat produced in a resistor due to a current flowing through it is ------- to the square of the current. (A. directly proportional, B. inversely proportional, C. not related)","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":18,"text":"Which quantity determines the rate at which electrical energy is delivered by a current? (A. electromotive force, B. electrical power, C. electric current)","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":19,"text":"Which of the following equations is the total work done in moving a unit positive charge round the complete circuit? (A. Ir, B. Ir − Ir, C. Ir + Ir)","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":20,"text":"Which of the following metals cannot be used as fuse wire? (A. silver, B. iron, C. tin-lead alloy)","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":21,"text":"On Which of the following effects of electric current a fuse operates? (A. Heating effect, B. Electrostatic effect, C. Magnetic effect)","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":22,"text":"If an electric stove of 1200 W is connected to a 220 V mains line, the current flowing through it is -------. A. 0.183A, B. 5.45 A, C. 264 000 A","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":23,"text":"Which of the following metals cannot be used as fuse wire? A. iron, B. silver, C. tin-lead alloy","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":24,"text":"What component of an electric iron is responsible for maintaining the selected temperature by switching the current on and off? A. resistor, B. thermostat, C. circuit breaker","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":25,"text":"The electromotive force (emf) of a source is defined as: (A. The potential difference across the terminals when no current flows. B. The potential difference when the current is flowing, C. The energy dissipated per unit charge)","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":26,"text":"What is the SI unit of electrical power? (A. watt, B. joule, C. volt)","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":27,"text":"What is electrical energy typically measured in? (A. watt (W), B. volts (V), C. joules (J))","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":28,"text":"At a temperature of -------, the tungsten filament emits white light. (A. 3000 °C, B. 2500 °C, C. 1800 °C)","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":29,"text":"Which of the following metals cannot be used as fuse wire? (A. iron, B. silver, C. tin-lead alloy)","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":30,"text":"On which factor does the heat produced in a current carrying conductor depend? (A. current, B. temperature, C. pressure)","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":31,"text":"When two batteries are connected in parallel, the voltage across each battery is: (A. The sum of the individual voltages, B. Equal to the voltage of one of the batteries, C. Zero)","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":32,"text":"What is the commercial unit of electrical energy? (A. joule, B. kilowatt-hour, C. watt)","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":33,"text":"In charging a battery, the potential difference between the terminals is equal to -------. (A. E+ Ir, B. Ir, C. IR)","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":34,"text":"There are joules in one kilowatt hour. 6 (A. 4.2, В. 1000, С. 3.6 × 10 )","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":35,"text":"Which quantity determines the rate at which electrical energy is delivered by a current? (A. Potential difference, B. Electrical energy, C. Electrical power)","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":36,"text":"The heating element of an electric iron is controlled by a ------- to maintain the selected temperature. (A. capacitor, B. resistor, C. thermostat)","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":37,"text":"M ica is a good electrical ------- and can withstand very high temperature. (A. conductor, B. semiconductor, C. insulator)","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":38,"text":"An electric stove has an electrical power ranging from 600 W to -------. (A. 1200 W, B. 2000 W, C. 2400 W)","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":39,"text":"A refrigerator has an electrical power ranging from 100 W to -------. (A. 250 Wb. 2000 W C. 1200 W)","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":40,"text":"The resultant emf of two batteries in ------- is the difference between the individual emfs. A. series opposing, B. series aiding, C. parallel","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":41,"text":"In a series aiding connection of two or more batteries, the resultant emf will: (A. remain the same as a single battery, B. decrease the overall voltage, C. increase the overall voltage).","source":"2026 (Set 3)"},{"number":42,"text":"The heating effect of electric current is applied in all of the following appliances except: (A. Electric stove, B. Electric iron, C. Refrigerator). SECTION B","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}]},"sectionB":{"B6a":[{"number":1,"text":"How does an emf of the source differ from potential difference across the external resistance? Why is an electric fuse required in all electrical appliances? When a battery is connected to a 2 Ω resistor it drives a current of 0.6 A through the resistor. When it is connected to a 7 Ω resistor it drives a current of 0.2 A through the resistor. Find the emf and the internal resistance of the battery.","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":2,"text":"What is the electrical energy? Express its unit. Why do we use fuses in an electric circuit? An electric circuit installed in an office contains a 10 A fuse and the voltage is 220 V. Ten 100 W electric lamps and two 150 W refrigerators are being used there. (i) Find the cost of using all the lamps and two refrigerators for 10 h. (ii) Find the maximum number of 60 W electric lamps which can be safely used in addition. (Assume that electricity cost 50 kyats per unit.)","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":3,"text":"What is electrical energy? How many joules are there in 1 kWh? Which quantity determines the rate at which electrical energy is delivered by a current? Why is electrical energy transformed into heat energy when a current flows through a resistor? An electric lamp of 60 Ω connected to a 240 V mains line is used for 45 min. (i) Find the amount of electrical energy dissipated in the lamp. (ii) Find the cost of using it if electricity costs 50 kyats per unit.","source":"2025 (Set 12)"}],"B6b":[{"number":1,"text":"Draw a simple circuit diagram of two batteries in series opposing connected with an external resistor. Two batteries each having an emf of 6 V and an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω are connected (i) in series and (ii) in parallel. Find the current in each case when the batteries are connected to a 1 Ω resistor.","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":2,"text":"Draw the circuit diagram for batteries in series aiding connected with an external resistor. When a battery is connected to a 3 Ω resistor, it drives a current of 0.6 A through the resistor. When it is connected to a 8 Ω resistor, it drives a current of 0.2 A through the resistor. Find the emf and the internal resistance of the battery.","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":3,"text":"Draw a simple circuit diagram of two batteries in series opposing connected with an external resistor. When a 12 V battery of negligible internal resistance is connected to a resistor, a current of 3 A flows through it. When another battery of emf 6 V is in the circuit in series with the first one, the current flowing through the resistor remains at 3 A. Find the internal resistance of the second battery.","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":4,"text":"Draw a diagram for an electric light bulb that is made of a glass bulb consisting a tungsten filament which has high melting point. An electric stove of 1200 W is connected to a 220 V mains line. (i) Find its resistance. (ii) Find the amount of calories produced in one second by it. (iii) Find the electrical power produced by it when the voltage of the mains line drops to 180 V.","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":5,"text":"Draw a simple circuit diagram of two batteries in series aiding connected with an external resistor. An electric stove of 1200 W is connected to a 220 V mains line. (i) Find its resistance. (ii) Find the current flowing through it. (iii) Find the amount of calories produced in one second by it. (iv) Find the electrical power produced by it when the voltage of the mains line drops to 180 V. -1 (J = 4.2 J cal )","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":6,"text":"Draw circuit diagrams of two batteries in (i) series aiding and (ii) series opposing arrangements connected with an external resistor R. Two batteries each having an emf of 6 V and an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω are connected (i) in series and (ii) in parallel. Find the current in each case when the batteries are connected to a 2 Ω resistor.","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":7,"text":"Draw a circuit diagram showing batteries connected in parallel along with an external resistor. An electric iron draws a current of 3 A when it is connected to a 220 V mains line. How many kcal of heat is produced per minute? How many joules are in 1 kWh?","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":8,"text":"Draw a circuit diagram showing batteries connected in series aiding with an external resistor. An electric circuit installed in a house contains a 5 A fuse and the voltage is 220 V. Find the maximum electrical power which can safely be used. What is the equivalent of 1 kilowatt-hour (kWh) in joules?","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":9,"text":"Draw the circuit diagram of batteries in series aiding connected with an external resistor. An electric circuit installed in an office contains a 10 A fuse and the voltage is 220 V. Ten 100 W electric lamps and two 150 W refrigerators are being used there. (i) Find the cost of using all the lamps and two refrigerators for 10 h. (ii) Find the maximum number of 60 W electric lamps which can be safely used in addition. (Assume that electricity costs 50 kyats per unit.)","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":10,"text":"Draw a circuit diagram showing two batteries in series aiding connected with an external resistor R. Label the emf E and internal resistance r for each battery, and indicate the direction of current flow. Two batteries each having an emf of 5 V and an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω are connected (i) in series and (ii) in parallel. Find the current in each case when the batteries are connected to a 1 Ω resistor.","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":11,"text":"Draw an illustration of the terminal voltage of a battery. An electric circuit installed in an office contains a 10 A fuse and the voltage is 220 V. Ten 100 W electric lamps and two 150 W refrigerators are being used there. (i) Find the cost of using all the lamps and two refrigerators for 10 h. (ii) Find the maximum number of 60 W electric lamps which can be safely used in addition. (Assume that electricity costs 50 kyats per unit.)","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}],"B8a":[{"number":1,"text":"Draw the diagrams to illustrate the electromotive force (emf) and terminal voltage of a battery.","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":2,"text":"What are open circuit and closed circuit? Illustrate with diagram. Draw the diagrams for electromotive force in an open circuit and terminal","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":3,"text":"Voltage of a battery in closed circuit. Draw the circuit diagrams for batteries in series aiding and batteries in","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":4,"text":"Parallel connected with an external resistor. Draw a circuit diagram of two batteries in parallel connected with an","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":5,"text":"External resistor.","source":"2026 (Set 1)"}],"B9a":[{"number":1,"text":"What are the advantages of connecting batteries in a series aiding configuration?","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":2,"text":"What is the difference between electromotive fore (emf) and potential difference (voltage)?","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":3,"text":"Why do we use fuses in an electric circuit? Why is electrical energy transformed into heat energy when a current flows through a resistor?","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":4,"text":"What is meant by terminal voltage (available voltage) of a battery and how is it related to emf of the battery?","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":5,"text":"On what factors does the internal resistance of a battery depend? Why is inert gas added in light bulb?","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":6,"text":"Why is electrical energy transformed into heat energy when a current flows through a resistor? Why is an electric fuse required in all electrical appliances? How many joules are there in 1 kWh?","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":7,"text":"In an electric circuit, which component is used for: (i) supply electricity (ii) close (or) open the electric circuit (iii) providing a path for the flow of electric current? What are open circuit and closed circuit?","source":"2026 (Set 1)"}],"B9b":[{"number":1,"text":"If a 1200 W electric iron is used for 1 h, by how many units does the electricity meter reading increased? Calculate the payment if one unit of electricity costs 35 kyats.","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":2,"text":"A battery has an emf of 6 V and an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω. How many batteries are necessary to pass a current of 1 A through a 22 Ω resistor in an electric circuit?","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":3,"text":"When two 6 V batteries, having the same internal resistance and connected in series, are connected to a 5 Ω resistor, the current in the circuit is 2 A. When these batteries are in parallel, a current of 1.5 A flows through when connected to another resistor. Find the resistance of the resistor.","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":4,"text":"Two batteries each having an emf of 6 V and an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω are connected (i) in series aiding and (ii) in parallel. Find the current in each case when the batteries are connected to a 1 Ω resistor.","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":5,"text":"An electric stove of 1200 W is connected to a 220 V mains line. (i) Find its resistance. (ii) Find the current flowing through it. (iii) Find the amount of calories produced in one second by it. (iv) Find the electrical power produced by it when the voltage of the mains line drops to 180 V.","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":6,"text":"When two 6 V batteries, having the same internal resistance and connected in series, are connected to a 5 Ω resistor, the current in the circuit is 2 A. When the batteries are in parallel, a current of 1.5 A flows through when connected to another resistor. Find the resistance of the resistor.","source":"2026 (Set 1)"}]}}'::jsonb,0,true),
