umber":3,"text":"In what year did Joseph Henry and Michel Faraday make their independent discoveries related to electric current and magnetic fields? (Α. 1813, Β. 1831, С. 1850)","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":4,"text":"Why is AC preferred over DC for long-distance power distribution of electrical power? (A. Bigger inductors, B. Lower energy losses, C. Thinner conductors)","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":5,"text":"What is the SI unit of magnetic flux density? (A. weber, B. tesla, C. ampere per metre)","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":6,"text":"------- current is good in long distance distribution of electrical power. (A. AC, B. DC, C. unidirectional)","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":7,"text":"Most generators give out -------. (A. alternating current, B. direct current, C.-both current).","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":8,"text":"There is no ideal transformer with ------- efficiency. (A. 99 %, B. 99.5 %, C. 100 %)","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":9,"text":"The SI unit of magnetic flux is the -------. (A. weber (Wb), B. tesla (T), C. ampere per metre (Am⁻¹))","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":10,"text":"Most of the transformers have full load efficiency -------. (A. between 95% to 98.5%, B. between 50% to 60%, C. 100%)","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":11,"text":"Which of the following meters can measure an alternating current? (A. Voltmeter, B. Ammeter, C. Moving coil galvanometer)","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":12,"text":"In ------- the electrons flow steadily in the same direction all the time. (A. an alternating current, B. a direct current, C. an electric current)","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":13,"text":"Because of power losses, there is no ideal transformer with ------ efficiency. (Α. 100%, Β. 95%, C. 98.5%)","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":14,"text":"Which of the following is reduced by using laminated iron core in a transformer? (A. copper loss, B. mechanical loss, C. eddy current loss)","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":15,"text":"Which of the following is not used to protect us from the possibility of receiving an electric shock? (A. live wire, B. earth wire, C. circuit breaker)","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":16,"text":"The magnetic flux is ------- when the magnetic field is parallel to the surface area. (A. minimum, B. maximum, C. zero)","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":17,"text":"------- is a scalar quantity. A. Magnetic flux, B. Magnetic flux density, C. Magnetic field strength","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":18,"text":"A device consuming 2 kW of power for 3 hours would use electrical energy of -------. A. 6 kWh, B. 1.5 kWh, C. 0.666 kWh","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":19,"text":"------- is kept at zero voltage by the electricity supply company. A. Live wire, B. Earth wire, C. Neutral wire","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":20,"text":"Ac cording to Lenz''s Law, the induced current in a closed circuit: (A. Supports the change in magnetic flux, B. Opposes the change in magnetic flux, C. Is independent of the change in magnetic flux)","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":21,"text":"What is the primary function of a neutral wire in an electrical system? (A. To provide safety by grounding the circuit, B. To carry excess current during overloads, C. To complete the circuit by returning current to the source)","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":22,"text":"In Us, the electricity standards are -------. (A. 10 V, 50 Hz, B. 120 V, 60 Hz, C. 230 V, 50 Hz)","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":23,"text":"Which of the following gives the polarity of the induced emf? (A. Ohm''s law, B. Lenz''s law, C. Faraday''s law)","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":24,"text":"There is no ideal transformer with ------- efficiency. (Α. 95%, Β. 98.5%, C. 100%)","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":25,"text":"In any electric appliance the ------- wire is always connected to the metal case. (A. live, B. earth, C. neutral)","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":26,"text":"The primary danger of electricity to humans is: (A. Voltage, B. Current, C. resistance)","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":27,"text":"When the field is perpendicular to the surface area, the magnetic flux is (A. zero, B. BA, C. maximum)","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":28,"text":"In transformer, the voltage in the secondary and the voltage in the primary have -------. (A. different frequency, B. same frequency, C. minimum frequency)","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":29,"text":"Which of the following is the SI unit of magnetic flux density? (A, tesla (T), B. ampere per metre (Am¹), C. weber (Wb))","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":30,"text":"In any electrical appliance the ------- wire is always connected to the metal case. (A. live, B. neutral, C. earth)","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":31,"text":"The ------- energy is transformed into electrical energy by a battery. (A. mechanical, B. heat, C. chemical)","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":32,"text":"Most of the transformers have full load efficiency from 95% to -------. (A. 100%, B. 98%, C. 98.5%)","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":33,"text":"The SI unit of magnetic field strength is the -------. (A. ampere per metre B. weber C. tesla)","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":34,"text":"A generator converts ------- energy into electrical energy. (A chemical B. mechanical C. thermal)","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":35,"text":"The current from the output of a telephone charger is -------. A. AC, B. DC, C. both AC and DC","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":36,"text":"The phenomenon in which a current flows through a wire loop due to a change in the magnetic lines of force through the loop is called: (A. Magnetic flux, B. Electromagnetic induction, C. Faraday''s law).","source":"2026 (Set 3)"},{"number":37,"text":"Which wire carries the current from the supply to the appliance? (A. Neutral wire, B. Earth wire, C. Live wire) SECTION B","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}]},"sectionB":{"B6a":[{"number":1,"text":"M ention the appropriate wiring circuit for the following electrical appliances (i) bulb and fluorescent lamp (ii) electric iron (iii) water pump motor (iv) electric stove. A square loop of wire of side 5.0 cm is in a uniform magnetic field 0.16 T. What is the magnetic flux in the loop (i) when magnetic field is perpendicular to the surface of the loop and (ii) when magnetic field is at an angle of 30° to the surface of the loop?","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"Why are ordinary circuit breakers and fuses not effective in preventing shocks? What are the magnetic parameters that you have known? A 2 kW transformer is used to step down an AC supply of 240 V to 60 V. (i) What will the output current be if there is a 10% power loss in the transformer? (ii) How large is the output current if there is no power loss (i.e. 100% efficiency)?","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":3,"text":"How many types of transformers are there? Which type of transformer is used in a welding machine? Explain. An electric welding machine uses a current of 400 A. The machine has a transformer whose primary coil has 400 turns and draws 4 A from a 220 V power line. (i) How many turns does the secondary coil have? (ii) What is the voltage across the secondary coil?","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":4,"text":"How many types of transformers are there? Which type of transformer is used in a welding machine? Explain. A transformer has 2000 turns in primary, 100 turns in secondary and its efficiency 100%. It is used for 10 V, 40 W bulb. Calculate (i) the supply voltage and (ii) the current through the input coil.","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":5,"text":"Differentiate between the magnetic flux and magnetic flux density. A square loop of wire of side 5.0 cm is in a uniform magnetic field 0.16 T. What is the magnetic flux in the loop (i) when magnetic field is perpendicular to the surface of the loop and (ii) when magnetic field is at an angle of 30° to the surface of the loop?","source":"2025 (Set 7)"}],"B6b":[{"number":1,"text":"Draw the induced current produced by moving magnet. 120 kW of electric power is sent to a small town from power plant 10 km away. The transmission lines have a resistance of 0.40 Ω per km. Calculate the power loss if the power is transmitted at (i) 240 V and (ii) 24 000V.","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"Draw the graphical representations of the magnitude of DC and AC voltages as a function of time. The current in an AC circuit at any time t seconds is given by I = 20 sin (100π t) A. Find (i) the peak value (maximum value) of current, the period and the frequency (ii) the value of the current when t = 0 (iii) the value of the current when t = 8 ms and (iv) the time when the current reaches 10 A.","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":3,"text":"Create a diagram illustrating the symbol used to represent a transformer in an electronic circuit and label its key components. A step-down transformer is used to light a 12 V, 24 W lamp from the 220 V mains. The current through the primary is 125 mA. What is the efficiency of the transformer?","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":4,"text":"Illustrate the graphical representations of the magnitude of DC and AC voltages as a function of time. A 2 kW transformer is used to step down an AC supply of 240 V to 60 V (i) What is the turns ratio of this transformer? (ii) What will the output current be if there is a 10% power loss in the transformer? (iii) How large is the output current if there is no power loss (i.e. 100% efficiency)?","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":5,"text":"Gi ve graphical representations of the magnitude of (i) DC voltage and (ii) AC voltage as a function of time. 120 kW of electric power is sent to a small town from a power plant 10 km away. The transmission lines have a resistance of 0.40 Ω per km. Calculate the power loss if the power is transmitted at (i) 240 V and (ii) 24 000 V.","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":6,"text":"Illustrate the graphical representations of the magnitude of DC and AC voltages as a function of time. A 3 kW transformer is used to step down an AC supply of 240 V to 60 V. (i) What is the turns ratio of this transformer? (ii) What will the output current be if there is a 10% power loss in the transformer? (iii) How large is the output current if there is no power loss (i.e. 100% efficiency)?","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":7,"text":"Draw the variation of induced emf as a function of ωt. The primary coil of a step-up transformer having 440 turns is connected to a 220 V alternating voltage source. The secondary delivers a voltage of 2400 V and a current of 4 mA. (i) How many turns are there in the secondary? (ii) What is the current in the primary? (iii) What is the power output?","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":8,"text":"Draw the simple transformer. A 2 kW transformer is used to step down an AC supply of 240 V to 60 V. (i) What is the turns ratio of this transformer? (ii) What will the output current be if there is a 10% power loss in the transformer? (iii) How large is the output current if there is no power loss (100% efficiency)?","source":"2026 (Set 1)"}],"B8a":[{"number":1,"text":"Draw the variation of the induced emf as a function of ωt.","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"Draw a diagram demonstrating how a moving magnet induces current nearby coil. Include key elements and direction indicators.","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":3,"text":"Gi ve graphical representations of the magnitude of (i) DC voltage and (ii) AC voltage as a function of time.","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":4,"text":"Draw the simple transformer and its symbol.","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":5,"text":"Draw the diagrams for simple transformer and its symbol.","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":6,"text":"Draw a diagram showing the induced current produced by a moving coil carrying current.","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":7,"text":"Draw a simple diagram of how induced current is produced in a loop of wire by a moving magnet.","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":8,"text":"Draw and label the symbol of a transformer, showing its primary and secondary windings, core, and any other key components.","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":9,"text":"Illustrate a labelled diagram of a transformer symbol, showing all key components.","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":10,"text":"Consider a uniform magnetic field B passing through a plane surface of area A. Draw two separate diagrams showing the orientation of the plane for (i) maximum magnetic flux and (ii) zero magnetic flux.","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":11,"text":"Draw a diagram that illustrates the induced current produced by a moving magnet.","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}],"B9a":[{"number":1,"text":"Explain each of the following: (i) A transformer will not work on DC. (ii) The core of a transformer needs to be laminated. (iii) If a transformer increases voltage, it reduces current.","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"State the equation of Faraday’s law for a wire loop with N identical turns. Why is Faraday’s law important? What does negative sign indicate in Faraday’s law of electromagnetic induction formula?","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":3,"text":"What is electromagnetic induction? State the methods by which an induced emf can be produced in a coil.","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":4,"text":"What is the major difference between alternating current (AC) and direct current (DC)? Why is AC better than DC in long distance distribution of electrical power? Is the current from the outlet of telephone charger, AC or DC?","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":5,"text":"To improve the efficiency of a transformer, what features should betaken into consideration?","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":6,"text":"Why is Faraday''s law important? Differentiate between the magnetic flux and magnetic flux density. Is the current from the outlet of telephone charger, AC or DC?","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":7,"text":"Explain (i) A transformer will not work on DC, (ii) The core of a transformer needs to be laminated.","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":8,"text":"Describe Faraday''s law of electromagnetic induction and its importance in the generation of electricity.","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":9,"text":"Write down the equation of Faraday''s law for a wire loop with N identical turns. What does negative sign indicate in Faraday''s law of electromagnetic induction formula? Does the induced emf in a circuit depend on the resistance of the circuit?","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":10,"text":"What are the colours of the live, neutral and earth wires in a wiring system? Explain the major difference between AC and DC current.","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":11,"text":"How many types of transformers are there? Which type of transformer is used in a welding machine? Explain your answer.","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":12,"text":"Explain each of the following: (i) A transformer will not work on DC. (ii) The core of a transformer needs to be laminated. (iii) If a transformer increases voltage, it reduces current.","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}],"B9b":[{"number":1,"text":"A step-down transformer is used to light a 12 V, 24 W lamp from the 240 V mains. The current through the primary is 125 mA. What is the efficiency of the transformer?","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"One coil of a transformer has 50 turns and the other coil has 1000 turns. The alternating voltage of 220 V is applied to the primary. Find the alternating voltage from the secondary when it is used as (i) a step-up transformer and (ii) a step-down transformer.","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":3,"text":"One coil of a transformer has 50 turns and the other coil has 1000 turns. The alternating voltage of 220 V is applied to the primary. Find the alternating voltage from the secondary when it is used as (i) a step-up transformer and (ii) a step-down transformer.","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":4,"text":"An electric welding machine uses a current of 400 A. The machine has a transformer whose primary coil has 400 turns and draws 4 A from a 220 V power line. (i) How many turns does the secondary coil have? (ii) What is the voltage across the secondary coil?","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":5,"text":"A circular coil of radius 8 cm and 20 turns is rotated about its vertical diameter with an angular speed of 150 rad s⁻¹ in a uniform horizontal -2 magnetic field of 3 × 10 T. Obtain the maximum emf induced in the coil. If the coil forms a closed loop of resistance 10 Ω, calculate the maximum value of current in the coil.","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":6,"text":"A circular coil of radius 8 cm and 20 turns is rotated about its vertical diameter with an angular speed of 150 rad s⁻¹ in a uniform horizontal magnetic field of 3 × 10-2 T. Obtain the maximum emf induced in the coil. If the coil forms a closed loop of resistance 10 Ω, calculate the maximum value of current in the coil.","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":7,"text":"The primary coil of a step-up transformer having 220 turns is connected to a 110 V alternating voltage source. The secondary delivers a voltage of 12 000 V and a current of 40 mA. (i) How many turns are there in the secondary? (ii) What is the current in the primary?","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":8,"text":"An electric welding machine uses a current of 400 A. The machine has a transformer whose primary coil has 400 turns and draws 4 A from a 220 V power line. (i) How many turns does the secondary coil have? (ii) What is the voltage across the secondary coil?","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":9,"text":"An electric welding machine uses a current of 400 A. The machine has a transformer whose primary coil has 400 turns and draws 4 A from a 220 V power line. (i) How many turns does the secondary coil have? (ii) What is the voltage across the secondary coil?","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":10,"text":"The primary coil of a step-up transformer having 220 turns is connected to a 110 V alternating voltage source. The secondary delivers a voltage of 12 000 V and a current of 40 mA. (i) How many turns are there in the secondary? (ii) What is the current in the primary?","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":11,"text":"The current in an AC circuit at any time t seconds is given by I = 20 sin (100π t) A. Find (i) the peak value (maximum value) of current, the period and the frequency (ii) the value of the current when t = 0 (iii) the value of the current when t = 8 ms (iv) the time when the current reaches 10 A.","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}]}}'::jsonb,0,true),
(12,'old_questions','Chapter 12','12','{"chapter":12,"sectionA":{"A1":[{"number":1,"text":"Zener diode is a heavily doped semiconductor p-n junction diode.","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"The commonly used invisible light for LED is white light.","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":3,"text":"One advantage of LEDs is their common use with low voltage and high current.","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":4,"text":"LCD s consume much more power than LEDs and gas-plasma displays.","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":5,"text":"Som e active electrical components are transistors, LEDs and LDR.","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":6,"text":"In The bright light, resistance of light depend resistor (LDR) is low.","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":7,"text":"A normal diode allows current to flow in both directions.","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":8,"text":"The current flows through Zener diode only in forward-bias mode.","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":9,"text":"Phot odiodes work in forward biased mode.","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":10,"text":"LE Ds do not directly produce white light.","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":11,"text":"LE Ds do not directly produce white light.","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":12,"text":"The resistance of the PTC (Positive Temperature Coefficient) thermistor decreases as temperature increases.","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":13,"text":"XN OR gate produces a ''0'' when both inputs are different.","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":14,"text":"In a digital system, information is represented using binary numbers, 0 and 1.","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":15,"text":"LE Ds do not directly produce white light.","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":16,"text":"The current flows through zener diode only in forward-bias mode.","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":17,"text":"A digital circuit uses 0s and 1s to represent data.","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":18,"text":"Active electrical components require a power source to operate.","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":19,"text":"Liquid crystals do not emit light directly.","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":20,"text":"Light emitting diode can directly produce white light and invisible light.","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":21,"text":"LD R is also called light sensitive variable capacitor.","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":22,"text":"A phot odiode converts light into electrical current.","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":23,"text":"NA ND gate produces a ‘0’ when both inputs are ‘1’.","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":24,"text":"Frequency modulation (FM) radio ranges up to 1200 bits per second.","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}],"A2":[{"number":1,"text":"------- break down occurs at junction which being heavily doped have narrow depleting layer.","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"A liquid crystal display (LCD) is ------- display.","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":3,"text":"A ------- is a semiconductor device that converts light into electrical current.","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":4,"text":"The basic operations in Boolean algebra are -------, OR, and NOT.","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":5,"text":"A -------, one of the most widely used in optoelectronics, is a semiconductor light source that emits light when current flows through it.","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":6,"text":"An ------- gate is a digital logic gate that outputs a high (1) signal only when all its inputs are high (1).","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":7,"text":"The photodiode is a semiconductor device that converts ------ into electrical current.","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":8,"text":"------ is the process of recovering audio signal from modulated wave.","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":9,"text":"The voltage drop across the zener diode always remains ------- irrespective of the applied voltage.","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":10,"text":"A thermistor is a temperature sensor that exhibits a large change in ------- proportional to a change in