bra are, ------- OR, and NOT.","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":28,"text":"The process of changing some characteristics of a carrier wave in accordance with the intensity of the signal is known as -------.","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":29,"text":"The basic unit of data in a digital system is referred to as a -------.","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":30,"text":"In communication systems, the technique of overlaying a message signal onto a carrier wave is known as -------.","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":31,"text":"The current is generated when photons are absorbed in the -------.","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":32,"text":"The OR gate with inverted output is called a ------- gate.","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":33,"text":"A ------- is a light controlled variable resistor.","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":34,"text":"The process of converting energy from one form to another is called -------.","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":35,"text":"The ------- of the photocurrent depends on the intensity of incident light.","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":36,"text":"The AND gate with inverted output is called a ------- gate.","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":37,"text":"A modern light source that requires ------- voltages is the light emitting diode (LED).","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":38,"text":"A thermistor can convert changes in ------- into changes in electric current.","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":39,"text":"A transducer contains ------- element and transduction element.","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":40,"text":"The resistance of ------- decreases as the light level increases.","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":41,"text":"The basic operations in Boolean algebra are AND, OR, and -------.","source":"2026 (Set 3)"},{"number":42,"text":"OL ED stands for ------- Light-Emitting Diode.","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}],"A3":[{"number":1,"text":"------- is used to control the brightness of street lamps. (A. LED, B. LDR, C. Thermistor)","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"A phot odiode is a ------- device that converts lights into electrical current. (A. insulator, B. conductor, C. semiconductor)","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":3,"text":"Which electrical component is used to control the brightness of street lamps? (A. LED, B. LDR, C. thermistor)","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":4,"text":"------- are massless and move at the speed of light in vacuum. (A. Photons, B. Neutrons, C. Electrons)","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":5,"text":"What is the main function of NOT gate in digital logic? (A. Performs the digital AND operation, B. Inverts the input signal, C. Executes addition)","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":6,"text":"What is the output of XNOR gate if both inputs are the same? (A. 0, B. 2, C. 1)","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":7,"text":"Ti me dilation becomes apparent especially as the speed of the system approaches that of -------. (A. light, B. sound, C. none of A and B)","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":8,"text":"------- is used to control the brightness of the night lamp. (A. LED, B. LDR, C. LCD)","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":9,"text":"A phot odiode converts ------- into electrical current. (A. light, B. resistance, C. temperature)","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":10,"text":"The photodiode can be used as a photodetector to detect the ------- signals. (A. optical, B. heat, C. chemical)","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":11,"text":"In Bright light, LDR becomes a ------- of electric current. (A. good conductor, B. poor conductor, C. good insulator)","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":12,"text":"There are ------- types of reverse breakdown regions in a zener diode. (A. one, B. two, C. three)","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":13,"text":"What semiconductor device that converts light into electrical current? (A. LED, B. light dependent resistor, C. photodiode)","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":14,"text":"A ------- is a device that transforms a signal from one energy form to another energy form. (A. transducer, B. capacitor, C. resistor)","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":15,"text":"The ------- the wavelength of the matter wave, the faster the particle moves. (A. larger, B. smaller, C. lower)","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":16,"text":"What are the fundamental building blocks of digital ICs? (A. logic gates, B. resistors, C. transistors)","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":17,"text":"Which gate produces a high output when one, and only one, of its inputs is high? (A. XOR, B. XNOR, C. NOR)","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":18,"text":"As light level increases, the LDR resistance -------. (A. is empty, B. increases, C. decreases)","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":19,"text":"A ------- is a semiconductor light source that emits light when current flows through it. (A. LED, B. photodiode, C. zener diode)","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":20,"text":"In ------- modulation, the amplitude of carrier wave remains constant with modulation. (A. phase, B. amplitude, C. frequency)","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":21,"text":"------- gate produces a ''1'' when both inputs match. (A. NOR, B. XOR, C. XNOR)","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":22,"text":"The OR gate with inverted output is called a ------- gate. (A. XOR, B. XNOR, C. NOR)","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":23,"text":"A phot odiode converts ------- into electrical current. (A. light, B. sound, C. heat)","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":24,"text":"What is the primary application of a Zener diode? (A. As a voltage regulator, B. As a rectifier, C. As an amplifier)","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":25,"text":"What should be the biasing of the LED? (A. forward bias, B. reverse bias, C. no biasing required)","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":26,"text":"Uranium is used for the generation of -------. (A. electricity, B. iron and steel, C. cement)","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":27,"text":"Radio and television are examples of ------- mode of communication. (A. broadcast, B. point to point, C. telephony)","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":28,"text":"What happens to the resistance of an LDR as the light intensity increases? (A. The resistance increases, B. The resistance decreases, C. The resistance remains the same)","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":29,"text":"In the Negative Temperature Coefficient (NTC) thermistor, the resistance ------- as the temperature increases. (A. increases, B. zero, C. decreases)","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":30,"text":"A ------- is a device for converting a non-electrical input into an electrical signal (or) vice versa. (A. transducer, B. transmitter, C. receiver) $","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":31,"text":"By using basic rules of Boolean algebra, the output of (A∙0) and (A∙ A) is equal to -------. (A. 0 (zero), B. 1 (one), C. A)","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":32,"text":"The fire alarm system consists of two logic gates, OR gate and ------- gate. (A. NOR, B. NAND, C. AND)","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":33,"text":"LD R consists of a disc of ------- material on its surface with two electrodes. (A) insulator (B) semiconductor (C) conductor","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":34,"text":"In parallel connection of batteries, the terminals of the ------- should be connected together. A. opposite polarity, B. mixed polarity, C. same polarity","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":35,"text":"LE Ds do not directly produce ------- light. (A. red, B. blue, C. white)","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":36,"text":"Which of the following is NOT listed as one of the six main pieces that comprise a radio receiver? (A. Antenna, B. Diode detector, C. Frequency modulator) SECTION B","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}]},"sectionB":{"B5b":[{"number":1,"text":"Where are LEDs used? Describe some applications of LEDs. What effect does an increase of light intensity on LDR have on its resistance? What is a disadvantage of LCD displays? Illustrate the block diagram of general electronic communication system.","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"What is meant by “AM and FM”? What are the differences between FM and AM? Draw the circuit symbol of LED and its forward biased characteristic curves.","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":3,"text":"What effect does an increase in light intensity have on the resistance of a light dependent resistor (LDR)? Is LDR also called light sensitive variable resistor? Is an LDR composed of semiconductor materials? Provide a circuit symbol illustrating the configuration of LDR.","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":4,"text":"Why is LDR also called light sensitive variable resistors? How does its resistance change (i) in the dark light and (ii) in the bright light? What is thermistor? What is the main difference between the negative temperature coefficient (NTC) and the positive temperature coefficient (PTC) thermistors? Draw their characteristic curves.","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":5,"text":"Describe the advantages of LED. Draw the diagram of a simple LED indicator circuit.","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":6,"text":"What are the differences between frequency modulation (FM) and amplitude modulation (AM)? Explain with illustrative diagrams.","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":7,"text":"Cons truct the truth table for two inputs different gates (OR, NOR, NAND, XOR and XNOR). Draw the circuit symbol and simple circuit diagram of photodiode.","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":8,"text":"What is a zener diode? How do you understand the avalanche breakdown and zener breakdown? What is the main difference between a zener diode and a normal diode? Draw the characteristic curve of the zener diode.","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":9,"text":"What is meant by \"AM and FM\"? What are the differences between FM and AM? Draw the diagram for simple LED indicator circuit. What are liquid crystals? Why do LCDs consume less power than LEDs","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":10,"text":"And gas-plasma displays? Where can LCDs be commonly found? Draw the simple circuit diagram of a photodiode. Give the formula for expressing De Morgan''s second theorem for two","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":11,"text":"Variables and construct its truth table. Describe the logic symbol, Boolean equation and truth table of XNOR gate. Draw the diagram of a simple LED indicator circuit.","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":12,"text":"What is photodiode? Give the function and two applications of photodiode. Plot a simple circuit diagram of a photodiode.","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":13,"text":"Describe two advantages and two disadvantages of LED. List two applications of LED. Draw circuit symbol for LED.","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":14,"text":"What is the disadvantage of Liquid Crystal Display (LCD)? Why does an LCD need a backlight, and what is the role of a polarizer in an LCD? Draw the symbol for an OR gate and label its inputs and output properly.","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":15,"text":"What is zener diode? What is the main difference between zener diode and normal diode? Where are photodiode used? Does photodiode work in reverse biased mode? Draw a circuit diagram of fire alarm system consists of smoke detector, heat detector and two logic gates.","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":16,"text":"Is LDR called light sensitive variable resistor? Why? Is LDR composed of semiconductor materials? How does its resistance change (i) in the dark light and (ii) in the bright light? Draw the simple circuit diagram of photodiode.","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":17,"text":"Explain the difference between active and passive electronic components, providing examples of each type. Draw the symbol for an AND gate and label its inputs and output properly. Describe the disadvantages of LED.","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":18,"text":"Give the main uses for Zener diode and LED. Draw the circuit diagram of fire alarm system. What are the basic components of an electronic communication system?","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":19,"text":"How many basic modes of communication are there? Explain with examples. Draw the block diagram for analog communication system. What is a photodiode? Where are they used? Explain the function of a","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":20,"text":"Photodiode. Why does a photodiode be used as a photodetector? Draw the circuit symbols of light dependent resistor (LDR) and thermistor.","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":21,"text":"When the zener diode is in forward-bias mode, what is its turn-on voltage? Explain zener effect. What are two types of reverse breakdown regions in a zener diode? Plot the I-V characteristics of a zener diode showing two breakdown regions.","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":22,"text":"Compare the point-to-point and broadcast modes of communication. Provide one practical example for each mode. State one advantage of digital communication. Draw and label the characteristic curve of a thermistor.","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}],"B7a":[{"number":1,"text":"Li st the main components of a simple radio receiver.","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":2,"text":"State De Morgan’s second theorem. Give the formula for expressing De Morgan’s second theorem for two variables and construct its truth table. Construct the truth table to prove the following Boolean algebra rule. (A + B) (A + C)= A + Bc","source":"2026 (Set 1)"}],"B8b":[{"number":1,"text":"Si mplify the following expressions if possible. $ $ (i) A + AB + ABC, (ii) (A + B) C + ABC","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":2,"text":"An amber-coloured LED with a forward voltage drop of 4 V is to be connected to a 9 V stabilized DC power supply. Calculate the value of the series resistor required to limit the forward current to less than 10 mA. Also calculate the current flowing through the diode if a 100 Ω of current limitting resistor is used.","source":"2025 (Set 12)"}],"B9a":[{"number":1,"text":"Draw the logic circuit represented by each of the following expressions: (i) A + B + C (ii) ABC (iv) AB + CD","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":2,"text":"Draw the circuit diagram illustrating the fire alarm system.","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":3,"text":"Draw the circuit symbol of LED and its characteristic curves.","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":4,"text":"Draw the characteristics of a zener diode and its circuit symbol.","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":5,"text":"Draw the logic circuit represented by each of the following expressions: (i) ABC, (ii) AB + C, (iii) AB + CD.","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":6,"text":"Draw the circuit diagram of fire alarm system.","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":7,"text":"Draw the logic circuit represented by each of the following expressions: (i) ABC (ii) AB + C (iii) AB + CD","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":8,"text":"Draw the block diagram of a simple radio receiver.","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":9,"text":"Draw the logic circuit represented by each of the following expressions: (i) A̅ + B̅, (ii) A + BC, (iii) AB + CD. Provide a labelled diagram of a NOR gate, an AND gate, and a NOT gate.","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":10,"text":"(inverter).","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":11,"text":"Draw the block diagram of general electronic communication system.","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":12,"text":"Draw the circuit diagram illustrating the street lighting system.","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":13,"text":"Provide a labelled diagram of an OR gate, a NAND gate, and a NOT gate.","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":14,"text":"Draw the circuit diagram illustrating the street lighting system.","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":15,"text":"Draw the circuit diagram of street lighting system.","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":16,"text":"Draw the block diagram for digital communication system.","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":17,"text":"Draw the logic circuit represented by each of the following expressions: $ $ (i) A + B, (ii) A + BC, (iii) AB + CD","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":18,"text":"Draw and label the block diagram of a simple radio receiver.","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}],"B9b":[{"number":1,"text":"Gi ve a short note on communication system. Write short notes on the components of a simple radio receiver.","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"What is thermistor? How many types of thermistors are there? Write down the main difference between them?","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":3,"text":"Li st four essential components required for a basic radio receiver.","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":4,"text":"Cons truct the truth tables to prove the following Boolean Algebra rules. $ (i) A + Ab = A + B, (ii) A + Ab = A.","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":5,"text":"Gi ve the formula for expressing De Morgan’s first theorem for two variables and construct its truth table.","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":6,"text":"What are advantages and disadvantages of light emitting diode (LED)?","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":7,"text":"What are the differences between FM and AM?","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":8,"text":"What is a transducer? Describe the logic symbol, Boolean equation and truth table of XOR gate. What is thermistor? How many types of thermistors are there? Name them.","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":9,"text":"Also write down the main difference between them.","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":10,"text":"What is meant by \"AM and FM\"? Give one advantage of FM over AM.","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":11,"text":"Gi ve the main uses for (i) the Zener diode and (ii) LED. What is the main difference between a normal diode and a zener diode?","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":12,"text":"Describe two advantages and two disadvantages of LED.","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":13,"text":"What is the main difference between a Zener diode and a normal diode? Describe two types of reverse breakdown regions in a Zener diode. Describe one common application of LEDs. Additionally, explain why","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":14,"text":"LEDs are preferred over traditional light sources in that application? Name the components of a simple radio receiver and briefly describe any","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":15,"text":"Two of them. What is meant by \"AM and FM\"? What are the differences between FM","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":16,"text":"And AM?","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":17,"text":"Li st two benefits and two drawbacks of using LED lights. Give the formula for expressing De Morgan''s second theorem for two","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":18,"text":"Variables and construct its truth table.","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":19,"text":"How are the electron-hole pairs produced in the photodiode? Where are photodiodes used? Explain the difference between active and passive electrical components","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":20,"text":"With examples. Give a brief account on frequency modulation (FM) and amplitude","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":21,"text":"Modulation (AM). Explain the function of a photodiode. How does light intensity affect the","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":22,"text":"Photocurrent?","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}]}}'::jsonb,0,true),
(12,'old_questions','Chapter 13','13','{"chapter":13,"sectionA":{"A1":[{"number":1,"text":"Beta particle is helium nucleus.","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"An inertial frame is a frame of reference that has no acceleration.","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":3,"text":"The term “radioactivity” is used to describe the rate at which a radioactive sample undergoes decay.","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":4,"text":"Gamma rays can be deflected by electric and magnetic fields.","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":5,"text":"A nuclear reaction is a process in which a beta radiation penetrates into a nucleus and changes its configuration.","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":6,"text":"Activity of a radioactive sample decreases with time.","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":7,"text":"Positron is also called the antiparticle of proton.","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":8,"text":"! In β decay, the atomic number of daughter nucleus increases by one.","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":9,"text":"Al l elements in nature are not radioactive.","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":10,"text":"Gamma rays have no charge.","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":11,"text":"Positron is also called the antiparticle of proton.","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":12,"text":"An inertial frame is a frame of reference that has no acceleration.","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":13,"text":"Relativistic effect usually becomes negligible when speed of the system becomes comparable to the speed of light.","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":14,"text":"Alpha particles consist of two protons and two neutrons, making them identical to a helium nucleus.","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":15,"text":"The wave nature of electrons is used instead of light in electron microscope.","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":16,"text":"! In β decay, the atomic number of daughter nucleus increases by one.","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":17,"text":"Beta particles are high-energy electrons or positrons emitte