mal or a plant dies carbon cycle stops and the carbon⁻¹⁴ in the remain gradually ------- by radioactive decay. (A. decreases, B. increases, C. constant)","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":3,"text":"What is emitted during beta decay? (A. Alpha particle, B. Neutrino, C. Beta particle)","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":4,"text":"What defines nuclear fission? (A. Fusion of atomic nuclei, B. Splitting of atomic nuclei into smaller parts, C. Combining of photons and neutrons)","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":5,"text":"The statement \"radium has a half-life of 1620 years\" means that if we start with N0 atoms of radium, ------- will remain after 1620 years. (A. N /2 atoms, B. N /4 atoms, C. N /8 atoms) 0 0 0","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":6,"text":"------- rays cannot be deflected by electric and magnetic fields. (A. Gamma, B. Beta, C. Alpha) A few heavy elements with atomic number greater than ------- are","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":7,"text":"Radioactive or unstable. (A. 92, B. 83, C. 100)","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":8,"text":"Radio and television are examples of ------- mode of communication. (A. broadcast, B. point to point, C. telephony) In alpha decay, an atomic nucleus emits an alpha particle with mass number","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":9,"text":"------- and atomic number reduces by two. (A. reduces by two, B. reduces by four, C. increases by four)","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":10,"text":"------- are massless and move at the speed of light in vacuum. (A. Neutrons, B. Protons, C. Photons)","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":11,"text":"Which rays cannot be deflected by electric and magnetic fields? (A. alpha ryas, B. beta rays, C. gamma rays)","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":12,"text":"------- cannot be deflected by electric and magnetic fields. (A. Alpha rays, B. Beta rays, C. Gamma rays)","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":13,"text":"Which of the following is not an inertial frame of reference? (A. rotation of earth about its own axis, B. a bus moving at a constant speed in a straight road, C. a person standing on a stationary train)","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":14,"text":"Gamma rays are the ------- of the three rays. (A. most penetrating, B. most ionizing, C. least ionizing)","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":15,"text":"What is the rate of decay of a radioactive sample called? A. activity, B. half-life, C. ionization","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":16,"text":"What nature of electrons is used in electron microscope? A. wave nature, B. particle nature, C. dual nature","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":17,"text":"What is the penetrating power of alpha particles compared to other radiation types? (A. High, B. Moderate, C. Low)","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":18,"text":"What is a tracer commonly composed of? (A. A small number of radioactive isotopes, B. A mixture of stable and unstable isotopes, C. A highly reactive chemical compound)","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":19,"text":"Which of the following defines the structure of space-time? (A. Special relativity theory, B. Newton laws of motion, C. General relativity theory)","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":20,"text":"------- are massless and move at the speed of light in vacuum. (A. Neutrons, B. Protons, C. Photons) When an animal or a plant dies carbon cycle stops and the carbon⁻¹⁴ in the","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":21,"text":"Remain gradually ------- by radioactive decay. (A. decreases, B. increases, C. constant)","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":22,"text":"The emission of radiation from an unstable nucleus is called: (A. Nuclear fission, B. Radioactivity, C. Nuclear fusion)","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":23,"text":"Which of the following particles is responsible for initiating nuclear fission reactions? (A. Neutrons, B. Protons, C. Electrons)","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":24,"text":"By measuring the activity of -------, the age of the remains of plants and animals can be estimated. (A. carbon 12, B. carbon 13, C. carbon 14)","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":25,"text":"The laws of physics are the ------- in all inertial frames of reference. (A. constant, B. different, C. same)","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":26,"text":"Complete the following decay process. Which decay process is it? ¹⁴₆C → ¹⁴₇N + ⁰₋₁e + ν̅ₑ. (A. ⁰₋₁e, β⁻ decay; B. ⁰₊₁e, β⁺ decay; C. γ, gamma decay.)","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":27,"text":"------- rays cannot be deflected by electric and magnetic fields. (A. Alpha, B. Beta, C. Gamma)","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":28,"text":"------- has no charge and negligibly small rest mass. (A. Positron, B. Neutron, C. Neutrino)","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":29,"text":"------- are massless and move at the speed of light in vacuum. (A. Neutrons, B. Photons, C. Electrons)","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":30,"text":"Tre atment with radiation is known as -------. (A. radioactivity, B. radiotherapy, C. radiography)","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":31,"text":"Activity of a radioactive sample ------- with time. (A. decreases, B. increases, C. does not change)","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":32,"text":"Ti me dilation becomes significant when the speed of the system -------. A. is close to the speed of light, B. is zero, C. is very low)","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":33,"text":"Which of the following is a dangerous radioactive fission product? (A. Carbon, B. Strontium, C. Helium)","source":"2026 (Set 3)"},{"number":34,"text":"Which radiation has no charge and is most penetrating? (A. Alpha ray, B. Beta ray, C. Gamma ray) SECTION B","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}]},"sectionB":{"B5b":[{"number":1,"text":"Rays. Draw a diagram to show the nuclear fission.","source":"2026 (Set 1)"}],"B7a":[{"number":1,"text":"What device is a nuclear reactor? Give a brief description of the essential component of nuclear reactor. Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of (i) a 0.65 kg basketball thrown at a speed of 10 ms⁻¹, (ii) a nonrelativistic electron with a kinetic energy of 1 eV.","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"What are radioisotopes? Give some examples. Give two medical applications of radioisotopes. A radioisotope has a half-life of 20 min. If there is initially 102.4 g of this isotope, how much time elapses for 12.8 g to be left?","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":3,"text":"Describe a comparison between Einstein’s Special and General Relativity theories, focusing two key points. Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of a 0.65 kg basketball thrown at a speed of 20 ms⁻¹. (h = 6.625 × 10!)$ Js)","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":4,"text":"Starting from the relation between the momentum p of a particle and its wavelength λ, obtain the de Broglie wavelength in terms of its kinetic energy. Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of a nonrelativistic electron with a kinetic energy of 1 eV. (h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, mₑ = 9.1 × 10⁻³¹ kg, 1 eV = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ J)","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":5,"text":"Describe the properties of gamma rays. A radioisotope has a half-life of 20 min. If there is initially 102.4 g of this isotope, how much time elapses for 12.8 g to be left?","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":6,"text":"What is a tracer? State some uses of radioactive tracers. Why is it important to use radioactive tracers with short half-lives in medical diagnosis? Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of (i) a 0.65 kg basketball thrown at a -1 speed of 10 ms , (ii) a nonrelativistic electron with a kinetic energy of 1 eV.","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":7,"text":"Compare the ionizing and penetrating powers of alpha, beta and gamma rays. Suppose that initially there was 100 mg of iodine⁻¹³¹ and its half-life is 8 days. How much would it be left after 24 days?","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":8,"text":"Define (i) half-life and (ii) nuclear reaction. If a fossil has 10% carbon⁻¹⁴ compared to a living sample, find the age of the fossil. (half-life of carbon⁻¹⁴ = 5730 years)","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":9,"text":"How can you explain the two main postulates of Einstein special theory of relativity? Why is it important to use radioactive tracers with short half- lives in medical diagnosis? Suppose there was 8 g of radon at t = 0 and its half-life is 3.8 days. How much would be left after (i) 7.6 days (ii) 11.4 days?","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":10,"text":"What does the statement \"radium has a half-life of 1620 years\" mean? Compare the penetrating power of alpha, beta, and gamma rays. A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (m = 1840 m ) pe","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":11,"text":"Explain Bohr''s second postulate of hydrogen atom using de Broglie hypothesis. Suppose that initially there was 100 mg of iodine⁻¹³¹ and its half-life is 8 days. How much would it be left after 24 days?","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":12,"text":"Li st the key differences between Einstein''s theories of special relativity and general relativity. One stary night, an earth-bound observer looking up the stars sees an extra- terrestrial spaceship flash across the sky. The ship is 50 m long and is traveling at 90 percent of the speed of light. What would the ship''s length be when measured from earth-bound frame of reference?","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":13,"text":"Explain the terms activity and half-life of a radioactive substance. Suppose that initially there was 100 mg of iodine⁻¹³¹ and its half-life is 8 days. How much would it be left after 24 days?","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":14,"text":"Suppose there was 8 g of radon at t = 0 and its half-life is 3.8 days. How much would be left after 7.6 days?","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":15,"text":"What is radioactivity? Who discovered radioactivity? Name some radioactive elements. Suppose that initially there was 100 mg of iodine⁻¹³¹ and its half-life is 8 days. How much would it be left after 24 days?","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":16,"text":"What do you understand half-life? Compare the ionizing and penetrating powers of alpha, beta and gamma rays. A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their -19 de Broglie wavelengths. (m = 1840 m ) (q = 1.6 × 10 C) pe","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":17,"text":"Describe the principle of the special theory of relativity. Explain its significance in modern physics and provide one example of how it applies to real-world scenarios. One starry night, an earth-bound observer looking up the stars sees an extra-terrestrial spaceship flash across the sky. The ship is 55 m long and travelling at 95% of the speed of light. What would the ship''s length be when measured from an earth-bound frame of reference?","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":18,"text":"Compare the ionizing and penetrating powers of alpha, beta and gamma rays. Can radioactive elements be produced artificially? Suppose that initially there was 100 mg of iodine⁻¹³¹ and its half-life is 8 days. How much would it be left after 24 days?","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":19,"text":"What is radioactivity? Name some radioactive elements. Describe the exponential law of radioactive decay. Initially at t = 0 there was 1 g of radon and at t = 3.8 days there was 0.5 g of radon. (i) What is the half-life of radon? (ii) How much of the element would be left after 7.6 days and 11.4 days?","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":20,"text":"What device is a nuclear reactor? Give a brief description of the essential component of a nuclear reactor. A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (m = 1840 m ) pe","source":"2025 (Set 12)"},{"number":21,"text":"Compare the ionizing and penetrating powers of alpha, beta, and gamma rays. Suppose there was 2 g of radon at t = 0 and its half-life is 3.8 days. How much would be left after 15.2 days?","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":22,"text":"What device is a nuclear reactor? Name the essential components of a nuclear reactor. If a fossil has 10% carbon⁻¹⁴ compared to a living sample, find the age of the fossil. (half-life of carbon⁻¹⁴ = 5730 years)","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}],"B8b":[{"number":1,"text":"Suppose there was 2 g of radon at t = 0 and its half-life is 3.8 days. How much would be left after 15.2 days.","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"In old days radios contained vacuum tubes that generated and speeded up electrons. A tube operates at 100 V. Find the speed of an electron and its de Broglie wavelength. (mₑ = 9.1 × 10⁻³¹ kg, qₑ = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C, h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s)","source":"2024 (Set 1)"},{"number":3,"text":"Suppose there was 8 g of radon at t = 0 and its half-life is 3.8 days. How much would be left after 7.6 days.","source":"2024 (Set 2)"},{"number":4,"text":"Calculate the relativistic factor γ, for (i) a particle traveling at 99.7 % of the speed of light and (ii) an object travelling 2 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹. (c = 3 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹)","source":"2024 (Set 3)"},{"number":5,"text":"The distance between two points, called the proper length L₀, is 1 km. An observer in motion with respect to the frame of reference of the two points measures 0.8 km, which is L. What is the relative speed of the frame of reference with respect to the observer?","source":"2024 (Set 4)"},{"number":6,"text":"If a fossil has 10% carbon⁻¹⁴ compared to a living sample, find the age of fossil. (half-life of carbobn⁻¹⁴ = 5730 years)","source":"2024 (Set 5)"},{"number":7,"text":"A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (m = 1840 m ) pe","source":"2024 (Set 6)"},{"number":8,"text":"A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de -34 -19 Broglie wavelengths. (m = 1840 m , h = 6.63 × 10 Js, q = 1.6 × 10 C) pe","source":"2025 (Set 1)"},{"number":9,"text":"Co -60 (half-life = 5.25 years) is often used as a radiation source in medicine. How long after a new sample is delivered, will the activity have decreased to # of its original value? +","source":"2025 (Set 2)"},{"number":10,"text":"Co -60 (half-life = 5.25 years) is often used as a radiation source in medicine. How long after a new sample is delivered, will the activity have decreased to # of its original value? +","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":11,"text":"Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of (i) a 0.65 kg basketball thrown at a -1 6 -1 speed of 10 ms , (ii) an electron moving with a speed of 0.59 × 10 ms . -34 -31 Evaluate your answer. (h = 6.62 × 10 Js, m = 9.1 × 10 g) e","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":12,"text":"A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. -19 -34 (q = 1.6 × 10 C, m = 1840 m , h = 6.62 × 10 Js) e pe","source":"2025 (Set 5)"},{"number":13,"text":"Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of a 0.70 kg basketball thrown at a -1 -34 speed of 10 ms . (h = 6.63 × 10 Js)","source":"2025 (Set 6)"},{"number":14,"text":"A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (m =1840 m , q = q = q =1.6 × 10-19 C) pe e p","source":"2025 (Set 7)"},{"number":15,"text":"How fast must a vehicle travel for 1 s of time measured on a passenger''s watch in the vehicle to differ by 1% for an observer measuring it from the ground outside?","source":"2025 (Set 8)"},{"number":16,"text":"Fi nd the de Broglie wavelength of an electron in the ground state of hydrogen atom. Radius of the first orbit of hydrogen atom is 0.53 Å. -34 -31 (h = 6.625 × 10 Js, m = 9.1 × 10 kg) e","source":"2025 (Set 9)"},{"number":17,"text":"Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of (i) a 0.70 kg basketball thrown at a speed of 10 ms⁻¹, (ii) a nonrelativistic electron with a kinetic energy of 1 -34 -31 eV. (h = 6.63x10 Js, mass of electron = 9.1 × 10 kg)","source":"2025 (Set 10)"},{"number":18,"text":"A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their -19 de Broglie wavelengths. (mp = 1840 me, q = 1.6 × 10 C )","source":"2025 (Set 11)"},{"number":19,"text":"The distance between two points, called the proper length L₀, is 1 km. An observer in motion with respect to the frame of reference of the two points measures 0.6 km, which is L. What is the relative speed of the frame of reference with respect to the observer?","source":"2026 (Set 1)"},{"number":20,"text":"Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of (i) a 0.65 kg basketball thrown at a speed of 10 ms⁻¹ and (ii) a nonrelativistic electron moving with a speed of 6 -1 -31 0.59 × 10 ms . Evaluate your answer. (me = 9.1 × 10 kg, h = 6.63 × -34 10 Js) In old days radios contained vacuum tubes that generated and speeded up","source":"2026 (Set 2)"},{"number":21,"text":"Electrons. A tube operates at 100 V. Find the speed of an electron and -31 de Broglie wavelength. (mass of an electron = 9.1 × 10 kg)","source":"2026 (Set 3)"}],"B9a":[{"number":1,"text":"Draw a graph illustrating the half-life of radium which has a half-life of 1620 years.","source":"2024 (SQ)"},{"number":2,"text":"Draw the diagrams to show the nuclear fission and fission chain reaction. Draw a graph to illustrate the half-life of radon. Radon has a half-life of","source":"2024 (Set 7)"},{"number":3,"text":"3.8 days. The half-life of radon is 3.8 days. Provide the graphical illustration of half-","source":"2025 (Set 3)"},{"number":4,"text":"Life of radioactive decay of 2 g of radon.","source":"2025 (Set 4)"},{"number":5,"text":"Draw a diagram to show the nuclear fission.","source":"2025 (Set 10)"}],"B9b":[{"number":1,"text":"What is carbon dating? How does the proportion of the carbon⁻¹⁴ in the remains of dead plants and animals gives clues about their age? Can the age of living plants and animals be determined by carbon dating method?","source":"2025 (Set 12)"}]}}'::jsonb,0,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The Ferris wheel starts from <strong>rest</strong> and reaches an angular velocity of 1.5 rad s<sup>-1</sup> over a 10 s period under the constant angular acceleration. </p><p>(i)&emsp;Find the angular acceleration of the Ferris wheel. </p><p>(ii)&emsp;How many <strong>revolutions</strong> does it make during 10 s?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({\\omega }_{0}\\) = 0 (from rest), \\(\\omega \\) = 1.5 rad s<sup>-1</sup>, t = 10 s</p><p>(i) \\(\\alpha \\) = ? (ii) \\(\\theta \\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\alpha \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\omega \\,-\\,{\\omega }_{0}}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1.5\\,-\\,0}{10}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\alpha \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.15 rad s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\omega \\)<sub>0</sub> t + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\alpha \\) t<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0 + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\times 0.15\\,\\times {10}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>7.5 rad</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>1 rev = 2\\(\\pi \\) rad</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>7.5 rad \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{1\\,\\mathrm{rev}}{2\\,\\pi \\,\\mathrm{rad}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{7.5\\,}{2\\,\\pi \\,}\\) rev = <strong>1.19 rev</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','No.5','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The angular velocity of a rotating rigid body increases from 500 rpm to 1500 rpm in 2 min. </p><p>(i) What is the angular acceleration of the body?</p><p>(ii) What <strong>angle</strong> does it turn through in this 2 min?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({\\omega }_{0}\\) = 500 rpm (rev min<sup>-1</sup>),&emsp;</p><p>\\(\\omega \\) = 1 500 rpm (rev min<sup>-1</sup>), t = 2 min</p><p>(i) \\(\\alpha \\) = ?, (ii) \\(\\theta \\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\alpha \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\omega \\,-\\,{\\omega }_{0}}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1500\\,-\\,500}{2}\\) = <strong>500 rev min</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\omega \\)<sub>0</sub> t + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\alpha \\) t<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>500 (2) + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) (500) 2<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>2 000 </strong><strong>rev</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\pi \\) \\(\\times \\) 2 000 rad = <strong>4000 </strong>\\(\\pi \\)<strong> rad</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','No.6','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A centrifuge rotor is accelerated from <strong>rest</strong> to 20 000 rpm in 30 s.</p><p>(i) What is its average angular acceleration? </p><p>(ii)&emsp;Through how many <strong>revolutions</strong> has the centrifuge rotor turned during its acceleration period, assuming constant angular acceleration?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({\\omega }_{0}\\) = 0 (from rest),</p><p>\\(\\omega \\) = 20 000 rpm (rev min<sup>-1</sup>)</p><p>t = 30 s = 30 s \\(\\times \\,\\frac{1\\,\\min}{60\\,s}\\) = 0.5 min</p><p>(i) \\(\\alpha \\) = ?&emsp;(ii) \\(\\theta \\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\alpha \\)  </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\omega \\,-\\,{\\omega }_{0}}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{20\\,000\\,-\\,0}{0.5}\\)  = <strong>40 000 rev min</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\omega \\)<sub>0</sub> t + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\alpha \\) t<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0 + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) (40 000) \\((\\,\\frac{1\\,}{2}\\,{)}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>5 000 </strong><strong>rev</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.2','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A ball is whirled with constant angular acceleration. From <strong>rest</strong>, it attains an angular velocity of 25 rad s<sup>-1</sup> after traversing an angular displacement of 41 rad. What is the angular acceleration of the ball?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({\\omega }_{0}\\) = 0 (from rest), \\(\\omega \\) = 25 rad s<sup>-1</sup>, </p><p>\\(\\theta \\) = 41 rad, \\(\\alpha \\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\omega \\)<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\omega }_{0}^{2}\\) + 2 \\(\\alpha \\) \\(\\theta \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(25\\)<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0 + 2 \\(\\alpha \\) (41)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(25\\)<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>82 \\(\\alpha \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\alpha \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{25}^{2}}{82}\\) = <strong>7.62 rad s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','No.7','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A figure skater is spinning with an angular velocity of 15 rad s<sup>-1</sup>. She then comes to a <strong>stop</strong> over a brief period of time. During this time, her angular displacement is 5.1 rad. Assuming constant angular acceleration, find (i) her angular acceleration, and (ii) the time during which she comes to rest.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({\\omega }_{0}\\) = 15 rad s<sup>-1</sup>,&emsp;\\(\\omega \\) = 0 (stop), \\(\\theta \\) = 5.1 rad</p><p>(i) \\(\\alpha \\) = ?&emsp;(ii) t = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\omega \\)<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\omega }_{0}^{2}\\) + 2 \\(\\alpha \\) \\(\\theta \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>0</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({15}^{2}\\)+ 2 \\(\\alpha \\) (5.1)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>10.2 \\(\\alpha \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>- \\({15}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\alpha \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{-\\,{15}^{2}}{10.2}\\) = <strong>- 22.06 rad s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\alpha \\)  </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\omega \\,-\\,{\\omega }_{0}}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\omega \\,-\\,{\\omega }_{0}}{\\alpha }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{0\\,-\\,15}{-\\,22.06}\\) = <strong>0.68 s</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The wheel of a car with radius 20 cm starts moving. The angular acceleration provided by the engine is 12 rad s<sup>-2</sup>. What is the tangential acceleration of the rim of the wheel?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 20 cm = 20 × \\({10}^{-2}\\) m, \\(\\alpha \\) = 12 rad s<sup>-2</sup>,</p><p><em>a</em><sub>T</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({a}_{T}\\)<sub><em> </em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>r \\(\\alpha \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>20 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\times \\) 12 = <strong>2.4 m s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'calculations','No.8','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A tire has a radius of 0.33 m, and its centre moves forward with a <strong>linear speed</strong> of 15 m s<sup>-1</sup>. (i) What is the angular velocity of the wheel? (ii) Relative to the axel, what is linear speed of a point located 0.175 m from the axel?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 0.33 m, v = 15 m s<sup>-1</sup><sup> </sup>(i) \\(\\omega \\) = ?</p><p>(ii) \\(v''\\) = ? at \\(r\\,''\\) = 0.175 m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>r \\(\\omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\omega \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{v}{r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{15}{0.33}\\) = <strong>45.45 rad s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>All the points on the tire have the same angular velocity. </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>\\(v''\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(r\\,''\\) \\(\\omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.175 \\(\\times \\) 45.45 = <strong>7.95 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'calculations','No.9','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A child spins a toy top, applying a force to the peg in the middle. The force applied results a tangential acceleration of the peg. If the radius of the peg is 0.5 cm, and the tangential acceleration applied is 0.54 m s<sup>-2</sup>, what is the angular acceleration of the top?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 0.5 cm = 0.5 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\)m, \\({a}_{T}\\)<sub> </sub>= 0.54 m s<sup>-2</sup>,</p><p>\\(\\alpha \\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({a}_{T}\\)<sub> </sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>r \\(\\alpha \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\alpha \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{a}_{T}}{r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{0.54\\,\\,\\,}{5\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}}\\) = <strong>108 rad s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A boy steps on a merry-go-round which has a radius of 5 m and is at rest. It starts accelerating at a constant rate up to an angular velocity of 5 rad s<sup>-1</sup> in 20 s. What is the distance traversed by the boy?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({\\omega }_{0}\\) = 0 (from rest), \\(\\omega \\) = 5 rad s<sup>-1</sup>, r = 5 m, </p><p>t = 20 s, s = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\alpha \\)  </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\omega \\,-\\,{\\omega }_{0}}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{5\\,-\\,0}{20}\\) = <strong>0.25 rad s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\omega \\)<sub>0</sub> t + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\alpha \\) t<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0 + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\times \\) 0.25 \\(\\times \\) 20<sup>2</sup> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>50 rad</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>s</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>r \\(\\theta \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>s</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>5 \\(\\times \\) 50 = <strong>250 m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.6','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A stone tied to a string is moving in a circle of radius 1.5 m at a constant speed 8 m s<sup>-1</sup>. Calculate the magnitude of the centripetal acceleration of the stone.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 1.5 m, v = 8 m s<sup>-1</sup>, <em>a</em><sub>c</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>a</em><sub>c</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}^{2}}{r}\\) = \\(\\frac{{8}^{2}}{1.5}\\) = <strong>42.67 m s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','No.10','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A 150 g ball at the end of a string is revolving uniformly in a horizontal circle of radius 0.6 m. The ball makes 2 revolutions in a second. What is its centripetal acceleration?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 0.6 m, m = 150 g, t = 1 s</p><p>\\(\\omega \\) = 2 rev s<sup>-1 </sup>= 4 \\(\\pi \\) rad s<sup>-1</sup>,<sup> </sup>\\(a\\)<sub>c</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>a</em><sub>c</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>r \\({\\omega }^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>a</em><sub>c</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.6 \\(\\times \\) \\({(4\\,\\pi )}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>94.8 m s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,11,true),
(12,'calculations','No.11','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A carousel is initially at rest. It is given a constant angular acceleration 0.06 rad s<sup>-2</sup>, which increases its angular velocity for 8 s. At t = 8 s, determine the <strong>magnitude</strong> of the following quantities: (i) the angular velocity of the carousel, (ii) the linear velocity of a child located 2.5 m from the centre, (iii) the tangential acceleration of the child, (iv) the centripetal acceleration of the child, and (v) the total linear acceleration of the child.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>\\({\\omega }_{0}\\) = 0, \\(\\alpha \\) = 0.06 rad s<sup>-2</sup>, t = 8 s</p><p>(i)  \\(\\omega \\) = ? (ii) v = ?, r = 2.5 m</p><p>(iii) <em>a</em><sub>T</sub> = ?, (iv) <em>a</em><sub>c</sub> = ?,&emsp;(v) <em>a</em> = ?,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\omega \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\omega \\)<sub>0</sub> + \\(\\alpha \\) t</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0 + 0.06 (8) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.48 rad s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>r \\(\\omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2.5 \\(\\times \\) 0.48 = <strong>1.2 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>(iii)</p></td><td><p><em>a</em><sub>T</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>r \\(\\alpha \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2.5 \\(\\times \\) 0.06 = <strong>0.15 m s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>(iv)</p></td><td><p><em>a</em><sub>c</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>r \\({\\omega }^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2.5 \\(\\times \\) \\({0.48}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.576 m s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>(v)</p></td><td><p><em>a</em></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{{a}_{c}^{2}\\,+\\,{a}_{T}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{(0.576{)}^{2}\\,+\\,(0.15{)}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.5952 m s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,12,true);
INSERT INTO educational_content (grade,category,title,chapter,content,sort_order,active) VALUES
(12,'calculations','Eg.4','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The platter of the hard drive of a computer uniformly rotates at 7200 rpm. If the reading head of the drive is located 3 cm from the rotational axis, what is the <strong>linear speed</strong> and the <strong>centripetal acceleration</strong> of the point on the platter just below the reading head? </p><p>&emsp;If a single bit requires 0.5 μm of length along the direction of motion, how many bits per second can the writing head writes when it is 3 cm from the axis?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 3 cm = 3 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\)m,</p><p>\\(\\omega \\) = 7200 rpm (rev min<sup>-1</sup>) </p><p>    = 7200 \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{rev}}{\\min}\\) = 7200 \\(\\frac{2\\,\\pi \\,\\mathrm{rad}}{60\\,s}\\) </p><p>&emsp;= <strong>240 </strong>\\(\\pi \\)<strong> rad s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup><strong> </strong></p><p>v = ?, <em>a</em><sub>c</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>r \\(\\omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>3 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\times \\,\\)240 \\(\\pi \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>22.62 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>a</em><sub>c</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}^{2}}{r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{22.62}^{2}}{3\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.705 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{4}\\)<strong> m s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>[OR]</strong></p></td><td><p><em>a</em><sub>c</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>r \\(\\omega \\)<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>3 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\times \\,\\)240 \\(\\pi \\) \\(\\times \\,\\)240 \\(\\pi \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.705 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{4}\\)<strong> m s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Distance per second moved = 22.62 m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Distance per bit = 0.5 \\(\\mu \\) m =0.5 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-6}\\) m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Number of bits per second</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>&emsp;= \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{distance}\\,\\mathrm{per}\\,\\mathrm{second}\\,\\mathrm{moved}}{\\mathrm{distance}\\,\\mathrm{per}\\,\\mathrm{bit}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>&emsp;= \\(\\frac{22.62}{5\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-7}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>&emsp;= <strong>4.524 5 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{7}\\)<strong> bits</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,13,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.5','1','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A centrifuge has a radius of 20 cm, and decelerates from a maximum rotational rate of 7.2 × 10<sup>3</sup> rpm to <strong>rest</strong> in 30 s under a <strong>constant angular acceleratio</strong>n. It is rotating counter clockwise. What is the magnitude of the resultant acceleration of a point at the tip of the centrifuge at 10 s? What is the direction of the resultant acceleration vector?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>r = 20 cm = 20 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\)m, </p><p>\\({\\omega }_{0}\\) = 7.2 × 10<sup>3</sup> rpm (rev min<sup>-1</sup>) </p><p>&emsp;= 7.2 × 10<sup>3</sup> \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{rev}}{\\min}\\) = 7200  \\(\\frac{2\\,\\pi \\,\\mathrm{rad}}{60\\,s}\\) </p><p>&emsp;= <strong>240 </strong>\\(\\pi \\)<strong> rad s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup> </p><p>\\(\\omega \\) = 0 (stop)&emsp;at t = 30 s</p><p>\\(a\\) = ?&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;at t = 10 s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>At t = 30 s,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\alpha \\)<em> </em></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{\\omega -\\,{\\omega }_{0}}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{0\\,-\\,240\\,\\pi \\,\\,\\mathrm{rad}}{30\\,s}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\alpha \\)<em> </em></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>- 8 </strong>\\(\\pi \\)<strong> rad s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>At t = 10 s,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\alpha \\)<em> </em></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>- 8 \\(\\pi \\) rad s<sup>-2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>a</em><sub>T</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>r \\(\\alpha \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>20 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\) (- 8 \\(\\pi \\)) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>- 5.03 </strong><strong>m s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>At t = 10 s,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\omega \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\({\\omega }_{0}\\) + \\(\\alpha \\) t</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>240 \\(\\pi \\) + (- 8 \\(\\pi \\)) (10)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>240 \\(\\pi \\) - 80 \\(\\pi \\) = <strong>160 </strong>\\(\\pi \\)<strong> rad s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>a</em><sub>c</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>r \\(\\omega \\)<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>20 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\) \\(\\times \\) 160 \\(\\pi \\) \\(\\times \\) 160 \\(\\pi \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>5.054 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{4}\\)<strong> m s</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Magnitude,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>a</em></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\sqrt{{a}_{c}^{2}\\,+\\,{a}_{T}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\,(5.054\\,\\times \\,{10}^{4}{)}^{2}+(-\\,5.03{)}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>5.054 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{4}\\)<strong> m s</strong><sup><strong>-2 </strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Direction,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>tan \\(ϕ\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{a}_{T}}{{a}_{c}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(ϕ\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>tan<sup>-1</sup> (\\(\\frac{{a}_{T}}{{a}_{c}}\\))</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(ϕ\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>tan<sup>-1</sup> (\\(\\frac{5.03}{5.054\\,\\times \\,{10}^{4}}\\))</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.0057</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,14,true),
(12,'calculations','No.7','2','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An 8.3 kg mass is attached to a string that has a <strong>breaking strength</strong> of 1500 N. If the mass is whirled in a <strong>horizontal circle</strong> of radius 80 cm, what maximum speed can it have?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Mass, m = 8.3 kg, T<sub>max</sub> = 1 500 N,&emsp;</p><p>r = 80 cm = 80 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\) m, g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup></p><p>maximum speed, v<sub>max</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For horizontal circle,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>       F<sub>C</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> T</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m\\,{v}_{\\max}^{2}}{r}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>T<sub>max</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{8.3\\,\\,{v}_{\\max}^{2}}{80\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-2}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1500</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({v}_{\\max}^{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1500\\,\\times \\,80\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-2}}{8.3}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sub>max</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1500\\,\\times \\,80\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-2}}{8.3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>12.02 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','No.9','2','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; What is the tension in a 1 m string that is spinning 0.5 kg stone in a <strong>horizontal circle</strong> with 3 rps?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>m = 0.5 kg, r = 1 m, g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup>, T = ?</p><p>\\(\\omega \\) = 3 rps (rev s<sup>-1</sup>)</p><p>&emsp;= 3 \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{rev}}{s}\\)   = 3 \\(\\frac{2\\,\\pi \\,\\mathrm{rad}}{s}\\) = 6 \\(\\pi \\) rad s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For horizontal circle,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F<sub>C</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> T</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>m r \\(\\omega \\)<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>T</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>T</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>m r \\(\\omega \\)<sup>2</sup> = 0.5 \\(\\times \\) 1 \\(\\times \\) (6 \\(\\pi {)}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>177.69 N</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','2','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A 60 cm rope is tied to the handle of a bucket which is then whirled in <strong>vertical circle</strong>. The mass of the bucket is 3 kg. If the tension of the rope at the lowest point in its path is 50 N, find the speed of the bucket at that point.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>m = 3 kg, g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup></p><p>r = 60 cm = 60 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\)m,&emsp;v = ?</p><p>Force acting on bucket are </p><p>Tension force, T = 50 N</p><p>Weight, w = mg = 3 \\(\\times \\,\\)9.8 = <strong>29.4 N</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For vertical circle, at lowest point,  </p><p>F<sub>net</sub> = T – w = 50 - 29.4 = <strong>20.6 N</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>(Since F<sub>net</sub> provides the centripetal acceleration)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F<sub>C</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>F<sub>net</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m\\,{v}^{2}}{r}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>F<sub>net</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{3\\,{v}^{2}}{60\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-2}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>20.6</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>20.6 \\(\\times {20\\times 10}^{-2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{20.6\\times {20\\times 10}^{-2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>2.03 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','No.6','2','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A 0.15 kg ball on the end of 1.1 m long cord (negligible mass) is swung in a <strong>vertical circle</strong>. (i) Determine the minimum speed the ball must have at the top of its arc so that the ball continues moving in a circle. (ii) Calculate the tension in the cord at the bottom of the arc, assuming the ball is moving at <strong>twice the speed</strong> of part (i).</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>m = 0.15 kg, r = 1.1 m, g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup></p><p>(i) v = ?, (ii) T = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>For vertical circle, At the top position, </p><p>F<sub>net</sub> = T + w  = T + mg</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>(Since F<sub>net</sub> provides the centripetal acceleration)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>At the top, For minimum speed, T<sub>min</sub> = 0</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F<sub>C</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>F<sub>net</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m\\,{v}^{2}}{r}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>T + mg</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m\\,{v}_{\\min}^{2}}{r}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>m g  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\,{v}_{\\min}^{2}}{r}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>g  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({v}_{\\min}^{2}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>g r</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sub>min</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\sqrt{g\\,r}\\) = \\(\\sqrt{9.8\\,\\times \\,1.1}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>3.283 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>At the bottom, the speed is twice than at the top. </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>v = 2 v<sub>min</sub> = 2 \\(\\times \\) 3.283 = 6.566 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>At the bottom, \\({F}_{C}\\)    = T - w </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>T</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({F}_{C}\\) + w</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m\\,{v}^{2}}{r}\\) + m g</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{0.15\\,(\\,{6.566\\,)}^{2}}{1.1}\\) + (0.15 \\(\\times \\) 9.8)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>7.349 N</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','No.11','2','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; In an atom, an electron moves in a circular path around the nucleus. The speed of the electron is approximately 2.2 × 10<sup>6</sup> m s<sup>-1</sup>. Find the centripetal force acting on the electron as it revolves in a circular orbit of radius 0.53 × 10<sup>-10</sup> m. (m<sub>e</sub> = 9.1 × 10<sup>−</sup><sup>31</sup> kg)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v = 2.2 × 10<sup>6</sup> m s<sup>-1</sup>, m<sub>e</sub> = 9.1 × 10<sup>−</sup><sup>31</sup> kg</p><p>r = 0.53 × 10<sup>-10</sup> m, F<sub>C</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F<sub>C</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m\\,{v}^{2}}{r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{9.1\\,\\,{10}^{-31}\\,(2.2\\,\\times \\,{10}^{6}\\,{)}^{2}}{0.53\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-10}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F<sub>C</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>8.3101 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{-8}\\)<strong> N </strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','2','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An athlete weighing 790 N is running a curve at a speed of 6 m s<sup>-1</sup> in an arc. The radius of curvature of the arc is 5 m. Find the centripetal force acting on him. </p><p>&emsp;Which force provides the centripetal force? </p><p>&emsp;What will happen to him if the radius of curvature is smaller?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>w = 790 N, v = 6 m s<sup>-1</sup>, r = 5 m, </p><p>g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup>, F<sub>C</sub> = ?</p><p>m = \\(\\frac{w}{g}\\) = \\(\\frac{790}{9.8}\\) = 80.61 kg</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F<sub>C</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m\\,{v}^{2}}{r}\\) =  \\(\\frac{80.61\\,(6\\,{)}^{2}}{5}\\) = <strong>580.4 N</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>\\(⇒\\)<strong> </strong></p><p>\\(⇒\\)<strong> </strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Frictional force between the feet and ground provides the centripetal force.</p><p>If the radius of curvature is smaller, the centripetal force will become greater. He will slip since the frictional force is less than the required centripetal force. [F<sub>f</sub> &lt; F<sub>C</sub>, he will slip]</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.1','2','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; <strong>&emsp;What is the banking angle</strong> for an expressway off-ramp curve of radius 50 m at a limiting speed of 50 km h<sup>-1</sup>?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 50 m, \\(\\theta \\) = ?, g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup></p><p>v = 50 km h<sup>-1</sup> = 50 \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{km}}{h}\\) = 50 \\(\\frac{{10}^{3}\\,m}{3600\\,s}\\) </p><p>   = 13.89 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>tan \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}^{2}}{r\\,g}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>tan \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{13.89}^{2}}{50\\,\\times 9.8}\\)   </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>tan<sup>-1</sup> \\(\\frac{{13.89}^{2}}{50\\,\\times 9.8}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>21.49</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)<strong> (or) 21</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)<strong> 29</strong>\\(''\\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','2','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A jet plane is flying around the airport with a speed of 800 km h<sup>-1</sup> along a circular path with a radius of 2 km as shown in given figure. <strong>At what angle </strong>must the wings of the plane be banked?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 2 km = 2 \\(\\times {10}^{3}\\)m, \\(\\theta \\) = ?, g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup></p><p>v = 800 km h<sup>-1</sup>= 800 \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{km}}{h}\\) = 800 \\(\\frac{{10}^{3}\\,m}{3600\\,s}\\) </p><p>   = 222.22 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>tan \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}^{2}}{r\\,g}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>tan \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{222.22}^{2}}{2\\,\\times \\,{10}^{3}\\,\\times \\,9.8}\\)   </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>tan<sup>-1</sup> \\(\\frac{{222.22}^{2}}{2\\,\\times \\,{10}^{3}\\,\\times \\,9.8}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>68.35</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)<strong> (or) 68</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)<strong> 2</strong>\\(1''\\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','No.8','2','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An aeroplane is circling above an airport in a horizontal circle at a speed of 400 km h<sup>-1</sup>. The banking angle of the wing is 20°. What is the radius of the circular path?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = ?, \\(\\theta \\) = 20°, g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup></p><p>v = 400 km h<sup>-1</sup>= 400 \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{km}}{h}\\) = 400 \\(\\frac{{10}^{3}\\,m}{3600\\,s}\\) </p><p>   = 111.11 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>tan \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}^{2}}{r\\,g}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>r</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}^{2}}{\\tan\\,\\theta \\,g}\\) =  \\(\\frac{{111.11}^{2}}{\\tan\\,20\\,\\times \\,9.8}\\) = <strong>3461 m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','No.10','2','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A curved roadway has a radius of curvature of 200 m, and a banking angle of 10°. What is the highest speed at which a car can round the curve safely? (Neglect the friction between the tire and the road.)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 200 m, \\(\\theta \\) = 10°, g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup>,<sup> </sup>v = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>tan \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}^{2}}{r\\,g}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>r g (tan \\(\\theta \\))</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{r\\,g\\,(\\tan\\,\\theta )}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{200\\times 9.8\\times \\tan\\,10^\\circ }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>18.59 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A gardener uses a water pipe of 2.5 cm diameter. It takes 1 min to fill 30 litre bucket. What is the initial speed of water coming out of the hose? Then, nozzle with an opening 0.5 cm<sup>2</sup> is attached to the hose. Find the water speed coming out from the nozzle.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For pipe (hose)</p><p>d<sub>1</sub> = 2.5 cm</p><p>r<sub>1</sub> = \\(\\frac{2.5\\,\\mathrm{cm}}{2}\\) = 1.25 cm</p><p>A<sub>1</sub> = \\(\\pi \\,{r}_{1}^{2}\\) </p><p>     = 3.142 \\(\\times \\,{1.25\\,}^{2}\\) </p><p>     = 4.91 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>\\({v}_{1}\\) = ?</p></td><td><p>For nozzle </p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A<sub>2</sub> = 0.5 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>\\({v}_{2}\\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>V = 30 litre = 30 \\(\\times \\) 1000 cm<sup>3</sup>, </p><p>t = 1 min = 60 s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>The volume rate</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\({A}_{1\\,}{v}_{1}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{30\\,\\times \\,1000\\,}{60}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>4.91 \\({v}_{1}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{30\\,\\times \\,1000\\,}{60\\,\\times \\,4.91}\\) = <strong>101.83 cm s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Using continuity equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({A}_{2\\,}{v}_{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\({A}_{1\\,}{v}_{1}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({v}_{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{A}_{1}\\,{v}_{1}}{{A}_{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{4.91\\,\\times \\,101.83}{0.5}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>999.97</strong><strong> </strong><strong>cm s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>[OR]</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>The volume rate</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\({A}_{2\\,}{v}_{2}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{30\\,\\times \\,1000\\,}{60}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>0.5 \\({v}_{2}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{30\\,\\times \\,1000\\,}{60\\,\\times \\,0.5}\\) = <strong>1000 cm s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; What area must a heating duct have, if air moving 3 m s<sup>-1</sup> along it can replenish the air every 15 min in a room of volume 300 m<sup>3</sup>? Assume the density of air remains constant.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v = 3 m s<sup>-1</sup>, V = 300 m<sup>3</sup> </p><p>t = 15 min = 15 \\(\\times \\) 60 = 900 s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Volume flow rate</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>A v</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{300}{900}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>A \\(\\times \\) 3</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{300}{900\\times \\,3\\,}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>A </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>A</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.11 m</strong><sup><strong>2</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Water runs into a fountain, filling all the pipes, at a steady rate of 0.75 m<sup>3</sup> s<sup>-1</sup>. (i) How fast will it shoot out of a hole 4.5 cm in diameter? (ii) At what speed will it shoot out if the diameter of the hole is three times as large?&emsp;</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>\\(\\frac{V}{t}\\) = 0.75 m<sup>3</sup> s<sup>-1</sup>, d = 4.5 cm</p><p>r = \\(\\frac{4.5\\,\\mathrm{cm}}{2}\\) = 2.25 cm = 2.25 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\) m</p><p>A = \\(\\pi \\,{r}^{2}\\) = 3.142 \\(\\times \\) (2.25 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\))<sup>2</sup> m<sup>2</sup></p><p>v = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Volume flow rate</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V}{t}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>A v</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>0.75</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>3.142 × (2.25 × \\({10}^{-2}\\))<sup>2</sup> v</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{0.75}{3.142\\,\\times \\,(2.25\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-2}{)}^{2}\\,}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>471.51 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>If the diameter of the hole is three times larger,</p><p>\\({d}_{2}\\) = 3 d<sub>1</sub></p><p>\\({r}_{2}\\) = 3 r<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>A<sub>2</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\pi \\,{r}_{2}^{2}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>A<sub>2</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\pi \\,\\)(3 r<sub>1</sub>)<sup>2</sup> = 9  \\(\\pi \\,{r}_{1}^{2}\\) = 9 A<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Using continuity equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p> \\({A}_{2\\,}{v}_{2}\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({A}_{1\\,}{v}_{1}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>9 \\({A}_{1\\,}{v}_{2}\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({A}_{1\\,}{v}_{1}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\({v}_{1}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>9 \\({v}_{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\({v}_{2}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}_{1}}{9}\\,\\) = \\(\\frac{471.51}{9}\\,\\) = <strong>52.39 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>[OR]</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>\\({d}_{2}\\) = 3 \\(\\times \\) 4.5 = 13.5 cm</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>r<sub>2</sub> = \\(\\frac{13.5}{2}\\) = 6.75 cm = 6.75 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-2</sup> m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>A<sub>2</sub> = \\(\\pi \\) \\({r}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Using continuity equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p> \\({A}_{2\\,}{v}_{2}\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({A}_{1\\,}{v}_{1}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>v<sub>2</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{A}_{1}{v}_{1}}{{A}_{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\pi \\,{r}_{1}^{2}{v}_{1}}{\\pi \\,{r}_{2}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{(2.25\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-2})}^{2}\\,\\times 471.51}{{(6.75\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{-2})}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>52.39 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.4','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Water tank of dimension 3 m × 3 m × 3 m and the base of the tank is 10 m above the ground. It takes 1 h to fill. (i) Find the power output of the pump to fill the tank. (ii) Find the flow rate through the pipe and the speed of the water flow in the pipe which has 5 cm radius.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>V = 3 m × 3 m × 3 m = 27 m<sup>3</sup></p><p>h = 10 + 3 = 13 m, t = 1 h = 3600 s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P                       </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{W}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m\\,g\\,h}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\rho \\,V\\,g\\,h\\,}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1000\\,\\times 27\\,\\times \\,9.8\\,\\times 13\\,}{3600}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>955.5 W</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>r</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>5 cm = 5 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\) m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{27}{3600}\\) = 7.5\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m<sup>3</sup> s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>A v</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\pi \\) r<sup>2</sup> v</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p> 7.5\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) = 3.142 \\(\\times (5\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-2}{)}^{2}\\) v</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{7.5\\times {10}^{-3}}{3.142\\,\\times (5\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-2}{)}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.96 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.6','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A shower head has 20 circular openings, each with radius 1 mm. The shower head is connected to a pipe with radius 0.8 cm. If the speed of water in the pipe is 3 m s<sup>-1</sup>, what is its speed as it exits the shower-head openings?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For pipe</p><p>\\({r}_{1}\\) = 0.8 cm </p><p>    = 0.8 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\)m</p><p>\\({A}_{1}\\)=  \\(\\pi \\,{r}_{1}^{2}\\) </p><p>\\({v}_{1}\\) = 3 m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>n<sub>1 </sub>= 1</p></td><td><p>For shower head</p><p>\\({r}_{2}\\) = 1 mm </p><p>    = 1 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m</p><p>\\({A}_{2}\\)=  \\(\\pi \\,{r}_{2}^{2}\\) </p><p>\\({v}_{2}\\) = ?</p><p>n<sub>2</sub> = 20</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Using continuity equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>n<sub>2</sub> \\({A}_{2\\,}{v}_{2}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>n<sub>1 </sub>\\({A}_{1\\,}{v}_{1}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({v}_{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{{n}_{1}\\,A}_{1\\,}{v}_{1}}{{{n}_{2}\\,A}_{2}}\\,\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{\\pi \\,{r}_{1}^{2}\\,\\times \\,{v}_{1}}{20\\,(\\,\\pi \\,{r}_{2}^{2}\\,)}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({v}_{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{(0.8\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-2}{)}^{2}\\,\\times \\,3}{20\\,(1\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}{)}^{2}}\\) = <strong>9.6 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'calculations','No.4','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; In an adult, the radius of aorta is normally ~ 1.5 cm and blood moves through it at an average speed of 30 cm s<sup>-1</sup>. If typical capillary has a radius of 5 × 10<sup>-6</sup> m, and blood passes through them with a velocity of 0.1 cm s<sup>-1</sup> approximately how many capillaries are in the body?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For aorta</p><p>\\({r}_{1}\\) = 1.5 cm</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\\({A}_{1}\\)=  \\(\\pi \\,{r}_{1}^{2}\\) </p><p>\\({v}_{1}\\) = 30 cm s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>n<sub>1</sub> = 1</p></td><td><p>For typical capillary</p><p>\\({r}_{2}\\) = 5 × 10<sup>-6</sup> m </p><p>    = 5 × 10<sup>-6</sup> × 10<sup>2</sup> cm</p><p>    = 5 × 10<sup>-4</sup> cm</p><p>\\({A}_{2}\\)=  \\(\\pi \\,{r}_{2}^{2}\\) </p><p>\\({v}_{2}\\) = 0.1 cm s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>n<sub>2</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Using continuity equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>n<sub>2</sub> \\({A}_{2\\,}{v}_{2}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>n<sub>1 </sub>\\({A}_{1\\,}{v}_{1}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>n<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{{n}_{1}\\,A}_{1\\,}{v}_{1}}{{A}_{2}\\,{v}_{2}}\\,\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{\\pi \\,{r}_{1}^{2}\\,\\times \\,{v}_{1}}{\\pi \\,{r}_{2}^{2}\\,\\times \\,{v}_{2}}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1.5\\,\\times \\,1.5\\,\\times \\,30}{5\\,\\,{10}^{-4}\\,\\times \\,5\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-4}\\,\\times \\,0.1}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>2.7 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{9}\\)<strong> capillaries</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.5','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Water flowing through a restriction in a <strong>horizontal pipe</strong> is shown in the given figure. The radius of the pipe at the left end and right end are 6 cm and 2 cm respectively. If the velocity and pressure of water at the left end of pipe are 1 m s<sup>-1</sup> and 200 kPa, find the velocity and pressure of water at the right end of the pipe.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>At left end</p><p>\\({r}_{1}\\) = 6 cm </p><p>    = 6 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\) m</p><p>p<sub>1</sub> = 200 k Pa </p><p>    = 200 \\(\\times {10}^{3}\\) Pa</p><p>v<sub>1</sub> = 1 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td><td><p>At right end</p><p>\\({r}_{2}\\) = 2 cm </p><p>     = 2 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\) m</p><p>p<sub>2</sub> = ?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>v<sub>2</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>\\(\\rho \\) = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>,<sup> </sup>h<sub>1</sub> = h<sub>2</sub> (horizontal pipe)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>Using continuity equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\({A}_{2\\,}{v}_{2}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\({A}_{1\\,}{v}_{1}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\({v}_{2}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{A}_{1}\\,{v}_{1}}{{A}_{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{\\pi \\,{r}_{1}^{2}\\,\\times \\,{v}_{1}}{\\pi \\,{r}_{2}^{2}}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\({v}_{2}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{(6\\,\\,\\,{10}^{-2})}^{2}\\,\\times \\,1}{{(2\\,\\,\\,{10}^{-2})}^{2}}\\) = <strong>9 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>Using Bernoulli’s theorem,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>p<sub>2</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>2</sub> = p<sub>1</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>p<sub>2 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) = p<sub>1 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>p<sub>2</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>p<sub>1</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) - \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>p<sub>1</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) [\\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) - \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) ]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>[200 \\(\\times {10}^{3}\\)] +  \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\times \\)1000 [ 1<sup>2</sup> - 9<sup>2</sup>]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><strong>160 000 Pa (or) 160 kPa</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.6','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Calculate the pressure and speed of water at points B and C shown below. (density of water is 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>At A,</p><p>A<sub>1 </sub>= 3 m<sup>2</sup></p><p>v<sub>1</sub> = 10 m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>p<sub>1</sub> = 300 kPa </p><p>    = 300\\(\\times {10}^{3}\\) Pa</p><p>h<sub>1</sub> = 20 m</p></td><td><p>At B,</p><p>A<sub>2 </sub>= 3 m<sup>2</sup></p><p>v<sub>2</sub> = ?</p><p>p<sub>2</sub> = ?</p><p>h<sub>2</sub> = 0 m</p></td><td><p>At C,</p><p>A<sub>3 </sub>= 6 m<sup>2</sup>,</p><p>v<sub>3</sub> = ?</p><p>p<sub>3</sub> = ?</p><p>h<sub>3</sub> = 0 m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"8\"><p>\\(\\rho \\) = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"8\"><p>Using continuity equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>  A<sub>2</sub> v<sub>2</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A<sub>1</sub> v<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>v<sub>2</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v<sub>1</sub> = <strong>10 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"7\"><p>Using Bernoulli’s theorem, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"7\"><p>p<sub>2</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>2</sub> = p<sub>1</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>p<sub>2 </sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>p<sub>1 </sub>+\\(\\,\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>[300\\(\\times {10}^{3}\\)] + [1000\\(\\times \\)9.8\\(\\times \\)20]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><strong>496 000 Pa (or) 496 kPa</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"7\"><p>Using continuity equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>A<sub>3</sub> v<sub>3</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A<sub>2</sub> v<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>v<sub>3</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{{A}_{2}{v}_{2}}{{A}_{3}}\\) = \\(\\frac{3\\,\\times \\,10\\,}{6}\\)  = <strong>5 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"7\"><p>Using Bernoulli’s theorem, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"7\"><p>p<sub>3 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{3}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>3</sub> = p<sub>2</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"7\"><p>p<sub>3 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{3}^{2}\\) = p<sub>2 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>p<sub>3</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>p<sub>2</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) - \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{3}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>p<sub>3</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>p<sub>2</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) [ \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) - \\({v}_{3}^{2}\\) ]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>496 000 + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\times \\) 1000[ 10<sup>2</sup> - 5<sup>2</sup>]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p><strong>533 500 Pa</strong><strong> </strong><strong>(or)</strong><strong> </strong><strong>533.5 kPa</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.7','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A <strong>sealed</strong> tank containing seawater to a height of 11 m also contains air above the water at a pressure of 4 atm. Water flows out from the bottom through a small hole. How fast is this water moving? </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>top water surface</p><p>h<sub>1</sub> = 11 m,</p><p>p<sub>1</sub> = 4 atm </p><p>    = 4\\(\\times \\)1.01\\(\\times {10}^{5}\\) Pa </p><p>    = 4.04 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{5}\\) Pa       </p><p>v<sub>1</sub> \\(\\approx \\) 0 (\\(\\because \\) A<sub>1</sub> &gt;&gt; A<sub>2</sub>)</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>at the bottom</p><p>h<sub>2</sub> = 0 m,</p><p>p<sub>2</sub> = 1 atm </p><p>    = 1.01 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{5}\\) Pa</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>v<sub>2</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>\\(\\rho \\) = 1025 kg m<sup>-3</sup> (sea water)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Using Bernoulli’s theorem,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>p<sub>2</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>2</sub> = p<sub>1</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>p<sub>2 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>p<sub>1 </sub>+ \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>p<sub>1</sub> + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub> – p<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\times \\) 1025 \\(\\times \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>[4.04 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{5}\\)] + [1025 \\(\\times \\) 9.8 \\(\\times \\) 11] - [1.01 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{5}\\)]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>512.5 \\(\\times \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>413495</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{413495}{512.5}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sub>2</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>28.4 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.8','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A small circular hole 6.00 mm in diameter is cut in the side of a large water tank, 14.0 m below the water level in the tank. The top of the tank is open to the air.</p><p>&emsp;Find (i) the speed of efflux of the water, and </p><p>&emsp;&emsp;(ii) the volume discharged per second. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>top water surface</p><p>h<sub>1</sub> = 14 m,</p><p>p<sub>1</sub> = 1 atm </p><p>    = 1.01 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{5}\\) Pa,    </p><p>v<sub>1</sub> \\(\\approx \\) 0 (\\(\\because \\) A<sub>1</sub> &gt;&gt; A<sub>2</sub>)</p></td><td><p>at the bottom</p><p>h<sub>2</sub> = 0 m,</p><p>p<sub>2</sub> = 1 atm </p><p>    = 1.01 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{5}\\) Pa,</p><p>v<sub>2</sub> = ?</p><p>d<sub>2</sub> = 6 mm </p><p>    = 6\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m</p><p>r<sub>2</sub> = \\(\\frac{6\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}}{2}\\) </p><p>    = 3\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>\\(\\rho \\) = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>(i)  v<sub>2</sub> =?&emsp;(ii) \\(\\frac{V}{t}\\) =?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Using Bernoulli’s theorem, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>p<sub>2</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>2</sub> = p<sub>1</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>p<sub>2 </sub>+ <sub> </sub>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) = p<sub>1</sub> + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>p<sub>1</sub> + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub> – p<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>1 atm + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub> – 1 atm</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>2 g h<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\sqrt{2\\,g\\,{h}_{1}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\sqrt{2\\times 9.8\\times 14}\\)  = <strong>16.57 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>volume discharged per second,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>A<sub>2</sub> v<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\pi \\,{r}_{2}^{2}\\) v<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>3.142 \\(\\times \\) (3 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-3}\\))<sup>2</sup> \\(\\times \\) 16.57</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>4.68 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{-4}\\)<strong> m</strong><sup><strong>3</strong></sup><strong> s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','No.3','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; One hypodermic syringe contains medicine with density 1010 kg m<sup>-3</sup>. The barrel of the syringe has a cross-sectional area 2.5×10<sup>-5</sup> m<sup>2</sup>, and the needle has a cross-sectional area 1\\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-8</sup> m<sup>2</sup>. The syringe is in <strong>horizontal</strong> position and injection is forced by 2 N acting on the plunger. Find the speed of the injection that enters into the patient. (The volume of syringe is 3 cc and injection time is 2 s)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>At barrel of syringe</p><p>A<sub>1</sub> = 2.5\\(\\times {10}^{-5}\\) m<sup>2</sup>,</p><p>F = 2 N</p><p>p<sub>1 </sub>= 1 atm<sub> + </sub>\\(\\frac{F}{{A}_{1}}\\)<sub>  </sub></p></td><td><p>At needle of syringe</p><p>A<sub>2</sub> = 1 \\(\\times {10}^{-8}\\) m<sup>2</sup>,</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>p<sub>2</sub> \\(\\approx \\) 1 atm<sub> </sub></p><p>    = 1.01 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{5}\\) Pa</p><p>v<sub>2</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>h<sub>1</sub> = h<sub>2 </sub>(for horizontal), \\(\\rho \\) = 1010 kg m<sup>-3</sup>, </p><p>V = 3 cc = 3 cm<sup>3</sup>, t = 2 s</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Using continuity equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>A<sub>1</sub> v<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>A<sub>2</sub> v<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>2.5 \\(\\times {10}^{-5}\\) v<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>1 \\(\\times {10}^{-8}\\) v<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1\\,\\times {10}^{-8}}{2.5\\,\\times {10}^{-5}}\\)<sub> </sub>v<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{v}_{2}}{2500}\\)<sub> </sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>v<sub>1 </sub>&lt;&lt; v<sub>2</sub>. So, v<sub>1</sub> can be neglected.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p> Using Bernoulli’s theorem, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>p<sub>2</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>2</sub> = p<sub>1</sub> + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>p<sub>2 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>p<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>p<sub>1</sub> – p<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>1 atm<sub> </sub>+<sub> </sub>\\(\\frac{F}{{A}_{1}}\\)<sub> </sub>– 1 atm</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\times \\)1010 \\(\\times {v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><sub> </sub>\\(\\frac{2}{2.5\\,\\times {\\,10}^{-5}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>505 \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>80 000</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{80\\,000}{505}\\)<sub> </sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{80\\,000}{505}}\\) = <strong>12.59 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,11,true),
(12,'calculations','No.5','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An aeroplane’s wings have a total surface area of 480 m<sup>2</sup>. The pressure difference upper and lower surfaces of each wing is 6500 Pa. Calculate the lift created.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = 480 m<sup>2</sup>, &emsp;lift, F = ?</p><p>Pressure difference, \\(∆\\)p = 6500 Pa</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)p</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{F}{A}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)p A = 6500 \\(\\times \\) 480</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>3.12 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> </strong>\\({10}^{6}\\)<strong> N</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,12,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.10','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Air is streaming past a <strong>horizontal</strong> aeroplane’s wings such that its speed is   120 m s<sup>-1</sup> at the upper surface and 90 m s<sup>-1</sup> at the lower surface. If the wing is 10 m long and 2 m wide and density of air is 1.3 kg m<sup>-3</sup>, find the <strong>net lift</strong> on it.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v<sub>1</sub> = 120 m s<sup>-1</sup>, v<sub>2</sub> = 90 m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>A = 10 \\(\\times \\) 2 = 20 m<sup>2</sup>, \\(\\rho \\) = 1.3 kg m<sup>-3</sup> </p><p>h<sub>1</sub> = h<sub>2</sub> (aeroplane’s wings are not too thick)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Using Bernoulli’s theorem, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>p<sub>2 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>2</sub> = p<sub>1 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>p<sub>2 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) = p<sub>1 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>p<sub>2</sub> – p<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) -  \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)p</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) [\\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) - \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) ]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\times \\) 1.3 [120<sup>2</sup> – 90<sup>2</sup>]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>4095 Pa</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)p</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{F}_{\\mathrm{net}}}{A}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F<sub>net</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> \\(∆\\)p A</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>4095 \\(\\times \\) 20 = <strong>81 900 N</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,13,true);
INSERT INTO educational_content (grade,category,title,chapter,content,sort_order,active) VALUES
(12,'calculations','Eg.8','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Air streams <strong>horizontally</strong> past a small aeroplane’s wings such that the speed is    70 m s<sup>-1</sup> over and 60 m s<sup>-1</sup> past the bottom surface. If the plane has a wing area of   16.2 m<sup>2</sup> on the top and on the bottom, what is the <strong>net vertical force</strong> that the air exerts on the airplane? The density of the air is 1.2 kg m<sup>-3</sup>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v<sub>1</sub> = 70 m s<sup>-1</sup>, v<sub>2</sub> = 60 m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>A = 16.2 m<sup>2</sup>, \\(\\rho \\) = 1.2 kg m<sup>-3</sup> </p><p>h<sub>1</sub> = h<sub>2</sub> (aeroplane’s wings are not too thick)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Using Bernoulli’s theorem, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>p<sub>2 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>2</sub> = p<sub>1 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) + \\(\\rho \\) g h<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>p<sub>2 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) = p<sub>1 </sub>+ \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>p<sub>2</sub> – p<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) -  \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p> \\(∆\\)p</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) [\\({v}_{1}^{2}\\) - \\({v}_{2}^{2}\\) ]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\times \\) 1.2 [70<sup>2</sup> – 60<sup>2</sup>]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>780 Pa</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)p</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{F}_{\\mathrm{net}}}{A}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F<sub>net</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> \\(∆\\)p A</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>780 \\(\\times \\) 16.2 = <strong>12 636 N</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,14,true),
(12,'calculations','No.6','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Derive expression for terminal velocity when a ball of radius r is dropped through a liquid of viscosity η and density ρ.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;The forces acting on the object are; </p><p>&emsp;-weight of the sphere ball, &emsp;</p><p>&emsp;&emsp;w = mg = ρ V g = \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\) π r<sup>3</sup> ρ<sub>1</sub> g </p><p>&emsp;-upward thrust, F<sub>1</sub> = mg = ρ V g = \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\) π r<sup>3</sup> ρ<sub>2 </sub>g</p><p>&emsp;-drag force, F = 6 π η r v </p><p>&emsp;At a constant velocity of the fall (terminal velocity), the upward and downward forces are in balance. </p><p>&emsp;&emsp;F<sub>1</sub> + F = w</p><p>&emsp;\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\) π r<sup>3</sup> ρ<sub>2 </sub>g + 6 π η r v = \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\) π r<sup>3</sup> ρ<sub>1</sub> g</p><p>&emsp; 6 π η r v&emsp;= \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\) π r<sup>3</sup> ρ<sub>1</sub> g - \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\) π r<sup>3</sup> ρ<sub>2</sub> g</p><p>&emsp; 6 π η r v&emsp;= \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\) π r<sup>3</sup> (ρ<sub>1</sub> - ρ<sub>2</sub>) g</p><p>&emsp;           v&emsp;= \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\times \\) \\(\\frac{\\,{r}^{3}\\,({\\rho }_{1}\\,-\\,{\\rho }_{2})\\,g}{6\\,\\,\\,r}\\)</p><p>&emsp;           v&emsp;= \\(\\frac{2\\,\\,g\\,{r}^{2}\\,({\\rho }_{1}\\,-\\,{\\rho }_{2})}{9\\,}\\)</p><p>&emsp;Where,&emsp;η = viscosity of the fluid,</p><p>&emsp;&emsp;g = the acceleration due to gravity,</p><p>&emsp;&emsp;ρ<sub>1</sub> = the density of the sphere,</p><p>&emsp;&emsp;ρ<sub>2</sub> = the density of the liquid,</p><p>&emsp;&emsp;r = radius of the falling sphere,</p><p>&emsp;&emsp;v = terminal velocity of sphere.&emsp;</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,15,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.9','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A metal plate of area 2.5 × 10<sup>-4</sup> m<sup>2</sup> is placed on a 0.25 × 10<sup>-3</sup> m thick layer of castor oil. If a force of 50 N is needed to move the plate with a velocity 3 × 10<sup>-2</sup> m s<sup>-1</sup>, calculate the coefficient of viscosity of castor oil.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = 2.5 × 10<sup>-4</sup> m<sup>2</sup>,</p><p>\\(∆\\)y = (0.25 × 10<sup>-3</sup> – 0) = 0.25 × 10<sup>-3</sup> m,            </p><p>F = - 50 N</p><p>(opposite to the direction of the motion),</p><p>\\(∆\\)v = (3 × 10<sup>-2</sup> – 0) = 3 × 10<sup>-2</sup> m s<sup>-1</sup>,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Velocity gradient</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{dv}}{\\mathrm{dy}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{∆v}{∆y}\\) = \\(\\frac{3\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-2}}{0.25\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}}\\)  = <strong>120 s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Shear stress</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\tau \\) = \\(\\frac{F}{A}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{-\\,50}{2.5\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-4}}\\)  = <strong>- 20 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{4}\\)<strong> N m</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>-  \\(\\frac{\\frac{F}{A}}{\\frac{\\mathrm{dv}}{\\mathrm{dy}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>-  \\(\\frac{(\\,-20\\,\\,\\times \\,{10}^{4}\\,)}{120}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.67 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>3</strong></sup><strong> Pa s</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,16,true),
(12,'calculations','No.7','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The shear stress at a point in a liquid is found to be 0.03 N m<sup>-2</sup>. The velocity gradient at the point is 0.15 s<sup>-1</sup>. What will be its viscosity (in poise)? (1 Pa s = 10 poise)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>shear stress,\\(\\tau \\) = \\(\\frac{F}{A}\\) = - 0.03 N m<sup>-2</sup> </p><p>(opposite to the direction of the motion)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Velocity gradient, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{dv}}{\\mathrm{dy}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{∆v}{∆y}\\) = <strong>0.15 s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>- \\(\\frac{\\frac{F}{A}}{\\frac{\\mathrm{dv}}{\\mathrm{dy}}}\\)   = - \\(\\frac{(-0.03)}{0.15}\\)  = <strong>0.2 Pa s</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.2 Pa s \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{10\\,\\mathrm{poise}}{1\\,\\mathrm{Pa}\\,s}\\) = <strong>2 poise</strong> </p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,17,true),
(12,'calculations','No.8','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A square plate 0.1 m side moves parallel to second plate with a velocity of 0.1 m s<sup>-1</sup>, both plates being immersed in water. If the viscous force is 0.002 N and the coefficient of viscosity is 0.01 poise, what is the distance between the plates? (1 Pa s = 10 poise)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = 0.1 m \\(\\times \\) 0.1 m = 0.01 m<sup>2</sup>,</p><p>\\(∆\\)v = (0.1 – 0) = 0.1 m s<sup>-1</sup>,</p><p>F = - 0.002 N </p><p>(opposite to the direction of the motion)</p><p>\\(\\eta \\) = 0.01 poise </p><p>   = 0.01 poise \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{1\\,\\mathrm{Pa}\\,s}{10\\,\\mathrm{poise}}\\) = 0.001 Pa s</p><p>\\(∆\\)y = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Velocity gradient</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{dv}}{\\mathrm{dy}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{∆v}{∆y}\\) = \\(\\frac{0.1}{∆y}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Shear stress, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{F}{A}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{-\\,0.002}{0.01}\\) = - 0.2 N m<sup>-2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>-  \\(\\frac{\\frac{F}{A}}{\\frac{\\mathrm{dv}}{\\mathrm{dy}}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{dv}}{\\mathrm{dy}}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>-  \\(\\frac{F}{A}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>0.001 \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{0.1}{∆y}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>- (- 0.2)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p> \\(\\frac{0.001\\times 0.1}{∆y}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> 0.2</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{∆y}{0.001\\times 0.1\\,}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{0.2}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)y</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{0.001\\times 0.1}{0.2}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>5</strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong>10</strong><sup><strong>-4</strong></sup><strong> m (or) 0.5 mm</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,18,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.10','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Determine the radius of a rain drop falling through air with terminal velocity 9 m s<sup>-1</sup>. Viscosity of air is 1.8×10<sup>-5</sup> Pa s, density of water is 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>, density of air is            1.21 kg m<sup>-3</sup>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v = 9 m s<sup>-1</sup>,&emsp;\\(\\eta \\) = 1.8 × 10<sup>-5</sup> Pa s, r = ?  </p><p>\\({\\rho }_{1}\\) = 1000 kg m<sup>-</sup><sup>3</sup>,   \\({\\rho }_{2}\\)= 1.21 kg m<sup>-3</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\,\\,g\\,{r}^{2}\\,({\\rho }_{1}\\,-\\,{\\rho }_{2})}{9\\,v}\\,\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>9 v \\(\\eta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(2\\,\\,g\\,{r}^{2}\\,({\\rho }_{1}\\,-\\,{\\rho }_{2})\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>r<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{9\\,v\\,\\eta }{2\\,g\\,({\\rho }_{1}\\,-\\,{\\rho }_{2})}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>r</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{9\\,v\\,\\eta }{2\\,g\\,({\\rho }_{1}\\,-\\,{\\rho }_{2})}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>r</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{9\\,\\times 9\\,\\times 1.8\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-5}}{2\\,\\times 9.8\\,(1000-1.21)}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>2.729 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{-4}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,19,true),
(12,'calculations','No.9','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Assume that a spherical object is flowing through water. Viscosity of water is 0.001 Pa s, radius of spherical object is 2 mm and the velocity of the object at particular instant is 2 m s<sup>-1</sup>. Find the drag force on the object due to the fluid. Assume that Stokes’ law is valid.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\eta \\) = 0.001 Pa s,&emsp;r = 2 mm = 2\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m,&emsp;</p><p>v = 2 m s<sup>-1</sup>,&emsp;Drag force, F = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>6 π η r v</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>6 \\(\\times \\) 3.142 \\(\\times \\) 0.001 \\(\\times \\) 2 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\times \\) 2</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>7.54 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-5}\\)<strong> N</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,20,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.11','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A horizontal circular loop of wire has a diameter of 5 cm and is lowered in a sample of crude oil. The additional force required to pull the loop out of the oil is 0.04 N; calculate the surface tension of the crude oil. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>d = 5 cm, r = \\(\\frac{5}{2}\\) = 2.5 cm = 2.5 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\) m</p><p>F = 0.04 N, surface tension,  \\(\\gamma \\) = ? </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Circumference of the loop,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>l</em></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\pi \\) r</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\times \\) 3.142 \\(\\times \\) 2.5 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.1571 m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Since the circular <strong>loop</strong> has <strong>two rims</strong> in contact with the liquid surface.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>γ   </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{F}{2\\,l}\\)   = \\(\\frac{0.04}{2\\,\\times \\,0.1571}\\)   = <strong>0.127 N m</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,21,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.12','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.12</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Calculate the force required to pull a flat circular plate of radius 15 cm from the surface of a liquid which has a surface tension of 0.053 N m<sup>-1</sup>. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 15 cm = 15 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\) m</p><p>surface tension, \\(\\gamma \\) = 0.053 N m<sup>-1</sup>, F = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Circumference of the loop,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>l</em></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\pi \\) r</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\times \\) 3.142 \\(\\times \\) 15 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>94.26 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Since the circular <strong>plate</strong> has <strong>only one rim</strong> in contact with the liquid surface,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>γ   </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{F}{l}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>γ <em>l</em> = 0.053 \\(\\times \\) 94.26 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.0499 N</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,22,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.13','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.13</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A needle has a length of 3.2 cm. When placed gently on the surface of the water in a glass, this needle will float if it is not too heavy. What is the weight of the heaviest needle? Assume that the surface tension of water is 0.073 N m<sup>-1</sup>. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><em>l</em> = 3.2 cm = 3.2 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\) m</p><p>surface tension, \\(\\gamma \\) = 0.073 N m<sup>-1</sup>, w = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Since the <strong>needle</strong> has <strong>two edges</strong> in contact with the liquid surface, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>γ   </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{F}{2\\,l}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>γ 2 <em>l</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>F</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.073 \\(\\times \\) 2 \\(\\times \\) 3.2 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>4.672 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)<strong> N</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>This force is the weight of the heaviest needle.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,23,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.14','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.14</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A soap film is formed on a <strong>rectangular frame of length</strong> 7 cm side dipping into soap solution. The frame hangs from the arm of a balance. An extra weight of 0.4 g is to be placed in the opposite pan to balance the pull on the frame. Calculate the surface tension of soap solution.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><em>l</em> = 7 cm = 7 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-2}\\) m, \\(\\gamma \\) = ?          </p><p>m = 0.4 g = 0.4 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-3</sup> kg, g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup></p><p>F = w </p><p>   = mg</p><p>   = 0.4 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-3</sup> \\(\\times \\) 9.8 = <strong>0.00392 N</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Since the <strong>rectangular frame</strong> has <strong>two edges</strong><strong> </strong>in contact with the soap solution,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>γ   </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{F}{2\\,l}\\) = \\(\\frac{0.00392\\,}{2\\,\\times \\,7\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-2}}\\) = <strong>0.028 N m</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,24,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.14','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.14</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; When a capillary tube stands upright in a beaker of water, the water rises <em>h</em> in the tube. If the radius of the tube is 2 mm, contact angle is 30°, density of water is 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup> and surface tension is 0.072 N m<sup>-1</sup>, calculate <em>h</em>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 2 mm = 2 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m, \\(\\gamma \\) = 0.072 N m<sup>-1</sup>          g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup></p><p>\\(\\theta \\) = 30\\(^\\circ \\) , \\(\\rho \\) = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>, h = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>h</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\,\\gamma \\cos \\theta }{\\rho \\,g\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\,\\times \\,0.072\\,\\times \\,\\cos 30^\\circ }{1000\\,\\times \\,9.8\\,\\times \\,2\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}\\,}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.0064 m (or) 0.64 cm</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,25,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.15','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.15</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; At a certain temperature, water has a surface tension of 0.072 N m<sup>-1</sup>. In a 3 mm diameter vertical tube if the liquid rises 6 mm above the liquid outside the tube, calculate the contact angle. Assume density of water ρ = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>d = 3 mm = 3 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m,</p><p>r = \\(\\frac{d}{2}\\) = \\(\\frac{3\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}}{2}\\) = 1.5 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m</p><p>\\(\\gamma \\) = 0.072 N m<sup>-1</sup>, g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup></p><p>\\(\\theta \\) = ?, \\(\\rho \\) = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>, </p><p>h = 6 mm = 6 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-3}\\) m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>h</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\,\\gamma \\cos \\theta }{\\rho \\,g\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\cos \\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\rho \\,g\\,r\\,h}{2\\,\\gamma }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>cos <sup>-1</sup> \\(\\left[\\frac{\\rho \\,g\\,r\\,h}{2\\,\\gamma }\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>cos <sup>-1</sup>\\(\\left[\\frac{1000\\times 9.8\\times 1.5\\times {10}^{-3}\\times 6\\times {10}^{-3}}{2\\,\\times \\,0.072\\,}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>52.23</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)<strong> (or) 52</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)<strong> 13</strong>\\(''\\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,26,true),
(12,'calculations','No.15','3','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.15</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Calculate the height to which water will rise in a capillary tube of diameter 1 mm. The surface tension of water is 0.072 N m<sup>-1</sup>, density of water is 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>. (Assume angle of contact is 0°.)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>d = 1 mm = 1 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-3}\\) m,</p><p>r = \\(\\frac{d}{2}\\) = \\(\\frac{1\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}}{2}\\) = 0.5 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m</p><p>\\(\\gamma \\) = 0.072 N m<sup>-1</sup>, g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup></p><p>\\(\\theta \\) = 0°, \\(\\rho \\) = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>, h = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>h</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\,\\gamma \\cos \\theta }{\\rho \\,g\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\,\\times \\,0.072\\,\\times \\,\\cos 0^\\circ }{1000\\,\\times \\,9.8\\,\\times \\,0.5\\,\\times {10}^{-3}\\,}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.0294 m (or) 2.94 cm</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp;</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,27,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','4','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; At present day, the rate of formation of fossil fuels (coal, petroleum, natural gas) is estimated to be about 4 billion kW (4 × l0<sup>9</sup> kW) and the world&#x27;s consumption of energy is of the order of 10<sup>17</sup> Btu/year. Show that the rate of consumption of fossil fuel is of the same order of magnitude as the rate of their formation and these energy sources are therefore non-renewable.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td><p>1 Btu = 1055 J </p><p>1 year = 365 \\(\\times \\) 24 \\(\\times \\) 3600 = 3.15 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>7</sup> s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>The rate of formation of fossil fuel</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&emsp;= 4 billion kW = 4 × l0<sup>9</sup> × l0<sup>3 </sup>W</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&emsp;= <strong>4 </strong><strong>×</strong><strong> l0</strong><sup><strong>12</strong></sup><strong> J s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>The world&#x27;s consumption of energy</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&emsp;= 10<sup>17</sup> Btu/year = \\(\\frac{{10}^{17}\\,\\mathrm{Btu}}{1\\,\\mathrm{year}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&emsp;= \\(\\frac{{10}^{17}\\,\\times \\,1055\\,J}{1\\,\\times 3.15\\,\\times \\,{10}^{7}\\,s}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&emsp;= <strong>3.35 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>12</strong></sup><strong> J s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Hence, the rate of consumption of fossil fuel is of the same order of magnitude as the rate of their formation and these energy sources are therefore non-renewable.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','4','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A home requires 62 kWh of heat on winter day to maintain a constant indoor temperature of 20\\(℃\\). Assume that the temperature of hot water outlet is 60\\(℃\\). (i) How much collector surface area does it need for a solar heating system that has a 20\\(\\%\\) efficiency? (ii) How large does the storage tank have to be to provide this much energy? (The average solar radiation <strong>per day</strong> in winter is about 6.5 kWh m<sup>-2</sup>)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>\\({∆Q}_{\\mathrm{req}}\\)= 62 kWh, \\({∆Q}_{\\mathrm{input}}\\) = 6.5 kWh m<sup>-2</sup></p><p>\\(\\eta \\) = 20\\(\\%\\) = 0.2</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\,\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{{∆Q}_{\\mathrm{output}}}{{∆Q}_{\\mathrm{input}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({∆Q}_{\\mathrm{output}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({∆Q}_{\\mathrm{input}}\\) \\(\\times \\) \\(\\eta \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>6.5 kWh m<sup>-2 </sup>\\(\\times \\) 0.2</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><strong>1.3 k </strong><strong>Wh</strong><strong> m</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Collector surface area</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{∆Q}_{\\mathrm{req}}}{{∆Q}_{\\mathrm{output}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{62\\,\\mathrm{kWh}}{1.3\\,k\\,\\mathrm{Wh}\\,{m}^{-2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>47.69 </strong>\\(\\approx \\)<strong> </strong><strong>48 m</strong><sup><strong>2</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>1 k Wh </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>3.6 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>6</sup> J</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({∆Q}_{\\mathrm{req}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>62 kWh = 62\\(\\times \\) 3.6 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>6</sup> J</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)T</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>60 – 20 = 40\\(℃\\) = 40 K</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>c = 4184 J kg<sup>-1</sup> K<sup>-1</sup> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({∆Q}_{\\mathrm{req}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>m c \\(∆\\)T</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>m</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{{∆Q}_{\\mathrm{req}}}{c\\,∆T}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{62\\,\\times \\,3.6\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{6}}{4184\\,\\times 40}\\) = <strong>1333.6 kg</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Volume of storage tank should be <strong>1334 </strong><strong>L</strong>.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.4','4','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The band gap of GaAs is 1.4 eV. Calculate the minimum wavelength of light for photovoltaic generation in a GaAs solar cell.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>E = 1.4 eV = 1.4 \\(\\times \\) 1.6 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-19</sup> J, \\(\\lambda \\) = ?</p><p>h = 6.626 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-34</sup> J s, c = 3 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>8</sup> m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>E</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{h\\,c}{\\lambda }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\lambda \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{h\\,c}{E}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6.626\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{-34}\\,\\times \\,3\\,\\times \\,{10}^{8}}{1.4\\,\\times \\,1.6\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-19}\\,\\,}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>8.87 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-7</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>887 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>-9</strong></sup><strong> m (or) 887 nm</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.5','4','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A 100 ft \\(\\times \\) 50 ft building has a flat roof. What is the average solar energy received by the roof in a month? (The solar radiation <strong>per day</strong> in winter is about 1600 Btu ft<sup>-2</sup>)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td><p>A = 100 ft \\(\\times \\) 50 ft = 5000 ft<sup>2 </sup></p><p>t = 1 month = 30 days</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Solar radiation per day = 1600 Btu ft<sup>-2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Energy received by roof in month</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>= 1600 Btu ft<sup>-2</sup> \\(\\times \\) 5000 ft<sup>2</sup> \\(\\times \\) 30</p><p>= 240 000 000 = <strong>24 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>7</strong></sup><strong> Btu</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.6','4','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Calculate the solar energy received by a standard hot water collector of dimensions  1 m \\(\\times \\) 2 m, over one hour at around noon, it the irradiance stays fairly constant at about 800 W m<sup>-2</sup>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td><p>A = 1 m \\(\\times \\) 2 m = 2 m<sup>2</sup>, t = 1 h = 3600 s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Solar radiation = 800 W m<sup>-2</sup> = 800 J s<sup>-1</sup> m<sup>-2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Solar energy received by 2 m<sup>2</sup> in 1 h </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>= 800 J s<sup>-1</sup> m<sup>-2 </sup>\\(\\times \\)<sup> </sup>3600 s \\(\\times \\) 2 m<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>= <strong>5.76 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>6</strong></sup><strong> J</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','4','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Determine the input power of the wind if the wind speed is 20 m s<sup>-1</sup> and blade length is 20 m. Density of air is 1.3 kg m<sup>-3</sup>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v = 20 m s<sup>-1</sup>,\\(\\rho \\) = 1.3 kg m<sup>-</sup><sup>3</sup>,r = 20 m,P = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = \\(\\pi \\) r<sup>2</sup> = 3.142 \\(\\times \\) 20<sup>2</sup> m<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) A v<sup>3</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\times \\) 1.3 \\(\\times \\) 3.142 \\(\\times \\) 20<sup>2</sup> \\(\\times \\) 20<sup>3</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>6.535 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>6</sup> W = <strong>6.535 MW</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'calculations','No.12','4','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.12</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The wind is blowing at 10 m s<sup>-1</sup>, how much total power produced by the wind turbine if the blades are 45 m long? Density of air is 1.3 kg m<sup>-3</sup>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v = 10 m s<sup>-1</sup>, \\(\\rho \\) = 1.3 kg m<sup>-3</sup></p><p>r = 45 m, &emsp;P = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = \\(\\pi \\) r<sup>2</sup> = 3.142 \\(\\times \\) 45<sup>2</sup> m<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) A v<sup>3</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\times \\) 1.3 \\(\\times \\) 3.142 \\(\\times \\) 45<sup>2</sup>  \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>3</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>4.136 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>6</sup> W = <strong>4.136 MW</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.4','4','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; At a hydroelectric power plant, the water pressure head is at a height of 300 m and the water flow available is 100 m<sup>3</sup> s<sup>-1</sup>. If the turbine generator efficiency is 60\\(\\%\\), estimate the electric power available from the plant. (g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup>, \\(\\rho \\) = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>h = 300 m, \\(\\overset{̇}{V}\\) = 100 m<sup>3</sup> s<sup>-1</sup>, \\(\\eta \\) = 60\\(\\%\\) = 0.6 </p><p>g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup>, \\(\\rho \\) = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>, P = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) \\(\\rho \\) \\(\\overset{̇}{V}\\) g h</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.6 \\(\\times \\) 1000 \\(\\times \\) 100 \\(\\times \\) 9.8 \\(\\times \\) 300</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>176.4 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>6</sup> W = <strong>176.4 MW</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','No.10','4','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An important hydroelectric plant has a head of 100 m and water volumetric flow rate of 10 000 m<sup>3</sup> s<sup>-1</sup>. The turbine generator efficiency is 60\\(\\%\\). What is the maximum power that the plant can produce? (Density of water = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>h = 100 m, \\(\\overset{̇}{V}\\) = 10 000 m<sup>3</sup> s<sup>-1</sup>,</p><p>\\(\\eta \\) = 60\\(\\%\\) = 0.6, g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup>, </p><p>\\(\\rho \\) = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>, P = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) \\(\\rho \\) \\(\\overset{̇}{V}\\) g h</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.6 \\(\\times \\) 1000 \\(\\times \\) 10 000 \\(\\times \\) 9.8 \\(\\times \\) 100</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>5880 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>6</sup> W = <strong>5880 MW</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','No.11','4','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A dam which maximum head of 200 m produces to 2000 MW electrical power. What is the rate of falling water on the turbines? The turbine generator efficiency is 50\\(\\%\\). (Density of water = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup>).</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>h = 200 m, \\(\\overset{̇}{V}\\) = ?, \\(\\eta \\) = 50\\(\\%\\) = 0.5</p><p>g = 9.8 m s<sup>-2</sup>, \\(\\rho \\) = 1000 kg m<sup>-3</sup></p><p>P = 2000 MW = 2000\\(\\times \\) 10<sup>6 </sup>W</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) \\(\\rho \\) \\(\\overset{̇}{V}\\) g h</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\overset{̇}{V}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{P}{\\eta \\,\\rho \\,g\\,h}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2000\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{6}\\,}{0.5\\,\\times 1000\\,\\times \\,9.8\\,\\times \\,200}\\) = <strong>2040 m</strong><sup><strong>3</strong></sup><strong> s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.8','4','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The hydro turbine receives water from a reservoir at an elevation of 100 m above it. What is the minimum water flow in kg s<sup>-1</sup> to produce a steady turbine output of 50 MW if the turbine generator efficiency is 75 \\(\\%\\)?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>h = 100 m, \\(\\eta \\) = 75\\(\\%\\) = 0.75</p><p>P = 50 MW = 50 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>6 </sup>W</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) \\(\\rho \\) \\(\\overset{̇}{V}\\) g h</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) \\(\\rho \\) \\(\\frac{V}{t}\\) g h</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) \\(\\frac{m}{t}\\) g h&emsp;&emsp;(\\(\\because \\) m = \\(\\rho \\) V)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{P}{\\eta \\,g\\,h}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{50\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{6}\\,}{0.75\\,\\times \\,9.8\\,\\times \\,100}\\) = <strong>68027 kg s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,11,true);
INSERT INTO educational_content (grade,category,title,chapter,content,sort_order,active) VALUES
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A person walking at a regular speed generations heat at the rate of 0.07 W. If the surface area of the body is 1.5 m<sup>2</sup> and heat is to be generated 0.03 m below the skin, what should be the temperature difference between the skin and interior of the body if the heat is to be conducted to the surface of the skin? (\\(k\\) = 5 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-5</sup> W m<sup>-1</sup> K<sup>-1</sup>)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>H = 0.07 W, A = 1.5 m<sup>2</sup>, <em>l</em> = 0.03 m</p><p>T<sub>2</sub> – T<sub>1</sub> = ?, \\(k\\) = 5 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-5</sup> W m<sup>-1</sup> K<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By rate of heat conduction,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>cond</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(k\\)<em> A</em> \\(\\frac{{T}_{2}\\,-\\,{T}_{1}}{l}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>T<sub>2</sub> – T<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{H}_{\\mathrm{cond}\\,}l}{k\\,A}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{0.07\\times 0.03\\,}{5\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{-5}\\,\\times 1.5}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>28 K (or) 28 </strong>\\(℃\\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','No.9','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The area and thickness of a glass plate of a window are 0.25 m<sup>2</sup> and 4 mm respectively. The temperature of inside surface of glass plate is 25 \\(℃\\) and its outside temperature is 26\\(℃\\). Find the amount of heat that passes through the glass plate in one hour. The thermal conductivity of glass is 0.78 W m<sup>-1</sup> K<sup>-1</sup>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = 0.25 m<sup>2</sup>, <em>l</em> = 4 mm = 4 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-3</sup> m</p><p>T<sub>2</sub> = 26 \\(℃\\) = 26 + 273 = 299 K</p><p>T<sub>1</sub> = 25 \\(℃\\) = 25 + 273 = 298 K</p><p>\\(k\\) = 0.78 W m<sup>-1</sup> K<sup>-1</sup>, \\(∆\\)Q = ? </p><p>t = 1 h = 3600 s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By rate of heat conduction,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>cond</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(k\\)<em> A</em> \\(\\frac{{T}_{2}\\,-\\,{T}_{1}}{l}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>cond</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{∆Q}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{∆Q}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(k\\)<em> A</em> \\(\\frac{{T}_{2}\\,-\\,{T}_{1}}{l}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)Q</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(k\\)<em> A</em> \\(\\frac{{T}_{2}\\,-\\,{T}_{1}}{l}\\) t</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.78 \\(\\times \\) 0.25 \\(\\frac{(299\\,-\\,298\\,)}{4\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{-3}}\\) \\(\\times \\) 3600</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>175 500 J</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','No.10','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; How much <strong>heat per second</strong> is conducted through a wooden wall of area 25 m<sup>2</sup> and thickness 0.04 m if the temperature inside is 20 \\(℃\\) and the temperature outside is -10 \\(℃\\) ? The thermal conductivity of wood is 8.37 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-2</sup> W m<sup>-1</sup> K<sup>-1</sup>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = 25 m<sup>2</sup>,<em> </em><em>l</em> = 0.04 m</p><p>T<sub>2</sub> = 20 \\(℃\\) = 20 + 273 = 293 K,</p><p>T<sub>1</sub> = - 10 \\(℃\\) = - 10 + 273 = 263 K </p><p>\\(k\\) = 8.37 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-2</sup> W m<sup>-1</sup> K<sup>-1</sup>, H = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By rate of heat conduction,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>cond</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(k\\)<em> A</em> \\(\\frac{{T}_{2}\\,-\\,{T}_{1}}{l}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>8.37 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-2</sup> \\(\\times \\) 25 \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{(293\\,-\\,263)\\,}{0.04}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1569.38 W</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1569.38 J s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A new computer chip with a surface area of 1 cm<sup>2</sup> <strong>generate</strong> 10 W of heat. Determine the <strong>convective heat transfer coefficient</strong> of the material needed to keep the temperature of the chip <strong>less than 20 </strong>\\(℃\\) above the environmental temperature. <strong>Can</strong> the chip be cooled with air, or will it require forced convection? Convective heat transfer coefficient of air is 2.5 to 25 W m<sup>-2</sup> K<sup>-1</sup>. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = 1 cm<sup>2</sup> = 1 (10<sup>-2</sup> m)<sup>2</sup> = 1 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-4</sup> m<sup>2</sup>,</p><p>H = -10 W (generate)</p><p>T<sub>2</sub> – T<sub>1</sub> = - 20 \\(℃\\) = - 20 K (T<sub>1</sub> &gt; T<sub>2</sub>)</p><p>q = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By rate of heat convection,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>conv</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>q A (T<sub>2</sub> – T<sub>1</sub>)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>q</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{H}_{\\mathrm{conv}}}{A\\,({T}_{2}-\\,{T}_{1})}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{-\\,10}{1\\,\\times 1{0}^{-4}\\,(-20)}\\,\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>5000 </strong><strong>W m</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup><strong> K</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Since convective heat transfer coefficient of air is very much less than 5000 W m<sup>-2</sup> K<sup>-1</sup>, the chip cannot be cooled with air. Therefore, it will require the forced convection. </p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; In a room, the temperature of water in a kettle is 80 \\(℃\\). The room temperature is    30 \\(℃\\) and the surface area of the kittle is 0.02 m<sup>2</sup>. If the emissivity is 0.9. Find the rate of heat loss due to radiation. (\\(\\sigma \\) = 5.685 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-8</sup> W m<sup>-2</sup> K<sup>-4</sup>)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>T<sub>2</sub> = 80 \\(℃\\) = 80 + 273 = 353 K</p><p>T<sub>1</sub> = 30 \\(℃\\) = 30 + 273 = 303 K</p><p>A = 0.02 m<sup>2</sup>, e = 0.9</p><p>H = ?&emsp;\\(\\sigma \\) = 5.685 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-8</sup> W m<sup>-2</sup> K<sup>-4</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By rate of heat radiation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>rad</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>A T<sup>4</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>out</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>A \\({T}_{2}^{4}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>in</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>A \\({T}_{1}^{4}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>lost</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>H<sub>out</sub> - H<sub>in</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>A \\({T}_{2}^{4}\\) - e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>A \\({T}_{1}^{4}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>A (\\({T}_{2}^{4}\\) - \\({T}_{1}^{4}\\))</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.9\\(\\times \\)5.685\\(\\times \\)10<sup>-8</sup>\\(\\times \\)0.02(\\({353}^{4}\\) - \\({303}^{4}\\))</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>7.26 W</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'calculations','No.11','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The filament of a 100 W electric bulb is made of tungsten. The emissivity of tungsten is 0.3 and its length is 0.2 m. Find the diameter of the filament, if its temperature is 3000 K when the bulb is switched on. (\\(\\sigma \\) = 5.685 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-8</sup> W m<sup>-2</sup> K<sup>-4</sup>)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>H = 100 W, e = 0.3, <em>l</em> = 0.2 m, T = 3000 K,</p><p>d = ?, \\(\\sigma \\) = 5.685 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-8</sup> W m<sup>-2</sup> K<sup>-4</sup></p><p>Area of filament, A = 2 \\(\\pi \\) r <em>l</em> = \\(\\pi \\) 2r <em>l</em> = \\(\\pi \\) d <em>l</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By rate of heat radiation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>rad</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>A T<sup>4</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>rad</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>\\(\\pi \\) d <em>l</em> T<sup>4</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{H}_{\\mathrm{rad}}}{e\\,\\sigma \\,\\pi \\,l\\,{T}^{4}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{100}{0.3\\,\\times \\,5.685\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{-8}\\,\\times \\,3.142\\,\\times \\,0.2\\,\\times \\,{3000}^{4}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.000115 = <strong>1.153 </strong>\\(\\times \\,1{0}^{-4}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'calculations','No.12','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.12</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The temperature of the filament is 2500 K when the bulb is switched on. The diameter of the filament is 0.1 mm and it is made of metal of emissivity 0.35. If the power is    40 W, find the length of the filament. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>T = 2500 K, d = 0.1 mm = 0.1 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-3</sup> m</p><p>e = 0.35, H = 40 W, <em>l</em> = ?</p><p>\\(\\sigma \\) = 5.685 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-8</sup> W m<sup>-2</sup> K<sup>-4</sup></p><p>Area of filament, A = \\(\\pi \\) d <em>l</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By rate of heat radiation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>rad</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>A T<sup>4</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>rad</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>\\(\\pi \\) d <em>l</em> T<sup>4</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>l</em></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{H}_{\\mathrm{rad}}}{e\\,\\sigma \\,\\pi \\,d\\,{T}^{4}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>= \\(\\frac{40}{0.35\\,\\times \\,5.685\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{-8}\\,\\times \\,3.142\\,\\times \\,0.1\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}\\,\\times \\,{2500}^{4}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>l</em></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.1638 m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'calculations','No.14','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.14</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; If the rate of energy radiation from a blackbody of area 100 cm<sup>2</sup> is 42 W, find the temperature of that blackbody.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = 100 cm<sup>2</sup> = 100 (10<sup>-2</sup> m)<sup>2</sup> </p><p>                     = 100 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-4</sup> m<sup>2</sup>,</p><p>H = 42 W, T = ?, e = 1 (for black body)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By rate of heat radiation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>rad</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>A T<sup>4</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>T<sup>4</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{H}_{\\mathrm{rad}}}{e\\,\\sigma \\,A}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>T</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{{H}_{\\mathrm{rad}}}{e\\,\\sigma \\,A}}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>T</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{42}{1\\,\\times \\,5.685\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{-8}\\,\\times \\,100\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-4}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>T</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>521.35 K</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','No.15','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.15</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Compare the rates of energy radiation of a blackbody at temperatures 327 \\(℃\\) and at 27 \\(℃\\).</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>T<sub>2</sub> = 327 \\(℃\\) = 327 + 273 = 600 K,</p><p>T<sub>1</sub> = 27 \\(℃\\) = 27 + 273 = 300 K</p><p>e = 1 (for black body) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By rate of heat radiation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>rad</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>A T<sup>4</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>A \\({T}_{2}^{4}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>e \\(\\sigma \\)<strong> </strong>A \\({T}_{1}^{4}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{H}_{2}}{{H}_{1}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\,e\\,\\sigma \\,A\\,{T}_{2}^{4}}{\\,e\\,\\sigma \\,A\\,{T}_{1}^{4}}\\) = \\(\\frac{\\,\\,{T}_{2}^{4}}{\\,\\,{T}_{1}^{4}}\\)  = (\\(\\frac{{T}_{2}}{{T}_{1}}\\))<sup>4</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\frac{600}{300}}^{4}\\) = 2<sup>4</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{H}_{2}}{{H}_{1}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>16</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>16 H</strong><sub><strong>1</strong></sub></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','No.13','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.13</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; From calculations based on the radiation measurement of solar energy falling on the earth it is found that sun is radiating energy at a rate of 62.5 M W m<sup>-2</sup>. Assuming that the sun is emitting energy as a blackbody, find the temperature of the surface of the sun.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({\\epsilon }_{0}\\) = 62.5 M W m<sup>-2</sup> = 62.5 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>6</sup> W m<sup>-2</sup>,</p><p>\\(\\sigma \\) = 5.685 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-8</sup> W m<sup>-2</sup> K<sup>-4</sup><sub>,</sub>&emsp;T = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Stefan-Boltzmann’s law,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({\\epsilon }_{0}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sigma \\) T<sup>4</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>T<sup>4</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{\\epsilon }_{0}}{\\sigma }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>T</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{{\\epsilon }_{0}}{\\sigma }}\\)  = \\(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{62.5\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{6}}{5.685\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{-8}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>T</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>5758 K</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','No.18','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.18</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An insulated system <strong>takes in</strong> 6.5 kcal of heat and has 2000 J of work done <strong>on it</strong>. What is the change in internal energy of the system? (1 kcal = 4184 J)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Q = + 6.5 kcal&emsp;(takes in)</p><p>    = + 6.5 \\(\\times \\) 4184 J = + 27196 J</p><p>W = - 2000 J (work done on the system)</p><p>\\(∆\\)U = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>According to first law of thermodynamics, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)U</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>Q - W</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>27196 - (- 2000)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>+ 29196 J = <strong>+ 2.92 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>4</strong></sup><strong> J</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,11,true),
(12,'calculations','No.19','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.19</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A heat engine undergoes a process in which its internal energy <strong>increases</strong> by 275 J while <strong>it is doing</strong> 360 J of work. How much heat is taken in (or given out) by the engine during this process? </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(∆\\)U = + 275 J (increases),</p><p>W = + 360 J (work done by the system)&emsp;</p><p>Q = ? </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>According to first law of thermodynamics, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)U</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>Q - W</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Q</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)U + W</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>275 + 360</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>+ 635 J </strong>(heat is taken in)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,12,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.4','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Find the change in internal energy of one mole of an ideal gas when its temperature change from 0\\(℃\\) to 100\\(℃\\).</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(∆\\)U = ?, n = 1 mole,</p><p>\\(∆\\)T = 100 – 0 = 100\\(℃\\) = 100 K,&emsp;</p><p>R = 8.3143 J mol<sup>-1</sup> K<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Change in internal energy</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)U</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{3}{2}\\) n R \\(∆\\)T</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{3}{2}\\) × 1 × 8.3143 × 100 </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1247.145 = <strong>+ 1.247 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>3</strong></sup><strong> J</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,13,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.6','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; In an isobaric pressure, a volume of a gas is expressed by absorption of heat constant pressure 2 atm. If the increment in volume is 0.5 m<sup>3</sup>, then find the work done by system.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>p = 2 atm = 2 \\(\\times \\) 1.013 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>5</sup> Pa,&emsp;</p><p>V<sub>f</sub> – V<sub>i</sub> = 0.5 m<sup>3</sup>, W = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For isobaric process,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>p (V<sub>f</sub> – V<sub>i</sub>)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 × 1.013 × 10<sup>5</sup> × 0.5</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>+ </strong><strong>1.013 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>5</strong></sup><strong> J</strong> (by the system)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,14,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.5','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; One gram of water (1 cm<sup>3</sup>) becomes 1671 cm<sup>3</sup> of steam when boiled at a pressure of   1 atm. The heat of vaporization at this pressure is 2265 J g<sup>-1</sup>. Compute the work done and the increase in internal energy.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>m = 1 g, p = 1 atm = 1.013 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>5</sup> Pa</p><p>L<sub>v</sub> = 2265 J g<sup>-1</sup></p><p>V<sub>i</sub> = 1 cm<sup>3</sup>,&emsp;V<sub>f</sub> = 1671 cm<sup>3</sup> </p><p>V<sub>f</sub> - V<sub>i</sub> = 1671 – 1 </p><p>&emsp;= 1670 cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>&emsp;= 1670 \\(\\times ({10}^{-2}\\,m{)}^{3}\\) </p><p>&emsp;= 1670 \\(\\times {10}^{-6}\\) m<sup>3</sup></p><p>W = ?,&emsp;&emsp;\\(∆\\)U = ? </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For isobaric process,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>p (V<sub>f</sub> – V<sub>i</sub>)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1.013 × 10<sup>5</sup> × 1670 ×\\({10}^{-6}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>+ 169.171 J</strong> (by the system)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Q</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>m L<sub>v</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1 × 2265 = <strong>+ 2265 J</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>According to first law of thermodynamics, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)U</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>Q - W</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2265 – 169.171</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>+ 2095.829 J</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,15,true),
(12,'calculations','No.21','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.21</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; In an isothermal process (27\\(℃\\)), 2 kilomole of an ideal gas is compressed from a volume of 4 litre to 1 litre. Find the work done on the system. (R = 8.3143 J mol<sup>-1</sup> K<sup>-1</sup>)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>T = 27\\(℃\\) = 27 + 273 = 300 K,</p><p>n = 2 kmol = 2 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>3</sup> mol</p><p>V<sub>i</sub> = 4 L = 4 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m<sup>3</sup></p><p>V<sub>f</sub> = 1 L = 1 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m<sup>3</sup></p><p>R = 8.3143 J mol<sup>-1</sup> K<sup>-1</sup>,&emsp;W = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For isothermal process, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>n R T ln \\(\\frac{{V}_{f}}{{V}_{i}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>3</sup> \\(\\times \\) 8.3143 \\(\\times \\) 300 \\(\\times \\) ln (\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\))</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>- 6915 640.32 J</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Since W is negative, work is done on the system.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,16,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.7','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An engine takes in 9220 J and does 1750 J of work each cycle while operating between 689\\(℃\\) and 397\\(℃\\). (a) What is its actual efficiency? (b) What is its maximum theoretical efficiency?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Q<sub>H</sub> = 9220 J, W = 1750 J</p><p>T<sub>H</sub> = 689\\(℃\\) = 689 + 273 = 962 K,</p><p>T<sub>C</sub> = 397\\(℃\\) = 397 + 273 = 670 K</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(a)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{W}{{Q}_{H}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1750}{9220}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> 0.19 = <strong>19 </strong>\\(\\%\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(b)</p></td><td><p>\\({\\eta }_{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1 - \\(\\frac{{T}_{C}}{{T}_{H}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1 - \\(\\frac{670}{962}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({\\eta }_{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> 0.304 = <strong>30.4 </strong>\\(\\%\\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,17,true),
(12,'calculations','No.22','5','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.22</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An automobile engine has an efficiency of 20\\(\\%\\) and produces an average of 23 000 J of mechanical work per second during operation. (i) How much <strong>heat input</strong> is required per second (ii) how much heat is discharged as <strong>waste</strong> <strong>heat</strong> from this engine per second?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\eta \\) = 20\\(\\%\\) = 0.2&emsp;W = 23 000 J</p><p>(i) Q<sub>H</sub> = ?&emsp;(ii) Q<sub>C</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\eta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{W}{{Q}_{H}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>0.2</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{23\\,000}{{Q}_{H}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({Q}_{H}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{23\\,000}{0.2\\,}\\) = <strong>115 000 J</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>Q<sub>H</sub> - Q<sub>C</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Q<sub>C</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>Q<sub>H</sub> - W</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>115 000 - 23 000</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>92 000 J</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,18,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; What is the speed of sound in (i) a steel rod (ii) water?</p><p>&emsp;Young’s modulus of steel is 20 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>10</sup> N m<sup>-2 </sup>and density of steel is 7.8 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>3</sup> kg m<sup>-3</sup>. </p><p>&emsp;The bulk modulus of water is 0.22 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>10</sup> N m<sup>-2</sup> and density of water is 10<sup>3</sup> kg m<sup>-3</sup>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Y = 20 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>10</sup> N m<sup>-2</sup>, \\(\\rho \\) = 7.8 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>3</sup> kg m<sup>-3</sup>  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The speed of sound in a steel rod,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{Y}{\\rho }}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{20\\,\\times \\,{10}^{10}}{7.8\\,\\times \\,{10}^{3}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>5.06 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>3</strong></sup><strong> m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup><strong> (or) 5063 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>B = 0.22 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>10</sup> N m<sup>-2</sup>, \\(\\rho \\) = 10<sup>3</sup> kg m<sup>-3</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The speed of sound in water,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{B}{\\rho }}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{0.22\\,\\times \\,{10}^{10}}{{10}^{3}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.48 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>3</strong></sup><strong> m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup><strong> (or) 1483 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','No.3','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The speed of sound in a particular liquid is 1.6 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>3 </sup>m s<sup>-1</sup>. If the bulk modulus of the liquid is 0.15 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>10</sup> N m<sup>-2</sup>, what is the density of the liquid?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>B = 0.15 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>10</sup> N m<sup>-2</sup>, </p><p>v = 1.6 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>3</sup> m s<sup>-1</sup>, \\(\\rho \\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The speed of sound in liquid,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{B}{\\rho }}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{B}{\\rho }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\rho \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{B}{{v}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{0.15\\,\\times \\,{10}^{10}}{{(1.6\\,\\times \\,{10}^{3})}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>585.94 kg m</strong><sup><strong>-3</strong></sup><strong>  </strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Calculate the velocity of sound in air at STP. The density of air at STP is 1.29 kg m<sup>-3</sup>. Assume air to be diatomic with \\(\\gamma \\) = 1.4. Also calculate the velocity of sound in air at       27 \\(℃\\).</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>At STP,&emsp;p = 1.01 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>5</sup> Pa, T = 273 K</p><p>&emsp;\\(\\rho \\) = 1.29 kg m<sup>-3</sup>,<em> </em>\\(\\gamma \\) = 1.4</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>The velocity of sound in air,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\,\\gamma \\,p}{\\rho }}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\,1.4\\,\\times 1.01\\,\\times \\,{10}^{5}}{1.29}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>331.077 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup><strong>&emsp;(at STP)</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>At STP</p></td><td><p>&emsp;&emsp;At 27\\(℃\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>T<sub>1</sub> = 273 K</p><p>v<sub>1</sub> = 331.07 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td><td><p>T<sub>2</sub> = 27+273 = 300 K</p><p>v<sub>2</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Since, v \\(\\propto \\) \\(\\sqrt{T}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\sqrt{T}\\) \\(\\times \\) constant</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{v}{\\sqrt{T}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>constant</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}_{2}}{\\sqrt{{T}_{2}}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{v}_{1}}{\\sqrt{{T}_{1}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}_{2}}{\\sqrt{300}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{331.07}{\\sqrt{273}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{331.07\\,\\times \\,\\sqrt{300}}{\\sqrt{273}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p> <strong>347.06 m s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; At a busy street corner, the intensity level of sound is 70 dB. What is intensity of sound in W m<sup>-2</sup>?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\beta \\) = 70 dB, I = ?, I<sub>0</sub> = 10<sup>-12</sup> W m<sup>-2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\beta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10 log<sub>10</sub> \\(\\frac{I}{{I}_{0}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>70</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10 log<sub>10</sub> \\(\\frac{I}{{10}^{-12}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>log<sub>10</sub> \\(\\frac{I}{{10}^{-12}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>log<sub>10</sub> \\(\\frac{I}{{10}^{-12}}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>7</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{I}{{10}^{-12}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10<sup>7</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10<sup>-12</sup> \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>7</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>10</strong><sup><strong>-5</strong></sup><strong> W m</strong><sup><strong>-2</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.4','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; What value of sound intensity in dB increases by a factor of 1000?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>I = 1000 I<sub>0 </sub>, \\(\\frac{I}{{I}_{0}}\\) = 1000,&emsp;\\(\\beta \\) = ? (dB)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\beta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10 log<sub>10</sub> \\(\\frac{I}{{I}_{0}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10 log<sub>10</sub> 1000</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\beta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10 \\(\\times \\) 3 = <strong>30 dB</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The sound level will increase 30 dB.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.2','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; If the intensity of sound is doubled, by how many decibels does the sound level increase?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p> <strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>I = 2 I<sub>0</sub> , \\(\\frac{I}{{I}_{0}}\\) = 2, &emsp;\\(\\beta \\) = ? (dB)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\beta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10 log<sub>10</sub> \\(\\frac{I}{{I}_{0}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10 log<sub>10</sub> 2</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\beta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10 \\(\\times \\) 0.3010 = <strong>3 dB</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The sound level will increase 3 dB.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'calculations','No.11','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A sonar echo returns to a submarine 1.2 s after being emitted. What is the distance to the object creating the echo? (Assume that the submarine is in the ocean, not in fresh water and the velocity of sound in water is 1500 m s<sup>-1</sup>.)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Echo time, t = 1.2 s, v = 1500 m s<sup>-1</sup>, d = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\,d}{t}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>2 d</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>v t</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{v\\,t}{2}\\) = \\(\\frac{1500\\,\\times 1.2}{2}\\) = <strong>900 m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true);
INSERT INTO educational_content (grade,category,title,chapter,content,sort_order,active) VALUES
(12,'calculations','Eg.5','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A bat flying at a speed of 20 m s<sup>-1</sup> towards a stationary moth emits sound wave of 340 m s<sup>-1</sup>. The bat hears the echoes 0.4 s later. </p><p>&emsp;(i)&emsp;Calculate the distance travelled by the&emsp;bat in 0.4 s. </p><p>&emsp;(ii)&emsp;Calculate the distance travelled by the &emsp;sound wave in 0.4 s. </p><p>&emsp;(iii)&emsp;Determine the initial distance between &emsp;the bat and the moth.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v<sub>b</sub> = 20 m s<sup>-1</sup>, v<sub>s</sub> = 340 m s<sup>-1</sup>, t = 0.4 s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>distance travelled by the bat, d<sub>b</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{d}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d<sub>b</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>v<sub>b</sub> t = 20 \\(\\times \\) 0.4 = <strong>8 m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>distance travelled by the sound, d<sub>s</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>v<sub>s</sub> t = 340 \\(\\times \\) 0.4 = <strong>136 m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Total distance = 8 + 136 = 144 m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>the initial distance between the bat and the moth = \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{total}\\,\\mathrm{distnace}}{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{144}{2}\\) = <strong>72 m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.3','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The sole survivor of a shipwreck swim to an island, which is 3000 m from a vertical cliff. He sees a ship anchored between the island and the cliff. A blast from the ship horn is heard twice with the time elapse of 4 s. Calculate distance between the ship and the survivor. (Speed of sound in air = 330 m s<sup>-1</sup>)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Distance between survivor and ship = d</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The distance between the survivor and cliff = 3000 m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The distance between the ship and cliff = 3000 - d</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v = 330 m s<sup>-1</sup>,&emsp;t<sub>2</sub> – t<sub>1</sub> = 4 s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{d}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{d}{v}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The time required for sound to reach from the ship to survivor, (For original sound)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>t<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{d}{v}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The time required for resound of ships horn to reach the survivor, (For echo)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>t<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{3000\\,+\\,(3000\\,-\\,d)}{v}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6000\\,-\\,d}{v}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>t<sub>2</sub> – t<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6000\\,-\\,d}{v}\\) - \\(\\frac{d}{v}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6000\\,-\\,2d}{v}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6000\\,-\\,2d}{330}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>6000 – 2d</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1320</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>- 2 d</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>- 4680</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>2340 m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.6','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A piezoelectric transducer produces ultrasound at a frequency of 10 MHz. Calculate the wavelength of this ultrasound in blood if the speed of ultrasound in blood is 1560 m s<sup>-1</sup>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>f = 10 MHz = 10 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>6</sup> Hz,</p><p>v = 1560 m s<sup>-1</sup>, \\(\\lambda \\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By wave equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>f \\(\\lambda \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\lambda \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{v}{f}\\)<sub> </sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1560}{10\\,\\times \\,{10}^{6}}\\)<sub> </sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.56  </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>-4</strong></sup><strong> m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','No.5','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; (i) Why the ultrasound is used in medical imaging rather than sound wave of audible frequencies or lower? </p><p>&emsp;(ii) The frequencies used in imaging are typically in the range of 1 to 15 MHz. What is the &emsp;range of wavelengths in human tissue where the velocity of sound is 1540 m s<sup>-1</sup>?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;(i) The ultrasound is used in medical imaging rather than sound wave of audible frequencies or lower. Because ultrasound have higher frequency and shorter wavelength. Shorter wavelengths are more easily reflected or refracted in the superficial tissues than longer wavelengths. Thus, medical imaging used ultrasound gives better resolution.</p><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>v = 1540 m s<sup>-1</sup>, \\(\\lambda \\) = ?</p><p>f<sub>1</sub><sub> </sub>= 1 MHz = 1 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{6}\\) Hz</p><p>f<sub>2</sub> = 15 MHz = 15 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{6}\\) Hz</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>By wave equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>f \\(\\lambda \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\lambda \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{v}{f}\\)<sub> </sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({\\lambda }_{1}\\) = \\(\\frac{v}{{f}_{1}}\\) </p></td><td><p>\\({\\lambda }_{2}\\) = \\(\\frac{v}{{f}_{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>   = \\(\\frac{1540}{1\\,\\times \\,{10}^{6}}\\)</p></td><td><p>   = \\(\\frac{1540}{15\\,\\times \\,{10}^{6}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>   = <strong>1.54 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td><td><p>   = <strong>0.103 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>The range of wavelengths is between 0.103 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m and 1.54 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,11,true),
(12,'calculations','No.6','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The velocity of ultrasound in lung (inclusive air), fat and skull bone are 600 m s<sup>-1</sup>, 1 450 m s<sup>-1</sup> and 4080 m s<sup>-1</sup> respectively, what are the wavelengths of ultrasound if the sound waves at 2 MHz are used?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>f = 2 MHz = 2 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>6</sup> Hz, \\(\\lambda \\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>In lung</p><p>v<sub>1</sub> = 600 m s<sup>-1</sup>, \\({\\lambda }_{1}\\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>In fat</p><p>v<sub>2</sub> = 1 450 m s<sup>-1</sup>, \\({\\lambda }_{2}\\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>In skull</p><p>v<sub>3</sub> = 4080 m s<sup>-1</sup>, \\({\\lambda }_{3}\\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By wave equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>f \\(\\lambda \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\lambda \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{v}{f}\\)<sub> </sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>In lung,&emsp;\\({\\lambda }_{1}\\)=  \\(\\frac{{v}_{1}}{f}\\)<sub> </sub>=<sub> </sub>\\(\\frac{600}{2\\,\\times \\,{10}^{6}}\\)<sub> </sub>= <strong>3 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-4}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>In fat,&emsp; \\({\\lambda }_{2}\\)= \\(\\frac{{v}_{2}}{f}\\)<sub> </sub>=<sub> </sub>\\(\\frac{1\\,450}{2\\,\\times \\,{10}^{6}}\\)<sub> </sub>= <strong>7</strong><strong>.25 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-4}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>In skull, \\({\\lambda }_{3}\\)= \\(\\frac{{v}_{3}}{f}\\)<sub> </sub>=<sub> </sub>\\(\\frac{4\\,080}{2\\,\\times \\,{10}^{6}}\\)<sub> </sub>= <strong>2.04 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,12,true),
(12,'calculations','No.7','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; To get the better resolution, higher frequencies ultrasound are used but at the expense of less penetration because sound waves are attenuated within the distance about 50 \\(\\lambda \\) in tissue. If the velocity of sound in soft tissue is 1500 m s<sup>-1</sup> and mean depth of thyroid is 0.75 cm. What is the most suitable frequency of ultrasound to diagnose thyroid?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v = 1500 m s<sup>-1 </sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>To get the better resolution, </p><p>attenuated within the distance = mean depth of thyroid</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>50 \\(\\lambda \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.75 cm</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>50 \\(\\lambda \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.75 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\) m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\lambda \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{0.75\\,\\times {10}^{-2}}{50}\\)<sub> </sub>= <strong>1.5 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-4}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By wave equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>f \\(\\lambda \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>f</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{v}{\\lambda }\\)<sub> </sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1500}{1.5\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-4}}\\)<sub> </sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10  \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>6</sup> = <strong>10 MHz</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,13,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.7','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An ambulance travelling at 44 m s<sup>-1</sup> approaches a car heading in a same direction at the speed of 28 m s<sup>-1</sup>. The ambulance driver has a siren sounding at 550 Hz. At what frequency does the driver of the car hear the siren? (Speed of siren sound = v = 330 m s<sup>-1</sup>)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For ambulance (source) </p><p>f<sub>s</sub> = 550 Hz</p><p>v<sub>s</sub> = 44 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td><td><p>For driver of the car (observer)</p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = ?</p><p>v<sub>o</sub> = 28 m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>v = 330 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>By Doppler equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,\\pm \\,{v}_{o}}{v\\,∓\\,{v}_{s}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Since the <strong>o</strong>bserver moves away from the source, - v<sub>o</sub> is used</p><p>The <strong>s</strong>ource moves towards the observer, - v<sub>s </sub>is used</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,-\\,{v}_{o}}{v\\,-\\,{v}_{s}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>550<em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{330\\,-\\,28}{330\\,-\\,44}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>580.77 Hz</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,14,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.7','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; In example 7, what will be the frequency of the siren heard by the driver of the car when the ambulance overtakes his car?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For ambulance (source) </p><p>f<sub>s</sub> = 550 Hz</p><p>v<sub>s</sub> = 44 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td><td><p>For driver of the car (observer)</p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = ?</p><p>v<sub>o</sub> = 28 m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>v = 330 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>By Doppler equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,\\pm \\,{v}_{o}}{v\\,∓\\,{v}_{s}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>When the ambulance overtakes the car,</p><p>The <strong>o</strong>bserver moves toward the source, + v<sub>o</sub> is used</p><p>The <strong>s</strong>ource moves away from the observer, + v<sub>s </sub>is used</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,+\\,{v}_{o}}{v\\,+\\,{v}_{s}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>550<em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{330\\,+\\,28}{330\\,+\\,44}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>526.47 Hz</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,15,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.8','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A monorail approaches a platform at a speed of 50 m s<sup>-1</sup> which it blows its whistle. A man standing on the platform hears the whistle with frequency 261 Hz. There is no wind and temperature is chilly 0\\(℃\\). What is the observed frequency of the whistle when the train is at rest? (The speed of sound in air at 0\\(℃\\) is 332 m s<sup>-1</sup>). (Old)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For train (source)</p><p>f<sub>s</sub> = ?</p><p>v<sub>s</sub> = 50 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td><td><p>For man (observer)</p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = 261 Hz</p><p>v<sub>o</sub> = 0 m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>v = 332 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>By Doppler equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,\\pm \\,{v}_{o}}{v\\,∓\\,{v}_{s}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Since the <strong>s</strong>ource moves towards the observer, - v<sub>s </sub>is used</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,+\\,{v}_{o}}{v\\,-\\,{v}_{s}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>261</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{332\\,+\\,0}{332\\,-\\,50}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>261</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{332}{282}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{282\\,\\times \\,261\\,}{332}\\) = <strong>221.69 Hz</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>When the train is at rest, f<sub>s</sub> = f<sub>o</sub><sup>&#x27;</sup> = 221.69 Hz</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,16,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.8','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A car is travelling at 29 m s<sup>-1</sup> towards a stationary whistle with a frequency of 625 Hz. If the speed of sound is 337 m s<sup>-1</sup>, what is the apparent frequency of the whistle as heard by the driver of the car. (new)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For whistle (source)</p><p>v<sub>s</sub> = 0</p><p>f<sub>s</sub> = 625 Hz</p></td><td><p>For car dirver (observer)</p><p>v<sub>o</sub> = 29 m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = ?</p><p>v = 337 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>By Doppler equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,\\pm \\,{v}_{o}}{v\\,∓\\,{v}_{s}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Since the <strong>o</strong>bserver moves towards the source, + v<sub>o</sub><sub> </sub>is used</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,+\\,{v}_{o}}{v}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>625<em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{337\\,+\\,29}{337}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>679</strong><strong> Hz</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,17,true),
(12,'calculations','No.12','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.12</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; (i)&emsp;What frequency is received by a person watching an oncoming ambulance moving at 110 km h<sup>-1</sup> and emitting a steady 800 Hz sound from its siren? The speed of sound on this day is 345 m s<sup>-1</sup>. </p><p>&emsp;(ii)&emsp;What frequency does she receive after the ambulance has passed?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>For ambulance (source)</p><p>f<sub>s</sub> = 800 Hz</p><p>v<sub>s</sub> = 110 km h<sup>-1</sup></p><p>    = 110 \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{km}}{h}\\) </p><p>    = 110 \\(\\frac{{10}^{3}\\,m}{3600\\,s}\\) </p><p>    = 30.56 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td><td><p>For person (observer)</p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = ?</p><p>v<sub>o</sub> = 0 m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>v = 345 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>By Doppler equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,\\pm \\,{v}_{o}}{v\\,∓\\,{v}_{s}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>Since the <strong>s</strong>ource moves towards the observer, - v<sub>s </sub>is used</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,+\\,{v}_{o}}{v\\,-\\,{v}_{s}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>800<em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{345\\,+\\,0}{345\\,-\\,30.56}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><strong>877.75 Hz</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>After the ambulance has passed,</p><p>the <strong>s</strong>ource moves away from the observer, + v<sub>s </sub>is used</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,+\\,{v}_{o}}{v\\,+\\,{v}_{s}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>800<em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{345\\,+\\,0}{345\\,+\\,30.56}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>734.9 Hz</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,18,true),
(12,'calculations','No.13','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.13</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A 5000 Hz sound wave is emitted by a stationary source. This sound reflects from an object moving 3.5 m s<sup>-1</sup> toward the source. What is the frequency of the wave reflected by moving object as detected by a detector at rest near the source?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>For moving object act as observer, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For source (stationary)</p><p>f<sub>s</sub> = 5000 Hz</p><p>v<sub>s</sub> = 0 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td><td><p>For moving object (observer)</p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = ?</p><p>v<sub>o</sub> = 3.5 m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>v = 345 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>By Doppler equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,\\pm \\,{v}_{o}}{v\\,∓\\,{v}_{s}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Since the <strong>observer</strong> moves towards the source, + v<sub>o</sub><sub> </sub>is used</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>f</em><sub><em>s</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,+\\,{v}_{o}}{v\\,+\\,{v}_{s}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>5000<em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{345\\,+\\,3.5}{345\\,+0}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>f</em><sub><em>o</em></sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>5050.7 Hz</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>For moving object act as source, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For moving object (source)</p><p>\\({f}_{s}^{''}\\)= f<sub>o</sub> = 5050.7 Hz</p><p>\\({v}_{s}^{''}\\)= v<sub>o</sub> = 3.5 m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>v = 345 m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td><td><p>For detector (observer)</p><p>\\({f}_{o}^{''}\\) = ?</p><p>\\({v}_{o}^{''}\\) = 0 m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>the <strong>s</strong>ource moves towards the observer, - \\({v}_{s}^{''}\\)<sub> </sub>is used</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({f}_{o}^{''}\\)<em> </em></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\({f}_{s}^{''}\\)<em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{v\\,+\\,{v}_{o}^{''}}{v\\,-\\,{v}_{s}^{''}}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>5050.7<em> </em>\\(\\left[\\frac{345\\,+\\,0}{345\\,-\\,3.5}\\right)]\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({f}_{o}^{''}\\)<em> </em></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>5102.5 Hz</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,19,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.8','6','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Calculate the displacement of air molecules (amplitude) for a sound having a frequency of 1000 Hz <strong>at the threshold of hearing</strong>. The speed of sound in air is 343 m s<sup>-1</sup> at 20\\(℃\\) and density of air is 1.29 kg m<sup>-3</sup>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>f = 1000 Hz, v = 343 m s<sup>-1</sup>, </p><p>\\(\\rho \\) = 1.29 kg m<sup>-3</sup>,&emsp;A = ?</p><p>𝜔 = 2 \\(\\pi \\) f </p><p>    = 2 \\(\\times \\) 3.142 \\(\\times \\) 1000 = 6284 rad s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>At the threshold of hearing, intensity of sound I = 1 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-12</sup> W m<sup>-2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\rho \\) v \\({\\omega }^{2}\\) A<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>1 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-12</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\) 1.29 \\(\\times \\) 343 \\(\\times \\) 6284<sup>2</sup> A<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-12</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1.29 \\(\\times \\) 343 \\(\\times \\) 6284<sup>2</sup> A<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>A<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-12}}{1.29\\,\\times 343\\,\\times \\,{6284}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>A</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>10.7 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>-12</strong></sup><strong> m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,20,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A nature photographer wishes to photograph a 28 m tall tree from a distance of 58 m. What focal length of lens should be used if the image is to fill the 24 mm height of the film?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({\\mathrm{OO}}^{''}\\) = + 28 m,&emsp;u = + 58 m </p><p>\\({\\mathrm{II}}^{''}\\) = - 24 mm (real, inverted)</p><p>     = - 24 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m, </p><p>f = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{I{I}^{''}}{O{O}^{''}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>- \\(\\frac{v}{u}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{-\\,24\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}}{28}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>- \\(\\frac{v}{58}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{24\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}}{28}\\,\\times \\) 58</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.049 m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Using lens formula,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{u}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{v}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{f}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{58}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{49.71\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{f}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>20.13</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{f}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{20.13}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>f</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>0.049</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>f</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>f</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.049 m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Calculate the power of the eyelens for viewing object at the longest and shortest distances possible with normal vision, assuming eyelens to retina distance of 2 cm.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>P = ?,&emsp;&emsp;v = 2 cm = 0.02 m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>object at the maximum (longest) distances of distinct vision, u = \\(\\infty \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Using lens formula,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{f}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{u}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{v}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{f}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{\\infty }\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{0.02}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{f}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>0 + 50&emsp;(\\(\\because \\frac{1}{\\infty }\\) = 0)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{f}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>50 </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Since, P = \\(\\frac{1}{f}\\), P</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>50 D</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>object at the least (shortest) distances of distinct vision, u = 25 cm = 0.25 m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Using lens formula,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{f}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{u}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{v}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{f}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{0.25}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{0.02}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{f}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p>54 </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>Since, P = \\(\\frac{1}{f}\\), P</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>54 D</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A compound microscope consists of two thin converging lenses. The focal length of the objective is 10 mm and that of the eyepiece is 20 mm. If an object is placed 11 mm from the object ive, the instrument produces <strong>an image at infinity</strong>. Calculate the separation of the lenses and the magnifying power of the instrument. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Objective lens</p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = 10 mm</p><p>u<sub>o</sub> = 11 mm</p></td><td><p>Eyepiece lens</p><p>f<sub>e</sub> = 20 mm</p><p>v<sub>e</sub> = \\(\\infty \\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>L = ?,&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;MP = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>For image at infinity,</p><p>v<sub>e</sub> = \\(\\infty \\),&emsp;&emsp;u<sub>e</sub> = f<sub>e</sub> = 20 mm</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>Using lens formula,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p> \\(\\frac{1}{{f}_{o}}\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{o}}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{{v}_{o}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{11}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{{v}_{o}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{v}_{o}}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\) - \\(\\frac{1}{11}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{v}_{o}}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{11}{110}\\) - \\(\\frac{10}{110}\\) = \\(\\frac{1}{110}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>v<sub>o</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>+ 110 mm</strong> (real image)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>L = v<sub>o</sub> + u<sub>e</sub> = 110 + 20 = <strong>130 mm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>MP</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{{v}_{o}}{{u}_{o}}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{250}{{u}_{e}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{110}{11}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{250}{20}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><strong>125</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.5','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A compound microscope 17 cm long has an eyepiece with a focal length of 2.5 cm and objective with focal length of 0.25 cm. What is the magnifying power for <strong>normal setting</strong>?</p><p>&emsp;(Hint: The magnified image of the objective lens forms at the focal point of the eyepiece for normal setting)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Objective lens</p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = 0.25 cm</p><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Eyepiece lens</p><p>f<sub>e</sub> = 2.5 cm</p><p>v<sub>e</sub> = \\(\\infty \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>L = 17 cm,&emsp;&emsp;MP = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>For normal setting</p><p>v<sub>e</sub> = \\(\\infty \\),&emsp;&emsp;u<sub>e</sub> = f<sub>e</sub> = 2.5 cm</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>L</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>v<sub>o</sub> + u<sub>e</sub> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>17</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>v<sub>o</sub> + 2.5</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sub>o</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>17 – 2.5 = <strong>+ 14.5 cm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Using lens formula,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{f}_{o}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{o}}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{{v}_{o}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{0.25}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{o}}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{14.5}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{o}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{0.25}\\) - \\(\\frac{1}{14.5}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{o}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{114}{29}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>u<sub>o</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{29}{114}\\) = <strong>0.25 cm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>MP</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{v}_{o}}{{u}_{o}}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{25}{{u}_{e}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>MP</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{14.5}{0.25}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{25}{2.5}\\) = <strong>580 </strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','No.11','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A compound microscope consists of two thin lenses, an objective of focal length 20 mm and an eyepiece of focal length 50 mm, placed 220 mm apart. If <strong>the final image is viewed at infinity</strong>, calculate the distance of the object from the objective. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Objective lens</p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = 20 mm</p><p>u<sub>o</sub> = ?</p></td><td><p>Eyepiece lens</p><p>f<sub>e</sub> = 50 mm</p><p>v<sub>e</sub> = \\(\\infty \\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>L = 220 mm</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>For image at infinity,</p><p>v<sub>e</sub> = \\(\\infty \\),&emsp;&emsp;u<sub>e</sub> = f<sub>e</sub> = 50 mm</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>L</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>v<sub>o</sub> + u<sub>e</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>220</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>v<sub>o</sub> + 50</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>v<sub>o</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>+ 170 mm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>Using lens formula,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&emsp;\\(\\frac{1}{{f}_{o}}\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{o}}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{{v}_{o}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{20}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{o}}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{170}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{o}}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{20}\\) - \\(\\frac{1}{170}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{o}}\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{3}{68}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>u<sub>o</sub></p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{68}{3}\\) = <strong>22.67 mm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>The object must be placed 22.67 mm from the objective lens. </p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.4','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A telescope consists of two converging lenses: an objective of focal length 500 mm and an eyepiece of focal length 50 mm. When the telescope is in <strong>normal adjustment</strong>: (i) What is the separation of the lenses? (ii) Where is the final image located? (iii) Is the image erect or inverted? (iv) What is the magnifying power?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Objective lens</p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = 500 mm</p></td><td><p>Eyepiece lens</p><p>f<sub>e</sub> = 50 mm</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>(i) L = ?&emsp;&emsp;(ii) v<sub>e</sub> = ?&emsp;</p><p>(iii) erect or inverted ?&emsp;(iv) MP = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>For telescope,</p><p>u<sub>o</sub> = \\(\\infty \\),&emsp;&emsp;v<sub>o</sub> = f<sub>o</sub> = 500 mm</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>For normal adjustment,</p><p>v<sub>e</sub> = \\(\\infty \\),&emsp;&emsp;u<sub>e</sub> = f<sub>e</sub> = 50 mm</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>L</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v<sub>o</sub> + u<sub>e</sub> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>f<sub>o</sub> + f<sub>e</sub> = 500 + 50 = <strong>550 mm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>The final image is located at <strong>infinity</strong>.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iii)</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>The image is <strong>inverted</strong>. (\\(\\because \\) it uses two converging lenses)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iv)</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>MP</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{v}_{o}}{{u}_{e}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{f}_{o}}{{f}_{e}}\\) = \\(\\frac{500}{50}\\) = <strong>10</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.6','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An astronomical telescope has its two-lens space 75.2 cm apart. If the objective lens has a focal length of 70 cm, what is the magnifying power of this telescope when viewing with a <strong>relaxed eye</strong>?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Objective lens</p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = 70 cm </p></td><td><p>Eyepiece lens</p><p>f<sub>e</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>L = 75.2 cm&emsp;&emsp;MP = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>For telescope,</p><p>u<sub>o</sub> = \\(\\infty \\),&emsp;&emsp;v<sub>o</sub> = f<sub>o</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>For relaxed eye,</p><p>v<sub>e</sub> = \\(\\infty \\),&emsp;&emsp;u<sub>e</sub> = f<sub>e</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>L</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>v<sub>o</sub> + u<sub>e</sub> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>L</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>f<sub>o</sub> + f<sub>e</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>75.2</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>70 + f<sub>e</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>f<sub>e</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>75.2 – 70 = <strong>5.2 cm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>MP</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{v}_{o}}{{u}_{e}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{f}_{o}}{{f}_{e}}\\) = \\(\\frac{70}{5.2}\\)  = <strong>13.46</strong> </p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'calculations','No.12','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.12</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A telescope consists of two converging lenses. When in <strong>normal adjustment</strong>, so that the image of a distance object is formed at infinity, the lenses are 450 mm apart, and the magnifying power is 8. What are the focal lengths of the two lenses? <strong>Is</strong> the image erect or inverted? </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Objective lens</p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = ?</p></td><td><p>Eyepiece lens</p><p>f<sub>e</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>L = 450 mm&emsp;&emsp;MP = 8</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>For telescope,</p><p>u<sub>o</sub> = \\(\\infty \\),&emsp;&emsp;v<sub>o</sub> = f<sub>o</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>For normal adjustment,</p><p>v<sub>e</sub> = \\(\\infty \\),&emsp;&emsp;u<sub>e</sub> = f<sub>e</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>L</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>v<sub>o</sub> + u<sub>e</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>450</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>f<sub>o</sub> + f<sub>e</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>f<sub>o</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>450 - f<sub>e</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>MP</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{v}_{o}}{{u}_{e}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{f}_{o}}{{f}_{e}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{450\\,-\\,{f}_{e}}{{f}_{e}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>8 f<sub>e</sub> </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>450 - f<sub>e</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>9 f<sub>e</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>450</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>f<sub>e</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>50 mm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>f<sub>o</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>450 – 50 = <strong>400 mm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>The image is inverted with respect to the object because this type of telescopes uses two converging lenses.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','No.13','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.13</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A telescope consists of two thin converging lenses of focal lengths 100 cm and 10 cm respectively. It is used to view an object 2000 cm from the objective. What is the separation of the lenses if the final image is 25 cm from the eyelens? Determine the magnifying power for an observer whose eye is close to the eyelens.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>For telescope, f<sub>o</sub> &gt; f<sub>e</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Objective lens</p><p>f<sub>o</sub> = 100 cm</p><p>u<sub>o</sub> = 2000 cm,&emsp;</p><p>v<sub>o</sub> \\(\\neq \\) f<sub>o</sub></p></td><td><p>Eyepiece lens</p><p>f<sub>e</sub> = 10 cm</p><p>v<sub>e</sub> = - 25 cm (virtual image),&emsp;u<sub>e</sub> \\(\\neq \\) f<sub>e</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>L = ?                        MP = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Using lens formula,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{f}_{o}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{o}}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{{v}_{o}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{100}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2000}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{{v}_{o}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{v}_{o}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{100}\\) - \\(\\frac{1}{2000}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{v}_{o}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{19}{2000}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>v<sub>o</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{2000}{19}\\) = <strong>105.26 cm</strong> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Using lens formula,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&emsp;\\(\\frac{1}{{f}_{e}}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{e}}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{{v}_{e}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{e}}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{(\\,-\\,25)}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{e}}\\) - \\(\\frac{1}{\\,25}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{e}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{25}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{u}_{e}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{7}{50}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>u<sub>e</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{50}{7}\\) = <strong>7.14 cm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>L</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>v<sub>o</sub> + u<sub>e</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>105.26 + 7.14 = <strong>112.4 cm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>MP</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{v}_{o}}{{u}_{e}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{105.26}{7.14}\\)  = <strong>14.74</strong> </p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.5','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; In a laser unit, laser beam of wavelength 6328 Å is emitted. How many photons are released per second if the output power is 1 mW? (Plank constant, h = 6.62 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-34}\\) Js)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\lambda \\) = 6328 Å = 6328 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{-10}\\)m,&emsp;</p><p>h = 6.62 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-34}\\) J s, c = 3 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{8}\\) m s<sup>-1</sup> </p><p>number of photon per second = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>P = 1 mW = 1 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) W = 1 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) J s<sup>-1</sup>,</p><p>Output energy in 1 s is \\({10}^{-3}\\) J.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Energy of a photon,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&emsp;E</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{h\\,c}{\\lambda }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6.62\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-34}\\,\\times \\,3\\,\\times \\,{10}^{8}}{6328\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-10}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>3.14 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{-19}\\)<strong> J</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Number of photons per second</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>&emsp;= \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{Output}\\,\\mathrm{energy}\\,\\mathrm{per}\\,\\mathrm{second}}{\\mathrm{Energy}\\,\\mathrm{of}\\,a\\,\\mathrm{photon}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>&emsp;= \\(\\frac{1\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}}{3.14\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-19}}\\) = <strong>3.18 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{15}\\)<strong> photons</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>၁ စက္ကန့်မှာထွက်လာတဲ့ ဖိုတွန်အရေအတွက်ကိုရှာလိုပါ က ၁ စက္ကန့်မှာထုတ်လွှတ်တဲ့ စွမ်းအင်ကိုတည်ပြီး ဖိုတွန် ၁ လုံးက ပိုင်တဲ့စွမ်းအင်နှင့်စား။</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.7','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; How many photons are emitted in 1 s by a 7.5 mW of CO<sub>2</sub> laser with the wavelength of 10.6 \\(\\mu \\)m? (Plank constant, h = 6.62 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-34}\\) J s)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\lambda \\) = 10.6 \\(\\mu \\)m = 10.6 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{-6}\\)m,</p><p>h = 6.62 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-34}\\) J s, c = 3 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{8}\\) m s<sup>-1</sup> </p><p>number of photon per second = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>P = 7.5 mW = 7.5 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-3}\\) J s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>Output energy in 1 s is 7.5 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)  J.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Energy of a photon,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>E</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{h\\,c}{\\lambda }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6.62\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-34}\\,\\times \\,3\\,\\times \\,{10}^{8}}{10.6\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.87 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{-20}\\)<strong> J</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Number of photons per second</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>&emsp;= \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{Output}\\,\\mathrm{energy}\\,\\mathrm{per}\\,\\mathrm{second}}{\\mathrm{Energy}\\,\\mathrm{of}\\,a\\,\\mathrm{photon}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>&emsp;= \\(\\frac{7.5\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-3}}{1.87\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-20}}\\) = <strong>4 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{17}\\)<strong> photons</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,11,true),
(12,'calculations','No.14','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.14</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A He-Ne laser emits photons with energies of 3.14 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-19}\\) J. What is the colour of the laser light? (Plank constant, h = 6.62 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-34}\\) J s)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>E = 3.14 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-19}\\) J,</p><p>h = 6.62 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-34}\\) J s, c = 3 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{8}\\) m s<sup>-1</sup>,</p><p>\\(\\lambda \\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Energy of a photon,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>E</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{h\\,c}{\\lambda }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>3.14 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-19}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6.62\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-34}\\,\\times \\,3\\,\\times \\,{10}^{8}}{\\lambda }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\lambda \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6.62\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-34}\\,\\times \\,3\\,\\times \\,{10}^{8}}{3.14\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-19}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\lambda \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>632.48 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-9}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>632.48 nm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The colour of the laser light is <strong>red</strong>.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,12,true);
INSERT INTO educational_content (grade,category,title,chapter,content,sort_order,active) VALUES
(12,'calculations','No.15','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.15</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An optical fibre used for communications has a core of refractive index 1.55 which is surrounded by cladding of refractive index 1.45. Calculate the critical angle of the core-cladding boundary.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>refractive index of core, n<sub>1</sub> = 1.55,</p><p>refractive index of cladding, n<sub>2</sub> = 1.45</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>sin i<sub>c</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><sub>1</sub> n <sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{n}_{2}}{{n}_{1}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1.45}{1.55}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>i<sub>c</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>sin<sup>-1</sup> \\(\\frac{1.45}{1.55}\\) = <strong>69.31</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)<strong> (or) 69</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)<strong> 18</strong>\\(''\\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,13,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.6','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The core of an optical fibre has a dimeter 2 \\(\\mu \\)m and refractive index of 1.63. The refractive index of the cladding is 1.5. Determine the maximum angle for which the light rays incident on the end of fibre rod to total internal reflection at the core to cladding interface. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>d = 2 \\(\\mu \\)m = 2 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-6}\\) m</p><p>refractive index of core, n<sub>1</sub> = 1.63,</p><p>refractive index of cladding, n<sub>2</sub> = 1.5</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>sin i<sub>c</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><sub>1</sub> n <sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{n}_{2}}{{n}_{1}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1.5}{1.63}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>i<sub>c</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>sin<sup>-1</sup> \\(\\frac{1.5}{1.63}\\) = <strong>66.96</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>From figure,</p><p>r + i<sub>c</sub> + 90\\(^\\circ \\) = 180\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 180\\(^\\circ \\) - 90\\(^\\circ \\) - i<sub>c</sub> = 90\\(^\\circ \\) - 66.96\\(^\\circ \\) = <strong>23.04</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Refraction at air-core interference, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By using Snell’s law,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>n<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\sin i}{\\sin r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>sin i</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>n<sub>1 </sub>sin r</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1.63 \\(\\times \\) sin 23.04\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>i</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>sin<sup>-1</sup> (1.63 \\(\\times \\) sin 23\\(^\\circ \\)) = <strong>39.64</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,14,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.7','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A 10 W fluorescent lamp has a luminous intensity of 35 cd. Find luminous flux it emits.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><em>I</em><sub><em>v</em></sub> = 35 cd, P = 10W,&emsp;\\(\\Phi \\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Solid angle for a sphere, \\(\\Omega \\) = 4 \\(\\pi \\) <em>sr</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>I</em><sub>v</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> \\(\\frac{\\Phi }{\\Omega }\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\Phi \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><em>I</em><sub><em>v</em></sub><em> </em>\\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>35 \\(\\times \\) 4 \\(\\pi \\) = <strong>439.8 </strong><em><strong>lm</strong></em></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,15,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.11','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The luminous intensity of a light source is 500 cd. Find the illuminance of a surface which is 10 m from source if light falls <strong>normally</strong> on it.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><em>I</em><sub><em>v</em></sub> = 500 cd,&emsp;E<sub>v</sub><sub> </sub>= ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Just below the lamp,&emsp;r = 10 m, \\(\\theta \\) = 0\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>E</em><sub>v</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{I}_{v}\\cos \\theta }{{r}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{500\\,\\cos 0}{{10}^{2}}\\)  = <strong>5 </strong><em><strong>lx</strong></em></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,16,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.8','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The luminous intensity of a source is 200 cd. The mounting height of the lamp is 6 m from the ground. Find the illuminance on the ground E<sub>v</sub>: (i) just below the lamp, (ii) 3 m horizontally away from the lamp on the ground. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p><em>I</em><sub><em>v</em></sub> = 200 cd, E<sub>v</sub>= ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Just below the lamp,&emsp;r = 6 m,&emsp;\\(\\theta \\) = 0\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>E</em><sub>v</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{I}_{v}\\cos \\theta }{{r}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{200\\,\\cos 0}{{6}^{2}}\\)  = <strong>5.55 </strong><em><strong>lx</strong></em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>မတ်မျဉ်းနှင့် အလင်းဦးတည်ချက်ကြားထောင့် \\(\\theta \\,\\) အလင်းသည် ထောင့်မတ်ကျလာသဖြင့် \\(\\theta \\) = 0\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>3 m horizontally away from the lamp on the ground,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>r<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>6<sup>2</sup> + 3<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>r</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{36+9}\\) = \\(\\sqrt{45}\\) m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>cos \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6}{r}\\) = \\(\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{45}}\\) = 0.8944</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p><em>E</em><sub>v</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{I}_{v}\\cos \\theta }{{r}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{200\\,\\times 0.8944}{{\\sqrt{45}}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{200\\,\\times \\,0.8944}{45}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>3.98 </strong><em><strong>lx</strong></em></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,17,true),
(12,'calculations','No.16','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.16</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Light from a lamp is falling <strong>normally</strong> on a surface distant 10 m from the lamp and the illuminance on it is 10 lux. In order to increase the illuminance 9 times, what distance will the lamp be placed from the surface?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Just below the lamp,&emsp;\\(\\theta \\) = 0\\(^\\circ \\)</p><p>E<sub>v1 </sub>= 10 lux,&emsp;&emsp;r<sub>1</sub> = 10 m,  </p><p>E<sub>v2</sub> = 9 E<sub>v1</sub> = 90 lux,&emsp;r<sub>2</sub> = ?  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By inverse square law of illuminance, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>E</em><sub>v</sub></p></td><td><p>\\(\\propto \\)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{r}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>E</em><sub>v</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{r}^{2}}\\) \\(\\times \\) constant</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>E<sub>v</sub> r<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>Constant</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>E<sub>v2</sub> \\({r}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>E<sub>v1</sub> \\({r}_{1}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>90 \\({r}_{2}^{2}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({r}_{2}^{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{10\\,\\times 100}{90}\\)<sub> </sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({r}_{2}^{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{100}{9}\\)<sub> </sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>r<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{10}{3}\\)<sub> </sub>= <strong>3.33 m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,18,true),
(12,'calculations','No.17','7','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.17</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Two light sources of 8 cd and 12 cd are placed on the same side of the photometer screen at a distance of 40 cm from it. Where should a 80 cd source be placed to balance the illuminance?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><em>I</em><sub><em>v</em></sub><sub>1</sub> = 8 cd,&emsp;r<sub>1</sub> = 40 cm = 0.4 m</p><p><em>I</em><sub><em>v</em></sub><sub>2</sub> = 12 cd,&emsp;r<sub>2</sub> = 40 cm = 0.4 m</p><p><em>I</em><sub><em>v3</em></sub> = 80 cd,&emsp;r<sub>3</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p><em>E</em><sub>v</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{I}_{v}}{{r}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>to balance the illuminance,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>E<sub>v1</sub> + E<sub>v2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>E<sub>v3</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{I}_{v1}}{{r}_{1}^{2}}\\) + \\(\\frac{{I}_{v2}}{{r}_{2}^{2}}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{I}_{v3}}{{r}_{3}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{8}{{0.4}^{2}}\\) + \\(\\frac{12}{{0.4}^{2}}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{80}{{r}_{3}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{0.4}^{2}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{4}{{r}_{3}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{0.4}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2}{{r}_{3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>r<sub>3</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.8 m = <strong>80 cm</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,19,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','8','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; What is the phase difference for two waves of the same frequency arriving at a point with the respective path lengths of 6\\(\\lambda \\) and 4.5\\(\\lambda \\)?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\Delta \\,x\\) = 6\\(\\lambda \\) – 4.5\\(\\lambda \\) = 1.5\\(\\lambda \\), \\(\\Delta ϕ\\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\Delta ϕ\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\pi }{\\lambda }\\) \\(\\Delta \\,x\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\pi }{\\lambda }\\) \\(\\times \\) 1.5 \\(\\lambda \\) = <strong>3</strong>\\(\\pi \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Thus, the two waves are out of phase.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','No.5','8','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; At what angle is the first-order maximum for 450 nm wavelength blue light falling <strong>on double slits</strong> separated by 0.05 mm?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For double slits, </p><p>\\(\\lambda \\) = 450 nm = 450 \\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\) m,</p><p>d = 0.05 mm = 0.05 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m,&emsp;\\(\\theta \\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For first-order bright, m = 1</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d sin θ</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>m λ</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>sin θ</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m\\,}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>θ</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\sin}^{-1} \\frac{m\\,}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>θ</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\sin}^{-1} \\frac{1\\,\\times \\,450\\,\\times {10}^{-9}\\,}{0.05\\,\\times {10}^{-3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.52</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','8','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; In <strong>a double slit</strong> interference experiment, the distance between the slits is 5 mm and the screen is 2 m from the slits. Yellow light from a sodium lamp is used and it has a wavelength of 5.89 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-7}\\)m. Find the distance between <strong>the first and second order</strong> <strong>bright</strong> fringes on the screen.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For double slits, </p><p>d = 5 mm = 5 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m, D = 2 m</p><p>\\(\\lambda \\) = 5.89 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-7}\\)m, \\(\\Delta \\)y =? </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\Delta \\)y</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\lambda \\,D}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{5.89\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-7}\\times \\,2}{5\\,\\times {10}^{-3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2.356 \\(\\times {10}^{-4}\\) m = <strong>0.2356 mm</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','No.7','8','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Find the distance between <strong>adjacent dark spots</strong> from <strong>a double </strong><strong>slits</strong> interference pattern if the wavelength of light is 500 nm, the distance between the slits is 1 mm, and the distance from the slit to the screen is 2 m.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For double slits, </p><p>d = 1 mm = 1 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m, D = 2 m, </p><p>\\(\\lambda \\) = 500 nm = 500 \\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\) m, \\(\\Delta \\)y =?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\Delta \\)y</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\lambda \\,D}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{500\\,\\times {10}^{-9}\\,\\times \\,2}{1\\,\\times {10}^{-3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.001 m = <strong>1 mm</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','No.9','8','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; If the distance between <strong>two slits</strong> is 0.05 mm and the distance to a screen is 2.5 m, find the spacing between the <strong>first-order and second-order</strong> <strong>bright fringes</strong> for yellow light of 580 nm wavelength. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For double slits, </p><p>d = 0.05 mm = 0.05 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m,&emsp;D = 2.5 m,</p><p>\\(\\lambda \\) = 580 nm = 580 \\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\) m, \\(\\Delta \\)y =? </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\Delta \\)y</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\lambda \\,D}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{580\\,\\times {10}^{-9}\\,\\times \\,2.5}{0.05\\,\\times {10}^{-3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.029 m</strong> (or) <strong>29 mm</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'calculations','No.6','8','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A beam of 650 nm light is directed upon <strong>two slits</strong> that are separated by a distance of     0.75 mm. A screen is placed 1.50 m away to capture the interference pattern. What is the distance <strong>from</strong> <strong>the 1</strong><sup><strong>st</strong></sup><strong> order maximum to the 3</strong><sup><strong>rd</strong></sup><strong> order minimum</strong>?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For double slits, </p><p>d = 0.75 mm = 0.75 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m,&emsp;D = 1.5 m,</p><p>\\(\\lambda \\) = 650 nm = 650 \\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\) m, \\(\\Delta \\)y =? </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For 1<sup>st</sup> order bright (maximum), m = 1</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>y<sub>m</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>m \\(\\frac{\\lambda \\,D}{d}\\) &emsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>y<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\lambda \\,D}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{650\\,\\times {10}^{-9}\\times \\,1.5}{0.75\\,\\times {10}^{-3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.0013 m = <strong>1.3 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For 3<sup>rd</sup> order dark (minimum), m = 2</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>y<sub>m</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>(m + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)) \\(\\frac{\\lambda \\,D}{d}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>y<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>(2 + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)) \\(\\frac{\\lambda \\,D}{d}\\) = \\(\\frac{5}{2}\\) \\(\\frac{\\lambda \\,D}{d}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{5}{2}\\) \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{650\\,\\times {10}^{-9}\\times \\,1.5}{0.75\\,\\times {10}^{-3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>3.25 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\Delta \\)y</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>y<sub>2</sub> – y<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>3.25 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) - 1.3 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.95 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','8','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A beam of green light from a laser light source is diffracted by <strong>a slit</strong> of width 0.55 mm. The diffraction pattern forms on a wall 2.06 m beyond the slit. The distance between the positions of the first minima on both sides of central bright fringe is 4.1 mm. Calculate the wavelength of the laser light. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For single slit, </p><p>\\(a\\) = 0.55 mm = 0.55 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m,&emsp;</p><p>D = 2.06 m, \\(\\lambda \\) = ? </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The width of the central maximum </p><p>&emsp;= 4.1 mm = 4.1 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The width of the central maximum </p><p>&emsp;= 2 \\(\\frac{\\lambda \\,D}{a}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>4.1 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\frac{\\lambda \\,D}{a}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\lambda \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{4.1\\,\\times {10}^{-3}\\times \\,a}{2\\,D}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{4.1\\,\\times {10}^{-3}\\times 0.55\\,\\times {10}^{-3}}{2\\times 2.06}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\lambda \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>547.3 \\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\) m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>547.3 nm</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'calculations','No.8','8','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Light of wavelength 580 nm is incident on <strong>a slit</strong> of width 0.3 mm. The observing screen is placed 2 m from the slit. Find the positions of the first dark fringes and the width of the central bright fringes. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For single slit, </p><p>\\(a\\) = 0.3 mm = 0.3 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m, D = 2 m,</p><p>\\(\\lambda \\) = 580 nm = 580 \\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\) m, y = ?,</p><p>The width of the central maximum = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For first dark fringes, m = 1</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>y</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>m \\(\\frac{\\lambda \\,D}{a}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{580\\,\\times {10}^{-9}\\times 2}{0.3\\,\\times {10}^{-3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.00387 m = <strong>3.87 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The width of the central maximum = 2 \\(\\frac{\\lambda \\,D}{a}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\,\\times \\,580\\,\\times {10}^{-9}\\times 2}{0.3\\,\\times {10}^{-3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.00773 m = 7.73 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) m </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> <strong>7.74 mm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>[OR]</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The width of the central maximum </p><p>= 2 y = 2 \\(\\times \\) 3.87 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) = <strong>7.74 mm</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.4','8','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Light of wavelength 457 nm illuminates a <strong>diffraction grating</strong> with 5000 lines cm<sup>-1</sup>. What is the <strong>second order</strong> diffracted angle?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\lambda \\) = 457 nm = 457 \\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\) m,</p><p>N = 5000 lines cm<sup>-1</sup>, \\(\\theta \\) = ?</p><p>for second order, m = 2</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{N}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{5000}\\) = 2 \\(\\times {10}^{-4}\\) cm</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\times {10}^{-6}\\) m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d sin \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>m \\(\\lambda \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>sin \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m\\,\\lambda }{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\sin}^{-1} \\frac{m\\,\\lambda }{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\sin}^{-1} \\frac{2\\times 457\\,\\times {10}^{-9}}{2\\,\\times {10}^{-6}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>27.19</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)<strong> (or) 27</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)<strong> 11</strong>\\(''\\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','No.11','8','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A <strong>diffraction grating</strong> has 2000 lines per centimetre. At what angle will the first-order maximum be for 520 nm wavelength green light?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\lambda \\) = 520 nm = 520 \\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\) m,</p><p>N = 2000 lines cm<sup>-1</sup>, \\(\\theta \\) = ?</p><p>for first-order, m = 1</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{N}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2000}\\) = 5 \\(\\times {10}^{-4}\\) cm </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>5 \\(\\times {10}^{-6}\\) m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d sin \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>m \\(\\lambda \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>sin \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m\\,\\lambda }{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\sin}^{-1} \\frac{m\\,\\lambda }{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\theta \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\sin}^{-1} \\frac{1\\,\\times 520\\,\\times {10}^{-9}}{5\\,\\times {10}^{-6}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>5.97</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)<strong> (or) 5</strong>\\(^\\circ \\)<strong> 58</strong>\\(''\\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','No.10','8','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A grating containing 4000 slits per centimeter is illuminated with a monochromatic light and produces the <strong>second-order</strong> bright line at a 30\\(^\\circ \\) angle. What is the wavelength of the light used?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>N = 4000 lines cm<sup>-1</sup>, \\(\\theta \\) = 30\\(^\\circ \\), \\(\\lambda \\) = ?</p><p>for second order, m = 2</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{N}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{4000}\\) = 2.5 \\(\\times {10}^{-4}\\) cm </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>2.5 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-6}\\)<strong> m</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d sin \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>m \\(\\lambda \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\lambda \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{d\\,\\sin\\,\\theta }{m}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2.5\\,\\times {10}^{-6}\\times \\sin 30^\\circ \\,}{2}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>625 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\)<strong> m = 625 nm</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,11,true),
(12,'calculations','No.12','8','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.12</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; How many lines per centimeter are there on a diffraction grating that gives a <strong>first-order</strong> maximum for 470 nm blue light at an angle of 25\\(^\\circ \\)?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>N = ?, \\(\\lambda \\) = 470 nm = 470 \\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\) m,</p><p>\\(\\theta \\) = 25\\(^\\circ \\)</p><p>for first-order, m = 1</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d sin \\(\\theta \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>m \\(\\lambda \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{m\\,\\lambda }{\\sin\\,\\theta }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1\\,\\times 470\\,\\times {10}^{-9}}{\\sin 25^\\circ }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1.112 \\(\\times {10}^{-6}\\) m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.112 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-4}\\)<strong> cm</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>d </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{N}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>N</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{1.112\\,\\times {10}^{-4}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>8992 lines cm</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp;</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,12,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A capacitor has a capacitance of 5 μF. How much of the charge should be removed in order that the potential difference between its plates decreases by 40 V?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C = 5 μF,&emsp;\\(∆\\)V = 40 V,&emsp;\\(∆\\)Q = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{∆Q}{∆V}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{∆Q}{40}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(∆\\)Q</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>200 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>C</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>200 μC of the charge should be removed to decrease potential difference 40 V.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','No.2','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; When a parallel-plate capacitor is connected to a 50 V battery each plate receives a charge of magnitude 0.002 C. Find its capacitance. If the capacitor is connected to a 100 V battery, does the capacitance change? Does the charge still remain the same?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>V = 50 V,&emsp;Q = 0.002 C,&emsp;C = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{Q}{V}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{0.002}{50}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> 4 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-5}\\) F</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>40 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-6}\\) F = <strong>40 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Although voltage is increase to 100 V, the capacitance does not change but the charge will change.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>V = 100 V, C = 40 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-6}\\) F, Q = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{Q}{V}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Q</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>40 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-6}\\) \\(\\times \\) 100</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>40 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-4}\\) C = <strong>0.004 C</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','No.3','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Choose the correct answer from the following.</p><p>&emsp;The plates of a parallel-plate capacitor of capacitance C are brought together to a third of their original separation. The capacitance is now</p><p>&emsp;A. \\(\\frac{1}{9}\\) C,&emsp;B. \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) C,&emsp;C. 3 C,&emsp;D. 9 C.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Original separation&emsp;= d</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Original capacitance&emsp;= C = \\(\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{d}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>New separation&emsp;= \\({d}^{''}\\) = \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) d</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>New capacitance&emsp;= \\({C}^{''}\\)= \\(\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{{d}^{''}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({C}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{\\frac{1}{3}\\,d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({C}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>3 \\(\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({C}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>3 C</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.4','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; When the distance between the two parallel-plate of a capacitor is doubled, by what percent does its capacitance change?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Original separation&emsp;= d</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Original capacitance&emsp;= C = \\(\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{d}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>New separation&emsp;= \\({d}^{''}\\) = 2d</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>New capacitance&emsp;= \\({C}^{''}\\)= \\(\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{{d}^{''}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({C}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{2\\,d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({C}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({C}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)<strong> C</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Change in capacitance, </p><p>\\(∆\\) C = C - \\({C}^{''}\\) = C - \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) C = \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)<strong> C</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>percent change</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{∆\\,C}{C}\\,\\times 100\\%\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\,C}{C}\\,\\times 100\\%\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>50 </strong>\\(\\%\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When the distance between the two parallel-plate of a capacitor is doubled, its capacitance decreases 50 \\(\\%\\).</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The area of each plate of parallel-plate capacitor is 1 m<sup>2</sup> and the distance between two plates is 1 mm. If the potential difference the plates is 120 V and the dielectric constant of the material inserted between them is 3, find (i) the capacitance of the parallel-plate capacitor, (ii) the magnitude of the charge on each plate, (iii) the electric field intensity between the plates.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = 1 m<sup>2</sup>, d = 1 mm = 1 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-3</sup> m,</p><p>V = 120 V,&emsp;\\(\\kappa \\) = 3</p><p>\\({\\epsilon }_{0}\\) = 8.85 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-12}\\) C<sup>2</sup> N<sup>-1</sup> m<sup>-2</sup> (or) F m<sup>-1</sup></p><p>(i) C = ?&emsp;(ii) Q = ?&emsp;(iii) E = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{3\\,\\times \\,8.85\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-12}\\,\\times 1}{1\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{-3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>2.655 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-8}\\)<strong> F (or) 26.55 nF</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{Q}{V}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Q</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2.655 \\(\\times {10}^{-8}\\) \\(\\times \\)120</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>3.186 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{-6}\\)<strong> C </strong><strong>(or) </strong><strong>3.186 </strong>\\(\\mu \\)<strong> C</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iii)</p></td><td><p>V</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>E d</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>E</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{120}{1\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{-3}}\\) = 120 \\(\\times \\,1{0}^{3}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.2 </strong>\\(\\times \\,1{0}^{5}\\)<strong> V m</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'calculations','No.7','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The capacitance of a parallel-plate capacitor is increased from 8 μF to 50 μF when a sheet of glass is inserted between its plates. What is the dielectric constant of the glass?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C<sub>0</sub> = 8 μF (with vacuum or air),&emsp;</p><p>C = 50 μF (with glass plate)&emsp;\\(\\kappa \\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\kappa \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{C}{{C}_{0}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\kappa \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{50\\,\\mu }{8\\,\\mu }\\)  = <strong>6.25</strong> </p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true);
INSERT INTO educational_content (grade,category,title,chapter,content,sort_order,active) VALUES
(12,'calculations','Rev.7','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A parallel-plate capacitor of capacitance ‘C’ is given the charge ‘Q’ and then disconnected from the circuit. How much work is required to pull apart the plates of this capacitor to twice their original separation?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Original separation&emsp;= d</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Original capacitance&emsp;= C = \\(\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{d}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>New separation&emsp;= \\({d}^{''}\\) = 2d</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>New capacitance&emsp;= \\({C}^{''}\\)= \\(\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{{d}^{''}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({C}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{2\\,d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({C}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({C}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)<strong> C</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Original energy stored = W = \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\frac{{Q}^{2}}{C}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>New energy stored&emsp;= \\({W}^{''}\\) = \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\frac{{Q}^{2}}{{C}^{''}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({W}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\frac{{Q}^{2}}{\\frac{1}{2}\\,C}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({W}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{Q}^{2}}{C}\\)<strong> </strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Required work&emsp;= \\({W}^{''}\\) - W</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;= \\(\\frac{{Q}^{2}}{C}\\) - \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\frac{{Q}^{2}}{C}\\) = \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)<strong> </strong>\\(\\frac{{Q}^{2}}{C}\\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; What potential difference must be applied across 10 μF capacitor if it is to have an energy content of 1 J?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C = 10 μF = 10 \\(\\times {10}^{-6}\\) F, W = 1 J, V = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) C V<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\,W}{C}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\,W}{C}}\\) = \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\,\\times 1}{10\\,\\times {10}^{-6}}}\\) = <strong>447.2 V</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','No.6','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The plates of a parallel-plate capacitor are 50 cm<sup>2</sup> in area and 1 mm apart, (i) What is its capacitance? (ii) When the capacitor is connected to a 24 V battery, what is the charge on each plate? (iii) What is the energy of the capacitor?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = 50 cm<sup>2</sup> = 50 \\({{10}^{-2}\\,m}^{2}\\) = 50 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-4</sup> m<sup>2</sup></p><p>d = 1 mm = 1 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-3</sup> m, V = 24 V, \\(\\kappa \\) = 1</p><p>\\({\\epsilon }_{0}\\) = 8.85 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-12}\\) C<sup>2</sup> N<sup>-1</sup> m<sup>-2</sup> (or) F m<sup>-1</sup></p><p>(i) C = ?&emsp;(ii) Q = ?&emsp;(iii) W = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\kappa \\,{\\epsilon }_{0}\\,A}{d}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1\\,\\times \\,8.85\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-12}\\,\\times \\,50\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{-4}\\,}{1\\,\\times \\,1{0}^{-3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>44.25 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-12}\\)<strong> F (or) 44.25 p F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{Q}{V}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Q</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>44.25 \\(\\times {10}^{-12}\\) \\(\\times \\) 24</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.062 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\)<strong> C (or) 1.062 n C</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iii)</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) Q V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) \\(\\times \\) 1.062 \\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\) \\(\\times \\) 24</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.2744 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-8}\\)<strong> J</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.4','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A charged capacitor of capacitance C = 35 μF is <strong>discharged</strong> through a resistor of resistance R = 120 Ω. (i) What is the time constant ‘τ’ of the discharging process? (ii) What is the elapsed time when the voltage <strong>falls</strong> to 10 % of its original value?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C = 35 μF = 35 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-6}\\)F, R = 120 Ω</p><p>(i) time constant, \\(\\tau \\) = ?&emsp;(ii) t = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>voltage falls to 10 % of its original value, V<sub>c</sub> = 10 % V<sub>0</sub> = 0.1 V<sub>0</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\tau \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>R C</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>120 \\(\\times \\) 35 \\(\\times {10}^{-6}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>4.2 </strong>\\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)<strong> s (or) 4.2 ms</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For discharging,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sub>C</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V<sub>0</sub> (\\({e}^{\\frac{-\\,t}{{R}_{L}\\,C}}\\))</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sub>C</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V<sub>0</sub> (\\({e}^{\\frac{-\\,t}{\\tau }}\\))</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>0.1 V<sub>0</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V<sub>0</sub> (\\({e}^{\\frac{-\\,t}{\\tau }}\\))</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>0.1</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({e}^{\\frac{-\\,t}{\\tau }}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>ln 0.1</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>ln \\({e}^{\\frac{-\\,t}{\\tau }}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>ln 0.1</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>- \\(\\frac{t}{\\tau }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>- ln 0.1 \\(\\tau \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>- ln 0.1\\(\\times \\)4.2 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>9.67 </strong>\\(\\times \\,{10}^{-3}\\)<strong> s (or) 9.67 ms</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','No.8','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; In a capacitor charging RC circuit, C = 50 μF. What is the value of resistance ‘R’ that would produce a voltage <strong>rise</strong> to 20% of supply voltage after 1 s?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C = 50 μF = 50 \\(\\times \\,{10}^{-6}\\)F, R = ?, t = 1 s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>voltage <strong>rise</strong> to 20% of supply voltage, V<sub>c</sub> = 20 % V<sub>0</sub> = 0.2 V<sub>0</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For charging,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sub>C</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V<sub>0</sub> (1 - \\({e}^{\\frac{-\\,t}{\\mathrm{RC}}}\\))</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>0.2 V<sub>0</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V<sub>0</sub> (1 - \\({e}^{\\frac{-\\,t}{\\mathrm{RC}}}\\))</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>0.2</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1 - \\({e}^{\\frac{-\\,t}{\\mathrm{RC}}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({e}^{\\frac{-\\,t}{\\mathrm{RC}}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1 – 0.2 = 0.8</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>ln (\\({e}^{\\frac{-\\,t}{\\mathrm{RC}}}\\))</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>ln 0.8</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>- \\(\\frac{t}{R\\,C}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>ln 0.8</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>- <em>t</em> </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>ln 0.8 R C</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{-\\,t}{\\ln\\,0.8\\,C}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{-\\,1}{\\ln\\,0.8\\,\\,\\times \\,50\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>89.628 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>3 </sup>\\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>89.628 k</strong>\\(\\,\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,11,true),
(12,'calculations','No.9','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Three capacitors have capacitances of 5 μF, 10 μF and 15 μF.</p><p>Find the equivalent capacitance when they are connected in parallel. </p><p>Find the equivalent capacitance when they are connected in series.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C<sub>1</sub> = 5 μF, C<sub>2</sub> = 10 μF, C<sub>3</sub> = 15 μF</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>1</sub>, C<sub>2</sub> and C<sub>3</sub> are connected in parallel</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C<sub>1</sub> + C<sub>2</sub> + C<sub>3 </sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>5 + 10 + 15 = <strong>30 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>1</sub>, C<sub>2</sub> and C<sub>3</sub> are connected in series</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{1}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{2}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{5}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{10}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{15}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{11}{30}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{30}{11}\\) = <strong>2.727 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,12,true),
(12,'calculations','No.10','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Find the capacitance that can be obtained by combining <strong>three</strong> 10 μF capacitors in <strong>all possible ways</strong>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C<sub>1</sub> = C<sub>2</sub> = C<sub>3</sub> = 10 μF</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>\\(⇒\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>1</sub>, C<sub>2</sub> and C<sub>3</sub> are connected in parallel</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C<sub>1</sub> + C<sub>2</sub> + C<sub>3 </sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10 + 10 + 10 = <strong>30 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>\\(⇒\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>1</sub>, C<sub>2</sub> and C<sub>3</sub> are connected in series</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{1}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{2}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{10}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{10}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1\\,+\\,1\\,+\\,1}{10}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{3}{10}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{10}{3}\\) = <strong>3.33 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>\\(⇒\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>1</sub> and C<sub>2</sub> are connected in parallel</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C<sub>p</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C<sub>1</sub> + C<sub>2</sub> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10 + 10 = 20 μF</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>p</sub> and C<sub>3</sub> are connected in series</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{p}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{20}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1+2}{20}\\) = \\(\\frac{3}{20}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{20}{3}\\) = <strong>6.67 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>\\(⇒\\)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>1</sub> and C<sub>2</sub> are connected in series</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{s}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{1}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{s}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1+1}{10}\\) = \\(\\frac{2}{10}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{10}{2}\\) = 5 μF</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>s</sub> and C<sub>3</sub> are connected in parallel</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C<sub>s</sub> + C<sub>3</sub> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>5 + 10 = <strong>15 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,13,true),
(12,'calculations','No.11','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; The equivalent capacitance is 10 μF when ‘n’ identical capacitors are connected in parallel and 0.4 μF when they are connected in series. Determine ‘n’ and the capacitance of each capacitor.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C<sub>p </sub>= 10 μF,&emsp;C<sub>s</sub> =  0.4 μF</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For n identical capacitors, </p><p>C<sub>1</sub> = C<sub>2</sub> = C<sub>3</sub> = ….. = C<sub>n</sub> = C</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>In parallel,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C<sub>p</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>n C ------------------ (1)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>In series,       </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{C}{n}\\) ------------------ (2)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>eq (1) \\(\\div \\) eq (2)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{C}_{p}}{{C}_{s}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{n\\,C}{\\frac{C}{n}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{C}_{p}}{{C}_{s}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>n C \\(\\frac{n}{C}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{10}{0.4}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>n<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>n</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{0.4}}\\) = <strong>5 capacitors</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>n = 5 in eq (2)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>0.4</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{C}{5}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.4 (5)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>2 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,14,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.5','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; If two capacitors having the capacitance of 4 μF and 12 μF are connected in series, find the equivalent capacitance of the combination of the two capacitors. If the potential difference of the combination is 200 V, find the potential difference of the 12 μF capacitor.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C<sub>1</sub> = 4 μF, C<sub>2</sub> = 12 μF,&emsp;V = 200 V,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>1</sub> and C<sub>2</sub> are connected in series</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{1}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{12}\\) = \\(\\frac{3\\,+\\,1}{12}\\)  = \\(\\frac{4}{12}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{12}{4}\\) = <strong>3 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{Q}{V}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Q</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>3 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-6</sup> \\(\\times \\) 200 = <strong>600 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>-6 </strong></sup><strong>C</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Q<sub>1</sub> = Q<sub>2</sub> = Q = <strong>600 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>-6 </strong></sup><strong>C (in series)</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{Q}{V}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{Q}_{2}}{{C}_{2}}\\) = \\(\\frac{600\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}{12\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}\\) = <strong>50 V</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,15,true),
(12,'calculations','No.14','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.14</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Three capacitors of capacitance 3 μF, 10 μF and 15 μF are connected in <strong>series</strong> with 100 V battery. What is the charge and the potential difference on each capacitor?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C<sub>1</sub> = 3 μF, C<sub>2</sub> = 10 μF, C<sub>3</sub> = 15 μF,&emsp;</p><p>V = 100 V</p><p>Q<sub>1</sub> = ?,&emsp;&emsp;Q<sub>2</sub> = ?,&emsp;&emsp;Q<sub>3</sub> = ?</p><p>V<sub>1</sub> = ?,&emsp;&emsp;V<sub>2</sub> = ?,&emsp;&emsp;V<sub>3</sub> = ? </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>1</sub>, C<sub>2</sub> and C<sub>3</sub> are connected in series</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{1}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{2}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{10}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{15}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{10\\,+\\,3\\,+\\,2}{30}\\)  = \\(\\frac{15}{30}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{30}{15}\\) = <strong>2 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{Q}{V}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Q</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C V </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-6</sup> \\(\\times \\) 100 </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>200 </strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong> 10</strong><sup><strong>-6 </strong></sup><strong>C</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Q<sub>1</sub> = Q<sub>2</sub> = Q<sub>3</sub> = Q = <strong>200</strong>\\(\\times \\)<strong>10</strong><sup><strong>-6 </strong></sup><strong>C (in series)</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{Q}_{1}}{{C}_{1}}\\) = \\(\\frac{200\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}{3\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}\\) = <strong>66.67 V</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{Q}_{2}}{{C}_{2}}\\) = \\(\\frac{200\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}{10\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}\\) = <strong>20 V</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{Q}_{2}}{{C}_{2}}\\) = \\(\\frac{200\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}{15\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}\\) = <strong>13.33 V</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,16,true),
(12,'calculations','No.12','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.12</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A 35 μF capacitor is needed, but only 10 μF capacitors are available. How should a minimum number of 10 μF capacitors be connected so that the combination has a capacitance of 35 μF?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>To get 35 μF</p><p>C<sub>1</sub> = C<sub>2</sub> = C<sub>3</sub> = ….. = C<sub>n</sub> = C = 10 μF</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>1</sub> and C<sub>2</sub> are connected in series</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{s}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{1}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{2}}\\,\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1\\,+\\,1}{10}\\)  =  \\(\\frac{2}{10}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{10}{2}\\) = <strong>5 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>3</sub>, C<sub>4</sub> and C<sub>5</sub> are connected in parallel</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C<sub>p</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C<sub>3</sub> + C<sub>4</sub> + C<sub>5</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>10 + 10 + 10 = <strong>30 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When C<sub>p</sub> and C<sub>s</sub> are connected in parallel</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C<sub>p</sub> + C<sub>s</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>30 + 5 = <strong>35 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>To get 35 μF, minimum number of 10 μF capacitors = 5</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,17,true),
(12,'calculations','No.13','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.13</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; There capacitors have capacitance of 3 μF, 10 μF and 15 μF. How should they be connected to obtain the equivalent capacitances of (i) 2 μF (ii) 9 μF (iii) 12.5 μF?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C<sub>1</sub> = 3 μF, C<sub>2</sub> = 10 μF,&emsp;C<sub>3</sub> = 15 μF</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>To get 2 μF,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C<sub>1</sub>, C<sub>2</sub> and C<sub>3</sub> are connected in series</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{1}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{2}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{10}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{15}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{10\\,+\\,3\\,+\\,2}{30}\\)  = \\(\\frac{15}{30}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{30}{15}\\) = <strong>2 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>To get 9 μF,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C<sub>2</sub> and C<sub>3</sub> are connected in series</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{s}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{2}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{15}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{s}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{3\\,+\\,2}{30}\\)  = \\(\\frac{5}{30}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{30}{5}\\) = 6 μF</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C<sub>s</sub> and C<sub>1</sub> are connected in parallel</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C<sub>s</sub> + C<sub>1</sub> = 6 + 3 = <strong>9 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>To get 12.5 μF,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C<sub>1</sub> and C<sub>3</sub> are connected in series</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{s}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{1}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{15}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{s}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{5\\,+\\,1}{15}\\)  = \\(\\frac{6}{15}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{15}{6}\\) = 2.5 μF</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>C<sub>s</sub> and C<sub>2</sub> are connected in parallel</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>C<sub>s</sub> + C<sub>2</sub> = 2.5 + 10 = <strong>12.5 </strong><strong>μ</strong><strong>F</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,18,true),
(12,'calculations','No.15','9','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.15</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A capacitor having a capacitance of 2 µF and a charge of 2000 μC is connected in series with another capacitor having a capacitance of 8 μF and a charge of 1600 μC.</p><p>(i) &emsp;Find the potential difference of the individual capacitors prior to the connection. </p><p>(ii)&emsp;Find the potential difference of the individual capacitors after the connection.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>C<sub>1</sub> = 2 μF,&emsp;C<sub>2</sub> = 8 μF</p><p>Q<sub>1</sub> = 2000 μC,&emsp;Q<sub>2</sub> = 1600 μC</p><p>(i) V<sub>1</sub> = ?, V<sub>2</sub> = ? (prior to the connection)</p><p>(ii) \\({V}_{1}^{''}\\) = ?, \\({V}_{2}^{''}\\) = ? (after the connection) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>Prior to the connection </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{Q}{V}\\) </p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{Q}_{1}}{{C}_{1}}\\) </p></td><td><p>V<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{Q}_{2}}{{C}_{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2000\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}{2\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}\\) </p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1600\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}{8\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1000 V</strong></p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>200 V</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>After the connection, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>V<sub>1</sub> + V<sub>2</sub> = 1000 + 200 = 1200 V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>When C<sub>1</sub> and C<sub>2</sub> are connected in series</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{C}_{1}}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{{C}_{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{C}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>\\(\\frac{4\\,+\\,1}{8}\\)  = \\(\\frac{5}{8}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>\\(\\frac{8}{5}\\) = 1.6 μF</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>\\(\\frac{Q}{V}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Q</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>C V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>1.6 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-6</sup> \\(\\times \\) 1200 = 1920 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-6 </sup>C</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"6\"><p>\\({Q}_{1}^{''}\\) = \\({Q}_{2}^{''}\\) = Q = 1920 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-6 </sup>C (in series)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({V}_{1}^{''}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>\\(\\frac{{Q}_{1}^{''}}{{C}_{1}}\\) = \\(\\frac{1920\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}{2\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}\\) = <strong>960 V</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({V}_{2}^{''}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>\\(\\frac{{Q}_{2}^{''}}{{C}_{2}}\\) = \\(\\frac{1920\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}{8\\,\\times \\,{10}^{-6}}\\) = <strong>240 V</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,19,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; When a battery is connected to a 2 \\(\\Omega \\) resistor it drives a current of 0.6 A through the resistor. When it is connected to a 7 \\(\\Omega \\) resistor it drives a current of 0.2 A through the resistor. Find the emf and the internal resistance of the battery. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>1</sub> = 2 \\(\\Omega \\),&emsp;I<sub>1</sub> = 0.6 A</p><p>R<sub>2</sub> = 7 \\(\\Omega \\),&emsp;I<sub>2</sub> = 0.2 A</p><p>E = ?,&emsp;&emsp;r = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation,&emsp;I = \\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{{R}_{1}\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>E</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I<sub>1</sub> (R<sub>1</sub> + r)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.6 (2 + r) ---------- (1)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{{R}_{2}\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>E</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I<sub>2</sub> (R<sub>2</sub> + r)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.2 (7 + r) ---------- (2)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>From Eq (1) and (2)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>0.6 (2 + r)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.2 (7 + r)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{0.6}{0.2}\\) (2 + r)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>7 + r </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>3 (2 + r)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>7 + r</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>6 + 3r</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>7 + r</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>2r</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>r</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.5 </strong>\\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 0.5 \\(\\Omega \\) in eq (1)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>E</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.6 (2 + 0.5) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.5 V</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','No.4','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; In the electric circuit shown below, find the reading of the ammeter A when the switch is (i) open (ii) closed. (Neglect the internal resistance of the battery.)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>1</sub> = 3 \\(\\Omega \\), &emsp;R<sub>2</sub> = R<sub>3</sub> = 2 \\(\\Omega \\),&emsp;</p><p>E = 20 V,&emsp;r = 0 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When the switch is open,</p><p>R<sub>1</sub> and R<sub>2</sub> are connected in series,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>R<sub>1</sub> + R<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>3 + 2 = 5 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{20}{5\\,+\\,0}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{20}{5}\\) = <strong>4 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\therefore \\) When the switch is open, the reading of the ammeter A is 4 A.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When the switch is closed,</p><p>R<sub>2</sub> and R<sub>3</sub> are connected in parallel,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{2}}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{3}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)  =  \\(\\frac{2}{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R<sub>p</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>p</sub> and R<sub>1</sub> are connected in series,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>R<sub>1</sub> + R<sub>p</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>3 + 1 = 4 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{20}{4\\,+\\,0}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{20}{4}\\) = <strong>5 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\therefore \\) When the switch is closed, the reading of the ammeter A is 5 A.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Find the current flowing through each resistor and the potential difference across the 1 \\(\\Omega \\) resistor in the circuit diagram given below.</p><p>&emsp;R<sub>1</sub> = 4 \\(\\Omega \\),&emsp;R<sub>2</sub> = 6 \\(\\Omega \\),&emsp;R<sub>3</sub> = 1 \\(\\Omega \\),</p><p>&emsp;E = 12 V&emsp;r = 0.6 \\(\\Omega \\),</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>1</sub> = 4 \\(\\Omega \\), &emsp;R<sub>2</sub> = 6 \\(\\Omega \\),&emsp;R<sub>3</sub> = 1 \\(\\Omega \\),</p><p>E = 12 V,&emsp;r = 0.6 \\(\\Omega \\)</p><p>I<sub>1</sub> = ?&emsp;&emsp;I<sub>2</sub> = ?&emsp;&emsp;I<sub>3</sub> = ?</p><p>V<sub>1</sub> = ?&emsp;&emsp;V<sub>2</sub> = ?&emsp;&emsp;V<sub>3</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>1</sub> and R<sub>2</sub> are connected in parallel,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{1}}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{2}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{5}{12}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R<sub>p</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{12}{5}\\) = 2.4 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>p</sub> and R<sub>3</sub> are connected in series,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>R<sub>p</sub> + R<sub>3</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2.4 + 1 = 3.4 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation, </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{12}{3.4\\,+\\,0.6}\\) = \\(\\frac{12}{4.0}\\) = <strong>3 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>I = I<sub>3</sub> = I<sub>p</sub> = <strong>3 A (in series)</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Ohm’s law,&emsp;V = IR</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sub>3</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I<sub>3</sub> R<sub>3 </sub>= 3 \\(\\times \\) 1 = <strong>3 V</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sub>p</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I<sub>p</sub> R<sub>p </sub>= 3 \\(\\times \\) 2.4 = <strong>7.2 V</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>V<sub>p</sub> = V<sub>1</sub> = V<sub>2</sub> = <strong>7.2 V (in parallel)</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Since, V = I R,&emsp;I = \\(\\frac{V}{R}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{1}}{{R}_{1}}\\) = \\(\\frac{7.2}{4}\\) = <strong>1.8 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{2}}{{R}_{2}}\\) = \\(\\frac{7.2}{6}\\) = <strong>1.2 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>I<sub>1</sub> = 1.8 A&emsp;I<sub>2</sub> = 1.2 A&emsp;I<sub>3</sub> = 3A</p><p>V<sub>1</sub> = 7.2 V&emsp;V<sub>2</sub> = 7.2 V&emsp;V<sub>3</sub> = 3 V</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.4','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Two batteries each having an emf of 6 V and an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω are connected (i) in series and (ii) in parallel. Find the current in each case when the batteries are connected to a 1 Ω resistor. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>E<sub>1</sub> = E<sub>2</sub> = 6 V,&emsp;r<sub>1</sub> = r<sub>2</sub> = 0.5 \\(\\Omega \\),</p><p>R = 1 Ω,&emsp;I = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When the batteries are connected in series,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>In series aiding,</p><p>Resultant emf, E = E<sub>1</sub> + E<sub>2</sub> = 6 + 6 = 12 V</p><p>Resultant r = r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>2</sub> = 0.5 + 0.5 = 1 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{12}{1+\\,1}\\)  = <strong>6 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>In series opposing,</p><p>Resultant emf, E = E<sub>1</sub> - E<sub>2</sub> = 6 - 6 = 0</p><p>Resultant r = r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>2</sub> = 0.5 + 0.5 = 1 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{0}{1+\\,1}\\)  = <strong>0 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When the batteries are connected in Parallel,</p><p>Resultant emf, E = E<sub>1</sub> = E<sub>2</sub> = 6 V</p><p>Resultant r = \\(\\frac{{r}_{1}}{2}\\) = \\(\\frac{0.5}{2}\\) = 0.25 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6}{1\\,+\\,0.25}\\)  = <strong>4.8 A</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.4','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A battery has an emf of 6 V and an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω. How many batteries are necessary to pass a current of 1 A through a 22 Ω resistor in an electric circuit? </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>E<sub>1</sub> = 6 V, r<sub>1</sub> = 0.5 \\(\\Omega \\), R = 22 Ω, I = 1 A</p><p>Number of batteries, n = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Ohm’s law, V = I R = 1 \\(\\times \\) 22 = <strong>22 V</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Since V &gt; E, the batteries must be connected in series aiding.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>In series aiding,</p><p>Resultant emf, E = E<sub>1</sub> + E<sub>2</sub> …… + E<sub>n</sub><sub> </sub></p><p>                           = 6 + 6 + …… + 6 = 6n</p><p>Resultant r = r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>2</sub> …… + r<sub>n</sub><sub> </sub></p><p>                  = 0.5 + 0.5 + …… + 0.5 = 0.5n</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6\\,n}{R\\,+\\,0.5\\,n}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I (R + 0.5 n)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>6 n</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>1 (22 + 0.5 n)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>6 n</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>22 + 0.5 n</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>6 n</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>22</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>5.5 n</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>n</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{22}{5.5}\\) = <strong>4</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\therefore \\) 4 batteries are necessary.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'calculations','No.5','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; When a 12 V battery of negligible internal resistance is connected to a resistor, a current of 3 A flows through it. When another battery of emf 6 V is in the circuit in series with the first one, the current flowing through the resistor remains at 3 A. Find the internal resistance of the second battery.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>E = 12 V,&emsp;r = 0 \\(\\Omega \\),&emsp;I = 3 A</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{12}{R\\,+\\,0}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>3 R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>12</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>4 </strong>\\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>E<sub>1</sub> = 12 V,&emsp;r<sub>1</sub> = 0 \\(\\Omega \\),&emsp;R = 4 \\(\\Omega \\)</p><p>E<sub>2</sub> = 6 V,&emsp;r<sub>2</sub> = ? ,&emsp;&emsp;I = 3 A</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>In series aiding,</p><p>Resultant emf, E = E<sub>1</sub> + E<sub>2</sub> = 12 + 6 = 18 V</p><p>Resultant r = r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>2</sub> = 0 + r<sub>2</sub> = r<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{18}{4\\,+\\,{r}_{2}}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>12 + 3 r<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>18</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>3 r<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>6</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>r<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>2 </strong>\\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\therefore \\) The internal resistance of the second battery is 2 \\(\\Omega \\).</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'calculations','No.6','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; When two 6 V batteries, having the same internal resistance and connected in series, are connected to a 5 \\(\\Omega \\) resistor, the current in the circuit is 2 A. When these batteries are in parallel, a current of 1.5 A flows through when connected to another resistor. Find the resistance of the resistor. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>E<sub>1</sub> = E<sub>2</sub> = 6 V,&emsp;r<sub>1</sub> = r<sub>2</sub>,&emsp;R = 5 \\(\\Omega \\), I = 2 A</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>In series aiding,</p><p>Resultant emf, E = E<sub>1</sub> + E<sub>2</sub> = 6 + 6 = 12 V</p><p>Resultant r = r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>2</sub> = r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>1</sub> = 2 r<sub>1</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>By circuit equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{12}{5\\,+\\,2{r}_{1}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>10 + 4 r<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>12</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>4 r<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>2</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>r<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><strong>0.5 </strong>\\(\\Omega \\)&emsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>r<sub>1</sub> = r<sub>2</sub> = r = 0.5 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>In parallel,</p><p>Resultant emf, E = E<sub>1</sub> = E<sub>2</sub> = 6 V</p><p>Resultant r = \\(\\frac{{r}_{1}}{2}\\) = \\(\\frac{0.5}{2}\\) = 0.25 \\(\\Omega \\) </p><p>I = 1.5 A,&emsp;\\({R}^{''}\\) = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>By circuit equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>1.5</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\,6}{{R}^{''}\\,+\\,0.25}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>1.5 (\\({R}^{''}\\) + 0.25)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>6</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({R}^{''}\\) + 0.25</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6}{1.5}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({R}^{''}\\) + 0.25</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>4</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({R}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>4 – 0.25</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({R}^{''}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>3.75 </strong>\\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.5','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; If a current of 2 A flows through a 50 \\(\\Omega \\) resistor for 30 min find the amount of electrical energy dissipated in the resistor.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>I = 2 A,&emsp;R = 50 \\(\\Omega \\),&emsp;</p><p>t = 30 min = 30 min \\(\\times \\,\\frac{1\\,h}{60\\,\\min}\\) = \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) h,</p><p>W = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I<sup>2</sup> R t</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2<sup>2</sup> \\(\\times \\) 50 \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>100 Wh </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>100 Wh \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{1\\,k\\,\\mathrm{Wh}}{1000\\,\\mathrm{Wh}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.1 k </strong><strong>Wh</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.6','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An electric lamp of 60 Ω connected to a 240 V mains line is used for 45 min. (i) Find the amount of electrical energy dissipated in the lamp. (ii) Find the cost of using it if electricity costs 35 kyats per unit.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R = 60 \\(\\Omega \\),&emsp;V = 240V,</p><p>t = 45 min = 45 min \\(\\times \\,\\frac{1\\,h}{60\\,\\min}\\) = \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) h,</p><p>(i) W = ?&emsp;(ii) cost of using = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}^{2}}{R}\\) t</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{240}^{2}}{60}\\,\\times \\) \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) = 720 Wh</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>720 Wh \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{1\\,k\\,\\mathrm{Wh}}{1000\\,\\mathrm{Wh}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>0.72 k </strong><strong>Wh</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>1 kWh = 1 unit of electricity</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>0.72 kWh = 0.72 unit</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Cost of using 0.72 kWh</p><p>&emsp;= 0.72 \\(\\times \\) 35 = <strong>25.2 kyats</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.6','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; When an air conditioner is connected to a 220 V mains line it draws a current of 10 A and is used for 6 h. (i) Find the amount of electrical energy consumed by it. (ii) Calculate the cost of using it if the electrical energy costs 50 kyats per unit.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>V = 220 V,&emsp;I = 10 A,&emsp;t = 6 h,                 </p><p>(i) W = ?&emsp;(ii) cost of using = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V I t</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>220 \\(\\times \\) 10 \\(\\times \\) 6 = 13200 Wh</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>13200 Wh \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{1\\,k\\,\\mathrm{Wh}}{1000\\,\\mathrm{Wh}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>13.2 k </strong><strong>Wh</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>1 kWh = 1 unit of electricity</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>13.2 kWh = 13.2 unit</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Cost of using 13.2 kWh </p><p>&emsp;= 50 \\(\\times \\,\\)13.2 = <strong>660 kyats</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.7','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; If a 1200 W electric iron is used for 50 min, by how many units does the electricity meter reading increase? Calculate the payment if one unit of electricity costs 35 kyats.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>P = 1200 W,&emsp;</p><p>t = 50 min = 50 min \\(\\times \\,\\frac{1\\,h}{60\\,\\min}\\) = \\(\\frac{5}{6}\\) h,</p><p>W = ?&emsp;&emsp;payment = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{W}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>P t</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1200 \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{5}{6}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1000 Wh \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{1\\,k\\,\\mathrm{Wh}}{1000\\,\\mathrm{Wh}}\\) = <strong>1 k </strong><strong>Wh</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>1 kWh = 1 unit of electricity</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p><strong>The electricity meter reading increases 1 unit of electricity.</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The payment = 1 \\(\\times \\) 35 = <strong>35 kyats</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,11,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.9','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; One 5 Ω, one 10 Ω and one 15 Ω resistors are connected in parallel. If each resistor has an electrical power rating of 0.5 W, find the maximum potential difference which may be supplied to the parallel combination and the current in each resistor.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>1</sub> = 5 Ω, R<sub>2</sub> = 10 Ω, R<sub>3</sub> = 15 Ω,</p><p>P = 0.5 W, V<sub>max</sub> = ? I<sub>1</sub> = ?, I<sub>2</sub> = ?, I<sub>3</sub> = ?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}^{2}}{R}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>P R</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\({V}_{\\max}^{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>P R<sub>min</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.5 \\(\\times \\) 5 = 2.5 </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V<sub>max</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>1.58 V</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For parallel combination, </p><p>V<sub>max</sub> = V<sub>1</sub> = V<sub>2</sub> = V<sub>3</sub> = <strong>1.58 V</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By using Ohm’s law,&emsp;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>V</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I R</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V}{R}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I<sub>1</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{1}}{{R}_{1}}\\) = \\(\\frac{1.58}{5}\\)  = <strong>0.316 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I<sub>2</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{2}}{{R}_{2}}\\) = \\(\\frac{1.58}{10}\\)  = <strong>0.158 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I<sub>3</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{3}}{{R}_{3}}\\) = \\(\\frac{1.58}{15}\\)  = <strong>0.105 A</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,12,true);
INSERT INTO educational_content (grade,category,title,chapter,content,sort_order,active) VALUES
(12,'calculations','Eg.8','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; If a 60 W electric lamp is connected to a 220 V mains line find (i) the current in the lamp (ii) the resistance of tungsten wire of the lamp (iii) the amount of charge passing through the filament in 1 min and (iv) the amount of heat produced by the filament in 1 min.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>P = 60 W,&emsp;V = 220 V</p><p>(i) I = ?&emsp;&emsp;(ii) R = ? </p><p>(iii) Q = ? t = 1 min = 60 s</p><p>(iv) H = ? t = 1 min = 60 s&emsp;</p><p>J = 4.2 J cal<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V I</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{P}{V}\\) = \\(\\frac{60}{220}\\)  = <strong>0.27</strong><strong>27</strong><strong> A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}^{2}}{R}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}^{2}}{P}\\) = \\(\\frac{220\\,\\times \\,220}{60}\\) = <strong>806.67 </strong>\\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iii)</p></td><td><p>Q</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I t</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.2727 \\(\\times \\) 60 = <strong>16.</strong><strong>36</strong><strong> C</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iv)</p></td><td><p>H</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V\\,I\\,t}{J}\\)  = \\(\\frac{P\\,t}{J}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{60\\,\\times \\,60}{4.2}\\)  = <strong>857.14 </strong><strong>cal</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>[OR]</strong></p></td><td><p>H</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}^{2}\\,t}{R\\,J}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{220}^{2}\\,\\times \\,60}{806.67\\,\\times 4.2}\\) = <strong>857.14 </strong><strong>cal</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,13,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.8','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An electric stove of 1200 W is connected to a 220 V mains line. (i) Find its resistance.   (ii) Find the current flowing through it. (iii) Find the amount of calories produced in one second by it. (iv) Find the electrical power produced by it when the voltage of the mains line drops to 180 V.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>P = 1200 W,&emsp;V = 220 V</p><p>(i) R = ?&emsp;(ii) I = ?&emsp;</p><p>(iii) H = ?,        t = 1 s</p><p>(iv) P = ?&emsp;V = 180 V, J = 4.2 J cal<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}^{2}}{R}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}^{2}}{P}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{220\\,\\times \\,220}{1200}\\) = <strong>40.33 </strong>\\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V I</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{P}{V}\\) = \\(\\frac{1200}{220}\\)  = <strong>5.45 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iii)</p></td><td><p>H</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V\\,I\\,t}{J}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{P\\,t}{J}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1200\\,\\times \\,1}{4.2}\\) = <strong>285.71 </strong><strong>cal</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>[OR]</strong></p></td><td><p>H</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> \\(\\frac{{V}^{2}\\,t}{R\\,J}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{220}^{2}\\,\\times \\,1}{40.33\\,\\times 4.2}\\) = <strong>285.71 </strong><strong>cal</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iv)</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}^{2}}{R}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{180\\,\\times \\,180}{40.33}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>803.37 W</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,14,true),
(12,'calculations','No.15','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.15</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An electric iron draws a current of 3 A when it is connected to a 220 V mains line. How many kcal of heat are produced per min?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>I = 3 A,&emsp;V = 220 V, &emsp;H = ? </p><p>t = 1 min = 60 s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V\\,I\\,t}{J}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{220\\,\\times \\,3\\,\\times \\,60}{4.2}\\) = <strong>9428.57 </strong><strong>cal</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>9428.57 cal \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{1\\,k\\,\\mathrm{cal}}{1000\\,\\mathrm{cal}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>9.43 k </strong><strong>cal</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,15,true),
(12,'calculations','No.16','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.16</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Find the amount of calories produced per second <strong>by a 2 </strong>\\(\\Omega \\)<strong> resistor</strong> in the circuit diagram shown below.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R = 2 \\(\\Omega \\),&emsp;E = 6 V,&emsp;r = 1 \\(\\Omega \\) </p><p>H = ?&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;t = 1 s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R+r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6}{2\\,+1}\\) = \\(\\frac{6}{3}\\) = <strong>2 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Joule’s law of electricity and heat,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{I}^{2}\\,R\\,t}{J}\\) &emsp;(by a 2 \\(\\Omega \\))</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\,\\times \\,2\\,\\times \\,2\\,\\times \\,1}{4.2}\\) = <strong>1.905 </strong><strong>cal</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,16,true),
(12,'calculations','No.18','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.18</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Find the amount of heat produced in 10 min <strong>by a 10 </strong>\\(\\Omega \\)<strong> resistor</strong> in the circuit diagram shown below.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R = 10 \\(\\Omega \\)</p><p>E<sub>1</sub> = 6 V,&emsp;r<sub>1</sub> = 0.5 \\(\\Omega \\),</p><p>E<sub>2</sub> = 6 V,&emsp;r<sub>2</sub> = 0.5 \\(\\Omega \\),</p><p>E<sub>3</sub> = 12 V,&emsp;r<sub>3</sub> = 1 \\(\\Omega \\),         </p><p>H = ?&emsp;t = 10 min = 10 \\(\\times \\) 60 = 600 s</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The batteries are connected in series aiding,</p><p>Resultant emf, E = E<sub>1</sub> + E<sub>2</sub> + E<sub>3 </sub></p><p>                            = 6 + 6 + 12 = 24 V</p><p>Resultant r = r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>2</sub> + r<sub>3</sub> </p><p>                  = 0.5 + 0.5 + 1 = 2 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{24}{10\\,+\\,2}\\) = <strong>2 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Joule’s law of electricity and heat,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{I}^{2}\\,R\\,t}{J}\\) &emsp;(by 10 \\(\\Omega \\) resistor)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\,\\times \\,2\\,\\times \\,10\\,\\times 600}{4.2}\\) = <strong>5714.28 </strong><strong>cal</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,17,true),
(12,'calculations','No.17','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.17</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Find the <strong>rate</strong> of production of heat <strong>by the equivalent resistance of resistors</strong> in the circuit diagram shown below. </p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>1</sub> = 2 \\(\\Omega \\), R<sub>2</sub> = 3 \\(\\Omega \\), R<sub>3</sub> = 4 \\(\\Omega \\), </p><p>E = 12 V, r = 1 \\(\\Omega \\),</p><p>\\(\\frac{H}{t}\\) = ?&emsp;<strong>(by the equivalent resistors)</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>2</sub> and R<sub>3</sub> are connected in parallel,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{2}}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{3}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{7}{12}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R<sub>p</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{12}{7}\\) = 1.71 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>p</sub> and R<sub>1</sub> are connected in series,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>R<sub>1</sub> + R<sub>p</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 + 1.71 = 3.71 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{12}{3.71\\,+\\,1}\\) = \\(\\frac{12}{4.71}\\) = <strong>2.55 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Joule’s law of electricity and heat,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{I}^{2}\\,R\\,t}{J}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{H}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{I}^{2}\\,R}{J}\\) (by the equivalent resistors)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2.55\\,\\times \\,2.55\\,\\times \\,3.71}{4.2}\\) = <strong>5.744 </strong><strong>cal</strong><strong> s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,18,true),
(12,'calculations','No.19','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.19</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; Find the <strong>rate</strong> of production of heat <strong>in the battery</strong> in the circuit diagram shown below.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>E = 12 V, r = 2 \\(\\Omega \\),</p><p>R<sub>1</sub> = 1 \\(\\Omega \\), R<sub>2</sub> = 1 \\(\\Omega \\), R<sub>3</sub> = 1.5 \\(\\Omega \\),         </p><p>\\(\\frac{H}{t}\\) = ?            <strong>(in the battery)</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>1</sub> and R<sub>2</sub> are connected in parallel,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{1}}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{{R}_{2}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{1}\\) + \\(\\frac{1}{1}\\)  =  \\(\\frac{1\\,+\\,1}{1}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{R}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2}{1}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) = 0.5 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>p</sub> and R<sub>3</sub> are connected in series,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>R<sub>p</sub> + R<sub>3</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.5 + 1.5 = 2 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By circuit equation,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{E}{R\\,+\\,r}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{12}{2\\,+\\,2}\\) = \\(\\frac{12}{4}\\) = <strong>3 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Joule’s law of electricity and heat,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>H</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{I}^{2}\\,R\\,t}{J}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{H}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{I}^{2}\\,R}{J}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{H}{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{I}^{2}\\,r}{J}\\) &emsp;(in the battery)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{3\\,\\times \\,3\\,\\times \\,\\,2}{4.2}\\) = <strong>4.286 </strong><strong>cal</strong><strong> s</strong><sup><strong>-1</strong></sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,19,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.10','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; What should the rating of the fuse be used for an electric stove of 1200 W, 220 V.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>P = 1200 W,&emsp;V = 220V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V I</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{P}{V}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1200}{220}\\) = <strong>5.45 A</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>1200 W electric stove will draw 5.45 A to operate.</p><p>The rating of the fuse should be <strong>6 A</strong>.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,20,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.10','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; A 3 A fuse is used in a circuit which contains a source of 220 V. Find the maximum power which can safely be consumed.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>I<sub>max</sub> = 3 A (fuse),&emsp;V = 220V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P<sub>max</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V I<sub>max</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>220 \\(\\times \\) 3 = <strong>660 W</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,21,true),
(12,'calculations','No.22','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.22</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An electric circuit installed in a house contains a 5 A fuse and the voltage is 220 V. Find the maximum electrical power which can safely be used?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>I<sub>max</sub> = 5 A (fuse),&emsp;V = 220V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P<sub>max</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V I<sub>max</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>220 \\(\\times \\) 5 = <strong>1100 W</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,22,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.9','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An electric circuit installed in a house contains a 5 A fuse and the voltage is 220 V. Can twenty 60 W electric lamps be used at the same time in that circuit?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>I<sub>max</sub> = 5 A (fuse),&emsp;V = 220V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P<sub>max</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V I<sub>max</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>220 \\(\\times \\) 5 = <strong>1100 W</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Electrical power of twenty 60 W electric lamps,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P<sub>used</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>20 \\(\\times \\) 60 = <strong>1200 W</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Since, P<sub>used</sub> &gt; P<sub>max</sub></p><p><strong>No,</strong> twenty 60 W electric lamps cannot be used at the same time in that circuit.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,23,true),
(12,'calculations','No.23','10','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.23</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp; An electric circuit installed in an office contains a 10 A fuse and the voltage is 220 V. Ten 100 W electric lamps and two 150 W refrigerators are being used there. (i) Find the cost of using all the lamps and two refrigerators for 10 h. (ii) Find the maximum number of   60 W electric lamps which can be safely used in addition. (Assume that electricity costs 50 kyats per unit)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Ans:</strong>&emsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>I<sub>max</sub> = 10 A (fuse),&emsp;V = 220V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P<sub>max</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V I<sub>max</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>220 \\(\\times \\) 10 = <strong>2200 W</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Electrical power of Ten 100 W electric lamps and two 150 W refrigerators,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>P<sub>used</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>[10\\(\\times \\)100] + [2\\(\\times \\)150] = <strong>1300 W</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{W}{t}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>W</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>P<sub>used</sub> t</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1300 \\(\\times \\) 10 = 13 000 Wh</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>13 000 Wh \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{1\\,k\\,\\mathrm{Wh}}{1000\\,\\mathrm{Wh}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p><strong>13 kWh</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>1 kWh = 1 unit of electricity</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>13 kWh = 13 unit</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Cost of using 13 kWh = 50 \\(\\times \\,\\)13 = <strong>650 kyats</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Remaining power</p><p>&emsp;= P<sub>max</sub> – P<sub>used</sub> = 2200 – 1300 = 900 W</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>n = \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{Remaining}\\,\\mathrm{power}}{60}\\)  = \\(\\frac{900}{60}\\) = <strong>15 lamps</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The maximum number of 60 W electric lamps which can be safely used in addition is 15 lamps.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,24,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; An AC generator has an output given by E = 150 sin 377 t. (i) Find the maximum emf output, the frequency of the source, and the emf and t = \\(\\frac{1}{120}\\) s. (ii) Find the maximum current in the circuit when generator is connected to a 50 \\(\\Omega \\) resistor in the figure.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>E = 150 sin 377 t</p><p>(i) E<sub>m</sub> = ? f = ? &nbsp; E = ?    at t = \\(\\frac{1}{120}\\) s</p><p>(ii) I<sub>m</sub> = ? &nbsp; R = 50 \\(\\Omega \\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By comparing E = E<sub>m</sub> sin (\\(\\omega \\) t)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>E<sub>m</sub> = 150 V,</p><p>\\(\\omega \\) = 377 rad s<sup>-1 </sup>= \\(\\frac{377\\ \\pi }{\\pi }\\) = 120 \\(\\pi \\) rad s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>E<sub>m</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>150 V</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\omega \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\pi \\) f</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>f</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\omega }{2\\ \\pi }\\)  = \\(\\frac{120\\ \\pi }{2\\ \\pi }\\) = 60 Hz</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>E</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>150 sin (377 t)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>150 sin (120 \\(\\pi \\) \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{1}{120}\\))</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>150 sin (\\(\\pi \\))</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>150 \\(\\times \\) sin (180) = 0</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>E<sub>m</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I<sub>m</sub> R</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I<sub>m</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{E}_{m}}{R}\\) = \\(\\frac{150}{50}\\) = 3 A</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; The current in an AC circuit at any time t seconds is given by I = 20 sin (100 \\(\\pi \\) t) A. Find (i) the peak value (maximum value) of current, the period and the frequency (ii) the value of the current when t = 0 (iii) the value of the current when t = 8 ms and (iv) the time when the current reaches 10 A.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>I = 20 sin (100 \\(\\pi \\) t) A</p><p>(i) I<sub>m</sub> = ? &nbsp; T = ? &nbsp; f = ?</p><p>(ii)  I = ? &nbsp; When, t = 0 s</p><p>(iii) I = ? &nbsp; When, t = 8 ms = 8 \\(\\times \\ {10}^{-3}\\) s</p><p>(iii) t = ? &nbsp; When, I = 10 A</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>By comparing I = I<sub>m</sub> sin (\\(\\omega \\) t)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>I<sub>m</sub> = 20 A, &nbsp; \\(\\omega \\) = 100 \\(\\pi \\) rad s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>I<sub>m</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>20 A</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\omega \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>2 \\(\\pi \\) f</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>f</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{\\omega }{2\\ \\pi }\\)  = \\(\\frac{100\\ \\pi \\ }{2\\ \\pi \\ }\\) = 50 Hz</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>T</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{f}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{50}\\) = 0.02 s = 20 ms</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>20 sin (100 \\(\\pi \\ \\times \\) 0)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>0</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iii)</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>20 sin (100 \\(\\pi \\times 8\\ \\times {10}^{-3}\\)) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>11.76 A</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iv)</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>20 sin (100 \\(\\pi \\) t)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>20 sin (100 \\(\\times \\) 180 t)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>0.5</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>sin (100 \\(\\times \\) 180 t)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>100 \\(\\times \\) 180 t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>sin<sup>-1</sup> 0.5</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>100 \\(\\times \\) 180 t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>30</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{30}{100\\ \\times 180}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1.67 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-3 </sup>s</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; A square loop of wire 10 cm on a side is in a magnetic field of 1.25 T. What are the maximum and minimum values of flux that can pass through the loop?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = 10 cm \\(\\times \\) 10 cm = 100 cm<sup>2</sup> </p><p>   = 100 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-4</sup> m<sup>2</sup> = 10<sup>-2</sup> m<sup>2</sup></p><p>B = 1.25 T</p><p>\\({\\phi }_{B}\\) = ? (for maximum and minimum) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({\\phi }_{B}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>B A cos \\(\\theta \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For maximum value, &nbsp; \\(\\theta \\) = 0\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({\\phi }_{B}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>B A cos 0\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1.25 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-2</sup> \\(\\times \\) 1 = 0.0125 Wb</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>For minimum value, &nbsp; \\(\\theta \\) = 90\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({\\phi }_{B}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>B A cos 90\\(^\\circ \\) = 0</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','No.9','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; A square loop of wire of side 5.0 cm is in a uniform magnetic field 0.16 T. What is the magnetic flux in the loop (i) when magnetic flied is perpendicular to the surface of the loop and (ii) when magnetic filed is at an angle of 30\\(^\\circ \\) to the surface of the loop?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>A = 5 cm \\(\\times \\) 5 cm = 25 cm<sup>2</sup> = 25 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-4</sup> m<sup>2</sup> </p><p>B = 0.16 T</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>(i)  \\({\\phi }_{B}\\) = ? \\(\\theta \\) = 0\\(^\\circ \\ \\)(ii)  \\({\\phi }_{B}\\) = ? \\(\\theta \\) = 60\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({\\phi }_{B}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>B A cos \\(\\theta \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When \\(\\vec{B}\\) is perpendicular to the surface of loop,    \\(\\theta \\) = 0\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>  \\({\\phi }_{B}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>B A cos 0\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.16 \\(\\times \\) 25 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-4</sup> \\(\\times \\) 1</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>4 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-4</sup> Wb</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>When \\(\\vec{B}\\) is at angle of 30\\(^\\circ \\) to surface,</p><p>\\(\\theta \\) = 90\\(^\\circ \\) - 30\\(^\\circ \\) = 60\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({\\phi }_{B}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>B A cos 60\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.16 \\(\\times \\) 25 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-4</sup> \\(\\times \\) cos 60\\(^\\circ \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-4</sup> Wb</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.4','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; A generator coil with 200 turns is rotated through one-fourth of a revolution in 15 ms. The turn of circular coil has a 5 cm radius and is in a uniform magnetic field of 1.25 T. Find the induced emf in 15 ms.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>N = 200 turns, &nbsp; \\(\\Delta \\) t = 15 ms = 15 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)s,</p><p>r = 5 cm = 5 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\) m, B = 1.25 T, E = ?</p><p>A = \\(\\pi \\ {r}^{2}\\) = 3.142 \\(\\times \\ {(5\\times \\ {10}^{-2})}^{2}\\) m<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({\\phi }_{B}\\) = B A cos \\(\\theta \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Since the area of the loop and magnetic flies are constant, change in magnetic flux due to rotational angle from 0\\(^\\circ \\) to 90\\(^\\circ \\) (one-fourth of a revolution)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\Delta {\\ \\phi }_{B}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>B A \\(\\Delta \\) (cos \\(\\theta \\))</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1.25 \\(\\times \\) 3.142 \\(\\times \\ {(5\\times \\ {10}^{-2})}^{2}\\ \\times \\) (cos 90\\(^\\circ \\) – cos 0\\(^\\circ \\))</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>- 0.0098 Wb</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>E</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>- N \\(\\frac{d{\\phi }_{B}}{dt}\\)  = - N \\(\\frac{∆{\\phi }_{B}}{∆t}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>- 200 \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{(\\ -0.0098\\ )}{(\\ 15\\ \\times {10}^{-3})}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>130.92 V</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'calculations','No.10','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; A circular coil of radius 8 cm and 20 turns is rotated about its vertical diameter with an angular speed of 150 rad s<sup>-1</sup> in a uniform horizontal magnetic field of 3 \\(\\times \\ {10}^{-2}\\) T. Obtain the maximum emf induced in the coil. If the coil forms a closed loop of resistance 10 \\(\\Omega \\), calculate the maximum value of current in the coil.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>N = 20 turns, &nbsp; r = 8 cm = 8 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\) m,</p><p>\\(\\omega \\) = 150 rad s<sup>-1</sup>, B = 3 \\(\\times \\ {10}^{-2}\\) T, E<sub>m</sub> = ?                 </p><p>R = 10 \\(\\Omega \\), &nbsp;  &nbsp; I<sub>m</sub> = ?</p><p>A = \\(\\pi \\ {r}^{2}\\) = 3.142 \\(\\times \\ {(8\\times \\ {10}^{-2})}^{2}\\) m<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>E<sub>m</sub> </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>N B A \\(\\omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>20 \\(\\ \\times \\) 3 \\(\\times \\ {10}^{-2}\\) \\(\\times \\) 3.142 \\(\\times {(8\\times \\ {10}^{-2})}^{2}\\times \\) 150</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1.81 V</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>E<sub>m</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I<sub>m</sub> R</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I<sub>m</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{E}_{m}}{R}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1.81}{10}\\)  = 0.181 A</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'calculations','No.11','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; The armature of a 60 Hz AC generator rotates in a magnetic field of 0.15 T. If the area of the coil is 2.0 \\(\\times \\ {10}^{-2}\\) m<sup>2</sup>, how many loops must the coil contain if the maximum output is to be 170 V.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>f = 60 Hz, &nbsp; B = 0.15 T,</p><p>A = 2.0 \\(\\times {10}^{-2}\\) m<sup>2</sup>, E<sub>m</sub> = 170 V, N = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\omega \\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\pi \\) f</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\(\\times \\) 3.142 \\(\\times \\) 60 = 377.04 rad s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>E<sub>m</sub> </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>N B A \\(\\omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>N</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{E}_{m}}{B\\ A\\ \\omega }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{170}{0.15\\times \\ 2.0\\ \\times \\ {10}^{-2}\\ \\times 377.04}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>N</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>150 turns</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.5','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; A step-down transformer is used to light a 12 V, 24 W lamp from the 240 V mains. The current through the primary is 125 mA. What is the efficiency of the transformer?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Primary coil</p><p>V<sub>p</sub> = 240 V</p><p>I<sub>p</sub> = 125 mA</p><p>   = 125 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) A</p></td><td><p>Secondary coil</p><p>V<sub>s</sub> = 12 V</p><p>P <sub>out</sub> = 24 W</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>Efficiency = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>P<sub>in</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>V<sub>p</sub> I<sub>p</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>240 \\(\\times \\) 125 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>30 W</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>Efficiency</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{P}_{out}}{{P}_{in}}\\ \\times 100\\%\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{24\\ W}{30\\ W}\\ \\times 100\\%\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>80 \\(\\%\\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.6','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; A 2 kW transformer is used to step down an AC supply of 240 V to 60 V (i) What is the turns ratio of this transformer? (ii) What will the output current be if there is a 10\\(\\%\\) power loss in the transformer? (iii) How large is the output current if there is no power loss (i.e. 100\\(\\%\\) efficiency)?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Primary coil</p><p>V<sub>p</sub> = 240 V</p><p>P <sub>in</sub> = 2 kW </p><p>      = 2 \\(\\times {10}^{3}\\) W</p></td><td><p>Secondary coil</p><p>V<sub>s</sub> = 60 V</p><p>P <sub>out</sub> = V<sub>s</sub> I<sub>s</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>(i)   turns ratio, \\(\\frac{{N}_{s}}{{N}_{p}}\\) = ?</p><p>(ii)  I<sub>s</sub> = ? &nbsp; power loss = 10\\(\\%\\) </p><p>(iii) I<sub>s</sub> = ? &nbsp; no power loss</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{s}}{{N}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{s}}{{V}_{p}}\\) = \\(\\frac{60}{240}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{s}}{{N}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>N<sub>s</sub> : N<sub>p</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>1 : 4</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>If there is a 10\\(\\%\\) power loss </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{P}_{\\ out}}{{P}_{\\ in}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>90\\(\\%\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>P<sub> out</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{90}{100}\\) \\(\\times \\) P<sub> in</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I<sub>s</sub> V<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(0.9\\times \\) P<sub> in</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{0.9\\ \\times \\ {P}_{in}}{{V}_{s}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{0.9\\ \\times \\ 2\\ \\times {10}^{3}}{60}\\)  = 30 A</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iii)</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>If there is no power loss </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{P}_{\\ out}}{{P}_{\\ in}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>100\\(\\%\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>P<sub> out</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{100}{100}\\) \\(\\times \\) P<sub> in</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>P<sub> out</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>P<sub> in</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I<sub>s</sub> V<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>2 \\(\\times {10}^{3}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{2\\ \\times {10}^{3}}{{V}_{s}}\\) = \\(\\frac{2\\ \\times {10}^{3}}{60}\\) = 33.33 A</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','No.12','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.12</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; One coil of a transformer has 50 turns and the other coil has 1000 turns. The alternating voltage of 220 V is applied to the primary. Find the alternating voltage from the secondary when it is used as (i) a step-up transformer and (ii) a step-down transformer.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>N<sub>1</sub> = 50 turns, &nbsp; N<sub>2</sub> = 1000 turns</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Primary coil</p><p>V<sub>p</sub> = 220 V</p></td><td><p>Secondary coil</p><p>V<sub>s</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>As a step-up transformer, &nbsp; N<sub>s</sub> &gt; N<sub>p</sub> </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>N<sub>s</sub> = 1000 turns, &nbsp;  N<sub>p</sub> = 50 turns</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{s}}{{V}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{s}}{{N}_{p}}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{s}}{220}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{1000}{50}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>4 400 V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>As a step-down transformer, &nbsp; N<sub>s</sub> &lt; N<sub>p</sub> </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>N<sub>s</sub> = 50 turns, &nbsp; N<sub>p</sub> = 1000 turns</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{s}}{{V}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{s}}{{N}_{p}}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{s}}{220}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{50}{1000}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>11 V</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','No.13','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.13</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; The primary coil of a step-up transformer having 220 turns is connected to a 110 V alternating voltage source. The secondary delivers a voltage of 12 000 V and a current of 40 mA. (i) How many turns are there in the secondary? (ii) What is the current in the primary? (iii) What is the power output?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Primary coil</p><p>N<sub>p</sub> = 220 turns</p><p>V<sub>p</sub> = 110 V</p></td><td><p>Secondary coil</p><p>V<sub>s</sub> = 12 000 V</p><p>I<sub>s </sub> = 40 mA = 40 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) A</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>(i) N<sub>s</sub> = ? &nbsp; (ii) I<sub>p</sub> = ? &nbsp; (iii) P<sub>out</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{s}}{{N}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{s}}{{V}_{p}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{s}}{220}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{12\\ 000}{110}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>N<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>24 000 turns</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{s}}{{V}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{I}_{p}}{{I}_{s}}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{12\\ 000}{110}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{I}_{p}}{40\\ \\times {10}^{-3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I<sub>p</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>4.364 A</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iii)</p></td><td><p>P<sub>out</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>V<sub>s</sub> I<sub>s</sub> </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>12 000 \\(\\times \\) 40 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) = 480 W</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,11,true),
(12,'calculations','No.14','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.14</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; An electric welding machine uses a current of 400 A. The machine has a transformer whose primary coil has 400 turns and draws 4 A from a 220 V power line. (i) How many turns does the secondary coil have? (ii) What is the voltage across the secondary coil?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Primary coil</p><p>N<sub>p</sub> = 400 turns</p><p>V<sub>p</sub> = 220 V</p><p>I<sub>p</sub> = 4 A</p></td><td><p>Secondary coil</p><p>I<sub>s </sub> = 400 A</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>(i) N<sub>s</sub> = ? &nbsp; (ii) V<sub>s</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{s}}{{N}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{I}_{p}}{{I}_{s}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{s}}{400}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{4}{400}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>N<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>4 turns</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{s}}{{V}_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{I}_{p}}{{I}_{s}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{s}}{220}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{4}{400}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>2.2 V</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,12,true),
(12,'calculations','No.15','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.15</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; A transformer has 2000 turns in primary, 100 turns in secondary and its efficiency 100\\(\\%\\). It is used for 10 V, 40 W bulb. Calculate (i) the supply voltage and (ii) the current through the input coil.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Primary coil</p><p>N<sub>p</sub> = 2000 turns</p></td><td><p>Secondary coil</p><p>N<sub>s</sub> = 100 turns</p><p>V<sub>s</sub> = 10 V</p><p>P<sub>out</sub> = 40 W</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>(i) V<sub>p</sub> = ? &nbsp; (ii) I<sub>p</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>For 100\\(\\%\\) efficiency, P<sub>out</sub> = P<sub>in</sub> = 40 W</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{p}}{{V}_{s}}\\)  </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{p}}{{N}_{s}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{p}}{10}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{2000}{100}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>p</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>200 V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>P<sub>in</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>I<sub>p</sub> V<sub>p</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>40</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>I<sub>p</sub> V<sub>p</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I<sub>p</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{40}{{V}_{p}}\\) = \\(\\frac{40}{200}\\) = 0.2 A</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,13,true);
INSERT INTO educational_content (grade,category,title,chapter,content,sort_order,active) VALUES
(12,'calculations','No.16','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.16</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; 120 kW of electric power is sent to a small town from a power plant 10 km away. The transmission lines have a resistance of 0.40 Ω per km. Calculate the power loss if the power is transmitted at (i) 240 V and (ii) 24 000 V.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>P = 120 kW = 120 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>3</sup> W</p><p>For 1 km, R = 0.40 Ω</p><p>For 10 km, R = 0.40 \\(\\times \\) 10 = 4 Ω</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>(i) P<sub>loss</sub> = ?, V = 240 V</p><p>(ii) P<sub>loss</sub> = ?, V = 24 000 V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V I</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{P}{V}\\) = \\(\\frac{120\\ \\times \\ {10}^{3}}{240}\\) = \\(\\frac{1000}{2}\\) = 500 A</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>P<sub>loss</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I<sup>2</sup> R = 500<sup>2</sup> \\(\\times \\) 4</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>100 0000 = 1000 kW</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>P</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V I</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{P}{V}\\) = \\(\\frac{120\\ \\times \\ {10}^{3}}{24\\ 000}\\) = \\(\\frac{1000}{200}\\) = 5 A</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>P<sub>loss</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I<sup>2</sup> R = 5<sup>2</sup> \\(\\times \\) 4</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>25 \\(\\times \\) 4 = 100 = 100 W</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,14,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.7','11','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; If an electrician accidentally touches a live wire of 220 V, what possible effect would he experience if his skin (i) were dry and had a resistance of 100 k\\(\\Omega \\)? (ii) were wet and had a resistance of 1000 \\(\\Omega \\).</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>V = 220 V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>If his skin were dry,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>100 k\\(\\Omega \\) = 100 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>3 </sup>\\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Ohm’s law,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>IR</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V}{R}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{220}{100\\ \\times \\ {10}^{3}}\\) = 2.2 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-3</sup> A = 2.2 mA</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The electrician would experience a mild shock.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>If his skin were wet,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1000 \\(\\Omega \\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>IR</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{V}{R}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{220}{1000}\\) = 220 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-3</sup> A = 220 mA</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The electrician would be electrocuted.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,15,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Figure shows the basic zener diode circuits. What will be the circuit behaviour if the zener diode is (i) working properly (ii) shorted and (ii) open-circuited? </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"4\"></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>If the zener diode is working properly, the voltage 𝑉<sub>0</sub> across the load (5 kΩ) will be nearly 6 V.</p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>If the zener diode is short, the voltage 𝑉<sub>0</sub> across the load will be 0 V. The same problem could also be caused by a shorted load resistor (5 kΩ) or an opened source resistor (1 kΩ).</p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>(iii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>If the zener diode is open-circuited, the voltage 𝑉<sub>0</sub> across the load (5 kΩ) is</p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>R<sub>total</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>R<sub>1</sub> + R<sub>2</sub> (in series)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>1 + 5 = 6 kΩ</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>By Ohm’s law,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>I R</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{V}{R}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>\\(\\frac{12}{6\\ \\times \\ {10}^{3}}\\) = 2 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) A</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>I<sub>1</sub> = I<sub>2</sub> = I = 2 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) A (in series)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"4\"><p>V<sub>0</sub> = V<sub>2</sub> = I<sub>2</sub> R<sub>2</sub> </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"2\"><p>2 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) \\(\\times \\) 5 \\(\\times {10}^{3}\\) = 10 V</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; An LED is lit from a 9 V supply and takes a current of 15 mA. Calculate the value of the current limiting resistor required for the LED. (Assume that the forward voltage drop will be 2 V).</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>V<sub>s</sub> = 9 V, I = 15 mA = 15 \\(\\times \\ {10}^{-3}\\) A,</p><p>V<sub>f</sub> = 2 V, &nbsp; R = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V<sub>f</sub> + V<sub>R</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>R</sub></p></td><td><p>= </p></td><td><p>\\({V}_{s}\\ -\\ {V}_{f}\\) = 9 – 2 = 7 V</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Ohm’s law,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>R</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I R</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{R}}{I}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{7}{15\\ \\times \\ {10}^{-3}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>466.67 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.3','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; An amber-coloured LED with a forward voltage drop of 2 V is to be connected to a 5 V stabilized DC power supply. Calculate the value of the series resistor required to limit the forward current to less than 10 mA. Also calculate the current flowing through the diode if a 100 Ω of current limiting resistor is used.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>V<sub>f</sub> = 2 V, &nbsp; V<sub>s </sub>= 5 V,          </p><p>I = 10 mA = 10 \\(\\times {10}^{-3}\\) A, &nbsp; R = ? </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V<sub>f</sub> + V<sub>R</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>R</sub></p></td><td><p>= </p></td><td><p>\\({V}_{s}-\\ {V}_{f}\\) = 5 – 2 = 3 V</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Ohm’s law,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>R</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> I R</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>R</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{R}}{I}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{3\\ }{10\\ \\times \\ {10}^{-3}}\\)  = 300 \\(\\Omega \\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>If R = 100 Ω, &nbsp; I = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>R</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I R</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{R}}{R}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{3\\ }{100}\\) = 0.03 A = 30 mA</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; In the figure the resistance of R<sub>2</sub> is 2000  and V<sub>in</sub> is 6 V. (i) In daylight the resistance of R<sub>1</sub> is 500 . Calculate the voltage across R<sub>2</sub>. (ii) In the dark the resistance of R<sub>1</sub> is         198 000 . Calculate the voltage across R<sub>2</sub>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R<sub>2</sub> = 2000 , &nbsp;  &nbsp; V<sub>in</sub> = 6 V,               </p><p>(i)  In daylight, R<sub>1</sub> = 500 , V<sub>2</sub> = V<sub>out</sub> = ?</p><p>(ii) In dark, R<sub>1</sub> = 198 000 , V<sub>2</sub> = V<sub>out</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Ohm’s law,</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{in}}{{R}_{1}+\\ {R}_{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6}{500\\ +\\ 2000}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2.4\\(\\times \\)10<sup>-3</sup> A (or) 2.4 mA</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>2</sub> = V<sub>out</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I R<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.0024 \\(\\times \\) 2000 = 4.8 V</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{in}}{{R}_{1}+\\ {R}_{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6}{198\\ 000\\ +\\ 2000}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>30\\(\\times \\)10<sup>-6</sup> A (or) 30 \\(\\mu \\)A</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>2</sub> = V<sub>out</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I R<sub>2</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>30\\(\\times \\)10<sup>-6</sup> \\(\\times \\) 2000 = 0.06 V</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.6','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; The circuit shows a potential divider, which consists of a fixed resistor and a light dependent resistor (LDR). The potential divider is used to switch on a lamp when it gets dark. The resistance of fixed resistor is 20 k. The potential difference across XY is 4 V when the lamp is switched on. What is the resistance of the light-dependent resistor (LDR)? (Hint: V<sub>s</sub> = V<sub>R</sub> + V<sub>LDR </sub>, I = \\(\\frac{{V}_{R}}{R}\\) , R<sub>LDR</sub> = \\(\\frac{{V}_{LDR}}{I}\\) )</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R = 20 k = 20 000 , &nbsp; V<sub>s</sub> = 6 V,               </p><p>V<sub>LDR</sub> = 4 V, &nbsp; R<sub>LDR</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V<sub>R</sub> + V<sub>LDR</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>R</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V<sub>s</sub> - V<sub>LDR</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>6 – 4 = 2 V</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Ohm’s law,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>R</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I R</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{R}}{R}\\) = \\(\\frac{2}{20\\ 000}\\) = 10<sup>-4</sup> A</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>LDR</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I R<sub>LDR</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>R<sub>LDR</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{LDR}}{I}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{4}{{10}^{-4}}\\) = 4 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>4</sup> = 40 k</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'calculations','No.2','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; A potential divider consists of an LDR and a resistor connected to a 6 V battery in the following figure. What should be the resistance of the LDR for the output to be 2.5 V?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>R = 10 k = 10 000 , &nbsp; V<sub>s</sub> = 6 V,               </p><p>V<sub>LDR</sub> = 2.5 V, &nbsp;  &nbsp; R<sub>LDR</sub> = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>s</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V<sub>R</sub> + V<sub>LDR</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>R</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>V<sub>s</sub> - V<sub>LDR</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>6 – 2.5 = 3.5 V</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By Ohm’s law,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>R</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I R</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>I</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{R}}{R}\\) = \\(\\frac{3.5}{10\\ 000}\\) = 3.5 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-4</sup> A</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>V<sub>LDR</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>I R<sub>LDR</sub></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>R<sub>LDR</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{V}_{LDR}}{I}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2.5}{{3.5\\ \\times \\ 10}^{-4}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.714 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>4</sup> = 7.14 k</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Check the following logic system carefully and then construct the truth table that follows:</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p>Ans:</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.4','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Check the following logic system carefully and then construct the truth table that follows:</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p>Ans:</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.10','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Write the truth table of the following circuit. To what gate is it equivalent?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p>Ans: &nbsp;  &nbsp; </p><p> &nbsp; It is equivalent to exclusive OR (XOR) gate.</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','No.5','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; In the giving table, P, Q, R and S are the outputs of four logic gates. Name the logic gate which represents each output.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p>Ans: &nbsp; The output P is AND gate.</p><p> &nbsp; The output Q is OR gate.</p><p> &nbsp; The output R is NAND gate.</p><p> &nbsp; The output S is NOR gate.</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','No.9','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Construct a truth table for each of the followings: </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p> &nbsp; (i) AB + BC  &nbsp;  &nbsp; (ii) (A + B) C </p><p> &nbsp; (iii) (A + B) (\\(\\overline{B}\\) + C)</p><p>Ans: &nbsp; (i) AB + BC</p><p> &nbsp; (ii) (A + B) C</p><p> &nbsp; (iii) (A + B) (\\(\\overline{B}\\) + C)</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,11,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.11','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; For the circuit below, write the value of Z as a Boolean expression, using A and B.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p>Ans: &nbsp;  &nbsp; Z = \\(\\overline{A}\\) + B</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,12,true),
(12,'calculations','No.8','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Draw the logic circuit represented by each of the following expressions: </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p> &nbsp; (i) A + B + C &nbsp; (ii) ABC  &nbsp;  &nbsp; </p><p> &nbsp; (iii) AB + C  &nbsp;  &nbsp; (iv) AB + CD</p><p>Ans: &nbsp; (i) A + B + C</p><p> &nbsp; (ii) ABC</p><p> &nbsp; (iii) AB + C</p><p> &nbsp; (iv) AB + CD</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,13,true),
(12,'calculations','No.7','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Simplify the following expressions if possible:</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p> &nbsp; (i) A + AB + A\\(\\overline{B}\\)C</p><p> &nbsp; (ii) (\\(\\overline{A}\\) + B) C + ABC</p><p>Ans: &nbsp; (i) A + AB + A\\(\\overline{B}\\)C </p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = A (1 + B) + A\\(\\overline{B}\\)C</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = A \\(⋅\\) 1 + A\\(\\overline{B}\\)C &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\) 1 + B = 1)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = A + A\\(\\overline{B}\\)C &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\) A \\(⋅\\) 1 = A)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = A (1 + \\(\\overline{B}\\)C)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = A \\(⋅\\) 1 &nbsp;  &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\) 1 + \\(\\overline{B}\\)C = 1)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = A &nbsp;  &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\) A \\(⋅\\) 1 = A)</p><p> &nbsp; (ii) (\\(\\overline{A}\\) + B) C + ABC</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = \\(\\overline{A}\\)C + BC + ABC</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = \\(\\overline{A}\\)C + BC (1 + A)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = \\(\\overline{A}\\)C + BC \\(⋅\\) 1 &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\) 1 + A = 1)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = \\(\\overline{A}\\)C + BC &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\) BC \\(⋅\\) 1 = BC)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = (\\(\\overline{A}\\) + B) C</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,14,true),
(12,'calculations','No.10','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Find the value of X for all possible values of variables. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p> &nbsp; (i) X = (A + B)C + B  &nbsp; (ii) X = (\\(\\overline{A+B}\\))C </p><p> &nbsp; (iii) X = A\\(\\overline{B}\\)C + AB</p><p>Ans: &nbsp; (i) X = (A + B)C + B</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = AC + BC + B</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = AC + B(C + 1)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = AC + B \\(⋅\\) 1 &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\) C + 1 = 1)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = AC + B &nbsp;  &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\) B \\(⋅\\) 1 = B)</p><p> &nbsp; (ii) X = (\\(\\overline{A+B}\\))C ဒီမောဂင်း သီအိုရမ်သုံးရန်</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = \\(\\overline{A}\\) \\(\\overline{B}\\) C &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\overline{A+B}\\) = \\(\\overline{A}\\) \\(\\overline{B}\\))</p><p> &nbsp; (iii) X = A\\(\\overline{B}\\)C + AB</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = A (\\(\\overline{B}\\)C + B)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = A (C + B) &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\) \\(\\overline{B}\\)C + B = C + B)</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,15,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.5','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Simplify the expression AB + A (B + C) + B (B + C) and draw the equivalent gate diagram.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p>Ans: &nbsp; AB + A (B + C) + B (B + C)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = AB + AB + AC + BB + BC</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = AB + AB + AC + B + BC &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\)BB = B)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = AB + AC + B + BC &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\)AB + AB = AB)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = AB + AC + B &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\) B + BC = B)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = B + AC &nbsp;  &nbsp; (\\(\\because \\) AB + B = B)</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,16,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.6','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Apply De Morgan&#x27;s theorems to the expression \\(\\overline{XYZ}\\) and \\(\\overline{X\\ +\\ Y\\ +\\ Z}\\).</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p>Ans: &nbsp; \\(\\overline{XYZ}\\) = \\(\\overline{X}\\) + \\(\\overline{Y}\\) + \\(\\overline{Z}\\)</p><p> &nbsp; \\(\\overline{X\\ +\\ Y\\ +\\ Z}\\) = \\(\\overline{X}\\) \\(\\overline{Y}\\) \\(\\overline{Z}\\)</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,17,true),
(12,'calculations','No.11','12','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.11</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Apply De Morgan&#x27;s theorems to the expression \\(\\overline{\\overline{ABC}}\\) and \\(\\overline{\\overline{A}\\ +\\ \\overline{B}\\ +\\ \\overline{C}\\ +\\overline{D}}\\).</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p>Ans: &nbsp; \\(\\overline{\\overline{ABC}}\\) = \\(\\overline{\\overline{A}\\ +\\ \\overline{B}\\ +\\ \\overline{C}}\\) = \\(\\overline{\\overline{A}}\\) \\(\\overline{\\overline{B}}\\) \\(\\overline{\\overline{C}}\\) = A B C</p><p> &nbsp; \\(\\overline{\\overline{A}\\ +\\ \\overline{B}\\ +\\ \\overline{C}\\ +\\overline{D}}\\) = \\(\\overline{\\overline{A}}\\) \\(\\overline{\\overline{B}}\\) \\(\\overline{\\overline{C}}\\) \\(\\overline{\\overline{D}}\\) = A B C D</p></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,18,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.1','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Suppose there was 2 g of radon at t = 0 and its half-life is 3.8 days. How much would be left after 15.2 days?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Initial amount = 2 g, &nbsp; </p><p>half-life, \\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\) = 3.8 days, &nbsp; </p><p>time elapsed, t = 15.2 days</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Number of half-life, n = \\(\\frac{time\\ elasped}{half-life}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p> &nbsp; = \\(\\frac{15.2}{3.8}\\) = 4</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Amount left after n half-life</p><p> &nbsp; = \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) \\(\\times \\) initial amount</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Amount left after 15.2 days (4 half-life)</p><p> &nbsp; = \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{4}\\) \\(\\times \\) 2 </p><p>&nbsp; = 0.125 g</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>[OR]</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({N}_{0}\\)= 2 g, &nbsp; \\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)= 3.8 days, &nbsp; \\({N}_{t}\\)= ?</p><p>t = 15.2 days</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By exponential law of radioactive decay,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{{T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 \\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693\\ \\times 15.2}{3.8}\\ )}\\) = 0.125 g</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'calculations','No.7','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>   &nbsp; Suppose there was 8 g of radon at t = 0 and its half-life is 3.8 days. How much would be left after (i) 7.6 days (ii) 11.4 days? </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Initial amount = 8 g</p><p>half-life, \\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\) = 3.8 days </p><p>(i) time elapsed, t = 7.6 day</p><p>(ii) time elapsed, t = 11.4 days</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Number of half-life, n = \\(\\frac{time\\ elasped}{half-life}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p> &nbsp; = \\(\\frac{7.6}{3.8}\\) = 2</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Amount left after n half-life</p><p> &nbsp; = \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) \\(\\times \\) initial amount</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Amount left after 7.6 days (2 half-life)</p><p> &nbsp; = \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{2}\\) \\(\\times \\) 8 = 2 g</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Number of half-life, n = \\(\\frac{time\\ elasped}{half-life}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = \\(\\frac{11.4}{3.8}\\) = 3</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Amount left after 11.4 days (3 half-life)</p><p> &nbsp; = \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{3}\\) \\(\\times \\) 8 = 1 g</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>[OR]</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({N}_{0}\\)= 8 g, &nbsp; \\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)= 3.8 days, &nbsp; \\({N}_{t}\\)= ?, &nbsp; </p><p>(i) t = 7.6 days &nbsp;  &nbsp; (ii) t = 11.4 days</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By exponential law of radioactive decay,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{{T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(i)</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>8 \\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693\\ \\times 7.6}{3.8}\\ )}\\) = 2 g</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>8 \\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693\\ \\times 11.4}{3.8}\\ )}\\) = 1 g</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.4','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Suppose that initially there was 100 mg of iodine-131 and its half-life is 8 days. How much would it be left after 24 days?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\) = 8 days, &nbsp; \\({N}_{0}\\) = 100 mg, &nbsp; </p><p>N<sub>t</sub> = ? &nbsp;  &nbsp; t = 24 days</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By exponential law of radioactive decay,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{{T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>100 \\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{8}\\ \\times \\ 24\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>12.5 mg</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>[OR]</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>initial amount = 100 mg, amount left = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Number of half-life, n = \\(\\frac{time\\ elasped,\\ \\ \\ t}{half-life,\\ \\ {\\ T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp; = \\(\\frac{24}{8}\\) = 3</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Amount left after n half-life</p><p> &nbsp; = \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) \\(\\times \\) initial amount</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Amount left after 24 days (3 half-life)</p><p> &nbsp; = \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{3}\\) \\(\\times \\) 100 = 12.5 mg</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.2','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; A radioisotope has a half-life of 20 min. If there is initially 102.4 g of this isotope, how much time elapses for 12.8 g to be left?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>half-life, \\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\) = 20 min, &nbsp; </p><p>Initial amount = 102.4 g,</p><p>amount left = 12.8 g</p><p>time elapsed, t = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Amount left after n half-life</p><p> &nbsp; = \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) \\(\\times \\) initial amount</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>12.8</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) \\(\\times \\) 102.4</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{12.8}{102.4}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{3}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>n</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>3</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Number of half-life, n = \\(\\frac{time\\ elasped,\\ \\ \\ t}{half-life,\\ \\ {\\ T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(n\\times \\) \\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(3\\times \\) 20 min = 60 min = 1 h</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>[OR]</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)= 20 min, &nbsp; \\({N}_{0}\\)= 102.4 g, &nbsp; \\({N}_{t}\\)= 12.8 g,</p><p>t = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>By exponential law of radioactive decay</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{{T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>12.8</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>102.4 \\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{20}\\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>0.125</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{20}\\ t\\ )}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>ln 0.125</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>ln \\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{20}\\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>ln 0.125</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{20}\\) t</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>ln 0.125 \\(\\left(\\ \\frac{-\\ 20\\ }{0.693}\\right)\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>60 min = 1 h</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.3','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Cobalt-60 (half-life = 5.25 years) is often used as a radiation source in medicine. How long after a new sample is delivered, will the activity have decreased to \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) of its original value?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,5,true);
INSERT INTO educational_content (grade,category,title,chapter,content,sort_order,active) VALUES
(12,'calculations','No.8','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>   &nbsp; Co-60 (half-life = 5.25 years) is often used as a radiation source in medicine. How long after a new sample is delivered, will the activity have decreased to \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) of its original value?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>half-life, \\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\) = 5.25 years, </p><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) = \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) \\({N}_{0}\\), &nbsp;  \\(\\frac{{N}_{t}}{{N}_{0}}\\)  = \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\), &nbsp;  &nbsp; t = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{{T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{t}}{{N}_{0}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{{T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\ t\\ )}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>ln \\((\\ \\frac{{N}_{t}}{{N}_{0}}\\ )\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{{T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\ \\) t</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>ln \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{5.25}\\ \\)t</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>- 2.079</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{5.25}\\ \\)t</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2.079 \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{5.25}{0.693}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>15.75 years</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>[OR]</p></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Amount left = \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) \\(\\times \\) initial amount</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Amount left after n half-life </p><p> &nbsp; = \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) \\(\\times \\) initial amount</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>\\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) \\(\\times \\) initial amount</p><p> &nbsp; = \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) \\(\\times \\) initial amount</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{3}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>n</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>3</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"5\"><p>Number of half-life, n = \\(\\frac{time\\ elasped,\\ \\ \\ t}{half-life,\\ \\ {\\ T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(n\\times \\) \\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(3\\times \\) 5.25 years = 15.75 years</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.3','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; If a fossil has 10 % carbon-14 compared to a living sample, find the age of the fossil. (half-life of carbon-14 = 5730 years) </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>half-life, \\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\) = 5730 years,</p><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{t}}{{N}_{0}}\\)  = 10 \\(\\%\\) = 0.1, age of the fossil, t = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({N}_{t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{{T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{t}}{{N}_{0}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{{T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\ t\\ )}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>ln ( \\(\\frac{{N}_{t}}{{N}_{0}}\\) ) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{{T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\ t\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>ln 0.1</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{5730}\\ t\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>- 2.303</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{5730}\\ t\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2.303 \\(\\times \\) \\(\\frac{5730}{0.693}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>19 042 years</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>age of the fossil = 19 042 years</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.4','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Potassium-40 has a half-life of 1300 million years. If the atomic ratio of potassium-40 to argon-40 in a rock sample is found to be 1:3, estimate the age of the rock. Assume that there was initially no argon in the rock and argon formed by the decay of potassium is trapped in the rock.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>half-life of K-40, \\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\) = 1300 million years,</p><p>age of the rock, t = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{K}\\ }{{N}_{Ar}}\\) = \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>\\(⟹\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Initially, </p><p> &nbsp; number of K-40 atoms = \\({N}_{0}\\)</p><p> &nbsp; number of Ar-40 atoms = 0</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>\\(⟹\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Finally,</p><p> &nbsp; number of K-40 atoms = \\({N}_{K}\\) = \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) \\({N}_{0}\\)</p><p> &nbsp; number of Ar-40 atoms = \\({N}_{Ar}\\)</p><p> &nbsp; \\({N}_{Ar}\\) = \\({N}_{0}\\) - \\({N}_{K}\\)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp;       = \\({N}_{0}\\) - \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\) \\({N}_{0}\\)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp;       = [1 - \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\)] \\({N}_{0}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{K}\\ }{{N}_{Ar}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\ {N}_{0}}{\\left[1\\ -\\ {\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\right]{N}_{0}\\ }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}}{1\\ -\\ {\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\frac{1}{{2}^{n}}}{1\\ -\\ \\frac{1}{{2}^{n}}}\\) =    \\(\\frac{\\frac{1}{{2}^{n}}}{\\frac{{2}^{n}\\ -\\ \\ 1}{{2}^{n}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p> \\(\\frac{1}{{2}^{n}}\\ \\times \\ \\frac{{2}^{n}}{{2}^{n}-1}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{{2}^{n}-1\\ }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({2}^{n}-1\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>3</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({2}^{n}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>4 = \\({2}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>n</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Number of half-life, n = \\(\\frac{time\\ elasped,\\ \\ \\ t}{half-life,\\ \\ {\\ T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>t</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(n\\times \\) \\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(2\\times \\) 1300 million years</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2600 million years</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>[OR]</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>half-life of K-40, \\({T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)= 1300 million years</p><p>age of the rock, t = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{K}\\ }{{N}_{Ar}}\\) = \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>\\(⟹\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Initially, </p><p> &nbsp; number of K-40 atoms = \\({N}_{0}\\)</p><p> &nbsp; number of Ar-40 atoms = 0</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>\\(⟹\\) </p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>Finally,</p><p> &nbsp; number of K-40 atoms = \\({N}_{K}\\) = \\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}\\)</p><p> &nbsp; number of Ar-40 atoms = \\({N}_{Ar}\\)</p><p> &nbsp; \\({N}_{Ar}\\) = \\({N}_{0}\\) – \\({N}_{K}\\)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp;       = \\({N}_{0}\\) – \\({N}_{0}\\) \\({e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}\\)</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp;       = [1 - \\({e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}\\)] \\({N}_{0}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{K}\\ }{{N}_{Ar}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{N}_{0}\\ {e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}}{[1\\ -\\ {e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}]\\ {N}_{0}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\ {e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}}{1\\ -\\ {e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>3 \\({e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(1\\ -\\ {e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>4 \\({e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({e}^{(-\\ \\lambda \\ t\\ )}\\)</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({e}^{(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{{T}_{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\ t\\ )}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.25</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(-\\ \\frac{0.693}{1300}\\ t\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>ln 0.25</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>t </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{-\\ 1300\\ ln 0.25}{0.693}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2600 million years</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>age of the rock = 2600 million years</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.5','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.5</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of (i) a 0.65 kg basketball thrown at a speed of 10 m s<sup>-1</sup>, (ii) a nonrelativistic electron with a kinetic energy of 1 eV.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>(i) m = 0.65 kg, &nbsp; v = 10 m s<sup>-1</sup>, &nbsp; \\(\\lambda \\) = ?, &nbsp; </p><p>h = 6.63 \\(\\times {10}^{-34}\\) J s</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The de Broglie wavelength associated with basketball,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>λ</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{h}{p}\\) = \\(\\frac{h}{m\\ v}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>λ</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6.63\\ \\times {10}^{-34}\\ }{0.65\\times 10}\\) = 1.02 \\(\\times {10}^{-34}\\) m</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(ii)</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>KE = 1 eV = 1.6 \\(\\times {10}^{-19}\\) J,</p><p>m = \\(9.1\\ \\times \\ {10}^{-31}\\) kg</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The de Broglie wavelength associated with electron,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>λ</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{2\\ m\\ KE}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6.63\\ \\times {10}^{-34}}{\\sqrt{2\\ \\times \\ 9.1\\ \\times \\ {10}^{-31}\\ \\times \\ 1.6\\ \\times {10}^{-19}}}\\)  </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1.23 \\(\\times {10}^{-9}\\) m</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'calculations','No.13','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.13</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>   &nbsp; A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (m<sub>p</sub> = 1840 m<sub>e</sub>)</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>m<sub>p</sub> = 1840 m<sub>e</sub>, &nbsp; V = 1 kV = 1000 V,</p><p>h = 6.63 \\(\\times {10}^{-34}\\) J s</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>KE = W = q V </p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp;  = 1000 eV </p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp;  = 1000 \\(\\times \\) 1.6 \\(\\times {10}^{-19}\\) </p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp;  = 1.6 \\(\\times {10}^{-16}\\) J</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The de Broglie wavelength associated with electron, </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>λ<sub>e</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{2\\ {m}_{e}\\ KE}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The de Broglie wavelength associated with proton, </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>λ<sub>p</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{2\\ {m}_{p}\\ KE}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{\\lambda }_{e}}{{\\lambda }_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{2\\ {m}_{e}\\ KE}}\\ }{\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{2\\ {m}_{p}\\ KE}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{\\lambda }_{e}}{{\\lambda }_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{2\\ {m}_{e}\\ KE}}\\ \\times \\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2\\ {m}_{p}\\ KE}}{h}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{\\lambda }_{e}}{{\\lambda }_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{{m}_{p}}}{\\sqrt{{m}_{e}}}\\) = \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1840\\ {m}_{e}}{{m}_{e}}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{\\lambda }_{e}}{{\\lambda }_{p}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{1840}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({\\lambda }_{e}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>42.895 \\({\\lambda }_{p}\\)</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'calculations','No.14','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.14</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>   &nbsp; In old days radios contained vacuum tubes that generated and speeded up electrons. A tube operates at 100 V. Find the speed of an electron and de Broglie wavelength. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><p> &nbsp; (mass of an electron = \\(9.1\\ \\times \\ {10}^{-31}\\)<sup> </sup>kg) </p><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>V = 100 V, &nbsp; m = 9.1 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-31 </sup>kg,</p><p>h = 6.63 \\(\\times {10}^{-34}\\) J s</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>KE = W = q V </p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp;  = 100 eV</p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp;  = 100 \\(\\times \\) 1.6 \\(\\times {10}^{-19}\\) </p><p> &nbsp;  &nbsp;  = 1.6 \\(\\times {10}^{-17}\\) J</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>KE</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) m v<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>v<sup>2</sup></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\ KE}{m}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\ KE}{m}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\ \\times \\ 1.6\\ \\times {10}^{-17}\\ }{9.1\\ \\times \\ {10}^{-31}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>5.93 \\(\\times {10}^{6}\\) m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The de Broglie wavelength associated with electron, </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>λ</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{2\\ m\\ KE}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{6.63\\ \\times {10}^{-34}}{\\sqrt{2\\ \\times \\ 9.1\\ \\times \\ {10}^{-31}\\times \\ 1.6\\ \\times {10}^{-17}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1.229 \\(\\times {10}^{-10}\\) m = 1.229 Å</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>[OR]</p></td><td><p>λ</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{h}{m\\ v}\\) = \\(\\frac{6.63\\ \\times {10}^{-34}\\ }{9.1\\ \\times \\ {10}^{-31}\\times \\ 5.93\\ \\times {10}^{6}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1.229 \\(\\times {10}^{-10}\\) m = 1.229 Å</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,11,true),
(12,'calculations','No.15','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.15</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>   &nbsp; Find the de Broglie wavelength of an electron in the ground state of hydrogen atom. Radius of the first orbit of hydrogen atom is 0.53 Å. </p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>r = 0.53 Å = 0.53 \\(\\times {10}^{-10}\\ \\)m, \\(\\lambda \\) = ?</p><p>for ground state, n = 1</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The de Broglie wavelength associated with electron,</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>2 \\(\\pi \\) r</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>n \\(\\lambda \\) &nbsp; (n = 1, 2, 3, 4, ......)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\lambda \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\ \\pi \\ r}{n}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{2\\ \\times \\ 3.142\\ \\times \\ 0.53\\ \\times {10}^{-10}}{1}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>3.33 \\(\\times {10}^{-10}\\ \\)m = 3.33 Å</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,12,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.9','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Calculate the relativistic factor \\(\\gamma \\), for a particle traveling at 99.7 percent of the speed of light.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v = 99.7\\(\\%\\) c = 0.997 c</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\gamma \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\gamma \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{(0.997\\ c)}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\gamma \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\ {0.997}^{2}}}\\)  = 12.92</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,13,true),
(12,'calculations','Rev.10','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Rev.10</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; Calculate the relativistic factor \\(\\gamma \\), for an object traveling at 2 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{8}\\) m s<sup>-1</sup>.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>v = 2 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{8}\\) m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\gamma \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\gamma \\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{(\\ 2\\ \\times \\ {10}^{8})}^{2}}{{(\\ 3\\ \\times \\ {10}^{8})}^{2}}}}\\)  = \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{(\\ 2\\ )}^{2}}{{(\\ 3\\ )}^{2}}}}\\)  = 1.34</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,14,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.6','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; A positron is a type of antimatter that is just like an electron, except that it has a positive charge. When a positron and an electron collide, their masses are completely annihilated and converted to energy in the form of gamma rays. If both particles have a rest mass of 9.11 \\(\\times \\) 10<sup>-31 </sup>kg, find the rest energy of each particle and the total energy of gamma rays in MeV.</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({m}_{0}\\) = 9.11 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{-31}\\)<sup> </sup>kg &nbsp; c = 3 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{8}\\) m s<sup>-1</sup></p><p>\\({E}_{0}\\) = ?, &nbsp; E = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The rest energy of an electron and a positron is</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>E<sub>0</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>m<sub>0</sub> c<sup>2</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>9.11 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{-31}\\times (\\) 3 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{8}{)}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>8.19 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{-14}\\) J</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>1 MeV = 1.6 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{-19}\\times \\) \\({10}^{6}J\\) </p><p> &nbsp; = 1.6 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{-13}J\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>E<sub>0</sub></p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>8.19 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{-14}J\\times \\ \\frac{1\\ MeV}{1.6\\ \\times \\ {10}^{-13}J}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.511 MeV</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>The total energy of gamma rays</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>E</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>2 E<sub>0</sub> = 2 \\(\\times \\) 0.511 = 1.022 MeV</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,15,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.7','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; One stary night, an earth-bound observer looking up the stars sees an extra-terrestrial spaceship flashacross the sky. The ship is 50 m long and is traveling at 95 percent of the speed of light. What would the ship’s length be when measured from earth-bound frame of reference?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({L}_{0}\\) = 50 m, v = 95\\(\\%\\) c = 0.95 c, &nbsp; L = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>L</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{L}_{0}}{\\gamma }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{L}_{0}}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>L</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({L}_{0}\\ \\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>L</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>50 \\(\\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{(0.95\\ c)}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>50 \\(\\sqrt{1-\\ {0.95}^{2}}\\) = 15.61 m</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,16,true),
(12,'calculations','No.16','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>No.16</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>   &nbsp; The distance between two points, called the proper length L<sub>0</sub> is 1 km. An observer in motion with respect to the frame of reference of the two points measures 0.8 km, which is L. What is the relative speed of the frame of reference with respect to the observer?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\({L}_{0}\\) = 1 km = \\({10}^{3}\\)m,</p><p>L = 0.8 km = 0.8 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{3}\\)m, &nbsp; v = ?</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>L</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{L}_{0}}{\\gamma }\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{L}_{0}}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>L</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\({L}_{0}\\ \\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{L}{{L}_{0}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({\\left(\\frac{L}{{L}_{0}}\\right)}^{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(1-\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1 - \\({\\left(\\frac{L}{{L}_{0}}\\right)}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1 - \\({\\left(\\frac{0.8\\ \\times \\ {10}^{3}}{{10}^{3}}\\right)}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.36</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{v}{c}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.6</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.6 c = 0.6 \\(\\times \\) 3 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{8}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1.8 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{8}\\) m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,17,true),
(12,'calculations','Eg.8','13','{"html":"<article class=\"problem-card\">\n  <div class=\"problem-number\"><span>Eg.8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"problem-content\">\n    <p class=\"problem-question\"><strong>Q:</strong>  &nbsp; How fast must a vehicle travel for 1 s of time measured on a passenger’s watch in the vehicle to differ by 1 % for an observer measuring it from the ground outside?</p>\n    <hr>\n    <details>\n      <summary><strong>Ans:</strong> အဖြေနှင့် တွက်နည်းကြည့်ရန် နှိပ်ပါ</summary>\n      <div class=\"problem-answer\"><div class=\"calculation-table-wrap\"><table class=\"calculation-table\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Ans:</p></td><td colspan=\"3\"><p>\\(∆{t}_{0}\\)= 1 s, </p><p>\\(\\Delta t\\) = \\(∆{t}_{0}\\)+ 1 % = 1 + 0.01 = 1.01 s</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\Delta t\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\gamma \\) \\(∆{t}_{0}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\Delta t\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}}}\\) \\(∆{t}_{0}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{\\Delta t}{∆{t}_{0}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{∆{t}_{0}}{\\Delta t}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{1-\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\({\\left(\\frac{∆{t}_{0}}{\\Delta t}\\right)}^{2}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(1-\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{{v}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1 - \\({\\left(\\frac{∆{t}_{0}}{\\Delta t}\\right)}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>1 - \\({\\left(\\frac{1}{1.01}\\right)}^{2}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{v}{c}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>\\(\\sqrt{1\\ -\\ {\\left(\\frac{1}{1.01}\\right)}^{2}}\\) </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>\\(\\frac{v}{c}\\) </p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.14 </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>v</p></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.14 c = 0.14 \\(\\times \\) 3 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{8}\\)</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>=</p></td><td><p>0.42 \\(\\times \\) \\({10}^{8}\\) m s<sup>-1</sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</article>"}'::jsonb,18,true),
(12,'old_questions','2024 Set 1 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2024 · 1','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2024 Set 1</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2024-set1","year":2024,"set":1,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"The two acceleration vectors a⃗_c and a⃗_T are perpendicular to each other."},{"number":"ii","text":"The normal force FN exerted by a banked road is parallel to the road."},{"number":"iii","text":"Wind energy is the kinetic energy of air in motion."},{"number":"iv","text":"Convection occurs only in a liquid or a gas, never in a solid."},{"number":"v","text":"An echo is repetition of sound due to the reflection of sound."},{"number":"vi","text":"For a vacuum, εᵣ = 1 and for other insulating materials εᵣ > 1."},{"number":"vii","text":"A source of electromotive force has an external resistance."},{"number":"viii","text":"A transformer is used to change the voltage of an alternating current."},{"number":"ix","text":"The commonly used invisible light for LED is white light."},{"number":"x","text":"An inertial frame is a frame of reference that has no acceleration."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"In uniform circular motion, the centripetal force and centripetal acceleration are ------ direction."},{"number":"ii","text":"Cohesion and adhesion are two types of ------ forces."},{"number":"iii","text":"Heat, light and ------ are the most common forms of energy."},{"number":"iv","text":"A black object is a good absorber and a good radiator whose ------ is close to one."},{"number":"v","text":"The ------ is the unit used for measuring sound intensity."},{"number":"vi","text":"flux (luminous power) Φ is measured in ------."},{"number":"vii","text":"The angular position of a point of a periodic wave is known as the ----."},{"number":"viii","text":"The capacitors are connected in ------ each capacitor has the same charge."},{"number":"ix","text":"In the SI system, the unit of capacitance is ------."},{"number":"x","text":"Batteries and electric generators are called sources of ------ force."},{"number":"xi","text":"An electric light bulb is made of a glass bulb consisting a ------ filament."},{"number":"xii","text":"In any electrical appliance the ------ wire is always connected to the metal case."},{"number":"xiii","text":"A ------ is a semiconductor device that converts light into electrical current."},{"number":"xiv","text":"The basic operations in Boolean algebra are ------, OR, and NOT."},{"number":"xv","text":"------ of food has potential to produce safe foods with long shelf life."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"The unit of angular velocity is ------. (A. metre per second, B. radian per second, C. radian per second squared)"},{"number":"ii","text":"Bernoulli’s equation can be derived using the ------ principle to a fluid flowing in a tube. (A. work energy, B. kinetic energy, C. potential energy)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Conversion of light energy into ------ is based on a phenomenon called photovoltaic effect. (A. heat energy, B. chemical energy, C. electrical energy)"},{"number":"iv","text":"In an ------ process, the volume is constant so that work done is zero. (A. isobaric, B. isochoric, C. isothermal)"},{"number":"v","text":"What material has the lowest speed of sound? (A. in solids, B. in liquids, C. in gases)"},{"number":"vi","text":"Which type of lenes are used in telescope? (A. convex, B. mirror, C. concave)"},{"number":"vii","text":"Wavefront is always ------ to the direction of propagation (or) rays. (A. perpendicular, B. opposite, C. parallel)"},{"number":"viii","text":"Which one is non-polarized capacitors? (A. supercapacitors, B. electrolytic capacitors, C. film capacitors)"},{"number":"ix","text":"A ------ is an electrical device that stores electrical energy in the form of an electric field. (A. resistor, B. capacitor, C. transistor)"},{"number":"x","text":"When a battery is connected to an external circuit, the terminal voltage of a battery is ------. (A. V = E, B. V = E - Ir, C. V = E + Ir)"},{"number":"xi","text":"There are ------ joule in one kilowatt hour (1 kWh). 6 (Α. 4.2, B. 3.6 × 10 , C. 1000)"},{"number":"xii","text":"The voltage of ------ goes alternately negative and positive, making the current flow backwards and forwards through the circuit. (A. live wire, B. neutral wire, C. earth wire)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"Which electrical component is used to control the brightness of street lamps? (A. LED, B. LDR, C. thermistor)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"------ are massless and move at the speed of light in vacuum. (A. Photons, B. Neutrons, C. Electrons)"},{"number":"xv","text":"When an animal or a plant dies carbon cycle stops and the carbon-14 in the remain gradually ------ by radioactive decay. (A. decreases, B. increases, C. constant)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"Under what condition the angular acceleration of a rotating object is equal to zero? In circular motion, how is a tangential acceleration produced? A 60 cm rope is tied to the handle of a bucket which is then whirled in a vertical circle. The mass of the bucket is 3 kg. If the tension of the rope at the lowest point in its path is 50 N, find the speed of the bucket at that point."}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"One liter of air is cooled at constant pressure until its volume is halved, and then it is allowed to expand isothermally back to its original volume. Draw the process on a p-V diagram. A compound microscope consists of two thin lenses, an objective of focal length 20 mm and an eyepiece of focal length 50 mm, placed 220 mm apart. If the final image is viewed at infinity, calculate the distance of the object from the objective."}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What is the main source of energy? What are non-renewable energy sources and renewable energy resources? The hydroturbine receives water from a reservoir at an elevation of 100 m above it. What is the minimum water flow in kg s⁻¹ to produce a steady turbine output of 50 MW if the turbine generator efficiency is 75 %?"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"What is meant by “AM and FM”? What are the differences between FM and AM? Draw the circuit symbol of LED and its forward biased characteristic curves."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"How does an emf of the source differ from potential difference across the external resistance? Why is an electric fuse required in all electrical appliances? When a battery is connected to a 2 Ω resistor it drives a current of 0.6 A through the resistor. When it is connected to a 7 Ω resistor it drives a current of 0.2 A through the resistor. Find the emf and the internal resistance of the battery."}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the graphical representations of the magnitude of DC and AC voltages as a function of time. The current in an AC circuit at any time t seconds is given by I = 20 sin (100πt) A. Find (i) the peak value (maximum value) of current, the period and the frequency (ii) the value of the current when t = 0 (iii) the value of the current when t = 8 ms and (iv) the time when the current reaches 10 A."}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"What are radioisotopes? Give some examples. Give two medical applications of radioisotopes. A radioisotope has a half-life of 20 min. If there is initially 102.4 g of this isotope, how much time elapses for 12.8 g to be left?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw (i) a diagram for circular motion of an object at constant speed, (ii) a vector diagram for change in velocity, and (iii) a vector diagram for Δt approaching zero. A beam of 650 nm light is directed upon two slits that are separated by a distance of 0.75 mm. A screen is placed 1.50 m away to capture the interference pattern. What is the distance from the first-order maximum to the third-order minimum?"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"What is the difference between laminar flow and turbulent flow? At a river junction, water streams are whirling; is it laminar or turbulent? How does temperature affect the viscosity of a fluid? Draw the diagram for charging and discharging a capacitor and voltage characteristic of the charging and discharging a capacitor."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What is Doppler effect? Express the Doppler equation in general form. Describe some applications of Doppler effect in a variety of fields. In old days radios contained vacuum tubes that generated and speeded up electrons. A tube operates at 100 V. Find the speed of an electron and de Broglie wavelength. (mass of an electron = 9.1 × 10⁻³¹ kg, charge of electron = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹C, h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s)"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"State the equation of Faraday’s law for a wire loop with N identical turns. Why is Faraday’s law important? What does negative sign indicate in Faraday’s law of electromagnetic induction formula? Draw the logic circuit represented by each of the following expressions: (i) A + B + C (ii) ABC (iv) AB + CD"}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"What is thermistor? How many types of thermistors are there? Write down the main difference between them? Three capacitors of capacitance 3 µF, 10 µF and 15 µF are connected in series with 100 V battery. What is the charge and the potential difference on each capacitor?"}]}}}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'old_questions','2024 Set 2 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2024 · 2','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2024 Set 2</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2024-set2","year":2024,"set":2,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"The centripetal force is the force acting towards the centre of curvature."},{"number":"ii","text":"The oil used in the motor car''s brake system is compressible."},{"number":"iii","text":"Solar energy is indeed classified as a type of non-renewable energy."},{"number":"iv","text":"Heat conduction represents a form of energy transfer."},{"number":"v","text":"Sound travels at different speeds depending on the medium through which it passes."},{"number":"vi","text":"When one side of a capacitor holds a positive charge, the other side holds an equal negative charge."},{"number":"vii","text":"Electromotive force is measured in volts."},{"number":"viii","text":"In Myanmar, the prevalent AC line frequency is 50 Hz, while the standard voltage utilized for residential and commercial applications falls within the voltage of 220 V to 240 V."},{"number":"ix","text":"One advantage of LEDs is their common use with low voltage and high current."},{"number":"x","text":"The term “radioactivity” is used to describe the rate at which a radioactive sample undergoes decay."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"------ force in a circular motion is not a real force; it acts radially away from the centre of the circle."},{"number":"ii","text":"-----, air, steam, and foam are generally considered to be compressible."},{"number":"iii","text":"The typical output of a solar cell is ------ energy."},{"number":"iv","text":"Heat convection is one of the primary ------ of heat transfer."},{"number":"v","text":"The SI unit of sound intensity is the ------ per square metre."},{"number":"vi","text":"An aperture is a circular opening through which the ------ passes."},{"number":"vii","text":"The angular position of a periodic wave is known as the ------ angle."},{"number":"viii","text":"------ is required to control the current and facilitate gradual charging or discharging in a capacitor circuit."},{"number":"ix","text":"In the series connection of the capacitors, each capacitor has the same ------."},{"number":"x","text":"Electrical energy is energy associated with the flow of charge through any part of ------."},{"number":"xi","text":"The potential difference is the amount of ------ required to move a unit charge from one end to another end of a circuit element."},{"number":"xii","text":"The current from the outlet of a phone charger is ------ current."},{"number":"xiii","text":"A ------, one of the most widely used in optoelectronics, is a semiconductor light source that emits light when current flows through it."},{"number":"xiv","text":"An ------ gate is a digital logic gate that outputs a high (1) signal only when all its inputs are high (1)."},{"number":"xv","text":"In gamma decay, the atomic number and mass number of the ------ and daughter nuclei remain unchanged."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"A ball attached to a string is whirled around a vertical circle. At the bottom of the arc, ------. (A. it has no net force, B. it has a net force acting upward, C. it has a net force acting downward)"},{"number":"ii","text":"Which of the following is the SI unit of surface tension? (A. newton (N), B. joule (J), C. newton per metre (Nm-¹))"},{"number":"iii","text":"Which of the following energy sources is considered a renewable energy source? (A. Coal, B. Natural gas, C. Wind)"},{"number":"iv","text":"Which of the following fields is primarily concerned with the study of systems involving energy in the form of heat and work? (A. Thermodynamics, B. Optics, C. Electrostatics)"},{"number":"v","text":"What does audibility refer to? (A. The quality of being able to be heard, B. The loudness of a sound, C. The frequency of a sound wave)"},{"number":"vi","text":"Which part of the eye functions similarly to the diaphragm in a camera, controlling the amount of light that enters the eye? (A. Cornea, B. Lens, C. Iris)"},{"number":"vii","text":"What does monochromatic light refer to? (A. Light of various wavelengths, B. Light of a single wavelength or colour, C. Light with no polarization)"},{"number":"viii","text":"By what percentage does the capacitance change when the distance between the two parallel plates of a capacitor is doubled? (Α. 25%, Β. 50%, С. 75%)"},{"number":"ix","text":"What does changing the charge on a capacitor primarily affect? (A. Capacitance, B. Voltage, C. Resistance)"},{"number":"x","text":"Which of the following statements is correct regarding most sources of electromotive force (EMF)? (A. EMF sources have no internal resistance., B. EMF sources have internal resistance., C. EMF sources have no internal capacitance.)"},{"number":"xi","text":"In what year did Joseph Henry and Michel Faraday make their independent discoveries related to electric current and magnetic fields? (Α. 1813, Β. 1831, С. 1850)"},{"number":"xii","text":"Why is AC preferred over DC for long-distance power distribution of electrical power? (A. Bigger inductors, B. Lower energy losses, C. Thinner conductors)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"What is the main function of NOT gate in digital logic? (A. Performs the digital AND operation, B. Inverts the input signal, C. Executes addition)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"What is emitted during beta decay? (A. Alpha particle, B. Neutrino, C. Beta particle)"},{"number":"xv","text":"What defines nuclear fission? (A. Fusion of atomic nuclei, B. Splitting of atomic nuclei into smaller parts, C. Combining of photons and neutrons)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"Differentiate between circular motion and rotational motion in Physics, providing an example for each type of motion. Water runs into a fountain, filling all the pipes, at a steady rate of 0.80 cm³ s⁻¹. How fast will it shoot out of a hole 4.5 cm in diameter?"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Does the photoelectric effect involve changes in frequency or wavelength of the waves? What specific effect is related to the change in frequency heard as a car, while sounding its horn, approaches and then moves away from an observer? Find the change in internal energy of one mole of an ideal gas when its temperature changes from 0℃ to 50℃. (R = 8.3143 J mol⁻¹ K⁻¹ )"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What exactly is a solar cell, and how does it work to produce electricity from sunlight? Determine the input power of the wind if the wind speed is 10 m s⁻¹ and blade length is 20 m. Density of air is 1.3 kg m⁻³."}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"What effect does an increase in light intensity have on the resistance of a light dependent resistor (LDR)? Is LDR also called light sensitive variable resistor? Is an LDR composed of semiconductor materials? Provide a circuit symbol illustrating the configuration of LDR."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"Identify three distinguished types of capacitors. What potential difference must be applied across a 20 µF capacitor if it is to have an energy content of 1 J?"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Create a diagram illustrating the symbol used to represent a transformer in an electronic circuit and label its key components. A step-down transformer is used to light a 12 V, 24 W lamp from the 220 V mains. The current through the primary is 125 mA. What is the efficiency of the transformer?"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"Describe a comparison between Einstein’s Special and General Relativity theories, focusing two key points. Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of a 0.65 kg basketball thrown at a speed of 20 m s⁻¹. (h = 6.625 × 10⁻³⁴ Js)"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Sketch a diagram illustrating the directions of centripetal force, centripetal acceleration and linear velocity in uniform circular motion. In a laser unit, laser beam of wavelength 6328 Å is emitted. How many photons are released per second if the output power is 1 mW? (h = 6.625 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹)"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Name three machines or systems in which centrifugal force is noticeable. Draw a diagram demonstrating how a moving magnet induces current nearby coil. Include key elements and direction indicators."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"How would you differentiate between interference and diffraction of light in the context of light? Suppose there was 8 g of radon at t = 0 and its half-life is 3.8 days. How much would be left after 7.6 days."}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"What are the advantages of connecting batteries in a series aiding configuration? Draw the circuit diagram illustrating the fire alarm system."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"List four essential components required for a basic radio receiver. If a 1200 W electric iron is used for 1 h, by how many units does the electricity meter reading increased? Calculate the payment if one unit of electricity costs 35 kyats."}]}}}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'old_questions','2024 Set 3 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2024 · 3','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2024 Set 3</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2024-set3","year":2024,"set":3,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"The tangential acceleration is present in nonuniform circular motion."},{"number":"ii","text":"When a skater forms a circle, he has to lean outwards."},{"number":"iii","text":"Fossil fuels are renewable sources of energy."},{"number":"iv","text":"Heat radiation does not require a material medium."},{"number":"v","text":"The intensity of an echo is less than that of the original sound."},{"number":"vi","text":"Variable capacitor is used as tuning capacitor."},{"number":"vii","text":"The practical unit of electrical energy is the joule."},{"number":"viii","text":"A transformer is used to change the voltage of an alternating current."},{"number":"ix","text":"LCDs consume much more power than LEDs and gas-plasma displays."},{"number":"x","text":"Gamma rays can be deflected by electric and magnetic fields."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"A ------ body is a body that does not deform or change shape."},{"number":"ii","text":"------ and adhesion are two types of intermolecular forces."},{"number":"iii","text":"Solar cells convert light energy into ------ energy."},{"number":"iv","text":"Thermal equilibrium occurs when the systems are at the same ------."},{"number":"v","text":"The speed of sound is ------ in solids than liquids and gases."},{"number":"vi","text":"Human eye is more sensitive to ------ light compared to other colors."},{"number":"vii","text":"Wavefront is always perpendicular to the direction of ------."},{"number":"viii","text":"The SI unit of capacitance is ------."},{"number":"ix","text":"If a 1200 W electric ion is used for 50 min, the electricity meter reading increases by ------ unit."},{"number":"x","text":"When a current flows through the nichrome coil of an electric stove, it produces ------ energy."},{"number":"xi","text":"In the lighting circuit, the light bulbs are arranged in ------ across the main line."},{"number":"xii","text":"The magnitude of induced emf in a wire loop is directly proportional to the rate of change of ------ through that loop."},{"number":"xiii","text":"The photodiode is a semiconductor device that converts ------ into electrical current."},{"number":"xiv","text":"------ is the process of recovering audio signal from modulated wave."},{"number":"xv","text":"An alpha particle consists of two protons and ------ neutrons."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"Centripetal force of ------ is required to move a body of mass 2 kg with a speed of 1 m s⁻¹ in a uniform circular motion of radius 5 m. (Α. 1.2 Ν, Β. 1.3 N, C. 0.4 N)"},{"number":"ii","text":"The viscosity of liquids ------ with an increase in temperature. (A. decreases, B. increases, C. remains constant)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Biomass is renewable ------ material that comes from plants and animals. (A. metallic, B. inorganic, C. organic)"},{"number":"iv","text":"------ is the ratio of the total emissive power of an object to that of the blackbody, at the same temperature and wavelength. (A. Conductivity, B. Emissivity, C. Resistivity)"},{"number":"v","text":"The intensity of a sound wave is directly proportional to the square of the ------ of the wave. (A. frequency, B. amplitude, C. wavelength)"},{"number":"vi","text":"------ is the defect of vision in which distant objects are seen clearly, but objects nearby are blurry. (A. Farsightedness, B. Nearsightedness, C. Blindness)"},{"number":"vii","text":"Monochromatic light has a single ------. (A. wavelength, B. amplitude, C. intensity)"},{"number":"viii","text":"Insulating materials have the dielectric constant values of ------. (A. one, B. greater than one, C. less than one)"},{"number":"ix","text":"The equivalent capacitance ------ when the individual capacitors are connected in series. (A. increases, B. decreases, C. does not change)"},{"number":"x","text":"The heating element of an electric iron is controlled by a ------ that switches the current on and off to maintain the selected temperature. (A. capacitor, B. thermostat, C. resistor)"},{"number":"xi","text":"------ is the rate of transfer of electrical energy. (A. Electrical power, B. Electrical energy, C. Electromotive force)"},{"number":"xii","text":"What is the SI unit of magnetic flux density? (A. weber, B. tesla, C. ampere per metre)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"What is the output of XNOR gate if both inputs are the same? (A. 0, B. 2, C. 1)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"Time dilation becomes apparent especially as the speed of the system approaches that of ---------- (A. light, B. sound, C. none of A and B)"},{"number":"xv","text":"The statement \"radium has a half-life of 1620 years\" means that if we start with N0 atoms of radium, ------ will remain after 1620 years. (A. N /2 atoms, B. N /4 atoms, C. N /8 atoms) 0 0 0"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"How do you understand capillary action? What will happen to the rise of liquid in a capillary tube if the radius of the tube is (i) increased and (ii) decreased? When a capillary tube stands upright in a beaker of water, the water rises h in the tube. If the radius of the tube is 2 mm, contact angle is 35°, density of water is 1000 kg m⁻³ and surface tension is 0.072 N m⁻¹, calculate h."}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the optical features of the eye and label each part. What frequency is received by a person watching an oncoming ambulance moving at 110 km h⁻¹ and emitting a steady 800 Hz sound from its siren? The speed of sound on this day is 345 m s⁻¹."}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"How does the wind power incident on the rotor area of a wind turbine depend on wind speed and rotor area? Theoretically, when wind speed doubles, how many times will the wind power potential be increased? The wind is blowing at 10 m s⁻¹. How much total power is produced by the wind turbine if the blades are 45 m long? (ρ_air = 1.3 kg m⁻³)"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"Why is LDR also called light sensitive variable resistors? How does its resistance change (i) in the dark light and (ii) in the bright light? What is thermistor? What is the main difference between the negative temperature coefficient (NTC) and the positive temperature coefficient (PTC) thermistors? Draw their characteristic curves."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"If an insulating material is inserted between the conductors of a capacitor in a vacuum, does its capacitance increase or decrease? Explain. The plates of a parallel-plate capacitor are 50 cm² in area and 1 mm apart. What is its capacitance? What is the charge on each plate when C² N⁻¹ m⁻² the capacitor is connected to a 24 V battery? (ε₀ = 8.85 × 10⁻¹² C² N⁻¹ m⁻²)"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a simple circuit diagram of two batteries in series opposing connected with an external resistor. Two batteries each having an emf of 6 V and an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω are connected (i) in series and (ii) in parallel. Find the current in each case when the batteries are connected to a 1 Ω resistor."}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"Starting from the relation between the momentum p of a particle and its associated wavelength λ, obtain the de Broglie wavelength of a particle in terms of its kinetic energy. Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of a nonrelativistic electron with a kinetic energy of 1 eV. (h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, m = 9.1 × 10⁻³¹ kg, 1 eV = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ J) e"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a diagram showing the directions of centripetal force, centripetal acceleration and linear velocity of an object in uniform circular motion. The filament of a 100 W electric bulb is made of tungsten. The emissivity of tungsten is 0.3 and its length is 0.2 m. Find the diameter of the filament, if its temperature is 3000 K when the bulb is switched on. (σ = 5.685 × 10⁻⁸ W m⁻² K⁻⁴ )"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Explain why there is tangential acceleration in addition to centripetal acceleration in nonuniform circular motion. Give graphical representations of the magnitude of (i) DC voltage and (ii) AC voltage as a function of time."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What are the conditions for constructive interference and destructive interference? Calculate the relativistic factor γ, for (i) a particle traveling at 99.7 % of the speed of light and (ii) an object travelling 2 × 10( m s⁻¹. (c = 3 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹)"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"What is electromagnetic induction? State the methods by which an induced emf can be produced in a coil. Draw the circuit symbol of LED and its characteristic curves."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"Construct the truth tables to prove the following Boolean Algebra rules. 5 (i) A + A B = A + B, (ii) A + A B = A. One coil of a transformer has 50 turns and the other coil has 1000 turns. The alternating voltage of 220 V is applied to the primary. Find the alternating voltage from the secondary when it is used as (i) a step-up transformer and (ii) a step-down transformer."}]}}}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'old_questions','2024 Set 4 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2024 · 4','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2024 Set 4</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2024-set4","year":2024,"set":4,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"In a uniform circular motion, the magnitude of the velocity remains constant, but the direction of the velocity continuously changes."},{"number":"ii","text":"Centripetal force is the force acting on an object in circular motion which is directed towards the axis of rotation or centre of curvature."},{"number":"iii","text":"Renewable energy sources do not pollute the environment."},{"number":"iv","text":"Heat can transfer between two systems that are the same temperature."},{"number":"v","text":"An echo is repetition of sound due to the vibration of sound."},{"number":"vi","text":"A capacitor is an electrical device that stores electrical energy in the form of a magnetic field."},{"number":"vii","text":"Electromotive force (emf) is the amount of energy provided by the battery per unit charge to move round the complete circuit."},{"number":"viii","text":"The currents flow in little circles in the iron core are eddy currents."},{"number":"ix","text":"Some active electrical components are transistors, LEDs and LDR."},{"number":"x","text":"A nuclear reaction is a process in which a beta radiation penetrates into a nucleus and changes its configuration."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"A ------ body is a body that does not deform or change shape."},{"number":"ii","text":"Centrifugal force in a circular motion is not a ------ force."},{"number":"iii","text":"----- energy sources are continuously replenished by natural processes."},{"number":"iv","text":"One of the basic requirements for heat transfer is the presence of a ---- difference."},{"number":"v","text":"Heat ----- is a transfer of heat that does not require a material medium."},{"number":"vi","text":"A camera is an ------ instrument that records an image of an object."},{"number":"vii","text":"A wavefront is a locus of all points having the same ------ in the wave."},{"number":"viii","text":"Electrolytic capacitors use the oxide layer as the ------ material."},{"number":"ix","text":"The sources of electromotive force convert ------ from some other forms into electrical form."},{"number":"x","text":"Electrical ------ is the rate of transfer of electrical energy."},{"number":"xi","text":"In the alternating current the direction of the flow of electrons changes ------."},{"number":"xii","text":"Magnetic field strength and magnetic flux density are ------ quantities."},{"number":"xiii","text":"The voltage drop across the zener diode always remains ------ irrespective of the applied voltage."},{"number":"xiv","text":"A thermistor is a temperature sensor that exhibits a large change in ---- proportional to a change in temperature."},{"number":"xv","text":"The atomic number and mass number are ------ in the decay process."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"Some of the examples of rotational motion are ------. (A. motion of the fan blades, B. the moon orbiting the earth, C. motion of the earth around the sun)"},{"number":"ii","text":"One of the centripetal forces is ------. (A. nuclear force, B. tension force, C. deforming force)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Non-renewable energy resources include ------. (A. coal, B. wind, C. solar)"},{"number":"iv","text":"In fluid, heat is mainly transferred by ------. (A. conduction, B. convection, C. radiation)"},{"number":"v","text":"Reflection of sound obeys the laws of ------. (A. reflection, B. refraction, C. emission)"},{"number":"vi","text":"A microscope uses lenses to make ------ images of objects. (A. clear, B. reduced, C. enlarged)"},{"number":"vii","text":"Constructive interference has ------ intensity. (A. minimum, B. maximum, C. normal)"},{"number":"viii","text":"Which capacitor is used as a tuning capacitor? (A. Electrolytic capacitor, B. Ceramic capacitor, C. Variable capacitor)"},{"number":"ix","text":"In an electric generator, ------ energy is converted into electrical energy. (A. mechanical, B. optical, C. thermal)"},{"number":"x","text":"The unit of electrical power P is ------. (A. joule (J), B. watt (W), C. ampere (A))"},{"number":"xi","text":"------ current is good in long distance distribution of electrical power. (A. AC, B. DC, C. unidirectional)"},{"number":"xii","text":"Most generators give out ------. (A. alternating current, B. direct current, C.-both current)."},{"number":"xiii","text":"------ is used to control the brightness of the night lamp. (A. LED, B. LDR, C. LCD)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"A photodiode converts ------ into electrical current. (A. light, B. resistance, C. temperature)"},{"number":"xv","text":"------ rays cannot be deflected by electric and magnetic fields. (A. Gamma, B. Beta, C. Alpha)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"Under what condition the angular acceleration of a rotating object is equal to zero? The Ferris wheel starts from rest and reaches an angular velocity of 1.5 rad s⁻¹ over a 10 s period under the constant angular acceleration. (i) Find the angular acceleration of the Ferris wheel. (ii) How many revolutions does it make during 10 s?"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the optical features of the eye. A home requires 62 kWh of heat on a winter day to maintain a constant indoor temperature of 20℃. Assume that the temperature of hot water outlet is 60℃. (i) How much collector surface area does it need for a solar heating system that has a 20% efficiency? (ii) How large does the storage tank have to be to provide this much energy? (The average solar radiation per day in winter is about 6.5 kWh m⁻², specific heat capacity of water, c = 4184 J kg-1 K⁻¹)"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"How does wind turbine generate electricity? Determine the input power of the wind if the wind speed is 20 m s⁻¹ and blade length is 20 m. Density of air is 1.3 kg m⁻³."}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"Describe the advantages of LED. Draw the diagram of a simple LED indicator circuit."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"When the charge on a capacitor is increased, does its capacitance increase? Explain. Find the capacitance that can be obtained by combining three 10 µF capacitors in all possible ways."}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the circuit diagram for charging and discharging a capacitor. A parallel-plate capacitor of capacitance ‘C’ is given the charge ‘Q’ and then disconnected from the circuit. How much work is required to pull apart the plates of this capacitor to twice their original separation?"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"Describe the properties of gamma rays. A radioisotope has a half-life of 20 min. If there is initially 102.4 g of this isotope, how much time elapses for 12.8 g to be left?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the illustrating constant volume flow rate in a pipe. A compound microscope consists of two thin lenses, an objective of focal length 20 mm and an eyepiece of focal length 50 mm, placed 220 mm apart. If the final image is viewed at infinity, calculate the distance of the object from the objective."}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Define the laminar flow and turbulent flow. Draw the simple transformer and its symbol."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What are the differences between interference and diffraction? The distance between two points, called the proper length L0 is 1 km. An observer in motion with respect to the frame of reference of the two points measures 0.8 km, which is L. What is the relative speed of the frame of reference with respect to the observer?"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"What is the difference between electromotive force (emf) and potential difference (voltage)? Draw the characteristics of a zener diode and its circuit symbol."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"Give the formula for expressing De Morgan’s first theorem for two variables and construct its truth table. One coil of a transformer has 50 turns and the other coil has 1000 turns. The alternating voltage of 220 V is applied to the primary. Find the alternating voltage from the secondary when it is used as (i) a step-up transformer and (ii) a step-down transformer."}]}}}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'old_questions','2024 Set 5 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2024 · 5','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2024 Set 5</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2024-set5","year":2024,"set":5,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"In rotational motion, the object rotates about an axis."},{"number":"ii","text":"The viscosity of gases increases with an increase in temperature."},{"number":"iii","text":"Biomass contains stored chemical energy."},{"number":"iv","text":"An isochoric process occurs at constant pressure."},{"number":"v","text":"Ultrasound cannot be heard by human ear."},{"number":"vi","text":"Variable capacitors mostly use air as the dielectric medium."},{"number":"vii","text":"A battery converts mechanical energy into electrical energy to provide electrical power."},{"number":"viii","text":"Magnetic field strength is vector quantity."},{"number":"ix","text":"In the bright light, resistance of light depend resistor (LDR) is low."},{"number":"x","text":"Activity of a radioactive sample decreases with time."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"In nonuniform circular motion, an object is moving in a circular path with a varying -------."},{"number":"ii","text":"Fluid dynamics concerns with the fluid in -------."},{"number":"iii","text":"A large amount of ------- energy is stored in the fossil fuels."},{"number":"iv","text":"The ------- is the unit used for measuring sound intensity."},{"number":"v","text":"The ------- of the note is determined by its frequency."},{"number":"vi","text":"The lens in a compound microscope nearer the object is called the ----."},{"number":"vii","text":"Bright fringe has ------- intensity."},{"number":"viii","text":"Film capacitors use ------- film as the dielectric medium."},{"number":"ix","text":"The practical unit of electrical energy is -------."},{"number":"x","text":"Electrical ------ is the rate of transfer of electrical energy."},{"number":"xi","text":"An alternating current is a current that reverses its ------- at regular time intervals."},{"number":"xii","text":"Faraday’s law gives the ------- of the induced (emf)."},{"number":"xiii","text":"A thermistor can covert changes in ---- into changes in electric current."},{"number":"xiv","text":"There are two types of ------- breakdown regions in a Zener diode."},{"number":"xv","text":"Alpha rays are the most ------- of the three rays."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"Centripetal acceleration is present in ------- circular motion. (A. only uniform, B. only nonuniform, C. both uniform and nonuniform)"},{"number":"ii","text":"The normal force FN exerted by a banked road is ------- to the road. (A. perpendicular, B. parallel, C. directed)"},{"number":"iii","text":"There are ------- types of concentrated solar power (CSP) technologies. (A. one, B. two, C. four)"},{"number":"iv","text":"SI unit of thermal conductivity of the material is -------. (A. watt per metre per kelvin (W m⁻¹ K⁻¹), B. watt per square metre (W m⁻²), C. watt (W))"},{"number":"v","text":"Thermal efficiency for a heat engine is the ratio of the work output to ------- input. (A. heat, B. work, C. intensity)"},{"number":"vi","text":"A ------- controls the time during which light enters the camera through the lens. (A. film, B. aperture, C. shutter)"},{"number":"vii","text":"If the path difference is -------, the waves will interfere destructively. (A. λ/2, B. λ, C. 2λ)"},{"number":"viii","text":"A capacitor consists of two ------- separated by a small distance. (A. conductors, B. insulators, C. semiconductors)"},{"number":"ix","text":"In an electric generator, ----- energy is converted into electrical energy. (A. heat, B. mechanical, C. chemical)"},{"number":"x","text":"There is no ideal transformer with ------- efficiency. (A. 99 %, B. 99.5 %, C. 100 %)"},{"number":"xi","text":"The SI unit of magnetic flux is the -------. (A. weber (Wb), B. tesla (T), C. ampere per metre (A m⁻¹))"},{"number":"xii","text":"------- use ceramic as the dielectric material. (A. Ceramic capacitors, B. Electrolytic capacitors, C. Supercapacitors)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"The photodiode can be used as a photodetector to detect the ------- signals. (A. optical, B. heat, C. chemical)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"A few heavy elements with atomic number greater than ------- are radioactive or unstable. (A. 92, B. 83, C. 100)"},{"number":"xv","text":"Radio and television are examples of ------- mode of communication. (A. broadcast, B. point to point, C. telephony)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"How are the flow rate and the fluid velocity related? What will happen to the rise of liquid in a capillary tube if the radius of the tube is (i) increased, (ii) decreased? The shear stress at a point in a liquid is found to be 0.03 N m⁻². The velocity gradient at the point is 0.15 s⁻¹. What will be its viscosity (in poise) (1 Pa s = 10 poise)"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the diagram for thermodynamic cycle of heat engine. One gram of water (1 cm³) becomes 1671 cm³ of steam when boiled at a pressure of 1 atm. The heat of vaporization at this pressure is 2265 J g⁻¹. Compute the work done and the increase in internal energy. (1 atm = 5 1.013 × 10 Pa)"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"Why is it better to use more renewable energy resources rather than non-renewable resources? A dam which maximum head of 200 m produces to 2000 MW electrical power. What is the rate of falling water on the turbines? The turbine generator efficiency is 50%. (Density of water = 1000 kg m⁻³)"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"What are the differences between frequency modulation (FM) and amplitude modulation (AM)? Explain with illustrative diagrams."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"What is the electrical energy? Express its unit. Why do we use fuses in an electric circuit? An electric circuit installed in an office contains a 10 A fuse and the voltage is 220 V. Ten 100 W electric lamps and two 150 W refrigerators are being used there. (i) Find the cost of using all the lamps and two refrigerators for 10 h. (ii) Find the maximum number of 60 W electric lamps which can be safely used in addition. (Assume that electricity cost 50 kyats per unit.)"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the circuit diagram for charging and discharging a capacitor. A charged capacitor of capacitance C = 35 μF is discharged through a resistor of resistance R =120 Ω. (i) What is the time constant τ” of the discharging process? (ii) What is the elapsed time when the voltage falls to 10% of its original value?"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"What is a tracer? State some uses of radioactive tracers. Why is it important to use radioactive tracers with short half-lives in medical diagnosis? Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of (i) a 0.65 kg basketball thrown at a speed of 10 m s⁻¹ ,(ii) a nonrelativistic electron with a kinetic energy of 1 eV."}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the diagram for circular motion of a particle of an object. (i) What frequency is received by a person watching an oncoming ambulance moving at 110 km h⁻¹ and emitting a steady 800 Hz from its siren? The speed of sound on this day is 345 m s⁻¹ . (ii) What frequency does she receive after the ambulance has passed?"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Give comparisons between centripetal force and centrifugal force. Draw the diagrams to illustrate the electromotive force (emf) and terminal voltage of a battery."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What are meant by farsightedness and nearsightedness and how can they be corrected? If a fossil has 10% carbon-14 compared to a living sample, find the age of fossil. (half-life of carbobn-14 = 5730 years)"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"What is the major difference between alternating current (AC) and direct current (DC)? Why is AC better than DC in long distance distribution of electrical power? Is the current from the outlet of telephone charger, AC or DC? Draw the logic circuit represented by each of the following expressions: (i) ABC, (ii) AB + C, (iii) AB + CD."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"What are the advantages and disadvantages of light emitting diodes (LEDs)? The equivalent capacitance is 10 μF when n identical capacitors are connected in parallel and 0.4 μF when they are connected in series. Determine n and the capacitance of each capacitor."}]}}}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'old_questions','2024 Set 6 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2024 · 6','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2024 Set 6</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2024-set6","year":2024,"set":6,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"Angular velocity and angular acceleration are scalar quantities."},{"number":"ii","text":"Inertia causes object to move in a circle."},{"number":"iii","text":"Energy demand is increased year by year."},{"number":"iv","text":"Some of the weather conditions are created by heat radiation."},{"number":"v","text":"An echo is repetition of sound due to the reflection of sound."},{"number":"vi","text":"The capacitors can be used in both electrical and electronic applications."},{"number":"vii","text":"A source of electromotive force has an internal resistance."},{"number":"viii","text":"A changing magnetic field could produce a current."},{"number":"ix","text":"A normal diode allows current to flow in both directions."},{"number":"x","text":"Positron is also called the antiparticle of proton."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"------- is a substance that offers no permanent resistance to deforming forces."},{"number":"ii","text":"A ------ is a body that does not deform or change shape."},{"number":"iii","text":"Nuclear energy is ------ energy."},{"number":"iv","text":"------ of heat engine is the ratio of work output to heat input."},{"number":"v","text":"For every 10 dB added to the sound level, the loudness of the sound is increased by ------."},{"number":"vi","text":"The lens nearer the object is called the ------."},{"number":"vii","text":"There are two types of wave front; plane-wave front and ------ wave front."},{"number":"viii","text":"A supercapacitor is an ------ with a capacitance value much higher than other capacitors."},{"number":"ix","text":"The capacitor is similar to a ------ battery."},{"number":"x","text":"If the current flowing through a resistor is doubled the amount of heat produced by it becomes ------ times larger."},{"number":"xi","text":"In generators, mechanical energy is converted into ------ energy."},{"number":"xii","text":"Bulbs in electrical wiring of houses are connected in ------ across the main line."},{"number":"xiii","text":"The voltage at which Zener breakdown occurs is called the ------."},{"number":"xiv","text":"Boolean algebra is a branch of ------."},{"number":"xv","text":"Activity is ------ of a radioactive sample."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"In horizontal circular motion, weight is always ------. (A. downward, B. upward, C. inward)"},{"number":"ii","text":"The study of the flow of fluid is called ------. (A. hydrostatic, B. hydrodynamics, C. hydraulic)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Biomass contains stored ------ energy. (A. chemical, B. thermal, C. electrical)"},{"number":"iv","text":"Heat convection process take place in a ------. (A. solid, B. gas, C. fluid)"},{"number":"v","text":"The speed of sound is ------ in solids than liquids and gases. (A. higher, B. lower, C. the same)"},{"number":"vi","text":"People with ------ can see clearly objects which are at infinity. (A. farsightedness, B. nearsightedness, C. normal vision)"},{"number":"vii","text":"------ needs at least two coherent sources of light. (A. Diffraction, B. Refraction, C. Interference)"},{"number":"viii","text":"The farad is a ------ unit of capacitance of a capacitor. (A. very small, B. normal, C. very large)"},{"number":"ix","text":"Electrical power is the rate of transfer of ------. (A. mechanical energy, B. chemical energy, C. electrical energy)"},{"number":"x","text":"Which of the following metals cannot be used as fuse wire? (A. iron, B. silver, C. tin-lead alloy)"},{"number":"xi","text":"Most of the transformers have full load efficiency ------. (A. between 95% to 98.5%, B. between 50% to 60%, C. 100%)"},{"number":"xii","text":"Which of the following meters can measure an alternating current? (A. Voltmeter, B. Ammeter, C. Moving coil galvanometer)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"In bright light, LDR becomes a ------ of electric current. (A. good conductor, B. poor conductor, C. good insulator)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"In alpha decay, an atomic nucleus emits an alpha particle with mass number ------ and atomic number reduces by two. (A. reduces by two, B. reduces by four, C. increases by four)"},{"number":"xv","text":"------ are massless and move at the speed of light in vacuum. (A. Neutrons, B. Protons, C. Photons)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"Describe the analogous kinematic equations of linear and angular motion. What is the tension in a 1 m long string that is spinning a 0.5 kg stone in a horizontal circle with 3 rev s⁻¹."}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the optical features of the human eye with labeled diagram. One gram of water (1 cm³) becomes 1671 cm³ of steam when boiled at a pressure of 1 atm. The heat of vaporization at this pressure is 2265 J g⁻¹. Compute the work done and the increase in internal energy."}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What is the main source of energy? State the changes in form of energy while producing hydroelectricity. How many photons are emitted in 1 s by a 7.5 mW CO₂ laser with wavelength 10.6 μm? (Planck’s constant, h = 6.62 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ )"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"Construct the truth table for two inputs different gates (OR, NOR, NAND, XOR and XNOR). Draw the circuit symbol and simple circuit diagram of photodiode."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"What must be done to increase the capacitance of a capacitor? The plates of a parallel-plate capacitor are 50 cm² in area and 1 mm apart. (i) What is its capacitance? (ii) When the capacitor is connected to a 24 V battery, what is the charge on each plate? (iii) What is the energy of the capacitor? (εᵣ = 1, ε₀ = 8.85 × 10⁻¹² C² N⁻¹ m⁻²)"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the circuit diagram for batteries in series aiding connected with an external resistor. When a battery is connected to a 3 Ω resistor, it drives a current of 0.6 A through the resistor. When it is connected to a 8 Ω resistor, it drives a current of 0.2 A through the resistor. Find the emf and the internal resistance of the battery."}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"Compare the ionizing and penetrating powers of alpha, beta and gamma rays. Suppose that initially there was 100 mg of iodine-131 and its half- life is 8 days. How much would it be left after 24 days?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the diagrams of (i) stream lines (ii) laminar flow and (iii) turbulent flow of fluid. An ambulance travelling at 44 m s⁻¹ approaches a car heading in a same direction at the speed of 28 m s⁻¹. The ambulance driver has a siren sounding at 550 Hz. At what frequency does the driver of the car hear the siren? What will be the frequency of the siren heard by the driver of the car when the ambulance overtakes his car? (Speed of siren sound = 330 m s⁻¹)"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Derive expression for terminal velocity when a ball of radius ‘r’ is dropped through a liquid of viscosity ‘h’ and density ‘r’. Draw the symbols of polarized capacitor, fixed capacitor and variable capacitor."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What will happen on the interference pattern of a double slit, if (i) separation between the two slits is decreased? (ii) wavelength of light is increased? A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (mₚ = 1840 mₑ ) p e"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"To improve the efficiency of a transformer, what features should be taken into consideration? Draw the circuit diagram of fire alarm system."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"What are the differences between FM and AM? An electric welding machine uses a current of 400 A. The machine has a transformer whose primary coil has 400 turns and draws 4 A from a 220 V power line. (i) How many turns does the secondary coil have? (ii) What is the voltage across the secondary coil?"}]}}}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'old_questions','2024 Set 7 (Foreign) | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2024 · 7','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2024 Set 7 (Foreign)</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2024-set7","year":2024,"set":7,"sample":false,"foreign":true,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"Centrifugal force in circular motion is a real force."},{"number":"ii","text":"The viscosity of liquids increases rapidly with an increase in temperature."},{"number":"iii","text":"The change in internal energy of a system is, ΔU = Q + W."},{"number":"iv","text":"Sound intensity is a direct measure of the energy reaching an ear drum."},{"number":"v","text":"A compact disc is an example of reflection gratings."},{"number":"vi","text":"A capacitor stores electrical energy in the form of a magnetic field."},{"number":"vii","text":"The sources of electromotive force convert energy from some other forms into electrical form."},{"number":"viii","text":"Current flowing in power transmission line is alternating current."},{"number":"ix","text":"The current flows through Zener diode only in forward-bias mode."},{"number":"x","text":"In β⁻ decay, the atomic number of daughter nucleus increases by one."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"When a car drives on a curved flat road (unbanked road), ------- force behaves as a centripetal force."},{"number":"ii","text":"------- acceleration is present in both uniform and non-uniform circular motion."},{"number":"iii","text":"The total amount of radiation energy passing through per unit area and per unit time is called -------."},{"number":"iv","text":"Carnot engine is not ------- efficient."},{"number":"v","text":"An echo is repetition of sound due to the ------- of sound."},{"number":"vi","text":"The pupil automatically dilates in dim light and ------- in bright light."},{"number":"vii","text":"The angular position of a point of a periodic wave is known as the ----."},{"number":"viii","text":"The energy stored by the capacitor is W = -------."},{"number":"ix","text":"The product of the resistance R and the capacitance C is called ------- of a capacitor charging or discharging process."},{"number":"x","text":"Electrical power is the rate of transfer of -------."},{"number":"xi","text":"The SI unit of magnetic flux density is -------."},{"number":"xii","text":"Faraday law gives the ------- of induced emf."},{"number":"xiii","text":"The process of changing some characteristics of a carrier wave in accordance with the intensity of the signal is kwon as -------."},{"number":"xiv","text":"The rate of decay of a radioactive sample is called -------."},{"number":"xv","text":"The momentum p of a particle and its associated wavelength λ are related by the equation λ = h/p."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"In uniform circular motion, the magnitude of ------- remains constant. (A. displacement, B. velocity, C. acceleration)"},{"number":"ii","text":"The force between molecules of same substance is called -------. (A. cohesion, B. adhesion, C. weak interaction)"},{"number":"iii","text":"What type of energy is stored in the fossil fuels? (A. heat energy, B. chemical energy, C. potential energy)"},{"number":"iv","text":"Isochoric process occurs at constant -------. (A. volume, B. temperature, C. pressure)"},{"number":"v","text":"What quantity determines the loudness of sound? (A. frequency, B. amplitude, C. wavelength)"},{"number":"vi","text":"What type of lens is used as an eyepiece to produce an erect final image in terrestrial telescope? (A. convex lens, B. concave lens, C. magnifying lens)"},{"number":"vii","text":"What type of wave emerges from a slit when a plane wave passes through a slit? (A. plane wave, B. circular wave, C. both circular and plane wave)"},{"number":"viii","text":"Two conductors of capacitor of capacitance C are brought together to a third of their original separation. What is its capacitance now? % % (A. C, B. C, C. 3 C, &"},{"number":"ix","text":"The capacitors are connected in series each capacitor has the same ----. (A. charge, B. potential difference, C. capacitance)"},{"number":"x","text":"On which factor does the heat produced in a current carrying conductor depend? (A. current, B. temperature, C. pressure)"},{"number":"xi","text":"In charging battery, the potential difference between the terminals is ------. (A. E + Ir, B. E – Ir, C. E)"},{"number":"xii","text":"If two batteries having equal emfs and equal internal resistances are connected in parallel, what is resultant internal resistance of combination? , 2 (A. 2 r, B. , C. r ) *"},{"number":"xiii","text":"There are ------- types of reverse breakdown regions in a zener diode. (A. one, B. two, C. three)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"What semiconductor device that converts light into electrical current? (A. LED, B. light dependent resistor, C. photodiode)"},{"number":"xv","text":"Which rays cannot be deflected by electric and magnetic fields? (A. alpha ryas, B. beta rays, C. gamma rays)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"Define laminar flow and turbulent flow of fluids. Calculate the pressure and speed of water at points B and C shown in the figure. At point A, v₁ = 10 m s⁻¹, p₁ = 300 kPa, A₁ = 3 m², and ρ_water = 1000 kg m⁻³."}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the diagram of a terrestrial telescope that uses a concave lens as an eyepiece. What is the phase difference for two waves of the same frequency arriving at a point with the respective path lengths of 6λ and 4.5λ? Is it constructive or destructive interference?"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What is biomass? Give one type of biomass energy source. Describe the sequence of energy transfer into electrical energy from (i) solar energy (ii) nuclear energy. The hydroturbine receives water from a reservoir at an elevation of 100 m above it. What is the minimum water flow in kg s⁻¹ to produce a steady turbine output of 50 MW if the turbine generator efficiency is 75%? (density of water = 1000 kg m⁻³, g = 9.8 m s⁻² )"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"What is a zener diode? How do you understand the avalanche breakdown and zener breakdown? What is the main difference between a zener diode and a normal diode? Draw the characteristic curve of the zener diode."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"When the distance between the two parallel plates of a capacitor is doubled, by what percent does its capacitance change? Three capacitors of capacitance 3 µF, 10 µF and 15 µF are connected in series with 100 V battery. What is the charge and the potential difference on each capacitor?"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Illustrate the graphical representations of the magnitude of DC and AC voltages as a function of time. A 2 kW transformer is used to step down an AC supply of 240 V to 60 V (i) What is the turns ratio of this transformer? (ii) What will the output current be if there is a 10% power loss in the transformer? (iii) How large is the output current if there is no power loss (i.e. 100% efficiency)?"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"Define (i) half-life and (ii) nuclear reaction. If a fossil has 10% carbon-14 compared to a living sample, find the age of the fossil. (half-life of carbon-14 = 5730 years)"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a diagram showing how the horizontal component of the normal force provides centripetal force when a car drives in a circular path on a banked road. (i) How much heat per second is conducted through a wooden wall of area 25 m² and thickness 0.04 m if the temperature inside is 20 °C and the temperature outside is −10 °C? The thermal conductivity of wood is 8.37 × 10⁻² W m⁻¹ K⁻¹. (ii) An engine takes in 9220 J and does 1750 J of work each cycle while operating between 689 °C and 397 °C. What is its actual efficiency?"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"In circular motion, how is a tangential acceleration produced? On a rotating carousel, a child sits on a horse near the outer edge, and another child sits on a lion halfway out from the centre. Which child has the greater linear velocity? What are open circuit and closed circuit? Illustrate with diagram."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What is Doppler effect? A rhinoceros uses frequencies down to 10 Hz to talk one another. Can rhinoceros be able to communicate over long distances further than 4 km? Why? Simplify the following expressions if possible. 5 5 (i) A + AB + ABC, (ii) (A + B) C + ABC"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"Why do we use fuses in an electric circuit? Why is electrical energy transformed into heat energy when a current flows through a resistor? Draw the diagrams to show the nuclear fission and fission chain reaction."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"What is a transducer? Describe the logic symbol, Boolean equation and truth table of XOR gate. A battery has an emf of 6 V and an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω. How many batteries are necessary to pass a current of 1 A through a 22 Ω resistor in an electric circuit?"}]}}}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'old_questions','2025 Set 1 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2025 · 1','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2025 Set 1</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2025-set1","year":2025,"set":1,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"Every particle on the rigid body has the same angular speed."},{"number":"ii","text":"A centripetal force makes the object to turn a curved path."},{"number":"iii","text":"Due to less emission of greenhouse gases, solar energy can also improve air quality."},{"number":"iv","text":"Some of the weather conditions are created by heat radiation."},{"number":"v","text":"The speed of sound is higher in liquids than solids."},{"number":"vi","text":"If one conductor of a capacitor has a charge +Q the other has a −Q."},{"number":"vii","text":"Electricity is produced by chemical reaction in the battery."},{"number":"viii","text":"A transformer is used to change the voltage of a direct current."},{"number":"ix","text":"Photodiodes work in forward biased mode."},{"number":"x","text":"All elements in nature are not radioactive."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"Centrifugal force acts radially -------- the centre of the circle."},{"number":"ii","text":"-------- helps bringing water up into the roots."},{"number":"iii","text":"The -------- energy is produced by the difference in sea levels."},{"number":"iv","text":"The -------- of an object depends on the wavelength of radiation."},{"number":"v","text":"An -------- is repetition of sound due to the reflection of sound."},{"number":"vi","text":"The fibre optics works on the principle of --------."},{"number":"vii","text":"The angular position of a point of a periodic wave is the --------."},{"number":"viii","text":"Electrolytic capacitor has a wide -------- capacity."},{"number":"ix","text":"The final current is equal to ------- when the capacitor is fully charged."},{"number":"x","text":"Electromotive force is a -------- quantity."},{"number":"xi","text":"The practical unit of electrical energy is --------."},{"number":"xii","text":"The -------- wire is usually at zero volt."},{"number":"xiii","text":"-------- diode allows current to flow in both directions."},{"number":"xiv","text":"Boolean algebra is a branch of --------."},{"number":"xv","text":"Neutrons released from a -------- reaction are fast neutrons."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"The motion of the blades of a fan is -------- motion. (A. uniform, B. linear, C. rotational)"},{"number":"ii","text":"Surface tension can also be referred to as a force because it is the tension between -------- molecules. (A. solid, B. liquid, C. fluid)"},{"number":"iii","text":"What principle pulls water into the penstock? (A. Gravity, B. Force of the volume of water, C. Turbine)"},{"number":"iv","text":"An -------- process occurs at a constant temperature. (A. isochoric, B. isobaric, C. isothermal)"},{"number":"v","text":"The loudness of the note depends upon the -------- of the wave that produces it. (A. amplitude, B. frequency, C. wavelength)"},{"number":"vi","text":"The yellow spot which is the most light-sensitive spot is --------. (A. behind the retina, B. in front of the retina, C. on the retina)"},{"number":"vii","text":"Huygens'' principle states that every point on a -------- may be considered as a source of secondary wavelets. (A. wavelet, B. wavefront, C. new wavefront)"},{"number":"viii","text":"When the capacitors are connected in series, each capacitor has the same --------. (A. charge, B. capacitance, C. potential difference)"},{"number":"ix","text":"The amount of heat produced in a resistor due to a current flowing through it is -------- to the square of the current. (A. directly proportional, B. inversely proportional, C. not related)"},{"number":"x","text":"Which quantity determines the rate at which electrical energy is delivered by a current? (A. electromotive force, B. electrical power, C. electric current)"},{"number":"xi","text":"In -------- the electrons flow steadily in the same direction all the time. (A. an alternating current, B. a direct current, C. an electric current)"},{"number":"xii","text":"Because of power losses, there is no ideal transformer with -------- efficiency. (Α. 100%, Β. 95%, C. 98.5%)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"A -------- is a device that transforms a signal from one energy form to another energy form. (A. transducer, B. capacitor, C. resistor)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"The -------- the wavelength of the matter wave, the faster the particle moves. (A. larger, B. smaller, C. lower)"},{"number":"xv","text":"-------- cannot be deflected by electric and magnetic fields. (A. Alpha rays, B. Beta rays, C. Gamma rays)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"Under what condition the angular acceleration of a rotating object is equal to zero? In circular motion how is tangential acceleration produced? The Ferris wheel starts from rest and reaches an angular velocity of 1.5 rad s⁻¹ over a 10 s period under the constant angular acceleration. (i) Find the angular acceleration of the Ferris wheel. (ii) How many revolutions does it make during 10 s?"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the diagram for thermodynamic cycle of heat engine. What frequency is received by a person watching an oncoming ambulance moving at 110 km h⁻¹ and emitting a steady 800 Hz sound from its siren? The speed of sound on this day is 345 m s⁻¹. What frequency does she receive after the ambulance has passed?"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"Why is it better to use more renewable energy resources rather than non-renewable resources? A dam with a maximum head of 200 m produces 2000 MW of electrical power. What is the rate of falling water on the turbines if the turbine-generator efficiency is 50%? (g = 9.8 m s⁻², ρ_water = 1000 kg m⁻³)"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"What is meant by \"AM and FM\"? What are the differences between FM and AM? Draw the diagram for simple LED indicator circuit."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"When an insulating material is inserted between the conductors of a capacitor in a vacuum, does its capacitance increase or decrease? Explain. What is the equivalent unit of farad? A 35 µF capacitor is needed, but only 10 µF capacitors are available. How should a minimum number of 10 µF capacitors be connected so that the combination has a capacitance of 35 µF?"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a simple circuit diagram of two batteries in series opposing connected with an external resistor. When a 12 V battery of negligible internal resistance is connected to a resistor, a current of 3 A flows through it. When another battery of emf 6 V is in the circuit in series with the first one, the current flowing through the resistor remains at 3 A. Find the internal resistance of the second battery."}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"How can you explain the two main postulates of Einstein special theory of relativity? Why is it important to use radioactive tracers with short half-lives in medical diagnosis? Suppose there was 8 g of radon at t = 0 and its half-life is 3.8 days. How much would be left after (i) 7.6 days (ii) 11.4 days?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a diagram to show the horizontal component of normal force provides centripetal force. A telescope consists of two thin converging lenses of focal lengths 100 cm and 10 cm respectively. It is used to view an object 2000 cm from the objective. What is the separation of the lenses if the final image is 25 cm from the eyelens? Determine the magnifying power for an observer whose eye is close to the eyelens."}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"What is the difference between laminar flow and turbulent flow? How does temperature affect the viscosity of liquids? Express the Bernoulli''s equation and explain the symbols. Draw the diagrams for simple transformer and its symbol."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What are the conditions for constructive interference and destructive interference? What happens to the interference pattern of a double slit if (i) the separation between the slits is decreased or (ii) the wavelength of light is increased? A proton and an electron are each accelerated from rest through a potential difference of 1 kV. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (mₚ = 1840 mₑ, q = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C, h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s)"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"Why is Faraday''s law important? Differentiate between the magnetic flux and magnetic flux density. Is the current from the outlet of telephone charger, AC or DC? Draw the logic circuit represented by each of the following expressions: (i) ABC (ii) AB + C (iii) AB + CD"}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"What is a thermistor? How many types of thermistors are there? Name them and state the main difference between them. A circular coil of radius 8 cm and 20 turns is rotated about its vertical diameter with an angular speed of 150 rad s⁻¹ in a uniform horizontal magnetic field of 3 × 10⁻² T."}]}}}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'old_questions','2025 Set 10 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2025 · 10','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2025 Set 10</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2025-set10","year":2025,"set":10,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"Angular velocity is the rate of rotation with respect to displacement."},{"number":"ii","text":"Centrifugal force in a circular motion is not a real force."},{"number":"iii","text":"Heat convection occurs only in a liquid or a gas, never in a solid."},{"number":"iv","text":"Solar energy is a type of non-renewable energy."},{"number":"v","text":"Constructive interference occurs when the phase difference is π radians."},{"number":"vi","text":"A capacitor stores electrical energy in the form of an electric field."},{"number":"vii","text":"Lenz''s law gives the direction of the induced emf."},{"number":"viii","text":"The practical unit of electrical energy is joule (J)."},{"number":"ix","text":"Active electrical components require a power source to operate."},{"number":"x","text":"Liquid crystals do not emit light directly."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"A satellite orbiting a planet is supported by the ---------."},{"number":"ii","text":"--------- refers to forces between molecules of same substance."},{"number":"iii","text":"A --------- is basically a p-n junction diode."},{"number":"iv","text":"An --------- process occurs at constant pressure."},{"number":"v","text":"By using ---------, the audible frequency range can be determined."},{"number":"vi","text":"Illuminance Ev is the total --------- incident on a surface per unit area."},{"number":"vii","text":"A --------- can disperse light into its wavelength components."},{"number":"viii","text":"For a vacuum, εᵣ = 1 and for other media ---------."},{"number":"ix","text":"A --------- is a thin short wire of tin-lead alloy."},{"number":"x","text":"Joule''s law of electricity and heat is given by ---------."},{"number":"xi","text":"One way to reduce power loss is to use very thick cables of --------- resistance."},{"number":"xii","text":"The lamps are connected in --------- in the lighting circuit."},{"number":"xiii","text":"The current is generated when photons are absorbed in the ---------."},{"number":"xiv","text":"The OR gate with inverted output is called a --------- gate."},{"number":"xv","text":"The SI unit for activity is ---------."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"If the angular velocity ω is increasing, the angular acceleration α is --. (A. positive, B. negative, C. zero)"},{"number":"ii","text":"Due to capillary action, a liquid will rise in a tube, if the angle of contact is ---------. (A. acute, B. obtuse, C. 90°)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Windmills convert wind energy directly into ---------. (A. electrical energy, B. mechanical energy, C. nuclear energy)"},{"number":"iv","text":"The --------- law of thermodynamics is an application of conservation energy for heat and thermodynamic processes. (A. first, B. second, C. third)"},{"number":"v","text":"--------- frequency sounds which are under the lower limit of audibility (20 Hz) are called infrasound. (A. Low, B. High, C. Normal)"},{"number":"vi","text":"When near objects are viewed, the ciliary muscles contract and the eyelens becomes ---------. (A. less convex, B. more convex, C. less concave)"},{"number":"vii","text":"Monochromatic light means that it has a --------- wavelength. (A. single, B. double, C. triple)"},{"number":"viii","text":"--------- can also be used in a time-dependent circuit (timer circuit). (A. Capacitors, B. Resistors, C. Insulators)"},{"number":"ix","text":"In charging a battery, the potential difference between the terminals is equal to ---------. (A. E+ Ir, B. Ir, C. IR)"},{"number":"x","text":"There are joules in one kilowatt hour. 6 (A. 4.2, В. 1000, С. 3.6 × 10 )"},{"number":"xi","text":"When the field is perpendicular to the surface area, the magnetic flux is (A. zero, B. BA, C. maximum)"},{"number":"xii","text":"In transformer, the voltage in the secondary and the voltage in the primary have ---------. (A. different frequency, B. same frequency, C. minimum frequency)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"In the Negative Temperature Coefficient (NTC) thermistor, the resistance --------- as the temperature increases. (A. increases, B. zero, C. decreases)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"A --------- is a device for converting a non-electrical input into an electrical signal (or) vice versa. (A. transducer, B. transmitter, C. receiver)"},{"number":"xv","text":"By measuring the activity of ---------, the age of the remains of plants and animals can be estimated. (A. carbon 12, B. carbon 13, C. carbon 14)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"How are the flow rate and fluid velocity related? On which factors does the viscosity of a liquid depend? Air streams horizontally past a small airplane’s wings such that the speed is 70 m s⁻¹ over the top surface and 60 m s⁻¹ past the bottom surface. If the plane has a wing area of 16.2 m² on the top and on the bottom, what is the net vertical force that the air exerts on the airplane? The density of the air is 1.2 kg m⁻³."}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a ray diagram of a terrestrial telescope. An automobile engine has an efficiency of 20% and produces an average of 23 000 J of mechanical work per second during operation. (i) How much heat input is required per second and (ii) how much heat is discharged as waste heat from this engine per second?"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What is biomass? Give the types of biomass energy sources. A hydro-turbine receives water from a reservoir at an elevation of 100 m above it. What is the minimum water flow in kg s⁻¹ to produce a steady turbine output of 50 MW if the turbine-generator efficiency is 75%? (g = 9.8 m s⁻², ρ_water = 1000 kg m⁻³)"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"Describe the disadvantages of LED. Give the main uses for Zener diode and LED. Draw the circuit diagram of fire alarm system."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"When the distance between two parallel plates having the charges of equal magnitude and opposite signs is reduced, what will happen to the capacitance and potential difference of the plates? Three capacitors of capacitances 3 µF, 10 µF and 15 µF are connected in series with 100 V battery. What is the charge and the potential difference on each capacitor?"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Illustrate the graphical representations of the magnitude of DC and AC voltages as a function of time. A 3 kW transformer is used to step down an AC supply of 240 V to 60 V. (i) What is the turns ratio of this transformer? (ii) What will the output current be if there is a 10% power loss in the transformer? (iii) How large is the output current if there is no power loss (i.e. 100% efficiency)?"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"Compare the ionizing and penetrating powers of alpha, beta and gamma rays. Can radioactive elements be produced artificially? Suppose that initially there was 100 mg of iodine-131 and its half-life is 8 days. How much would it be left after 24 days?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a diagram to show the directions of centripetal force, centripetal acceleration and linear velocity of an object in uniform circular motion. Light of wavelength 580 nm is incident on a slit of width 0.3 mm. The observing screen is placed 2 m from the slit. Find the positions of the first dark fringes and the width of the central bright fringes."}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Express any two relations between the linear and rotational quantities. Why is centripetal acceleration produced in a circular motion? Draw the circuit diagrams for batteries in series aiding and batteries in parallel connected with an external resistor."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"Give two applications of echo. Why is the intensity of an echo less than that of the original sound? Is there a Doppler shift if the source and observer move in the same direction with the same velocity? Explain. Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of (i) a 0.70 kg basketball thrown at a speed of 10 m s⁻¹ and (ii) a nonrelativistic electron with a kinetic energy of 1 eV. (h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, mₑ = 9.1 × 10⁻³¹ kg)"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"Write down the equation of Faraday''s law for a wire loop with N identical turns. What does negative sign indicate in Faraday''s law of electromagnetic induction formula? Does the induced emf in a circuit depend on the resistance of the circuit? Draw a diagram to show the nuclear fission."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"Give the formula for expressing De Morgan''s second theorem for two variables and construct its truth table. An electric stove of 1200 W is connected to a 220 V mains line. (i) Find its resistance. (ii) Find the current flowing through it. (iii) Find the amount of calories produced in one second by it. (iv) Find the electrical power produced by it when the voltage of the mains line drops to 180 V."}]}}}'::jsonb,10,true),
(12,'old_questions','2025 Set 11 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2025 · 11','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2025 Set 11</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2025-set11","year":2025,"set":11,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"In uniform circular motion, it has both tangential acceleration and centripetal acceleration."},{"number":"ii","text":"An electron orbiting the nucleus is supported by the centrifugal force."},{"number":"iii","text":"The tidal energy is produced by the difference in sea levels."},{"number":"iv","text":"The blackbody is a perfect absorber of radiation."},{"number":"v","text":"Sound waves can travel through a vacuum."},{"number":"vi","text":"When capacitors having different capacitances are connected in parallel, they have the same charge."},{"number":"vii","text":"When a current flows through the nichrome coil, it produces heat energy."},{"number":"viii","text":"The direct current is a steady unidirectional current."},{"number":"ix","text":"Light emitting diode can directly produce white light and invisible light."},{"number":"x","text":"Shielding is a protective barrier, usually a dense material."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"One revolution per second (1 rps) is equal to -------- radian per second."},{"number":"ii","text":"In turbulent flow, the flow or path of the fluid particles are --------."},{"number":"iii","text":"-------- is one of the most powerful renewable sources of energy."},{"number":"iv","text":"The -------- of a system is the sum of the energies of all the constituent particles."},{"number":"v","text":"Young''s modulus and the bulk modulus are -------- properties of the medium."},{"number":"vi","text":"The -------- is a circular opening through which the light passes."},{"number":"vii","text":"------- is always perpendicular to the direction of propagation (or) rays."},{"number":"viii","text":"The working voltages of the film capacitors are up to -------- V."},{"number":"ix","text":"The charge of a capacitor is directly proportional to its --------."},{"number":"x","text":"In an electric generator, ----- energy is converted into electrical energy."},{"number":"xi","text":"The tungsten filament becomes hot when a -------- flows through it."},{"number":"xii","text":"The core of a transformer is built up of thin iron sheets of high resistance, called --------."},{"number":"xiii","text":"A -------- is a light controlled variable resistor."},{"number":"xiv","text":"The process of converting energy from one form to another is called -- ------."},{"number":"xv","text":"When the plants and animals are ----, they absorb and give out carbon."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"Limiting speed of a car to turn successfully the banked road depends on the --------. (A. angle of banking, B. friction, C. weight of the car)"},{"number":"ii","text":"The drag force resisting the fall of small spherical objects through a fluid medium is expressed by --------. (A. Pascal''s law, B. Stokes'' ław, C. Bernoulli''s equation)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Which of the following is a non-renewable source of energy? (A. Sun, B. Wind, C. Fossil fuels)"},{"number":"iv","text":"In which medium does the heat conduction take place? (A. in solid, B. in liquid, C. in gas)"},{"number":"v","text":"What value of sound intensity in dB increases by a factor of 100? (A. 100 dB, B. 30 dB, C. 20 dB)"},{"number":"vi","text":"Which of the following is the SI basic unit of luminous intensity? (A. lux (lx), B. candela (cd), C. lumen (lm))"},{"number":"vii","text":"In a double slit experiment, if the distance between the slits and the screen is increased, the fringe width will --------. (A. increase, B. decrease, C. not change)"},{"number":"viii","text":"When the distance between the two parallel plates of a capacitor is doubled, by what percent does its capacitance change? (A. decreases 50%, B. increases 50%, C. decreases 0%)"},{"number":"ix","text":"Which quantity determines the rate at which electrical energy is delivered by a current? (A. Potential difference, B. Electrical energy, C. Electrical power)"},{"number":"x","text":"The heating element of an electric iron is controlled by a -------- to maintain the selected temperature. (A. capacitor, B. resistor, C. thermostat)"},{"number":"xi","text":"Which of the following is the SI unit of magnetic flux density? (A, tesla (T), B. ampere per metre (Am¹), C. weber (Wb))"},{"number":"xii","text":"In any electrical appliance the -------- wire is always connected to the metal case. (A. live, B. neutral, C. earth) ;"},{"number":"xiii","text":"By using basic rules of Boolean algebra, the output of (A∙0) and (A∙ A) is equal to --------. (A. 0 (zero), B. 1 (one), C. A)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"The laws of physics are the -------- in all inertial frames of reference. (A. constant, B. different, C. same)"},{"number":"xv","text":"Complete the following decay process. Which decay process is it? ¹⁴₆C → ¹⁴₇N + ⁰₋₁e + ν̅ₑ. (A. ⁰₋₁e, β⁻ decay; B. ⁰₊₁e, β⁺ decay; C. γ, gamma decay.)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"As water in a level pipe passes from a narrower cross-sectional area to a wider cross-sectional area, does the pressure change? Explain. A large storage tank, open at the top and filled with water, develops a small hole in its side at a point 14.0 m below the water level. The rate of flow from the leak is found to be 4.69 × 10⁻⁴ m³ s⁻¹. Determine (i) the speed at which the water leaves the hole and (ii) the diameter of the hole. (g = 9.8 m s⁻²)"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a clear diagram of the human eye and label its important parts. A grating containing 4000 slits per centimetre is illuminated with a monochromatic light and produces the second-order bright line at a 30° angle. What is the wavelength of the light used?"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What is biomass? Give the types of biomass energy sources. A home requires 62 kWh of heat on a winter day to maintain a constant indoor temperature of 20 °C. Assume that the temperature of hot water outlet is 60 °C. (i) How much collector surface area does it need for a solar heating system that has a 20% efficiency? (ii) How large does the storage tank have to be to provide this much energy? (The average solar radiation per day in winter is about 6.5 kWh m⁻², 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J)"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"What are the basic components of an electronic communication system? How many basic modes of communication are there? Explain with examples. Draw the block diagram for analog communication system."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"On what factors does the capacitance of a capacitor depend? In capacitor charging and discharging, why is a resistor required to connect with the capacitor? The plates of a parallel-plate capacitor are 50 cm² in area and 1 mm apart. (i) What is its capacitance? (ii) When the capacitor is connected to a 24 V battery, what is the charge on each plate? (iii) What is the energy of the capacitor? (ε₀ = 8.85 × 10⁻¹² F m⁻¹)"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the circuit diagram of batteries in series aiding connected with an external resistor. An electric circuit installed in an office contains a 10 A fuse and the voltage is 220 V. Ten 100 W electric lamps and two 150 W refrigerators are being used there. (i) Find the cost of using all the lamps and two refrigerators for 10 h. (ii) Find the maximum number of 60 W electric lamps which can be safely used in addition. (Assume that electricity costs 50 kyats per unit.)"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"What is radioactivity? Name some radioactive elements. Describe the exponential law of radioactive decay. Initially at t = 0 there was 1 g of radon and at t = 3.8 days there was 0.5 g of radon. (i) What is the half-life of radon? (ii) How much of the element would be left after 7.6 days and 11.4 days?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the diagram to show the directions of centripetal force, centripetal acceleration and linear velocity for uniform circular motion. One gram of water (1 cm³) becomes 1671 cm³ of steam when boiled at a⁻¹ pressure of 1 atm. The heat of vaporization at this pressure is 2265 J g . Compute the work done and the increase in internal energy. (l atm = 5 1.013 × 10 Pa)"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Imagine a car driving over a hillock at a constant speed. Once the car has reached the apex of the hillock, does it have the acceleration? If so, what is the direction of acceleration? Does the centripetal force and centrifugal force constitute an action- reaction pair? Explain. Draw the parallel-plate capacitor and circuit diagram for charging a capacitor."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"How many cases are there in the Doppler effect? Describe them and express the general Doppler-effect equation. A proton and an electron are each accelerated from rest through a potential difference of 1 kV. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (mₚ = 1840 mₑ, q = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C)"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"What are the colours of the live, neutral and earth wires in a wiring system? Explain the major difference between AC and DC current. Draw the circuit diagram illustrating the street lighting system."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"How are the electron-hole pairs produced in the photodiode? Where are photodiodes used? An electric welding machine uses a current of 400 A. The machine has a transformer whose primary coil has 400 turns and draws 4 A from a 220 V power line. (i) How many turns does the secondary coil have? (ii) What is the voltage across the secondary coil?"}]}}}'::jsonb,11,true),
(12,'old_questions','2025 Set 12 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2025 · 12','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2025 Set 12</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2025-set12","year":2025,"set":12,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"In a circular motion, the object just moves in a circle."},{"number":"ii","text":"A satellite orbiting a planet is supported by the centrifugal force."},{"number":"iii","text":"A solar cell is basically a p-n junction diode."},{"number":"iv","text":"Doppler ultrasound is a technique that is used to examine blood flow."},{"number":"v","text":"The shutter speed is expressed in terms of the exposure time."},{"number":"vi","text":"The potential difference of the capacitor is twice the potential difference between two conductors of the capacitor."},{"number":"vii","text":"A silver filament is used in an electric light bulb."},{"number":"viii","text":"The lamps are connected in parallel in the lighting circuit."},{"number":"ix","text":"LDR is also called light sensitive variable capacitor."},{"number":"x","text":"Beta rays are less penetrating than alpha rays."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"Angular velocity is the rate of change of angular displacement with respect to ---------."},{"number":"ii","text":"The resistance to fluid motion (or) internal resistance of fluid is called ---------."},{"number":"iii","text":"--------- is extremely hot liquid and semi-liquid rock located under Earth''s surface."},{"number":"iv","text":"The emissivity of an object depends on the --------- of radiation."},{"number":"v","text":"The sonar is a type of technology that works based on ---------."},{"number":"vi","text":"The aperture can be made wide or narrow by adjusting the ---------."},{"number":"vii","text":"Distance between two --------- bright (or dark) fringes is called the fringe width."},{"number":"viii","text":"The capacitors are connected in series each capacitor has the --------- charge."},{"number":"ix","text":"Batteries and generators are called sources of --------- force."},{"number":"x","text":"The unit of electrical power is the ---------."},{"number":"xi","text":"The direct current is a steady --------- current."},{"number":"xii","text":"Lenz''s law is a good example of the principle of conservation of ------."},{"number":"xiii","text":"The --------- of the photocurrent depends on the intensity of incident light."},{"number":"xiv","text":"The AND gate with inverted output is called a --------- gate."},{"number":"xv","text":"Einstein''s general relativity theory is most useful in the field of --------."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"Centrifugal pump, converts mechanical energy into -------- energy. (A. chemical, B. hydraulic, C. thermal)"},{"number":"ii","text":"Cohesion refers to forces between molecules of -------- substances. (A. same, B. different, C. normal)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Solar energy is the radiant light and heat from the --------. (A. moon, B. sun, C. battery)"},{"number":"iv","text":"An isobaric process occurs at constant --------. (A. volume, B. temperature, C. pressure)"},{"number":"v","text":"The Doppler effect is used to measure the -------- of detected objects. (A. velocity, B. length, C. distance)"},{"number":"vi","text":"The film consists of a thin layer of chemical compounds of --------. (A. copper, B. silver, C. gold)"},{"number":"vii","text":"Monochromatic light means that it has a -------- wavelength. (A. single, B. double, C. multiple)"},{"number":"viii","text":"A -------- capacitor is a non-polarized capacitor. (A. ceramic, B. variable, C. electrolytic)"},{"number":"ix","text":"Mica is a good electrical -------- and can withstand very high temperature. (A. conductor, B. semiconductor, C. insulator)"},{"number":"x","text":"An electric stove has an electrical power ranging from 600 W to ------. (A. 1200 W, B. 2000 W, C. 2400 W)"},{"number":"xi","text":"The -------- energy is transformed into electrical energy by a battery. (A. mechanical, B. heat, C. chemical)"},{"number":"xii","text":"Most of the transformers have full load efficiency from 95% to --------. (A. 100%, B. 98%, C. 98.5%)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"The fire alarm system consists of two logic gates, OR gate and -------- gate. (A. NOR, B. NAND, C. AND)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"-------- rays cannot be deflected by electric and magnetic fields. (A. Alpha, B. Beta, C. Gamma)"},{"number":"xv","text":"-------- has no charge and negligibly small rest mass. (A. Positron, B. Neutron, C. Neutrino)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"Describe the relation between the linear and rotational quantities for displacement, tangential velocity and tangential acceleration. A boy steps on a merry-go-round which has a radius of 5 m and is at rest. It starts accelerating at a constant rate up to an angular velocity of 6 rad s⁻¹ in 30 s. What is the distance traversed by the boy?"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the ray diagram of an astronomical telescope. A telescope consists of two converging lenses. When in normal adjustment, so that the image of a distant object is formed at infinity, the lenses are 500 mm apart, and the magnifying power is 9. What are the focal lengths of the two lenses?"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"One end of a poker is placed in fire. After some time, the other end becomes hot. Explain how heat is transferred along the poker. Name the method of heat transfer in this case. A diffraction grating has 4000 lines per centimetre. At what angle will the second-order maximum be for 625 nm wavelength green light?"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"What is a photodiode? Where are they used? Explain the function of a photodiode. Why does a photodiode be used as a photodetector? Draw the circuit symbols of light dependent resistor (LDR) and thermistor."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"What is electrical energy? How many joules are there in 1 kWh? Which quantity determines the rate at which electrical energy is delivered by a current? Why is electrical energy transformed into heat energy when a current flows through a resistor? An electric lamp of 60 Ω connected to a 240 V mains line is used for 45 min. (i) Find the amount of electrical energy dissipated in the lamp. (ii) Find the cost of using it if electricity costs 50 kyats per unit."}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the variation of induced emf as a function of ωt. The primary coil of a step-up transformer having 440 turns is connected to a 220 V alternating voltage source. The secondary delivers a voltage of 2400 V and a current of 4 mA. (i) How many turns are there in the secondary? (ii) What is the current in the primary? (iii) What is the power output?"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"What device is a nuclear reactor? Give a brief description of the essential component of a nuclear reactor. A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (mₚ = 1840 mₑ ) p e"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a diagram to show the horizontal component of normal force provides centripetal force when a car drives on a banked road. What frequency is received by a person watching an oncoming ambulance moving at 110 km h⁻¹ and emitting a steady 800 Hz sound from its siren? The speed of sound on this day is 345 m s⁻¹."}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"What are dynamic viscosity and kinematic viscosity? Express the SI unit of viscosity. On which factors does the viscosity of a liquid depend? Draw the symbols of polarized capacitor, fixed capacitor and variable capacitor."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What is biomass? Give the types of biomass energy sources. An amber-coloured LED with a forward voltage drop of 4 V is to be connected to a 9 V stabilized DC power supply. Calculate the value of the series resistor required to limit the forward current to less than 10 mA. Also calculate the current flowing through the diode if a 100 Ω of current limiting resistor is used."}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"When the distance between two parallel plates having the charges of equal magnitude and opposite signs is reduced, what will happen to the capacitance and potential difference of the plates? When an insulating material is inserted between the conductors of a capacitor in a vacuum, does its capacitance increase or decrease? Explain. Draw the circuit diagram of street lighting system."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"What is carbon dating? How does the proportion of the carbon-14 in the remains of dead plants and animals gives clues about their age? Can the age of living plants and animals be determined by carbon dating method? If two capacitors having the capacitances of 5 µF and 20 µF are connected in series, find the equivalent capacitance of the combination of the two capacitors. If the potential difference of the combination is 200 V, find the potential difference of 20 µF capacitor. - 164 -"}]}}}'::jsonb,12,true),
(12,'old_questions','2025 Set 2 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2025 · 2','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2025 Set 2</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2025-set2","year":2025,"set":2,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"Centripetal acceleration is present only in uniform circular motion."},{"number":"ii","text":"In the present of centripetal force, the object would move along a circle."},{"number":"iii","text":"Nuclear energy is a renewable energy source."},{"number":"iv","text":"The upper limit of audibility is about 200, 000 Hz."},{"number":"v","text":"The position of fringes depends on the wavelength of the light source."},{"number":"vi","text":"The dielectric strength of insulating materials is smaller than that of air."},{"number":"vii","text":"Electromotive force is not actually a force."},{"number":"viii","text":"The frequency of AC current is 50 Hz in US and 60 Hz in Europe."},{"number":"ix","text":"LEDs do not directly produce white light."},{"number":"x","text":"Gamma rays have no charge."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"The motion of a fan''s blades is ---------- motion."},{"number":"ii","text":"Capillarity does not occur for ---------- liquids."},{"number":"iii","text":"Achieving the perfect ---------- sun rays is the optimal orientation so that solar panels receive direct light throughout the day."},{"number":"iv","text":"Silver coated object whose emissivity is much ---------- than 1."},{"number":"v","text":"The greater the frequency, the ---------- is the pitch."},{"number":"vi","text":"One of the unique properties of a laser beam is ----------."},{"number":"vii","text":"The SI unit for illuminance is lux(lx). 1 lx is equal to ---------- lm m²."},{"number":"viii","text":"The capacitor was originally known as a ----------."},{"number":"ix","text":"The two batteries have equal emfs and equal internal resistances, the current flowing through each battery is ---------."},{"number":"x","text":"For appliances above 700 W, a ---------- fuse should be fitted."},{"number":"xi","text":"When increased the voltage 10 kV to 20 kV at the power station, the power loss will be reduced to ---------- times."},{"number":"xii","text":"For one turn of a wire loop, the magnitude of induced emf is ----------."},{"number":"xiii","text":"In transducer, the sensing element is called the ----------."},{"number":"xiv","text":"---------- is a form of point-to-point communication."},{"number":"xv","text":"Neutrons released from a fission reaction are ---------- neutrons."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"Which force is essential on a banked road? (A. centrifugal force, B. centripetal force, C. frictional force)"},{"number":"ii","text":"Which law expresses the drag force resisting the fall of small spherical objects through a fluid medium under the influence of gravity? (A. Boyle''s law, B. Charles'' law, C. Stokes'' law)"},{"number":"iii","text":"What is the main constituent of fossil fuels? (A. coal, B. crude oil, C. carbon)"},{"number":"iv","text":"For a gas system, how much work is done in an isometric process? (A. smaller than zero, B. greater than zero, C. equal to zero)"},{"number":"v","text":"Which of these effects describes the change in pitch we hear when a fast-moving motorbike goes past? (A. refraction, B. reflection, C. Doppler)"},{"number":"vi","text":"Which of the following does not make use of total internal reflection? (A. endoscope, B. oscilloscope, C. optical fibres)"},{"number":"vii","text":"Which colour of light will have the smallest diffraction angle in a grating? (A. red, B. orange, C. violet)"},{"number":"viii","text":"Which of the following capacitors are polarized capacitors? (A. electrolytic capacitors, B. ceramic capacitors, C. film capacitors)"},{"number":"ix","text":"What is the time constant τ of a capacitor charging or discharging process? (A. the product of the resistance and the capacitance, B. the sum of the resistance and the capacitance, C. the ratio of the resistance to the capacitance)"},{"number":"x","text":"Which of the following equations is the total work done in moving a unit positive charge round the complete circuit? (A. I R, B. I R − I r, C. I R + I r)"},{"number":"xi","text":"Which of the following is reduced by using laminated iron core in a transformer? (A. copper loss, B. mechanical loss, C. eddy current loss)"},{"number":"xii","text":"Which of the following is not used to protect us from the possibility of receiving an electric shock? (A. live wire, B. earth wire, C. circuit breaker)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"What are the fundamental building blocks of digital ICs? (A. logic gates, B. resistors, C. transistors)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"Which gate produces a high output when one, and only one, of its inputs is high? (A. XOR, B. XNOR, C. NOR)"},{"number":"xv","text":"Which of the following is not an inertial frame of reference? (A. rotation of earth about its own axis, B. a bus moving at a constant speed in a straight road, C. a person standing on a stationary train)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"When does the rotating object have an angular acceleration? Under what condition is the angular acceleration of a rotating object constant? A centrifuge rotor is accelerated from rest to 20 000 rpm in 30 s. (i) What is its average angular acceleration? (ii) Through how many revolutions has the centrifuge rotor turned during its acceleration period, assuming constant angular acceleration?"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the illustration of four quantities of photometry. (i) What frequency is received by a person watching an oncoming ambulance moving at 110 km h⁻¹ and emitting a steady 800 Hz sound from its siren? The speed of sound on this day is 345 m s⁻¹. (ii) What frequency does she receive after the ambulance has passed?"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"Why is solar energy renewable? Give any two examples of the use of nuclear energy. The hydroturbine receives water from a reservoir at an elevation of 100 m above it. What is the minimum water flow in kg s⁻¹ to produce a steady turbine output of 50 MW if the turbine generator efficiency is 75%?"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"What are liquid crystals? Why do LCDs consume less power than LEDs and gas-plasma displays? Where can LCDs be commonly found? Draw the simple circuit diagram of a photodiode."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"Why are ordinary circuit breakers and fuses not effective in preventing shocks? What are the magnetic parameters that you have known? A 2 kW transformer is used to step down an AC supply of 240 V to 60 V. (i) What will the output current be if there is a 10% power loss in the transformer? (ii) How large is the output current if there is no power loss (i.e. 100% efficiency)?"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a diagram for an electric light bulb that is made of a glass bulb consisting a tungsten filament which has high melting point. An electric stove of 1200 W is connected to a 220 V mains line. (i) Find its resistance. (ii) Find the amount of calories produced in one second by it. (iii) Find the electrical power produced by it when the voltage of the mains line drops to 180 V."}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"What does the statement \"radium has a half-life of 1620 years\" mean? Compare the penetrating power of alpha, beta, and gamma rays. A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (mₚ = 1840 mₑ ) p e"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a diagram to show the centripetal force on the ball and its reaction force on the hand when a person whirls a ball on the end of a string in a horizontal circle around his head. In a room, the temperature of water in a kettle is 80 °C. The room temperature is 30 °C and the surface area of the kettle is 0.02 m². If the emissivity is 0.9, find the rate of heat loss due to radiation. (σ = 5.685 × 10⁻⁸ W m⁻² K⁻⁴ )"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"As water in a level pipe pass from narrower cross-sectional area of pipe to a wider cross-sectional area, does the pressure change? Explain. Draw the symbols of (i) a polarized capacitor, (ii) a fixed capacitor, and (iii) a variable capacitor."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What is the difference between diffraction grating and prism? What is an example of diffraction grating in everyday life? How are diffraction gratings used in spectrometers? Co-60 (half-life = 5.25 years) is often used as a radiation source in medicine. How long after a new sample is delivered, will the activity have decreased to ! of its original value? \""}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"What must be done to increase the capacitance of a capacitor? What are the differences between capacitors in series and those connected in parallel? Draw the block diagram of a simple radio receiver."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"What is meant by \"AM and FM\"? Give one advantage of FM over AM. A circular coil of radius 8 cm and 20 turns is rotated about its vertical diameter with an angular speed of 150 rad s⁻¹ in a uniform horizontal magnetic field of 3 × 10-2 T. Obtain the maximum emf induced in the coil. If the coil forms a closed loop of resistance 10 Ω, calculate the maximum value of current in the coil."}]}}}'::jsonb,2,true);
INSERT INTO educational_content (grade,category,title,chapter,content,sort_order,active) VALUES
(12,'old_questions','2025 Set 3 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2025 · 3','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2025 Set 3</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2025-set3","year":2025,"set":3,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"A rigid body is a body that does not deform or change shape."},{"number":"ii","text":"Cohesion refers to forces between molecules of different substances."},{"number":"iii","text":"Heat radiation is a transfer of heat that require a material medium."},{"number":"iv","text":"The pupil controls the amount of light energy entering the eye."},{"number":"v","text":"The width of the central maximum depends on width of the slit."},{"number":"vi","text":"A supercapacitor (SC) is also called an ultracapacitor."},{"number":"vii","text":"The practical unit of electrical energy is joule (J)."},{"number":"viii","text":"Transformers work on AC, but not on DC."},{"number":"ix","text":"LEDs do not directly produce white light."},{"number":"x","text":"Positron is also called the antiparticle of proton."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"The direction of tangential acceleration is always ------- to the circular path."},{"number":"ii","text":"The SI unit of surface tension is -------."},{"number":"iii","text":"------- is being used to power submarines and ship."},{"number":"iv","text":"The SI unit of heat flux density is -------."},{"number":"v","text":"Bats and whales use ultrasound in -------."},{"number":"vi","text":"The film consists of a thin layer of chemical compounds of -------."},{"number":"vii","text":"Bright and dark fringes are formed -------."},{"number":"viii","text":"The equivalent unit of farad is -------."},{"number":"ix","text":"The dielectric constant of vacuum or air is taken as -------."},{"number":"x","text":"The electrical energy is related to the amount of heat as -------."},{"number":"xi","text":"In an electric generator, ------- energy is converted into electrical energy."},{"number":"xii","text":"Magnetic flux density is a ------- quantity."},{"number":"xiii","text":"------- work in reverse biased mode."},{"number":"xiv","text":"------- are massless and move at the speed of light in vacuum."},{"number":"xv","text":"Activity of a radioactive sample ------- with time."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"Analogue of mass in rotational motion is -------. (A. moment of inertia, B. angular momentum, C. angular velocity)"},{"number":"ii","text":"The electric force acting on an electron orbiting the nucleus is ------- force. (A. linear, B. centripetal, C. tangential)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Which of the following is a non-renewable source of energy? (A. Sun, B. Fossil fuels, C. Wind)"},{"number":"iv","text":"The total emissive power of objects other than a black body is -------. (Α. ε = e ε , Β. ε = 2 ε , C. ε = 3 ε ) ο ο ο"},{"number":"v","text":"The ------- the amplitude, the louder the note. (A. same, B. lower, C. greater)"},{"number":"vi","text":"What is the SI unit of illuminance? (A. candela per square metre (cd m²), B. lux (lx), C. candela (cd))"},{"number":"vii","text":"Constructive interference has ------- intensity. (A. minimum, B. maximum, C. normal)"},{"number":"viii","text":"Film capacitors and ceramic capacitors are ------- capacitors. (A. simplest, B. polarized, C. non-polarized)"},{"number":"ix","text":"Variable capacitors mostly use ------- as the dielectric medium. (A. air, B. oxide layer, C. ceramic)"},{"number":"x","text":"Which of the following metals cannot be used as fuse wire? (A. silver, B. iron, C. tin-lead alloy)"},{"number":"xi","text":"On which of the following effects of electric current a fuse operates? (A. Heating effect, B. Electrostatic effect, C. Magnetic effect)"},{"number":"xii","text":"The magnetic flux is ------- when the magnetic field is parallel to the surface area. (A. minimum, B. maximum, C. zero)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"As light level increases, the LDR resistance -------. (A. is empty, B. increases, C. decreases)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"A ------- is a semiconductor light source that emits light when current flows through it. (A. LED, B. photodiode, C. zener diode)"},{"number":"xv","text":"Gamma rays are the ------- of the three rays. (A. most penetrating, B. most ionizing, C. least ionizing)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"Derive kinematic viscosity ν of the liquid using Stokes'' law. A horizontal circular loop of wire has a diameter of 5 cm and is lowered in a sample of crude oil. The additional force required to pull the loop out of the oil is 0.04 N; calculate the surface tension of the crude oil."}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a p-V diagram for the four reversible processes of Carnot cycle. What frequency is received by a person watching an oncoming ambulance moving at 110 km h⁻¹ and emitting a steady 800 Hz sound from its siren? The speed of sound on this day is 345 m s⁻¹. What frequency does she receive after the ambulance has passed?"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What is irradiance? Write down its SI unit. What is the power conversion efficiency of the solar panel? The wind is blowing at 10 m s⁻¹, how much total power produce by the wind turbine if the blades are 45 m long? Density of air is 1.3 kg m⁻³."}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"Give the formula for expressing De Morgan''s second theorem for two variables and construct its truth table. Describe the logic symbol, Boolean equation and truth table of XNOR gate. Draw the diagram of a simple LED indicator circuit."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"What must be done to increase the capacitance of a capacitor? The equivalent capacitance is 10 µF when n identical capacitors are connected in parallel and 0.4 µF when they are connected in series. Determine n and the capacitance of each capacitor."}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a simple circuit diagram of two batteries in series aiding connected with an external resistor. An electric stove of 1200 W is connected to a 220 V mains line. (i) Find its resistance. (ii) Find the current flowing through it. (iii) Find the amount of heat produced in calories in one second. (iv) Find the electrical power produced by it when the voltage of the mains line drops to 180 V. (1 cal = 4.2 J)"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"Explain Bohr''s second postulate of hydrogen atom using de Broglie hypothesis. Suppose that initially there was 100 mg of iodine-131 and its half-life is 8 days. How much would it be left after 24 days?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a diagram showing circular motion of a particle of the object. The luminous intensity of a source is 200 cd. The mounting height of the lamp is 6 m from the ground. Find the illuminance on the ground Ev: (i) just below the lamp, (ii) 3 m horizontally away from the lamp on the ground."}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Derive the equation tan θ = v²/(rg), relating the banking angle θ to the speed v at which the cyclist is travelling and the radius of curvature r. Draw a diagram showing the induced current produced by a moving coil carrying current."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What are the conditions for constructive interference and destructive interference? What is the difference between Fresnel diffraction and Fraunhofer diffraction? Co-60 (half-life = 5.25 years) is often used as a radiation source in medicine. How long after a new sample is delivered, will the activity have decreased to ! of its original value? \""}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"A parallel-plate capacitor of capacitance C is given the charge Q and then disconnected from the circuit. How much work is required to pull apart the plates of this capacitor to twice their original separation? Draw a graph to illustrate the half-life of radon. Radon has a half-life of 3.8 days."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"Give the main uses for (i) the Zener diode and (ii) LED. What is the main difference between a normal diode and a zener diode? The primary coil of a step-up transformer having 220 turns is connected to a 110 V alternating voltage source. The secondary delivers a voltage of 12 000 V and a current of 40 mA. (i) How many turns are there in the secondary? (ii) What is the current in the primary?"}]}}}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'old_questions','2025 Set 4 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2025 · 4','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2025 Set 4</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2025-set4","year":2025,"set":4,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"When a skater forms a circle, she has to lean outwards."},{"number":"ii","text":"When the angular velocity is increasing, the angular acceleration vector points in the same direction as the angular velocity."},{"number":"iii","text":"Solar cell generates electricity using a chemical reaction."},{"number":"iv","text":"Heat conduction occurs only in a liquid or a gas, never in a solid."},{"number":"v","text":"The speed of sound is the same for different media."},{"number":"vi","text":"The capacitance of a capacitor depends on the nature of the insulator between the two conductors of that capacitor."},{"number":"vii","text":"Electromotive force is measured in unit of volt (V)."},{"number":"viii","text":"The current from the outlet of telephone charger is DC (direct current)."},{"number":"ix","text":"The resistance of the PTC (Positive Temperature Coefficient) thermistor decreases as temperature increases."},{"number":"x","text":"An inertial frame is a frame of reference that has no acceleration."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"The average angular acceleration of a rotor which is accelerated from rest to 900 rpm in 10 s is -------- rad s⁻²."},{"number":"ii","text":"The viscosity of gases -------- with an increase in temperature."},{"number":"iii","text":"The -------- energy is produced by the difference in sea levels."},{"number":"iv","text":"-------- of an object depends to a large extent on how shiny it is."},{"number":"v","text":"The loudness of the note depends upon the -------- of the wave that produces it."},{"number":"vi","text":"The -------- in the eye is similar to the aperture in the camera."},{"number":"vii","text":"-------- light means that it has a single wavelength."},{"number":"viii","text":"-------- capacitors are used in radio tuning applications."},{"number":"ix","text":"The electric light bulb converts most of the electrical energy into ------ and light energy."},{"number":"x","text":"The practical unit of electrical energy is --------."},{"number":"xi","text":"A transformer is used to change the -------- of an alternating current."},{"number":"xii","text":"In the lighting circuit, the light bulbs are arranged in -------- across the mains line."},{"number":"xiii","text":"A -------- is a device for converting a non-electrical input into an electrical signal."},{"number":"xiv","text":"An alpha particle consists of two protons and -------- neutrons."},{"number":"xv","text":"A particle of mass m, moving with velocity v has the wavelength λ = --------, where h is Planck''s constant."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"When a car in motion takes a sudden turn in a curved path, passengers in the car experience ---------. A. an outward push, B. an inward pull, C. a downward force"},{"number":"ii","text":"The speed of water spraying from a hose -------- by making the hose area smaller. A. does not change, B. decreases, C. increases"},{"number":"iii","text":"Which of the following energy sources is classified as renewable? A. solar energy, B. natural gas, C. nuclear energy"},{"number":"iv","text":"What is the SI unit of thermal conductivity? (A. W m⁻¹ K⁻¹, B. W m⁻², C. W m K)"},{"number":"v","text":"How does the intensity of a wave I vary with its amplitude A? 1 A. I ∝ A³, Β. 1 ∝ A², C. 1 ∝ + A"},{"number":"vi","text":"Which color of light is more sensitive to the human eye? A. red, B. blue, C. green"},{"number":"vii","text":"If the violet light in Young''s double slit experiment is replaced by red light, the fringe width will --------. A. decrease, B. increase, C. not change"},{"number":"viii","text":"The dielectric constant εᵣ of insulating materials is --------. A. greater than 1, B. less than 1, C. equal to 0"},{"number":"ix","text":"How does the capacitance of a capacitor vary when the charge on the capacitor is increased? A. increases, B. remains constant, C. decreases"},{"number":"x","text":"-------- is a scalar quantity. A. Magnetic flux, B. Magnetic flux density, C. Magnetic field strength"},{"number":"xi","text":"If an electric stove of 1200 W is connected to a 220 V mains line, the current flowing through it is --------. A. 0.183A, B. 5.45 A, C. 264 000 A"},{"number":"xii","text":"Which of the following metals cannot be used as fuse wire? A. iron, B. silver, C. tin-lead alloy"},{"number":"xiii","text":"In -------- modulation, the amplitude of carrier wave remains constant with modulation. A. phase, B. amplitude, C. frequency"},{"number":"xiv","text":"-------- gate produces a ''1'' when both inputs match. A. NOR, B. XOR, C. XNOR"},{"number":"xv","text":"What is the rate of decay of a radioactive sample called? A. activity, B. half-life, C. ionization"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"What is centripetal force? Does it result from the effect of inertia? When a bob is swinging in the vertical circle, at which point on the circular path is the tension in the rope the greatest? A 60 cm rope is tied to the handle of a bucket which is then whirled in a vertical circle. The mass of the bucket is 2 kg. If the tension of the rope at the lowest point in its path is 50 N, find the speed of the bucket at that point. (g = 9.8 m s⁻²²)"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Plot the pressure versus volume for isobaric and isochoric processes. Light of wavelength 580 nm is incident on a slit of width 0.3 mm. The observing screen is placed 2 m from the slit. Find the positions of the first dark fringes and the width of the central bright fringes."}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What are the three main elements of solar water heating systems installed in homes? How does it work? A home requires 62 kWh of heat on a winter day to maintain a constant indoor temperature of 25 °C. Assume that the temperature of hot water outlet is 60 °C. How large does the storage tank of the solar heating system have to be to provide the required energy? (Specific heat capacity of water c = 4184 J kg⁻¹ K⁻¹ and 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J)"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"What is photodiode? Give the function and two applications of photodiode. Plot a simple circuit diagram of a photodiode."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"How many types of transformers are there? Which type of transformer is used in a welding machine? Explain. An electric welding machine uses a current of 400 A. The machine has a transformer whose primary coil has 400 turns and draws 4 A from a 220 V power line. (i) How many turns does the secondary coil have? (ii) What is the voltage across the secondary coil?"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw voltage characteristics of charging and discharging a capacitor. The plates of a parallel-plate capacitor are 50 cm² in area and 1 mm apart. (i) What is its capacitance? (ii) When the capacitor is connected to a 24 V battery, what is the charge on each plate? (iii) What is the energy of the capacitor? (ε₀ = 8.85 × 10⁻¹² F m⁻¹)"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"List the key differences between Einstein''s theories of special relativity and general relativity. One stary night, an earth-bound observer looking up the stars sees an extra-terrestrial spaceship flash across the sky. The ship is 50 m long and is traveling at 90 percent of the speed of light. What would the ship''s length be when measured from earth-bound frame of reference?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the acceleration vectors of an object moving in (i) uniform and (ii) nonuniform circular motions. How many photons are emitted per second by a 7.5 mW of CO₂ laser with the wavelength of 10.6 µm? (h = 6.62 × 10-34 J s)"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"What are the differences between laminar flow and turbulent flow? Draw a simple diagram of how induced current is produced in a loop of wire by a moving magnet."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What is an echo of a sound wave? Give its two applications. What will you do if your classroom has echoes? Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of (i) a 0.65 kg basketball thrown at a speed of 10 m s⁻¹ and (ii) an electron moving with a speed of 0.59 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹. Evaluate your answer. (h = 6.62 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, mₑ = 9.1 × 10⁻³¹ kg)"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"What is meant by terminal voltage (available voltage) of a battery and how is it related to emf of the battery? The half-life of radon is 3.8 days. Provide the graphical illustration of half-life of radioactive decay of 2 g of radon."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"Describe two advantages and two disadvantages of LED. When two 6 V batteries, having the same internal resistance and connected in series, are connected to a 5 resistor, the current in the circuit is 2 A. When these batteries are in parallel, a current of 1.5 A flows through when connected to another resistor. Find the resistance of the resistor."}]}}}'::jsonb,4,true),
(12,'old_questions','2025 Set 5 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2025 · 5','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2025 Set 5</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2025-set5","year":2025,"set":5,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"In uniform circular motion, the angular speed of the object is constant."},{"number":"ii","text":"A ball attached to a string and whirled around a vertical circle experiences a net downward force at the bottom of the arc."},{"number":"iii","text":"The tidal energy is produced by the difference in sea levels."},{"number":"iv","text":"The first law of thermodynamics is an application of the conservation of energy for heat and thermodynamic processes."},{"number":"v","text":"If the amplitude of the sound wave is doubled, the intensity becomes eight times greater."},{"number":"vi","text":"A capacitor stores electrical energy in the form of magnetic field."},{"number":"vii","text":"Electromotive force is measured in unit of joule (J)."},{"number":"viii","text":"A transformer is used to change the voltage of an alternating current."},{"number":"ix","text":"XNOR gate produces a ''0'' when both inputs are different."},{"number":"x","text":"Relativistic effect usually becomes negligible when speed of the system becomes comparable to the speed of light."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"The direction of the angular velocity vector is ---------- to the plane of rotation, and along the axis of rotation."},{"number":"ii","text":"The volume of a liquid does not depend on pressure if the ---------- is constant."},{"number":"iii","text":"Nuclear energy is non-renewable as the uranium fuels used are consumed in the nuclear ---------- reaction."},{"number":"iv","text":"The object which can absorb all the electromagnetic radiations falling upon it is called a ----------."},{"number":"v","text":"An ---------- is repetition of sound due to the reflection of sound."},{"number":"vi","text":"In the terrestrial telescope a ---------- lens is used as an eyepiece to produce an erect final image."},{"number":"vii","text":"There are two types of wavefront; plane wavefront and ----------."},{"number":"viii","text":"If the potential difference of the capacitor is 1 V when it is given a charge 1 C, its capacitance is ----------."},{"number":"ix","text":"Electrical power is the rate of transfer of ----------."},{"number":"x","text":"James Prescott Joule in 1841 experimentally studied the ---------- effect of electric current."},{"number":"xi","text":"The magnitude of induced emf in a wire loop is directly proportional to the rate of change of ---------- through that loop."},{"number":"xii","text":"Lenz''s law is a good example of the principle of conservation of ------."},{"number":"xiii","text":"A ---------- is a temperature sensor that exhibits a large change in resistance proportional to a change in temperature."},{"number":"xiv","text":"---------- rays cannot be deflected by electric and magnetic fields."},{"number":"xv","text":"SI unit of activity of a radioactive sample is ----------."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"What is the magnitude of the centripetal force of an object of mass m moving along a circle of radius r with angular speed ω? A. m r ω², B. m r ω, C. m r² ω"},{"number":"ii","text":"Motor car brake oil is ---------- A. compressible, B. non-compressible, C. volatile"},{"number":"iii","text":"A large amount of ---------- energy is stored in the fossil fuels. A. nuclear, B. electrical, C. chemical"},{"number":"iv","text":"The internal energy of an ideal gas is ---------- to the absolute temperature. A. directly proportional, B. inversely proportional, C. equal"},{"number":"v","text":"If a star is approaching the earth the spectral lines would shift towards ---------- end. A. blue, B. red, C. green"},{"number":"vi","text":"The core of a fibre-optic cable is made of ----------. A. copper wire, B. thin strand of glass, C. lead wire"},{"number":"vii","text":"The angular position of a point of a periodic wave is called the --------. A. phase angle, B. wavelength, C. amplitude"},{"number":"viii","text":"When the distance between the two parallel plates of a capacitor is doubled, by what percent does its capacitance change? A. decreases by 50%, B. increases by 50%, C. decreases by 25%"},{"number":"ix","text":"The dielectric constant εᵣ of insulating materials is ----------. A. greater than 1, B. less than 1, C. equal to 0"},{"number":"x","text":"What component of an electric iron is responsible for maintaining the selected temperature by switching the current on and off? A. resistor, B. thermostat, C. circuit breaker"},{"number":"xi","text":"A device consuming 2 kW of power for 3 hours would use electrical energy of ------- A. 6 kWh, B. 1.5 kWh, C. 0.666 kWh"},{"number":"xii","text":"---------- is kept at zero voltage by the electricity supply company. A. Live wire, B. Earth wire, C. Neutral wire"},{"number":"xiii","text":"The OR gate with inverted output is called a ---------- gate. A. XOR, B. XNOR, C. NOR"},{"number":"xiv","text":"A photodiode converts ---------- into electrical current. A. light, B. sound, C. heat"},{"number":"xv","text":"What nature of electrons is used in electron microscope? A. wave nature, B. particle nature, C. dual nature"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"What is capillary action, and which forces are responsible for it? Calculate the height to which water will rise in a capillary tube of diameter 1 mm. The surface tension of water is 0.072 N m⁻¹. Assume the angle of contact is 0°. (ρ_water = 1000 kg m⁻³, g = 9.8 m s⁻²)"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the diagrams of human eye showing how the eyelens changes its shape to obtain a sharp image on the retina when viewing (i) near objects and (ii) distant objects. If the rate of energy radiation from a blackbody of area 100 cm² is 42W, find the temperature of that blackbody. (σ = 5.685 × 10⁻⁸ W m⁻² K⁻⁴ )"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What are the major components of hydropower plants? State the changes in the form of energy while producing hydroelectricity. A dam with a maximum head of 200 m produces 2000 MW electrical power. What is the rate of falling water on the turbines if the turbine-generator efficiency is 50%? (ρ_water = 1000 kg m⁻³, g = 9.8 m s⁻²)"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"Describe two advantages and two disadvantages of LED. List two applications of LED. Draw circuit symbol for LED."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"How many types of transformer are there? Which type of transformer is used in a welding machine? Explain. A transformer has 2000 turns in primary, 100 turns in secondary and its efficiency 100%. It is used for 10 V, 40 W bulb. Calculate (i) the supply voltage and (ii) the current through the input coil."}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw circuit diagrams of two batteries in (i) series aiding and (ii) series opposing arrangements connected with an external resistor R. Two batteries each having an emf of 6 V and an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω are connected (i) in series and (ii) in parallel. Find the current in each case when the batteries are connected to a 2 Ω resistor."}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"Explain the terms activity and half-life of a radioactive substance. Suppose that initially there was 100 mg of iodine-131 and its half-life is 8 days. How much would it be left after 24 days?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"A car of mass m is moving at constant speed v on a frictionless road of banking angle θ. Draw a force diagram showing all forces acting on the car. Indicate the component of normal force which provides the centripetal force. If the distance between two slits is 0.05 mm and the distance to a screen is 2.5 m, find the spacing between the first and second-order bright fringes for yellow light of wavelength 580 nm."}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Explain why tangential acceleration exists in addition to centripetal acceleration in nonuniform circular motion. Plot voltage characteristics of charging and discharging a capacitor."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What is Doppler effect? Give three applications of Doppler effect. A proton and an electron are each accelerated through a potential difference of 1 kV from rest. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (q = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C, mₚ = 1840 mₑ , h = 6.62 × 10⁻³⁴ J s) e p e"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"Describe the energy W of a capacitor in terms of (i) Q and V, (ii) Q and C, and (iii) C and V (Q is the charge, C is the capacitance and V is the potential difference). What is the equivalent unit of farad (F)? Draw the logic circuit represented by each expression: (i) A̅ + B̅, (ii) A + BC, (iii) AB + CD."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"What is the main difference between a Zener diode and a normal diode? Describe two types of reverse breakdown regions in a Zener diode. The plates of a parallel-plate capacitor are 50 cm² in area and 1 mm apart. (i) What is its capacitance? (ii) When the capacitor is connected to a 24 V battery, what is the charge on each plate? (ε₀ = 8.85 × 10⁻¹² C² N⁻¹ m⁻²)"}]}}}'::jsonb,5,true),
(12,'old_questions','2025 Set 6 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2025 · 6','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2025 Set 6</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2025-set6","year":2025,"set":6,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"If an object rotates with constant angular velocity, its acceleration is zero."},{"number":"ii","text":"Banking of roads involves lowering the outer edge of the curved road relative to the inner edge."},{"number":"iii","text":"Renewable energy sources are finite and cannot be replenished once consumed."},{"number":"iv","text":"In a gasoline engine, the combustion occurs explosively by an electric spark during the explosion process, while the piston does not move."},{"number":"v","text":"Echoes can be heard separately from the original sound when the source of the sound is much closer to the observer than to the reflecting surface."},{"number":"vi","text":"The total capacitance of capacitors in parallel is equal to the sum of their individual capacitances."},{"number":"vii","text":"The voltage of a battery remains constant regardless of the current drawn from it."},{"number":"viii","text":"In an AC (alternating current) circuit, the current changes direction periodically."},{"number":"ix","text":"In a digital system, information is represented using binary numbers, 0 and 1."},{"number":"x","text":"Alpha particles consist of two protons and two neutrons, making them identical to a helium nucleus."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"When a car in motion takes a sudden turn in a curved path, passengers in the car experience an outward push due to the ------- force acting on them."},{"number":"ii","text":"The air flow moving above the top curved surface of the wing has a longer distance to travel and needs to go ------- to have the same transit time as the air traveling along the lower flat surface."},{"number":"iii","text":"Achieving the perfect perpendicular sun rays is the optimal ------- so that solar panels receive direct light throughout the day."},{"number":"iv","text":"The object which can absorb all the electromagnetic radiations falling upon it is called a ---------."},{"number":"v","text":"The range of frequencies a person can hear is known as the -------."},{"number":"vi","text":"The ------- is the coloured portion of the eye and controls the amount of light entering the eye."},{"number":"vii","text":"When light passes through a small opening or around an obstacle, it spreads out, a phenomenon known as -------."},{"number":"viii","text":"The energy stored in a capacitor is directly proportional to the square of the ------- across its plates."},{"number":"ix","text":"The dielectric may be able to withstand a ------- electric field between the plates than air."},{"number":"x","text":"The heating effect of electric current in a resistor is given by the formula -------."},{"number":"xi","text":"The rate at which electrical energy is converted into heat in a resistor is called ------- and is measured in watts."},{"number":"xii","text":"In an AC circuit, the voltage and current vary sinusoidally with time, whereas in a DC circuit, both the voltage and current remain constant over -------."},{"number":"xiii","text":"A photodiode converts ------- energy into electrical energy when exposed to light."},{"number":"xiv","text":"An LDR (Light Dependent Resistor) decreases its ------- as the intensity of light falling on it increases."},{"number":"xv","text":"The half-life of a radioactive substance is the time required for half of the atoms in a sample to -------."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"The direction of the velocity vector of an object in uniform circular motion: (A. Remains constant, B. Changes continuously. C. Changes only at specific points)"},{"number":"ii","text":"What does high viscosity indicate about a fluid? (A. It flows easily, B. It has strong internal friction, C. It is always a gas)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Which statement is true? (A. Wind farms cause high pollution, B. Modern turbines reduce noise and flicker, C. Hydropower has no negative impacts)"},{"number":"iv","text":"Heat transfer processes are primarily studied in which field? (A. Thermodynamics, B. Fluid mechanics, C. Thermal engineering)"},{"number":"v","text":"The speed of sound varies depending on: (A. The type of medium, B. The color of the medium, C. The shape of the sound wave)"},{"number":"vi","text":"Which part of the human eye is responsible for adjusting the focus of light to form a clear image on the retina? (A. Iris, B. Lens, C. Cornea)"},{"number":"vii","text":"What is the phase difference between two waves that are perfectly in phase? (A. 0°, В. 90°, С. 180°)"},{"number":"viii","text":"What happens to the capacitance of a variable capacitor when the distance between the plates is increased? (A. Capacitance increases, B. Capacitance decreases, C. Capacitance remains the same)"},{"number":"ix","text":"The electromotive force (emf) of a source is defined as: (A. The potential difference across the terminals when no current flows. B. The potential difference when the current is flowing, C. The energy dissipated per unit charge)"},{"number":"x","text":"What is the SI unit of electrical power? (A. watt, B. joule, C. volt)"},{"number":"xi","text":"According to Lenz''s Law, the induced current in a closed circuit: (A. Supports the change in magnetic flux, B. Opposes the change in magnetic flux, C. Is independent of the change in magnetic flux)"},{"number":"xii","text":"What is the primary function of a neutral wire in an electrical system? (A. To provide safety by grounding the circuit, B. To carry excess current during overloads, C. To complete the circuit by returning current to the source)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"What is the primary application of a Zener diode? (A. As a voltage regulator, B. As a rectifier, C. As an amplifier)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"What is the penetrating power of alpha particles compared to other radiation types? (A. High, B. Moderate, C. Low)"},{"number":"xv","text":"What is a tracer commonly composed of? (A. A small number of radioactive isotopes, B. A mixture of stable and unstable isotopes, C. A highly reactive chemical compound)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"On which three factors does the viscosity of a liquid depend? At a certain temperature, water has a surface tension of 0.072 N m⁻¹. In a 4 mm diameter vertical tube, if the liquid rises 6 mm above the liquid outside the tube, calculate the contact angle. Assume the density of water ρ = 1000 kg m⁻³ and acceleration due to gravity g = 10 m s⁻²."}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Sketch the Pressure-Volume (p-V) diagram for an isothermal process of an ideal gas and label it appropriately. What value of sound intensity in dB increases by a factor of 10000?"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What are the environmental impacts of using non-renewable energy sources? At a hydroelectric power plant, the water pressure head is at a height of 300 m and the water flow available is 100 m³ s⁻¹. If the turbine-generator efficiency is 70%, estimate the electric power available from the plant. (g = 9.8 m s⁻², ρ_water = 1000 kg m⁻³)"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"What is the disadvantage of Liquid Crystal Display (LCD)? Why does an LCD need a backlight, and what is the role of a polarizer in an LCD? Draw the symbol for an OR gate and label its inputs and output properly."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"When an insulating material is inserted between the conductors of a capacitor in a vacuum, does its capacitance increase or decrease? Explain. What potential difference must be applied across a 10 µF capacitor if it is to have an energy content of 1.5 J?"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a circuit diagram showing batteries connected in parallel along with an external resistor. An electric iron draws a current of 3 A when it is connected to a 220 V mains line. How many kcal of heat is produced per minute? How many joules are in 1 kWh?"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"List the main components of a simple radio receiver. Suppose there was 8 g of radon at t = 0 and its half-life is 3.8 days. How much would be left after 7.6 days?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a labelled diagram to illustrate the resultant acceleration of an object in nonuniform circular motion. Two light sources of 8 cd and 12 cd are placed on the same side of the photometer screen at a distance of 40 cm from it. Where should an 80 cd source be placed to balance the illuminance?"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Does the centripetal force and centrifugal force constitute an action- reaction pair? Do they obey Newton''s third law? Draw and label the symbol of a transformer, showing its primary and secondary windings, core, and any other key components."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"Why do two light waves sometimes combine to make a brighter light and other times cancel each other out? Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of a 0.70 kg basketball thrown at a speed of 10 m s⁻¹. (h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s)"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"Explain (i) A transformer will not work on DC, (ii) The core of a transformer needs to be laminated. Provide a labelled diagram of a NOR gate, an AND gate, and a NOT gate (inverter)."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"Describe one common application of LEDs. Additionally, explain why LEDs are preferred over traditional light sources in that application? A 35 µF capacitor is needed, but only 10 µF capacitors are available. How should a minimum number of 10 µF capacitors be connected so that the combination has a capacitance of 35 µF?"}]}}}'::jsonb,6,true),
(12,'old_questions','2025 Set 7 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2025 · 7','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2025 Set 7</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2025-set7","year":2025,"set":7,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"The centripetal acceleration and linear velocity are perpendicular to each other at every point in the path."},{"number":"ii","text":"When whirling a body attached to a string, the tension force behaves as a centripetal force."},{"number":"iii","text":"At the earth''s surface solar radiation has an intensity of approximately 1350 W m⁻²."},{"number":"iv","text":"The major heat transfer in human beings is due to the flow of warm blood."},{"number":"v","text":"Reflection of sound does not obey the laws of reflection."},{"number":"vi","text":"Film capacitors and ceramic capacitors have positive and negative terminals."},{"number":"vii","text":"Electromotive force is not actually a force."},{"number":"viii","text":"A transformer is used to change the voltage of an alternating current."},{"number":"ix","text":"LEDs do not directly produce white light."},{"number":"x","text":"The wave nature of electrons is used instead of light in electron microscope."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"--------- is used to measure and regulate the speed of a machine."},{"number":"ii","text":"The SI unit of viscosity is sometimes referred to as the ---------."},{"number":"iii","text":"--------- is a common gas found in swamps."},{"number":"iv","text":"The emissivity of an object depends on the --------- of radiation."},{"number":"v","text":"--------- is the special ability of emitting sounds and interpreting the echoes."},{"number":"vi","text":"As the magnifying power increases, the --------- of images is reduced."},{"number":"vii","text":"The distance between two adjacent bright (or dark) fringes is called ---------."},{"number":"viii","text":"In practice, typical devices have capacitances ranging from ---------."},{"number":"ix","text":"The total work done in moving a unit positive charge round the complete circuit is ---------"},{"number":"x","text":"--------- is a good electrical insulator and can withstand very high temperature."},{"number":"xi","text":"Magnetic flux density is related to magnetic field strength by ---------."},{"number":"xii","text":"The currents flow in little circles in the iron core are called ---------."},{"number":"xiii","text":"The resistance of LDR depends on the --------- falling on its surface."},{"number":"xiv","text":"The wired connections between two points are known as ---------."},{"number":"xv","text":"In medicine, --------- are effectively used in diagnostic procedures."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"One revolution per minute is about ---------. (A. 0.105 rad s¹, B. 0.95 rad s¹, C. 1.57 rad s¹)"},{"number":"ii","text":"Adhesion refers to forces between molecules of substance ---------. (A. same, B. different, C. other)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Today''s world consumption of energy is of the order of --------- Btu/year. 27 7 17 (Α. 10 , B. 10 , C. 10 )"},{"number":"iv","text":"All real engines are --------- efficient than Carnot engine. (A. less, B. more, C. higher)"},{"number":"v","text":"For every 10 dB added to the sound level, the loudness of the sound is increased by --------- times. (A. 10, B. 20, C. 30)"},{"number":"vi","text":"When taking a photograph in bright light a --------- f-number must be used. (A. small, B. large, C. zero)"},{"number":"vii","text":"Two positions are in phase if phase difference are ---------. (Α. 0, 2π, 4π, 6π …., Β. π, 3π, 5π …., C. π/2, 3π /2, 5π /2….)"},{"number":"viii","text":"Which type of energy does the capacitor store? (A. kinetic, B. potential, C. both)"},{"number":"ix","text":"What is electrical energy typically measured in? (A. watt (W), B. volts (V), C. joules (J))"},{"number":"x","text":"At a temperature of ----------, the tungsten filament emits white light. (A. 3000 °C, B. 2500 °C, C. 1800 °C)"},{"number":"xi","text":"In US, the electricity standards are ---------. (A. 10 V, 50 Hz, B. 120 V, 60 Hz, C. 230 V, 50 Hz)"},{"number":"xii","text":"Which of the following gives the polarity of the induced emf? (A. Ohm''s law, B. Lenz''s law, C. Faraday''s law)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"What should be the biasing of the LED? (A. forward bias, B. reverse bias, C. no biasing required)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"Uranium is used for the generation of ---------. (A. electricity, B. iron and steel, C. cement)"},{"number":"xv","text":"Which of the following defines the structure of space-time? (A. Special relativity theory, B. Newton laws of motion, C. General relativity theory)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"Show the expression for terminal velocity when a ball of radius r is dropped through a liquid of viscosity η and density ρ. Air streams horizontally past a small airplane’s wings such that the speed is 70 m s⁻¹ over the top surface and 60 m s⁻¹ past the bottom surface. If the plane has a wing area of 16.2 m² on the top and on the bottom, what is the net vertical force that the air exerts on the airplane? The density of the air is 1.2 kg m⁻³."}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Illustrate the position of particular bright and dark fringes on the screen in Young''s double slit experiment. How much heat per second is conducted through a wooden wall of area 25 m² and thickness 0.04 m if the temperature inside is 20 °C and the temperature outside is -10 °C? The thermal conductivity of wood is 8.37 × 10⁻² W m⁻¹ K⁻¹ ."}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"How does wind power generate electricity? The wind is blowing at 10 m s⁻¹ , how much total power produce by the wind turbine if the blades are 45 m long? Density of air is 1.3 kg m ."}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"What is zener diode? What is the main difference between zener diode and normal diode? Where are photodiode used? Does photodiode work in reverse biased mode? Draw a circuit diagram of fire alarm system consists of smoke detector, heat detector and two logic gates."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"Differentiate between the magnetic flux and magnetic flux density. A square loop of wire of side 5.0 cm is in a uniform magnetic field 0.16 T. What is the magnetic flux in the loop (i) when magnetic field is perpendicular to the surface of the loop and (ii) when magnetic field is at an angle of 30° to the surface of the loop?"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a diagram which shows the variation of capacitor voltage (V ) C with time (t) during charging process. A capacitor having a capacitance of 2 µF and a charge of 2000 µC is connected in series with another capacitor having a capacitance of 8 µF and a charge of 1600 µC. (i) Find the potential difference of the individual capacitors prior to the connection. (ii) Find the potential difference of the individual capacitors after the connection."}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"What is radioactivity? Who discovered radioactivity? Name some radioactive elements. Suppose that initially there was 100 mg of iodine-131 and its half-life is 8 days. How much would it be left after 24 days?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a diagram showing how the horizontal component of the normal force provides centripetal force when a body moves in a circular path on a banked road. (i) What frequency is received by a person watching an oncoming ambulance moving at 110 km h⁻¹ and emitting a steady 800 Hz sound from its siren? The speed of sound on this day is 345 m s⁻¹. (ii) What frequency does she receive after the ambulance has passed?"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"When will the object have a tangential acceleration? Express the formula for magnitude of resultant acceleration and explain the symbols in it. Draw the diagrams for electromotive force in an open circuit and terminal voltage of a battery in closed circuit."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What is a useful application of fibre optics? Name the dispersion elements used in the optical spectrometer. State two essential processes to initiate laser action. A proton and an electron are each accelerated from rest through a potential difference of 1 kV. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (mₚ = 1840 mₑ, qₑ = qₚ = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C)"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"On what factors does the internal resistance of a battery depend? Why is inert gas added in light bulb? Draw the block diagram of general electronic communication system."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"Name the components of a simple radio receiver and briefly describe any two of them. An electric welding machine uses a current of 400 A. The machine has a transformer whose primary coil has 400 turns and draws 4 A from a 220 V power line. (i) How many turns does the secondary coil have? (ii) What is the voltage across the secondary coil?"}]}}}'::jsonb,7,true),
(12,'old_questions','2025 Set 8 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2025 · 8','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2025 Set 8</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2025-set8","year":2025,"set":8,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"Angular velocity and angular acceleration are scalar quantities."},{"number":"ii","text":"When a skater forms a circle, he has to lean outwards."},{"number":"iii","text":"If the height of waterfall of hydroelectric power plant, is increased, the available output power will be decreased."},{"number":"iv","text":"The intensity of a wave is inversely proportional to the square of the amplitude of the wave."},{"number":"v","text":"The human eye is very similar to a camera in many aspects."},{"number":"vi","text":"Variable capacitors mostly use air as the dielectric medium."},{"number":"vii","text":"The material used for fuse should have high melting point."},{"number":"viii","text":"A transformer is used to change the voltage of an alternating current."},{"number":"ix","text":"The current flows through zener diode only in forward-bias mode."},{"number":"x","text":"In β⁻ decay, the atomic number of the daughter nucleus increases by one."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"--------- acceleration is present in both uniform and non-uniform circular motion."},{"number":"ii","text":"--------- and adhesion are two types of intermolecular forces."},{"number":"iii","text":"Heat, --------- and electricity are the most common forms of energy."},{"number":"iv","text":"The total emissive power of a blackbody is directly proportional to the --------- power of absolute temperature."},{"number":"v","text":"The speed of sound is --------- in solids than liquids and gases."},{"number":"vi","text":"A camera is an --------- instrument that records an image of an object."},{"number":"vii","text":"There are two types of wavefront: plane wavefront and --------- wavefront."},{"number":"viii","text":"The capacitor is similar to a --------- battery."},{"number":"ix","text":"The energy stored by the capacitor is W = ---------."},{"number":"x","text":"Batteries and --------- are called sources of electromotive force."},{"number":"xi","text":"Bulbs in electrical wiring of houses are connected in --------- across the mains line."},{"number":"xii","text":"Faraday''s law gives the --------- of the induced emf."},{"number":"xiii","text":"The basic operations in Boolean algebra are, --------- OR, and NOT."},{"number":"xiv","text":"The process of changing some characteristics of a carrier wave in accordance with the intensity of the signal is known as ---------."},{"number":"xv","text":"--------- is a material to slow down fast neutrons released from a fission process in a nuclear reactor."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"Centrifugal pump is a hydraulic machine which works by the use of --------- force acting on the fluid. (A. centripetal, B. centrifugal, C. tangential)"},{"number":"ii","text":"Which of the following is the SI unit of surface tension? (A. newton(N), B. joule(J), C. newton per metre(N m⁻¹))"},{"number":"iii","text":"What type of energy is stored in the fossil fuels? (A. heat energy, B. chemical energy, C. potential energy)"},{"number":"iv","text":"Heat convection process takes place in a ---------. (A. solid, B. gas, C. fluid)"},{"number":"v","text":"What quantity that determines the loudness of sound? (A. frequency, B. amplitude, C. wavelength)"},{"number":"vi","text":"A microscope uses lenses to make --------- images of objects. (A. clear, B. reduced, C. enlarged)"},{"number":"vii","text":"If the path difference is --------- the waves will interfere destructively. (Α. λ/2, Β. λ, C. 2λ)"},{"number":"viii","text":"What capacitor is used as a tuning capacitor? (A. electrolytic capacitor, B. ceramic capacitor, C. variable capacitor)"},{"number":"ix","text":"Which of the following metals cannot be used as fuse wire? (A. iron, B. silver, C. tin-lead alloy)"},{"number":"x","text":"On which factor does the heat produced in a current carrying conductor depend? (A. current, B. temperature, C. pressure)"},{"number":"xi","text":"There is no ideal transformer with --------- efficiency. (Α. 95%, Β. 98.5%, C. 100%)"},{"number":"xii","text":"In any electric appliance the --------- wire is always connected to the metal case. (A. live, B. earth, C. neutral)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"Radio and television are examples of --------- mode of communication. (A. broadcast, B. point to point, C. telephony)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"--------- are massless and move at the speed of light in vacuum. (A. Neutrons, B. Protons, C. Photons)"},{"number":"xv","text":"When an animal or a plant dies carbon cycle stops and the carbon-14 in the remain gradually --------- by radioactive decay. (A. decreases, B. increases, C. constant)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"Describe the analogous kinematic equations of linear and angular motion. The Ferris wheel starts from rest and reaches an angular velocity of 2.0 rad s¹ over a 10 s period under the constant angular acceleration. (i) Find the angular acceleration of Ferris wheel. (ii) How many revolutions does it make during 10 s?"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a ray diagram of a terrestrial telescope that uses a concave lens as an eyepiece. Calculate the velocity of sound in air at STP. The density of air at STP is 1.29 kg m⁻³. Assume air to be diatomic with γ = 1.4. Also calculate the velocity of sound in air at 27 °C."}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What is biomass? State the changes in the form of energy while producing (i) solar energy and (ii) geothermal energy. An important hydroelectric plant has a head of 100 m and water volumetric flow rate of 10 000 m³ s⁻¹. The turbine-generator efficiency is 60%. What is the maximum power that the plant can produce? (ρ_water = 1000 kg m⁻³, g = 9.8 m s⁻²)"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"Is LDR called light sensitive variable resistor? Why? Is LDR composed of semiconductor materials? How does its resistance change (i) in the dark light and (ii) in the bright light? Draw the simple circuit diagram of photodiode."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"If an insulating material is inserted between the conductors of a capacitor in a vacuum, does its capacitance increase or decrease? Explain. A charged capacitor of capacitance C = 35 µF is discharged through a resistor of resistance R = 100 Ω. What is the elapsed time when the voltage falls to 10% of its original value?"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Give graphical representations of the magnitude of (i) DC voltage and (ii) AC voltage as a function of time. 120 kW of electric power is sent to a small town from a power plant 10 km away. The transmission lines have a resistance of 0.40 Ω per km. Calculate the power loss if the power is transmitted at (i) 240 V and (ii) 24 000 V."}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"What do you understand by half-life? Compare the ionizing and penetrating powers of alpha, beta and gamma rays. A proton and an electron are each accelerated from rest through a potential difference of 1 kV. What are their kinetic energies? Compare their de Broglie wavelengths. (mₚ = 1840 mₑ, q = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C)"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Sketch a diagram illustrating the horizontal component of normal force provides centripetal force when a car drives in a circular path on a banked road. A grating containing 4000 slits per centimetre is illuminated with a monochromatic light and produces the second-order bright line at a 31° angle. What is the wavelength of the light? And what is the colour of the light used?"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"How do you understand capillary action? What will happen to the rise of liquid in a capillary tube if the radius of the tube is (i) increased and (ii) decreased? Give a reason for your answer. Create a diagram illustrating the voltage characteristics of charging and discharging a capacitor."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What is thermal conductivity? Why does heat transfer take place between an object and its surrounding? What is the relation between the total emissive power of an object and the total emissive power of a blackbody when both are at the same temperature? How fast must a vehicle travel for 1 s of time measured on a passenger''s watch in the vehicle to differ by 1% for an observer measuring it from the ground outside?"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"Why is electrical energy transformed into heat energy when a current flows through a resistor? Why is an electric fuse required in all electrical appliances? How many joules are there in 1 kWh? Draw the circuit diagram illustrating the street lighting system."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"What is meant by \"AM and FM\"? What are the differences between FM and AM? Two batteries each having an emf of 6 V and an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω are connected (i) in series aiding and (ii) in parallel. Find the current in each case when the batteries are connected to a 1 Ω resistor"}]}}}'::jsonb,8,true),
(12,'old_questions','2025 Set 9 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2025 · 9','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2025 Set 9</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2025-set9","year":2025,"set":9,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"In uniform circular motion, the velocity of an object changes due to a continuous change in direction, even though its speed stays constant."},{"number":"ii","text":"Motor car brake oil is considered to be compressible."},{"number":"iii","text":"Fossil fuels are replenished quickly enough to be considered a renewable energy source."},{"number":"iv","text":"Conduction is the transfer of heat through direct contact between particles of a substance."},{"number":"v","text":"The Doppler effect occurs only when the source of sound is moving, not the listener."},{"number":"vi","text":"Capacitors in parallel have the same charge on each capacitor."},{"number":"vii","text":"When batteries are connected in series, the total voltage is the sum of the individual voltages."},{"number":"viii","text":"According to Lenz''s law, the direction of induced current resists the change causing it."},{"number":"ix","text":"A digital circuit uses 0s and 1s to represent data."},{"number":"x","text":"Beta particles are high-energy electrons or positrons emitted during radioactive decay."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"The force that keeps an object moving in a circular path is directed towards the ------- of the circle."},{"number":"ii","text":"At a river junction where water streams are wirling, the flow is usually ------- rather than laminar."},{"number":"iii","text":"Renewable sources of energy include wind, solar, and -------."},{"number":"iv","text":"The natural process of heat transfer between an object and its surroundings is driven by ------- differences, aiming to reach thermal equilibrium."},{"number":"v","text":"The number of vibrations per second, which determines the pitch of sound, is called the ------- of sound."},{"number":"vi","text":"The component of a camera that regulates the amount of light entering is known as the -------."},{"number":"vii","text":"An optical device used to separate light into its component wavelengths by diffraction is called ------- grating."},{"number":"viii","text":"The ability of a capacitor to store an electric charge is measured in -------."},{"number":"ix","text":"The formula that represents the energy stored in a capacitor is -------."},{"number":"x","text":"The total electrical energy consumed in a circuit is measured in -------."},{"number":"xi","text":"Electrical power can be expressed as the product of ------- and current."},{"number":"xii","text":"In power transmission, transformers are utilized to adjust the -------."},{"number":"xiii","text":"The basic unit of data in a digital system is referred to as a -------."},{"number":"xiv","text":"In communication systems, the technique of overlaying a message signal onto a carrier wave is known as -------."},{"number":"xv","text":"The principle that describes light as having both wave-like and particle-like characteristics is called -------."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"In rotational motion under constant angular acceleration, which of the following quantities changes uniformly over time? (A. Angular displacement, B. Angular velocity, C. Moment of inertia)"},{"number":"ii","text":"Why does a river flow faster when passing through a narrow section (defile)? (A. Decreased flow velocity, B. Conservation of energy, C. Conservation of mass)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Non-renewable energy sources are finite and cannot be easily replenished within a short timeframe. Examples include: (A. Solar power, B. Wind energy, C. Coal)"},{"number":"iv","text":"Which method of heat transfer does not require a medium? (A. Conduction, B. Convection, C. Radiation)"},{"number":"v","text":"Which property of sound determines its loudness? (A. Frequency, B. Amplitude, C. Wavelength)"},{"number":"vi","text":"What principle is utilized in a compound microscope to achieve high magnification? (A. Refraction of light through a convex lens, B. Total internal reflection, C. Diffraction of light)"},{"number":"vii","text":"When two waves are completely out of phase, what is their phase difference? (A. 0°, B. 90°, С. 180°)"},{"number":"viii","text":"The capacitance of a parallel plate capacitor increases when: (A. The distance between the plates increases, B. The area of the plates increases, C. The dielectric constant decreases)"},{"number":"ix","text":"In a combination of capacitors, the total capacitance is less than the smallest individual capacitance in: (A. Series combination, B. Parallel combination, C. Neither series nor parallel)"},{"number":"x","text":"When two batteries are connected in parallel, the voltage across each battery is: (A. The sum of the individual voltages, B. Equal to the voltage of one of the batteries, C. Zero)"},{"number":"xi","text":"What is the commercial unit of electrical energy? (A. joule, B. kilowatt-hour, C. watt)"},{"number":"xii","text":"The primary danger of electricity to humans is: (A. Voltage, B. Current, C. resistance)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"What happens to the resistance of an LDR as the light intensity increases? (A. The resistance increases, B. The resistance decreases, C. The resistance remains the same)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"The emission of radiation from an unstable nucleus is called: (A. Nuclear fission, B. Radioactivity, C. Nuclear fusion)"},{"number":"xv","text":"Which of the following particles is responsible for initiating nuclear fission reactions? (A. Neutrons, B. Protons, C. Electrons)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"How does dynamic viscosity differ from kinematic viscosity? When a capillary tube stands upright in a beaker of water, the water rises h in the tube. If the radius of the tube is 2.5 mm, the contact angle is 30°, the density of water is 1000 kg m⁻³ and the surface tension is 0.072 N m⁻¹, calculate h. (g = 10 m s⁻²)"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the Pressure-Volume (p-V) diagram comparing the adiabatic process and the isothermal process for an ideal gas. A bat flying at a speed of 10 m s towards a stationary moth emits sound wave of 340 m s⁻¹. The bat hears the echoes 0.4 s later. (i) Calculate the distance travelled by the bat in 0.4 s. (ii) Calculate the distance travelled by the sound wave in 0.4 s."}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"Distinguish renewable energy sources from non-renewable energy sources, giving one example for each. Determine the input power of the wind if the wind speed is 10 m s⁻¹ and the blade length is 20 m. The density of air is 1.3 kg m⁻³."}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"Explain the difference between active and passive electronic components, providing examples of each type. Draw the symbol for an AND gate and label its inputs and output properly."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"What is the concept of capacitance, and what factors influence the capacitance of a capacitor? Three capacitors have capacitances of 5 µF, 10 µF and 15 µF. (i) Find the equivalent capacitance when they are connected in parallel. (ii) Find the equivalent capacitance when they are connected in series."}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a circuit diagram showing batteries connected in series aiding with an external resistor. An electric circuit installed in a house contains a 5 A fuse and the voltage is 220 V. Find the maximum electrical power which can safely be used. What is the equivalent of 1 kilowatt-hour (kWh) in joules?"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"Describe the principle of the special theory of relativity. Explain its significance in modern physics and provide one example of how it applies to real-world scenarios. One starry night, an earth-bound observer looking up the stars sees an extra-terrestrial spaceship flash across the sky. The ship is 55 m long and travelling at 95% of the speed of light. What would the ship''s length be when measured from an earth-bound frame of reference?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Create a diagram to represent uniform circular motion. Clearly indicate the directions of centripetal force, centripetal acceleration, and linear velocity at a specific point on the circular path. Label each vector accurately to show their respective orientations. Light from a lamp is falling normally on a surface distant 10 m from the lamp and the illuminance on it is 10 lux. In order to increase the illuminance 9 times, what distance will the lamp be placed from the surface?"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Under what condition the angular acceleration of a rotating object is equal to zero? In circular motion, how is a tangential acceleration produced? Illustrate a labelled diagram of a transformer symbol, showing all key components."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What happens when two light waves meet, and why do they sometimes make light brighter or cancel it out? Find the de Broglie wavelength of an electron in the ground state of the hydrogen atom. The radius of the first orbit of hydrogen is 0.53 Å. (h = 6.625 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, mₑ = 9.1 × 10⁻³¹ kg)"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"Describe Faraday''s law of electromagnetic induction and its importance in the generation of electricity. Provide a labelled diagram of an OR gate, a NAND gate, and a NOT gate."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"List two benefits and two drawbacks of using LED lights. A 40 µF capacitor is needed, but only 8 µF capacitors are available. How should a minimum number of 8 µF capacitors be connected so that the combination has a capacitance of 40 μF?"}]}}}'::jsonb,9,true),
(12,'old_questions','2026 Set 1 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2026 · 1','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2026 Set 1</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2026-set1","year":2026,"set":1,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"The angular acceleration is equal to zero when there is no change in angular speed."},{"number":"ii","text":"The SI unit of viscosity is newton per metre squared."},{"number":"iii","text":"Flat plate collectors are the least common type of collector."},{"number":"iv","text":"A black object is a good absorber and a good radiator."},{"number":"v","text":"The retina is the light sensitive area of the cells, at the front of the eye."},{"number":"vi","text":"A capacitor consists of two conductors separated by a small distance."},{"number":"vii","text":"The practical unit of electrical energy is kilowatt hour."},{"number":"viii","text":"The lamps are connected in parallel in the lighting circuit."},{"number":"ix","text":"A photodiode converts light into electrical current."},{"number":"x","text":"Neutrons released from a fission reaction are slow neutrons."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"The direction of tangential acceleration is always -------- to the circular path."},{"number":"ii","text":"An attractive force exists between the sun and the earth in a direction -------- to the path of the earth."},{"number":"iii","text":"A large amount of -------- energy is stored in the fossil fuels."},{"number":"iv","text":"A series of processes in which a system is brought back to its initial state is called a --------."},{"number":"v","text":"The SI units of Young’s modulus and the bulk modulus are --------."},{"number":"vi","text":"The human eye responds only to light having wavelengths between about 400 nm and --------."},{"number":"vii","text":"-------- coherent light is used in the double slits experiment."},{"number":"viii","text":"Variable capacitors mostly use air as the -------- medium."},{"number":"ix","text":"The equivalent capacitance of the capacitors connected in -------- is the sum of the capacitances of the individual capacitors."},{"number":"x","text":"In parallel connection of batteries, care must be taken that the terminal of the -------- polarity should be connected together."},{"number":"xi","text":"Mica is a good electrical -------- and can withstand very high temperature."},{"number":"xii","text":"In the alternating current the direction of the flow of electrons changes --------."},{"number":"xiii","text":"A modern light source that requires -------- voltages is the light emitting diode (LED)."},{"number":"xiv","text":"A thermistor can convert changes in -------- into changes in electric current."},{"number":"xv","text":"-------- relativity is most useful in the field of nuclear physics."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"Centrifugal pump converts mechanical energy into -------- energy by the use of centrifugal force acting on the fluid. (A. hydraulic, B. electrical, C. chemical)"},{"number":"ii","text":"Adhesion refers to forces between molecules of -------- substances. (A. same, B. different, C. normal)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Non-renewable energy sources are available only in -------- supply. (A. limited, B. unlimited, C. constant)"},{"number":"iv","text":"An isothermal process occurs at a constant --------. (A. pressure B. volume C temperature)"},{"number":"v","text":"The speed of sound is -------- in solids than liquids and gases. (A. lower B. higher C. smaller)"},{"number":"vi","text":"-------- is a defect of vision in which near objects are seen clearly, but objects far away are blurry. (A. Farsightedness B. Nearsightedness C. Blindness)"},{"number":"vii","text":"The bright and dark fringes in a diffraction pattern are created by ------ of diffracted light waves. (A. interference B. reflection C. refraction)"},{"number":"viii","text":"-------- can also be used in a time-dependent circuit (timer circuit). (A. Inductors B. Resistors C. Capacitors)"},{"number":"ix","text":"The value of dielectric constant of vacuum is --------. (A. zero B. one C. two)"},{"number":"x","text":"A refrigerator has an electrical power ranging from 100 W to --------. (A. 250 W B. 2000 W C. 1200 W)"},{"number":"xi","text":"The SI unit of magnetic field strength is the --------. (A. ampere per metre B. weber C. tesla)"},{"number":"xii","text":"A generator converts -------- energy into electrical energy. (A. chemical B. mechanical C. thermal)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"LDR consists of a disc of -------- material on its surface with two electrodes. (A. insulator B. semiconductor C. conductor) - 166 -"},{"number":"xiv","text":"-------- are massless and move at the speed of light in vacuum. (A. Neutrons B. Photons C. Electrons)"},{"number":"xv","text":"Treatment with radiation is known as --------. (A. radioactivity B. radiotherapy C. radiography)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"(i) How are the flow rate and fluid velocity related? (ii) Which force causes capillary action rise? A square plate 0.1 m side moves parallel to second plate with a velocity of 0.1 m s⁻¹, both plates being immersed in water. If the viscous force is 0.002 N and the coefficient of viscosity is 0.01 poise, what is the distance between the plates? (1 Pa s = 10 poise)"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a p-V diagram for the four reversible processes of Carnot cycle. An automobile engine has an efficiency of 20% and produces an average of 24000 J of mechanical work per second during operation. (i) How much heat input is required per second and (ii) How much heat is discharged as waste heat from this engine per second?"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What are the major types of renewable energy sources? State the changes in form of energy while producing hydroelectricity. How many lines per centimetre are there in a diffraction grating that gives a first-order maximum for 470 nm blue light at an angle of 25°?"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"What are alpha, beta and gamma rays? Describe the properties of alpha rays. Draw a diagram to show the nuclear fission."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"(i) When the charge on a capacitor is increased, does its capacitance increase? Explain. (ii) A capacitor stores charge Q at a potential difference V. What happens if the voltage applied to the capacitor is doubled? The equivalent capacitance is 10 µF when n identical capacitors are connected in parallel and 0.4 µF when they are connected in series. Determine n and the capacitance of each capacitor."}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the simple transformer. A 2 kW transformer is used to step down an AC supply of 240 V to 60 V. (i) What is the turns ratio of this transformer? (ii) What will the output current be if there is a 10% power loss in the transformer? (iii) How large is the output current if there is no power loss (100% efficiency)?"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"State De Morgan’s second theorem. Give the formula for expressing De Morgan’s second theorem for two variables and construct its truth table. Construct the truth table to prove the following Boolean algebra rule. (A + B) (A + C)= A + B C"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a diagram to show the centripetal force on the ball and its reaction force on the hand when a person whirls a ball on the end of a string in a horizontal circle around his head. (i) What frequency is received by a person watching an oncoming ambulance moving at 110 km h⁻¹ and emitting a steady 800 Hz sound from its siren? The speed of sound on this day is 345 m s⁻¹. (ii) What frequency does she receive after the ambulance has passed?"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Under what condition the angular acceleration of a rotating object is equal to zero? In circular motion, how is a tangential acceleration produced? Suppose a piece of food is on the edge of a rotating microwave oven plate. Does it experience tangential acceleration, centripetal acceleration, or both when the plate rotates at constant angular velocity and the plate slows down to stop? Draw a circuit diagram of two batteries in parallel connected with an external resistor."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What are meant by farsightedness and nearsightedness and how can they be corrected? The distance between two points, called the proper length L₀, is 1 km. An observer in motion with respect to the frame of reference of the two points measures 0.6 km, which is L. What is the relative speed of the frame of reference with respect to the observer?"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"In an electric circuit, which component is used for: (i) supply electricity (ii) close (or) open the electric circuit (iii) providing a path for the flow of electric current? What are open circuit and closed circuit? Draw the block diagram for digital communication system."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"Explain the difference between active and passive electrical components with examples. When two 6 V batteries, having the same internal resistance and connected in series, are connected to a 5 Ω resistor, the current in the circuit is 2 A. When the batteries are in parallel, a current of 1.5 A flows through when connected to another resistor. Find the resistance of the resistor. - 168 -"}]}}}'::jsonb,1,true),
(12,'old_questions','2026 Set 2 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2026 · 2','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2026 Set 2</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2026-set2","year":2026,"set":2,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"The direction of earth’s angular velocity vector is along the axis joining its poles."},{"number":"ii","text":"A fluid with low viscosity flows easily."},{"number":"iii","text":"The sun emits the maximum irradiance in the infrared region of the spectrum."},{"number":"iv","text":"Heat conduction occurs only in a liquid or a gas, never in a solid."},{"number":"v","text":"In the terrestrial telescope a convex lens is used as an eyepiece to produce an erect final image."},{"number":"vi","text":"The dielectric constant of water is larger than that of vacuum."},{"number":"vii","text":"A small amount of argon is filled in an electric light bulb."},{"number":"viii","text":"The SI unit of magnetic flux density is the weber (Wb)."},{"number":"ix","text":"NAND gate produces a ‘0’ when both inputs are ‘1’."},{"number":"x","text":"Gamma rays can be stopped by a thick sheet of paper."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"An object of mass 2 kg moves in a circle with radius 0.5 m at constant speed of 3 m s⁻¹ The net force directed toward the center is -------- N."},{"number":"ii","text":"The angular speed is the ------ for all points on a rotating circular plate."},{"number":"iii","text":"The -------- energy is produced by the difference in sea levels."},{"number":"iv","text":"-------- of an object depends to a large extent on how shiny it is."},{"number":"v","text":"The pitch of a sound is determined by its --------."},{"number":"vi","text":"The compound microscope has at least -------- convex lenses."},{"number":"vii","text":"-------- light is used in Young’s double-slit experiment."},{"number":"viii","text":"The electrical energy W stored in the capacitor is given, in terms of charge Q and potential difference V, by --------."},{"number":"ix","text":"A 1200 W electric kettle is used for 50 minutes. The electricity consumed is -------- k Wh."},{"number":"x","text":"1 k Wh of electrical energy is equal to -------- J."},{"number":"xi","text":"In the lighting circuit there are only two wires, live and --------."},{"number":"xii","text":"-------- law gives the magnitude of the induced emf in electromagnetic induction."},{"number":"xiii","text":"A transducer contains -------- element and transduction element."},{"number":"xiv","text":"The resistance of -------- decreases as the light level increases."},{"number":"xv","text":"An inertial frame is a frame of reference that has no --------."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"A cyclist moves along a curved track. To avoid slipping, the cyclist must --------. (A. lean outward, B. stand straight, C. lean inward)"},{"number":"ii","text":"What makes a small insect able to walk on the surface of water? (A. viscosity, B. surface tension, C. water pressure)"},{"number":"iii","text":"What is the main source of geothermal energy? A. sun, B. earth’s interior, C. ocean currents"},{"number":"iv","text":"Heat conduction occurs most rapidly in --------. A. metals, B. wood, C. air"},{"number":"v","text":"How does the intensity of a wave I vary with its amplitude A? A. I ∝ A2 B. I ∝ A3 C. I ∝ 1/A"},{"number":"vi","text":"Which wavelength corresponds to the maximum sensitivity of the human eye under daylight? A. 450 nm (blue), B. 555 nm (green), C. 700 nm (red)"},{"number":"vii","text":"Slits per unit length in a diffraction grating is called --------. A. grating constant, B. grating element, C. grating frequency"},{"number":"viii","text":"The product of the resistance and the -------- is called the time constant of a capacitor charging or discharging process. A. capacitance, B. inductance, C. voltage"},{"number":"ix","text":"When the distance between the two parallel plates of a capacitor is doubled, the capacitance becomes -------- of its initial value. (A. 20 %, B. 50 %, C. 80 %)"},{"number":"x","text":"The resultant emf of two batteries in -------- is the difference between the individual emfs. A. series opposing, B. series aiding, C. parallel"},{"number":"xi","text":"The current from the output of a telephone charger is --------. A. AC, B. DC, C. both AC and DC"},{"number":"xii","text":"In parallel connection of batteries, the terminals of the -------- should be connected together. A. opposite polarity, B. mixed polarity, C. same polarity"},{"number":"xiii","text":"LEDs do not directly produce -------- light. A. red, B. blue, C. white"},{"number":"xiv","text":"Activity of a radioactive sample -------- with time. A. decreases, B. increases, C. does not change"},{"number":"xv","text":"Time dilation becomes significant when the speed of the system ------. A. is close to the speed of light, B. is zero, C. is very low - 170 -"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"What is capillary action? Explain its cause in terms of adhesive and cohesive forces. State one necessary condition for a liquid to rise in a capillary tube. At a certain temperature, water has a surface tension of 0.072 N m⁻¹. In a 3 mm diameter vertical tube, if the liquid rises 6 mm above the liquid outside the tube, calculate the contact angle. (ρ_water = 1000 kg m⁻³, g = 9.8 m s⁻²)"}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the waveforms of (i) two sounds with the same loudness but different pitch and (ii) two sounds with the same pitch but different loudness. In an isothermal process at 27 °C, 2 kilomoles of an ideal gas are compressed from a volume of 4 litres to 1 litre. Find the work done on the system. (R = 8.3143 J mol⁻¹ K⁻¹)"}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What is the relation between the theoretical wind power, wind speed and rotor area of a wind turbine? If the radius of the rotor is doubled, by what factor does the wind power increase? Assume the wind speed is constant. The wind is blowing at 10 m s⁻¹. Calculate the total power produced by the wind turbine if the blades are 45 m long. (ρ_air = 1.3 kg m⁻³)"}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"When the zener diode is in forward-bias mode, what is its turn-on voltage? Explain zener effect. What are two types of reverse breakdown regions in a zener diode? Plot the I-V characteristics of a zener diode showing two breakdown regions."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"Write down the advantages of inserting dielectrics (insulating materials) between the plates of a capacitor. A charged capacitor of capacitance C = 35 μF is discharged through a resistor of resistance R = 120 Ω. What is the elapsed time when the voltage falls to 10% of its original value?"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a circuit diagram showing two batteries in series aiding connected with an external resistor R. Label the emf E and internal resistance r for each battery, and indicate the direction of current flow. Two batteries each having an emf of 5 V and an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω are connected (i) in series and (ii) in parallel. Find the current in each case when the batteries are connected to a 1 Ω resistor."}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"Compare the ionizing and penetrating powers of alpha, beta, and gamma rays. Suppose there was 2 g of radon at t = 0 and its half-life is 3.8 days. How much would be left after 15.2 days?"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"A plane of mass m is flying at constant speed v along a circular path with its wings banked at angle θ to the vertical. Draw a diagram showing all forces acting on the plane, and indicate which component of lift force provides the centripetal force. An astronomical telescope has its two lenses 75.2 cm apart. If the objective lens has a focal length of 70 cm, what is the magnifying power of this telescope when viewing with a relaxed eye?"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Distinguish between circular motion and rotational motion. Provide an example for each type of motion. Consider a uniform magnetic field B passing through a plane surface of area A. Draw two separate diagrams showing the orientation of the plane for (i) maximum magnetic flux and (ii) zero magnetic flux."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What are the conditions for constructive interference and destructive interference between two coherent waves? Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of (i) a 0.65 kg basketball thrown at a speed of 10 m s⁻¹ and (ii) a nonrelativistic electron moving with a speed of 0.59 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹. Evaluate your answer. (mₑ = 9.1 × 10⁻³¹ kg, h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s)"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"How many types of transformers are there? Which type of transformer is used in a welding machine? Explain your answer. Draw the logic circuit represented by each of the following expressions: ) ) (i) A + B, (ii) A + BC, (iii) AB + CD"}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"Give a brief account on frequency modulation (FM) and amplitude modulation (AM). The primary coil of a step-up transformer having 220 turns is connected to a 110 V alternating voltage source. The secondary delivers a voltage of 12000 V and a current of 40 mA. (i) How many turns are there in the secondary? (ii) What is the current in the primary? - 172 -"}]}}}'::jsonb,2,true),
(12,'old_questions','2026 Set 3 | Grade 12 Physics','Set 2026 · 3','{"html":"<header class=\"oq-intro\"><span>GRADE 12 PHYSICS</span><h2>2026 Set 3</h2><p>Section A သို့မဟုတ် Section B ကို ရွေးချယ်ပါ။</p></header><section id=\"oq-paper-content\" aria-label=\"မေးခွန်းများ\"></section>","paper":{"key":"2026-set3","year":2026,"set":3,"sample":false,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"Angular velocity is the rate of rotation with respect to time."},{"number":"ii","text":"Centripetal and centrifugal forces are equal."},{"number":"iii","text":"Solar collectors transfer heat from solar radiation to water."},{"number":"iv","text":"Wood is a better conductor of heat than copper."},{"number":"v","text":"Soft materials absorb sound."},{"number":"vi","text":"Charging a capacitor means connecting the capacitor to a resistor."},{"number":"vii","text":"A fuse wire must be made of a material with a high melting point."},{"number":"viii","text":"A great industrial current is known as direct current."},{"number":"ix","text":"Frequency modulation (FM) radio ranges up to 1200 bits per second."},{"number":"x","text":"The Michelson Morley experiment provided evidence for the existence of the ether."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"The equation ω² = ω₀² + 2αθ is analogous to ----------- in linear motion."},{"number":"ii","text":"There are ----------- ways to measure the fluid''s viscosity."},{"number":"iii","text":"The power available in the wind is proportional to the ----------- of the wind speed."},{"number":"iv","text":"The emissivity of an object depends on the ----------- of radiation."},{"number":"v","text":"Bats and dolphins use ----------- in echolocation."},{"number":"vi","text":"People with normal vision can see clearly objects which are at ---------."},{"number":"vii","text":"A diffraction grating consists of a large number of parallel slits of the same width separated by equal ----------- spaces."},{"number":"viii","text":"Placing a resistor in the charging circuit ---------- the charging process."},{"number":"ix","text":"In charging a battery, the potential difference between the terminals is equal to -----------."},{"number":"x","text":"Electric light bulbs are of various ----------- and electric power."},{"number":"xi","text":"A rotating coil in a magnetic field is the basic of an -----------."},{"number":"xii","text":"The power sockets in a house are connected by means of a -----------."},{"number":"xiii","text":"The basic operations in Boolean algebra are AND, OR, and -----------."},{"number":"xiv","text":"OLED stands for ----------- Light-Emitting Diode."},{"number":"xv","text":"Photons are ----------- and move at the speed of light in vacuum."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"Which statement correctly applies Newton''s third law to the centripetal force provided by a rope pulling a ball in a circle? (A. the reaction force is the force the ball exerts on the hand, directed outward, B. the reaction force is the centrifugal force acting on the ball, C. the reaction force is the gravitational force on the ball)"},{"number":"ii","text":"Which of the following is a characteristic assumption of an ideal laminar fluid flow? (A. The fluid is highly compressible, B. The flow has zero viscosity, C. The fluid flow is turbulent)"},{"number":"iii","text":"Which is NOT a socioeconomic factor that contributes to the energy crisis? (A. Population, B. Urbanization, C. The temperature of the Sun)"},{"number":"iv","text":"An ideal gas undergoes an isothermal expansion. What can be said about the change in its internal energy (∆U)? (A. ∆U > 0, B. ∆U = 0, C. ∆U < 0)"},{"number":"v","text":"When a source of sound moves away from a stationary observer, the observed frequency of the sound: (A. is greater than the source frequency, B. is less than the source frequency, C. is equal to the source frequency)."},{"number":"vi","text":"What is the main function of the cladding in an optical fibre? (A. To protect the core from external damage, B. To increase the core''s refractive index, C. To provide a lower refractive index to cause total internal reflection in the core)"},{"number":"vii","text":"What is the nature of the wavefront far away from the source? (A. Spherical wavefront, B. Plane wavefront, C. Cylindrical wavefront)"},{"number":"viii","text":"The energy stored in a charged capacitor is given by (A. W = QV, B. W = 1/2 VQ, C. W = CV)."},{"number":"ix","text":"In a series aiding connection of two or more batteries, the resultant emf will: (A. remain the same as a single battery, B. decrease the overall voltage, C. increase the overall voltage)."},{"number":"x","text":"The heating effect of electric current is applied in all of the following appliances except: (A. Electric stove, B. Electric iron, C. Refrigerator)."},{"number":"xi","text":"The phenomenon in which a current flows through a wire loop due to a change in the magnetic lines of force through the loop is called: (A. Magnetic flux, B. Electromagnetic induction, C. Faraday''s law). - 174 -"},{"number":"xii","text":"Which wire carries the current from the supply to the appliance? (A. Neutral wire, B. Earth wire, C. Live wire)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"Which of the following is NOT listed as one of the six main pieces that comprise a radio receiver? (A. Antenna, B. Diode detector, C. Frequency modulator)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"Which of the following is a dangerous radioactive fission product? (A. Carbon, B. Strontium, C. Helium)"},{"number":"xv","text":"Which radiation has no charge and is most penetrating? (A. Alpha ray, B. Beta ray, C. Gamma ray)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"What is the difference between laminar flow and turbulent flow? Which type of fluid flow is assumed when applying Bernoulli’s principle? A gardener uses a water pipe of 2.5 cm diameter. It takes 1 min to fill 30 litre bucket. What is the initial speed of water coming out of the hose? Then nozzle with an opening 0.5 cm² is attached to the hose. Find the water speed coming out from the nozzle."}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a ray diagram of an astronomical telescope. Calculate the velocity of sound in air at STP. The density of air at STP is 1.29 kg m⁻³. Assume air to be diatomic with γ = 1.4. Also calculate the velocity of sound in air at 27 °C."}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"What is the main source of energy? What are the advantages of geothermal energy compared to other energy sources? The wind is blowing at 10 m s⁻¹. How much total power is produced by the wind turbine if the blades are 45 m long? The density of air is 1.3 kg m⁻³."}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"Compare the point-to-point and broadcast modes of communication. Provide one practical example for each mode. State one advantage of digital communication. Draw and label the characteristic curve of a thermistor."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"In capacitor charging and discharging, why is a resistor required to connect with the capacitor? Does a capacitor allow AC current to pass but block DC current after being fully charged? The plates of a parallel-plate capacitor are 50 cm² in area and 1 mm apart. (i) What is its capacitance? (ii) When the capacitor is connected to a 24 V battery, what is the charge on each plate? (iii) What is the energy of the capacitor?"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw an illustration of the terminal voltage of a battery. An electric circuit installed in an office contains a 10 A fuse and the voltage is 220 V. Ten 100 W electric lamps and two 150 W refrigerators are being used there. (i) Find the cost of using all the lamps and two refrigerators for 10 h. (ii) Find the maximum number of 60 W electric lamps which can be safely used in addition. (Assume that electricity costs 50 kyats per unit.)"}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"What device is a nuclear reactor? Name the essential components of a nuclear reactor. If a fossil has 10% carbon-14 compared to a living sample, find the age of the fossil. (half-life of carbon-14 = 5730 years)"}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw a diagram showing the relationship between the angular velocity vector ω⃗, position vector r⃗, and linear velocity v⃗ of a particle in circular motion. In a room, the temperature of water in a kettle is 80 °C. The room temperature is 30 °C and the surface area of the kettle is 0.02 m². If the emissivity is 0.9, find the rate of heat loss due to radiation. (σ = 5.685 × 10⁻⁸ W m⁻² K⁻⁴)"}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"Does the centripetal force and centrifugal force constitute an action- reaction pair? Explain. Draw a diagram that illustrates the induced current produced by a moving magnet."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"What does “two waves are coherent” mean? Why is monochromatic coherent light used in the double-slit experiment? In the past, radios contained vacuum tubes that generated and accelerated electrons. A tube operates at 100 V. Find the speed of an electron and its de Broglie wavelength. (mₑ = 9.1 × 10⁻³¹ kg)"}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"Explain each of the following: (i) A transformer will not work on DC. (ii) The core of a transformer needs to be laminated. (iii) If a transformer increases voltage, it reduces current. Draw and label the block diagram of a simple radio receiver."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"Explain the function of a photodiode. How does light intensity affect the photocurrent? The current in an AC circuit at any time t seconds is given by I = 20 sin (100πt) A. Find (i) the peak value (maximum value) of current, the period and the frequency (ii) the value of the current when t = 0 (iii) the value of the current when t = 8 ms (iv) the time when the current reaches 10 A."}]}}}'::jsonb,3,true),
(12,'old_questions','2024 Sample Question','Set 2024 · SQ','{"html":"","paper":{"key":"2024-sq","year":2024,"set":null,"sample":true,"foreign":false,"sectionA":{"1":[{"number":"i","text":"The angular acceleration of rotating object is always zero."},{"number":"ii","text":"The centripetal force is the force acting towards the centre of the circular path."},{"number":"iii","text":"The sun is one of the most powerful renewable energies."},{"number":"iv","text":"Two common defects of vision are farsightedness and nearsightedness."},{"number":"v","text":"The decibel (dB) is the unit used for measuring sound intensity."},{"number":"vi","text":"A resistor is an electrical device that stores electrical energy in the form of electric field."},{"number":"vii","text":"The SI unit of the electromotive force of a battery is newton."},{"number":"viii","text":"The changing magnetic field could produce a current."},{"number":"ix","text":"Zener diode is a heavily doped semiconductor p-n junction diode."},{"number":"x","text":"Beta particle is helium nucleus."}],"2":[{"number":"i","text":"In a circular motion, the object just moves in a -------."},{"number":"ii","text":"Centrifugal force in a circular motion is not a ------- force."},{"number":"iii","text":"Wind energy is the energy generated or produced by harnessing the --- ---- of the wind."},{"number":"iv","text":"Heat engine is a system that converts heat to ------- energy."},{"number":"v","text":"Sound travels ------- in moist (or) humid air."},{"number":"vi","text":"A camera is an optical instrument that forms and ------- an image of an object."},{"number":"vii","text":"Monochromatic light means that it has a ------- wavelength."},{"number":"viii","text":"The capacitance of capacitor is ratio of the ------- to the potential difference."},{"number":"ix","text":"The potential difference each capacitor is the same in ------- combination of the capacitors."},{"number":"x","text":"The value of Joule’s of mechanical equivalent of heat (J) is -------."},{"number":"xi","text":"The unit of magnetic flux density (B) is -------."},{"number":"xii","text":"In the lighting circuit, the light bulbs are arranged in ------- across the mains line."},{"number":"xiii","text":"------- break down occurs at junction which being heavily doped have narrow depleting layer."},{"number":"xiv","text":"A liquid crystal display (LCD) is ------- display."},{"number":"xv","text":"Alpha rays are the ------- penetrating of the three rays."}],"3":[{"number":"i","text":"The angular acceleration is equal to zero when there is no change -----. (A. in angular speed, B. in direction of rotation, C. in angular velocity)"},{"number":"ii","text":"The SI unit of viscosity is -------. (A. Pascal second, B. newton per metre, C. metre per second)"},{"number":"iii","text":"What principle pulls water into the penstock? (A. Gravity, B. Force of the volume of water, C. Turbine)"},{"number":"iv","text":"An isochoric process occurs at constant -------. (A. pressure, B. volume, C. temperature)"},{"number":"v","text":"Heat engine is a system that converts heat to ------- energy. (A. mechanical, B. electrical, C. chemical)"},{"number":"vi","text":"In an optical fibre, the light is transmitted through the -------. (A. core, B. cladding, C. jacket)"},{"number":"vii","text":"The core of fibre-optic cable is made of -------. (A. copper wire, B. thin strand of glass, C. lead wire)"},{"number":"viii","text":"Which of the following metals cannot be used as fuse wire? (A. iron, B. silver, C. tin-lead alloy)"},{"number":"ix","text":"A capacitor is ------- device that stores electrical energy. (A. an electrical, B. a mechanical, C. a chemical)"},{"number":"x","text":"The unit of electrical power (P) is the -------. (A. ampere, B. watt, C. farad)"},{"number":"xi","text":"The SI unit of magnetic flux density is the -------. (A. weber, B. tesla, C. ampere per metre)"},{"number":"xii","text":"There is ------- in 1 kWh. (A. 6.3 × 10⁶ J, B. 1.6 × 10⁶ J, C. 3.6 × 10⁶ J)"},{"number":"xiii","text":"------- is used to control the brightness of street lamps. (A. LED, B. LDR, C. Thermistor)"},{"number":"xiv","text":"A photodiode is a ------- device that converts lights into electrical current. (A. insulator, B. conductor, C. semiconductor)"},{"number":"xv","text":"Alpha rays can be deflected by -------. (A. electric field, B. magnetic field, C. electric and magnetic field)"}]},"sectionB":{"4a":[{"number":"","text":"Consider a rotating circular plate of a lathe machine. Are the angular and tangential speeds at any point on the plate the same? Explain. Why is centripetal acceleration produced in a circular motion? A 60 cm rope is tied to the handle of a bucket which is then whirled in vertical circle. The mass of the bucket is 3 kg. If the tension of the rope at the lowest point in its path is 50 N, find the speed of the bucket at that point."}],"4b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw ray diagram of an astronomical telescope. A beam of green light from a laser light source is diffracted by a slit of width 0.55 mm. The diffraction pattern forms on a wall 20.6 m beyond the slit. The distance between the positions of the first minima on both sides of the central bright fringe is 4.1mm. Calculate the wavelength of the laser light."}],"5a":[{"number":"","text":"Why does the energy demand increase year by year? What is a main source of power of a hydroelectric power plant? Determine the input power of the wind if the wind speed is 20 m s⁻¹ and blade length is 20 m. Density of air is 1.3 kg m⁻³."}],"5b":[{"number":"","text":"Where are LEDs used? Describe some applications of LEDs. What effect does an increase of light intensity on LDR have on its resistance? What is a disadvantage of LCD displays? Illustrate the block diagram of general electronic communication system."}],"6a":[{"number":"","text":"Mention the appropriate wiring circuit for the following electrical appliances (i) bulb and fluorescent lamp (ii) electric iron (iii) water pump motor (iv) electric stove. A square loop of wire of side 5.0 cm is in a uniform magnetic field 0.16 T. What is the magnetic flux in the loop (i) when magnetic field is perpendicular to the surface of the loop and (ii) when magnetic field is at an angle of 30° to the surface of the loop?"}],"6b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the induced current produced by moving magnet. 120 kW of electric power is sent to a small town from power plant 10 km away. The transmission lines have a resistance of 0.40 Ω per km. Calculate the power loss if the power is transmitted at (i) 240 V and (ii) 24 000V."}],"7a":[{"number":"","text":"What device is a nuclear reactor? Give a brief description of the essential component of nuclear reactor. Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of (i) a 0.65 kg basketball thrown at a speed of 10 m s⁻¹, (ii) a nonrelativistic electron with a kinetic energy of 1 eV."}],"7b":[{"number":"","text":"Draw the resultant acceleration of nonuniform circular motion. What is the speed of sound in (i) a steel rod and (ii) water? Young’s modulus of steel is 2.0 × 10¹¹ N m⁻² and its density is 7.8 × 10³ kg m⁻³. The bulk modulus of water is 0.22 × 10¹⁰ N m⁻² and its density is 1.0 × 10³ kg m⁻³."}],"8a":[{"number":"","text":"For an object moving in a circle with constant angular velocity, what is the direction of acceleration of the object? When a bob is swinging in the vertical circle at which point on the circular part is the tension in the rope the greatest? Draw the variation of the induced emf as a function of ωt."}],"8b":[{"number":"","text":"How does wind power generate electricity? Why are wind and solar energies more popular than ocean energy? Suppose there was 2 g of radon at t = 0 and its half-life is 3.8 days. How much would be left after 15.2 days."}],"9a":[{"number":"","text":"Explain each of the following: (i) A transformer will not work on DC. (ii) The core of a transformer needs to be laminated. (iii) If a transformer increases voltage, it reduces current. Draw a graph illustrating the half-life of radium which has a half-life of 1620 years."}],"9b":[{"number":"","text":"Give a short note on communication system. Write short notes on the components of a simple radio receiver. A step-down transformer is used to light a 12 V, 24 W lamp from the 240 V mains. The current through the primary is 125 mA. What is the efficiency of the transformer?"}]}}}'::jsonb,0,true);
